ecial":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-03T05:16:56.429526+00:00","operations":[{"id":"a53b5ac3-0df4-49d2-b924-14e8f6e221e2","data":{"value":"low-light vision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can see in dim light as though it were bright light, so you ignore the concealed condition due to dim light.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19604,"type":"action","before":{"id":19604,"cost":null,"name":"Aid","type":"action","uuid":"58279098319844","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"An ally is about to use an action that requires a skill check or attack roll.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2292","book":"Player Core","page":"416"},"foundry":{"rules":[]},"unselectable":false},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:28:17.88536+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You try to help your ally with a task. To use this reaction, you must first prepare to help, usually by using an action (<abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr>) during your turn. You must explain to the GM exactly how you're trying to help, and they determine whether you can Aid your ally.\n\nWhen you use your Aid reaction, attempt a skill check or attack roll of a type decided by the GM. The typical DC is 15, but the GM might adjust this DC for particularly hard or easy tasks. The GM can add any relevant traits to your preparatory action or to your Aid reaction depending on the situation, or even allow you to Aid checks other than skill checks and attack rolls.\n\n**Critical Success** You grant your ally a +2 circumstance bonus to the triggering check. If you're a master with the check you attempted, the bonus is +3, and if you're legendary, it's +4.\n\n**Success** You grant your ally a +1 circumstance bonus to the triggering check.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your ally takes a –1 circumstance penalty to the triggering check.","availability":null,"requirements":"The ally is willing to accept your aid, and you have prepared to help (see below).","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19604,"cost":null,"name":"Aid","type":"action","uuid":"58279098319844","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"An ally is about to use an action that requires a skill check or attack roll.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2292","book":"Player Core","page":"416"},"foundry":{"rules":[]},"unselectable":false},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:28:17.88536+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You try to help your ally with a task. To use this reaction, you must first prepare to help, usually by using an action (<abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr>) during your turn. You must explain to the GM exactly how you're trying to help, and they determine whether you can Aid your ally.\n\nWhen you use your Aid reaction, attempt a skill check or attack roll of a type decided by the GM. The typical DC is 15, but the GM might adjust this DC for particularly hard or easy tasks. The GM can add any relevant traits to your preparatory action or to your Aid reaction depending on the situation, or even allow you to Aid checks other than skill checks and attack rolls.\n\n**Critical Success** You grant your ally a +2 circumstance bonus to the triggering check. If you're a master with the check you attempted, the bonus is +3, and if you're legendary, it's +4.\n\n**Success** You grant your ally a +1 circumstance bonus to the triggering check.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your ally takes a –1 circumstance penalty to the triggering check.","availability":null,"requirements":"The ally is willing to accept your aid, and you have prepared to help (see below).","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19606,"type":"action","before":{"id":19606,"cost":null,"name":"Arrest a Fall","type":"action","uuid":"8434443717222138","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"You fall.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2308","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:28:44.193953+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt an Acrobatics check or Reflex save to slow your fall. The DC is typically 15, but it might be higher due to air turbulence or other circumstances.\n\n**Success** You take no damage from the fall.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a fly Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19606,"cost":null,"name":"Arrest a Fall","type":"action","uuid":"8434443717222138","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"You fall.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2308","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:28:44.193953+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt an Acrobatics check or Reflex save to slow your fall. The DC is typically 15, but it might be higher due to air turbulence or other circumstances.\n\n**Success** You take no damage from the fall.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a fly Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19608,"type":"action","before":{"id":19608,"cost":null,"name":"Balance","type":"action","uuid":"7614015615752326","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ACROBATICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2369","book":"Player Core","page":"233"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:29:29.475662+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move across a narrow surface or uneven ground, attempting an Acrobatics check against its Balance DC. You are Off-Guard while on a narrow surface or uneven ground.\n\n**Critical Success** You move up to your Speed.\n\n**Success** You move up to your Speed, treating it as difficult terrain (every 5 feet costs 10 feet of movement).\n\n**Failure** You must remain stationary to keep your balance (wasting the action) or you fall. If you fall, your turn ends.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall and your turn ends.\n\nSample Balance Tasks\n--------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** tangled roots, uneven cobblestones\n*   **Trained** wooden beam\n*   **Expert** deep, loose gravel\n*   **Master** tightrope, smooth sheet of ice\n*   **Legendary** razor's edge, chunks of floor falling in midair","availability":null,"requirements":"You are in a square that contains a narrow surface, uneven ground, or another similar feature.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19608,"cost":null,"name":"Balance","type":"action","uuid":"7614015615752326","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ACROBATICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2369","book":"Player Core","page":"233"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:29:29.475662+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move across a narrow surface or uneven ground, attempting an Acrobatics check against its Balance DC. You are Off-Guard while on a narrow surface or uneven ground.\n\n**Critical Success** You move up to your Speed.\n\n**Success** You move up to your Speed, treating it as difficult terrain (every 5 feet costs 10 feet of movement).\n\n**Failure** You must remain stationary to keep your balance (wasting the action) or you fall. If you fall, your turn ends.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall and your turn ends.\n\nSample Balance Tasks\n--------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** tangled roots, uneven cobblestones\n*   **Trained** wooden beam\n*   **Expert** deep, loose gravel\n*   **Master** tightrope, smooth sheet of ice\n*   **Legendary** razor's edge, chunks of floor falling in midair","availability":null,"requirements":"You are in a square that contains a narrow surface, uneven ground, or another similar feature.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19609,"type":"action","before":{"id":19609,"cost":null,"name":"Burrow","type":"action","uuid":"5967795478730342","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2310","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:29:45.36276+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You dig your way through dirt, sand, or a similar loose material at a rate up to your burrow Speed. You can't burrow through rock or other substances denser than dirt unless you have an ability that allows you to do so.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a burrow Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19609,"cost":null,"name":"Burrow","type":"action","uuid":"5967795478730342","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2310","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:29:45.36276+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You dig your way through dirt, sand, or a similar loose material at a rate up to your burrow Speed. You can't burrow through rock or other substances denser than dirt unless you have an ability that allows you to do so.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a burrow Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19611,"type":"action","before":{"id":19611,"cost":null,"name":"Cast a Spell","type":"action","uuid":"3222895456836016","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:30:43.277321+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Spells can vary in how many actions they take, as shown in the spell’s stat block. You cast cantrips, spells from spell slots, and focus spells using the same process, but must expend the spell when casting a spell from a spell slot and must spend 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell. Some rules will refer to the Cast a Spell activity, such as “if the next action you use is to Cast a Spell.” Any spell qualifies as a Cast a Spell activity, and any characteristics of the spell use those of the specific spell you’re casting.\n\n### **Costs and Loci**\n\nSome spells require you to pay a cost or provide a locus. If the spell lists a cost, you must have the listed money, valuable materials, or other resources to cast the spell (such as gems or magical reagents), and they're expended during the casting.\n\nA locus is an object that funnels or directs the magical energy of the spell but is not consumed in its casting. As part of Casting the Spell, you retrieve the locus (if necessary, and if you have a free hand), and you can put it away again if you so choose. Loci tend to be expensive, and you need to acquire them in advance to cast the spell, but they aren't expended like costs are. Unless noted otherwise, a locus has negligible Bulk.\n\n### **Long Casting Times**\n\nSome spells take minutes or hours to cast. You can’t use other actions or reactions while casting such a spell, though at the GM’s discretion, you might be able to speak a few sentences. As with other activities that take a long time, these spells have the exploration trait, and you can’t cast them in an encounter. If combat breaks out while you’re casting one, your spell is disrupted.\n\n### **Disrupted and Lost Spells**\n\nSome abilities and spells can disrupt a spell, causing it to have no effect and be lost. When you lose a spell, you’ve already expended the spell slot and spent the spell’s costs and actions. If a spell is disrupted during a [Sustain](link_action_19858) action, the spell immediately ends.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19611,"cost":null,"name":"Cast a Spell","type":"action","uuid":"3222895456836016","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:30:43.277321+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Spells can vary in how many actions they take, as shown in the spell’s stat block. You cast cantrips, spells from spell slots, and focus spells using the same process, but must expend the spell when casting a spell from a spell slot and must spend 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell. Some rules will refer to the Cast a Spell activity, such as “if the next action you use is to Cast a Spell.” Any spell qualifies as a Cast a Spell activity, and any characteristics of the spell use those of the specific spell you’re casting.\n\n### **Costs and Loci**\n\nSome spells require you to pay a cost or provide a locus. If the spell lists a cost, you must have the listed money, valuable materials, or other resources to cast the spell (such as gems or magical reagents), and they're expended during the casting.\n\nA locus is an object that funnels or directs the magical energy of the spell but is not consumed in its casting. As part of Casting the Spell, you retrieve the locus (if necessary, and if you have a free hand), and you can put it away again if you so choose. Loci tend to be expensive, and you need to acquire them in advance to cast the spell, but they aren't expended like costs are. Unless noted otherwise, a locus has negligible Bulk.\n\n### **Long Casting Times**\n\nSome spells take minutes or hours to cast. You can’t use other actions or reactions while casting such a spell, though at the GM’s discretion, you might be able to speak a few sentences. As with other activities that take a long time, these spells have the exploration trait, and you can’t cast them in an encounter. If combat breaks out while you’re casting one, your spell is disrupted.\n\n### **Disrupted and Lost Spells**\n\nSome abilities and spells can disrupt a spell, causing it to have no effect and be lost. When you lose a spell, you’ve already expended the spell slot and spent the spell’s costs and actions. If a spell is disrupted during a [Sustain](link_action_19858) action, the spell immediately ends.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19612,"type":"action","before":{"id":19612,"cost":null,"name":"Climb","type":"action","uuid":"5724384233395263","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2374","book":"Player Core","page":"234"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:31:17.849811+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt an Athletics check to move a maximum distance of 5 feet up, down, or across an incline. You're off-guard while climbing unless you have a climb Speed. The GM determines the DC based on the nature of the incline and environmental circumstances; you might get an automatic critical success on an incline that's trivial to climb. If your land Speed is 40 feet or higher, increase the maximum distance by 5 feet for every 20 feet of Speed above 20 feet.\n\n**Critical Success** You move along the incline, increasing the maximum distance by 5 feet.\n\n**Success** You move along the incline.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall. If you began the climb on stable ground, you fall and land Prone.\n\nSample Climb Tasks\n------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** ladder, steep slope, low-branched tree\n*   **Trained** rigging, rope, typical tree\n*   **Expert** wall with small handholds and footholds\n*   **Master** ceiling with handholds and footholds, rock wall\n*   **Legendary** smooth surface","availability":null,"requirements":"You have both hands free","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19612,"cost":null,"name":"Climb","type":"action","uuid":"5724384233395263","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2374","book":"Player Core","page":"234"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:31:17.849811+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt an Athletics check to move a maximum distance of 5 feet up, down, or across an incline. You're off-guard while climbing unless you have a climb Speed. The GM determines the DC based on the nature of the incline and environmental circumstances; you might get an automatic critical success on an incline that's trivial to climb. If your land Speed is 40 feet or higher, increase the maximum distance by 5 feet for every 20 feet of Speed above 20 feet.\n\n**Critical Success** You move along the incline, increasing the maximum distance by 5 feet.\n\n**Success** You move along the incline.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall. If you began the climb on stable ground, you fall and land Prone.\n\nSample Climb Tasks\n------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** ladder, steep slope, low-branched tree\n*   **Trained** rigging, rope, typical tree\n*   **Expert** wall with small handholds and footholds\n*   **Master** ceiling with handholds and footholds, rock wall\n*   **Legendary** smooth surface","availability":null,"requirements":"You have both hands free","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19613,"type":"action","before":{"id":19613,"cost":null,"name":"Coerce","type":"action","uuid":"5895801530397232","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1486,1457,1458,1448,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"INTIMIDATION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2394","book":"Player Core","page":"240"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:32:12.916278+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With threats either veiled or overt, you attempt to bully a creature into doing what you want. You must spend at least 1 minute of conversation with the creature. At the end of the conversation, attempt an Intimidation check against the target's Will DC, modified by any circumstances the GM determines. (The attitudes referenced in the effects below are summarized in the Changing Attitudes section at the bottom)\n\n**Critical Success** The target gives you the information you seek or agrees to follow your directives so long as they aren't likely to harm the target in any way. The target continues to comply for an amount of time determined by the GM but not exceeding 1 day, at which point the target becomes unfriendly (if it wasn't already unfriendly or hostile). However, the target is too scared of you to retaliate—at least in the short term.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but once the target becomes unfriendly, they might decide to act against you—for example, by reporting you to the authorities or assisting your enemies.\n\n**Failure** The target doesn't do what you say, and if they were not already unfriendly or hostile, they become unfriendly.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target refuses to comply, becomes hostile if they weren't already, and is temporarily immune to your Coercion for at least 1 week.\n\nChanging Attitudes\n------------------\n\nYour influence on NPCs is measured with a set of attitudes that reflect how they view your character. These are only a brief summary of a creature's disposition. The GM will supply additional nuance based on the history and beliefs of the characters you're interacting with, and their attitudes can change in accordance with the story. The attitudes are detailed in the Conditions Appendix and are summarized here.\n\n*   **Helpful:** Willing to help you and responds favorably to your requests.\n    \n*   **Friendly:** Has a good attitude toward you, but won't necessarily stick their neck out to help you.\n    \n*   **Indifferent:** Doesn't care about you either way. (Most NPCs start out indifferent.)\n    \n*   **Unfriendly:** Dislikes you and doesn't want to help you.\n    \n*   **Hostile:** Actively works against you—and might attack you just because of their dislike.\n    \n\nNo one can ever change the attitude of a player character with these skills. You can roleplay interactions with player characters, and even use Diplomacy results if the player wants a mechanical sense of how convincing or charming a character is, but players make the ultimate decisions about how their characters respond.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19613,"cost":null,"name":"Coerce","type":"action","uuid":"5895801530397232","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1486,1457,1458,1448,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"INTIMIDATION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2394","book":"Player Core","page":"240"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:32:12.916278+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With threats either veiled or overt, you attempt to bully a creature into doing what you want. You must spend at least 1 minute of conversation with the creature. At the end of the conversation, attempt an Intimidation check against the target's Will DC, modified by any circumstances the GM determines. (The attitudes referenced in the effects below are summarized in the Changing Attitudes section at the bottom)\n\n**Critical Success** The target gives you the information you seek or agrees to follow your directives so long as they aren't likely to harm the target in any way. The target continues to comply for an amount of time determined by the GM but not exceeding 1 day, at which point the target becomes unfriendly (if it wasn't already unfriendly or hostile). However, the target is too scared of you to retaliate—at least in the short term.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but once the target becomes unfriendly, they might decide to act against you—for example, by reporting you to the authorities or assisting your enemies.\n\n**Failure** The target doesn't do what you say, and if they were not already unfriendly or hostile, they become unfriendly.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target refuses to comply, becomes hostile if they weren't already, and is temporarily immune to your Coercion for at least 1 week.\n\nChanging Attitudes\n------------------\n\nYour influence on NPCs is measured with a set of attitudes that reflect how they view your character. These are only a brief summary of a creature's disposition. The GM will supply additional nuance based on the history and beliefs of the characters you're interacting with, and their attitudes can change in accordance with the story. The attitudes are detailed in the Conditions Appendix and are summarized here.\n\n*   **Helpful:** Willing to help you and responds favorably to your requests.\n    \n*   **Friendly:** Has a good attitude toward you, but won't necessarily stick their neck out to help you.\n    \n*   **Indifferent:** Doesn't care about you either way. (Most NPCs start out indifferent.)\n    \n*   **Unfriendly:** Dislikes you and doesn't want to help you.\n    \n*   **Hostile:** Actively works against you—and might attack you just because of their dislike.\n    \n\nNo one can ever change the attitude of a player character with these skills. You can roleplay interactions with player characters, and even use Diplomacy results if the player wants a mechanical sense of how convincing or charming a character is, but players make the ultimate decisions about how their characters respond.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19614,"type":"action","before":{"id":19614,"cost":null,"name":"Command an Animal","type":"action","uuid":"4398828153695138","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"NATURE","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2400","book":"Player Core","page":"242"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:32:37.517632+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You issue an order to an animal. Attempt a Nature check against the animal's Will DC. The GM might adjust the DC if the animal has a good attitude toward you, you suggest a course of action it was predisposed toward, or you offer it a treat.\n\nYou automatically fail if the animal is hostile or unfriendly to you. If the animal is helpful to you, increase your degree of success by one step. You might be able to Command an Animal more easily with a feat like [Ride](link_feat_20492).\n\nMost animals know the [Drop Prone](link_action_19630), [Leap](link_action_19735), [Seek](link_action_19845), [Stand](link_action_19851), [Stride](link_action_19855), and [Strike](link_action_19856) basic actions. If an animal knows an activity, such as a horse's Gallop, you can Command the Animal to perform the activity, but you must spend as many actions on Command an Animal as the activity's number of actions. You can also spend multiple actions to Command the Animal to perform that number of basic actions on its next turn; for instance, you could spend 3 actions to Command an Animal to [Stride](link_action_19855) three times or to [Stride](link_action_19855) twice and then make a [Strike](link_action_19856).\n\n**Success** The animal does as you command on its next turn.\n\n**Failure** The animal is hesitant or resistant, and it does nothing.\n\n**Critical Failure** The animal misbehaves or misunderstands, and it takes some other action determined by the GM.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19614,"cost":null,"name":"Command an Animal","type":"action","uuid":"4398828153695138","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"NATURE","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2400","book":"Player Core","page":"242"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:32:37.517632+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You issue an order to an animal. Attempt a Nature check against the animal's Will DC. The GM might adjust the DC if the animal has a good attitude toward you, you suggest a course of action it was predisposed toward, or you offer it a treat.\n\nYou automatically fail if the animal is hostile or unfriendly to you. If the animal is helpful to you, increase your degree of success by one step. You might be able to Command an Animal more easily with a feat like [Ride](link_feat_20492).\n\nMost animals know the [Drop Prone](link_action_19630), [Leap](link_action_19735), [Seek](link_action_19845), [Stand](link_action_19851), [Stride](link_action_19855), and [Strike](link_action_19856) basic actions. If an animal knows an activity, such as a horse's Gallop, you can Command the Animal to perform the activity, but you must spend as many actions on Command an Animal as the activity's number of actions. You can also spend multiple actions to Command the Animal to perform that number of basic actions on its next turn; for instance, you could spend 3 actions to Command an Animal to [Stride](link_action_19855) three times or to [Stride](link_action_19855) twice and then make a [Strike](link_action_19856).\n\n**Success** The animal does as you command on its next turn.\n\n**Failure** The animal is hesitant or resistant, and it does nothing.\n\n**Critical Failure** The animal misbehaves or misunderstands, and it takes some other action determined by the GM.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19616,"type":"action","before":{"id":19616,"cost":null,"name":"Cover Tracks","type":"action","uuid":"4830882910041218","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1505,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SURVIVAL","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2407","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:33:26.948942+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You cover your tracks, moving up to half your travel Speed. You don’t need to attempt a Survival check to cover your tracks, but anyone tracking you must succeed at a Survival check against your Survival DC if it is higher than the normal DC to Track.\n\nIn some cases, you might Cover Tracks in an encounter. In this case, Cover Tracks is a single action and doesn't have the [exploration](link_trait_1457) trait.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19616,"cost":null,"name":"Cover Tracks","type":"action","uuid":"4830882910041218","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1505,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SURVIVAL","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2407","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:33:26.948942+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You cover your tracks, moving up to half your travel Speed. You don’t need to attempt a Survival check to cover your tracks, but anyone tracking you must succeed at a Survival check against your Survival DC if it is higher than the normal DC to Track.\n\nIn some cases, you might Cover Tracks in an encounter. In this case, Cover Tracks is a single action and doesn't have the [exploration](link_trait_1457) trait.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19617,"type":"action","before":{"id":19617,"cost":null,"name":"Craft","type":"action","uuid":"7287622649882976","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1466,1433,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2385","book":"Player Core","page":"237"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:34:26.991595+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can make an item from raw materials. You need the [Alchemical Crafting](link_feat_19894) skill feat to create [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items and the [Magical Crafting](link_feat_20319) feat to create [magic](link_trait_1504) items.\n\nTo craft an item, you must meet the following requirements:\n\n*   The item is your level or lower. An item that doesn't list a level is level 0. If the item is 9th level or higher, you must be a master in Crafting, and if it's 17th or higher, you must be legendary.\n    \n*   The item must be common, or you must otherwise have access to it.\n    \n*   You have an appropriate set of tools and, in many cases, a workshop. For example, you need access to a smithy to forge a metal shield, or an Alchemist's Lab to produce alchemical items.\n    \n*   You must supply raw materials worth at least half the item's Price. You always expend at least that amount of raw materials when you Craft successfully. If you're in a settlement, you can usually spend currency to get the amount of raw materials you need, except in the case of rarer precious materials.\n    \n\nYou attempt a Crafting check after you spend 2 days of work setting up, or 1 day if you have the item's formula. The GM determines the DC to Craft the item based on its level, rarity, and other circumstances.\n\nIf your attempt to create the item is successful, you expend the raw materials you supplied. You can pay the remaining portion of the item's Price in materials to complete the item immediately, or you can spend additional downtime days working on it. For each additional day you spend, reduce the value of the materials you need to expend to complete the item. This amount is determined using the [Income Earned](link_action_19631) table, based on your proficiency rank in Crafting and using your own level instead of a task level.\n\nAfter any of these downtime days, you can complete the item by spending the remaining portion of its Price in materials. If the downtime days you spend are interrupted, you can return to finish the item later, continuing where you left off. An example of Crafting appears in the sidebar.\n\n**Critical Success** Your attempt is successful. Each additional day spent Crafting reduces the materials needed to complete the item by an amount based on your level + 1 and your proficiency rank in Crafting.\n\n**Success** Your attempt is successful. Each additional day spent Crafting reduces the materials needed to complete the item by an amount based on your level and your proficiency rank.\n\n**Failure** You fail to complete the item. You can salvage the raw materials you supplied for their full value. If you want to try again, you must start over.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fail to complete the item. You ruin 10% of the raw materials you supplied, but you can salvage the rest. If you want to try again, you must start over.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19617,"cost":null,"name":"Craft","type":"action","uuid":"7287622649882976","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1466,1433,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2385","book":"Player Core","page":"237"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:34:26.991595+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can make an item from raw materials. You need the [Alchemical Crafting](link_feat_19894) skill feat to create [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items and the [Magical Crafting](link_feat_20319) feat to create [magic](link_trait_1504) items.\n\nTo craft an item, you must meet the following requirements:\n\n*   The item is your level or lower. An item that doesn't list a level is level 0. If the item is 9th level or higher, you must be a master in Crafting, and if it's 17th or higher, you must be legendary.\n    \n*   The item must be common, or you must otherwise have access to it.\n    \n*   You have an appropriate set of tools and, in many cases, a workshop. For example, you need access to a smithy to forge a metal shield, or an Alchemist's Lab to produce alchemical items.\n    \n*   You must supply raw materials worth at least half the item's Price. You always expend at least that amount of raw materials when you Craft successfully. If you're in a settlement, you can usually spend currency to get the amount of raw materials you need, except in the case of rarer precious materials.\n    \n\nYou attempt a Crafting check after you spend 2 days of work setting up, or 1 day if you have the item's formula. The GM determines the DC to Craft the item based on its level, rarity, and other circumstances.\n\nIf your attempt to create the item is successful, you expend the raw materials you supplied. You can pay the remaining portion of the item's Price in materials to complete the item immediately, or you can spend additional downtime days working on it. For each additional day you spend, reduce the value of the materials you need to expend to complete the item. This amount is determined using the [Income Earned](link_action_19631) table, based on your proficiency rank in Crafting and using your own level instead of a task level.\n\nAfter any of these downtime days, you can complete the item by spending the remaining portion of its Price in materials. If the downtime days you spend are interrupted, you can return to finish the item later, continuing where you left off. An example of Crafting appears in the sidebar.\n\n**Critical Success** Your attempt is successful. Each additional day spent Crafting reduces the materials needed to complete the item by an amount based on your level + 1 and your proficiency rank in Crafting.\n\n**Success** Your attempt is successful. Each additional day spent Crafting reduces the materials needed to complete the item by an amount based on your level and your proficiency rank.\n\n**Failure** You fail to complete the item. You can salvage the raw materials you supplied for their full value. If you want to try again, you must start over.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fail to complete the item. You ruin 10% of the raw materials you supplied, but you can salvage the rest. If you want to try again, you must start over.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19618,"type":"action","before":{"id":19618,"cost":null,"name":"Crawl","type":"action","uuid":"5129533339137004","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2293","book":"Player Core","page":"416"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:34:34.654007+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move 5 feet by crawling and continue to stay Prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are prone and your Speed is at least 10 feet.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19618,"cost":null,"name":"Crawl","type":"action","uuid":"5129533339137004","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2293","book":"Player Core","page":"416"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:34:34.654007+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move 5 feet by crawling and continue to stay Prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are prone and your Speed is at least 10 feet.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19619,"type":"action","before":{"id":19619,"cost":null,"name":"Create a Diversion","type":"action","uuid":"3530932677340844","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2387","book":"Player Core","page":"237"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:35:02.826251+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With a gesture, a trick, or some distracting words, you can create a diversion that draws creatures' attention elsewhere. If you use a gesture or trick, this action gains the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait. If you use distracting words, it gains the [auditory](link_trait_1469) and [linguistic](link_trait_1458) traits.\n\nAttempt a single Deception check and compare it to the Perception DCs of the creatures whose attention you're trying to divert. Whether or not you succeed, creatures you attempt to divert gain a +4 circumstance bonus to their Perception DCs against your attempts to Create a Diversion for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** You become hidden to each creature whose Perception DC is less than or equal to your result. (The hidden condition allows you to [Sneak](link_action_19850) away.) This lasts until the end of your turn or until you do anything except [Step](link_action_19853) or use the Stealth skill to [Hide](link_action_19726) or [Sneak](link_action_19850). If you [Strike](link_action_19856) a creature, the creature remains off-guard against that attack, and you then become observed. If you do anything else, you become observed just before you act unless the GM determines otherwise.\n\n**Failure** You don't divert the attention of any creatures whose Perception DC exceeds your result, and those creatures are aware you were trying to trick them.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19619,"cost":null,"name":"Create a Diversion","type":"action","uuid":"3530932677340844","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2387","book":"Player Core","page":"237"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:35:02.826251+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With a gesture, a trick, or some distracting words, you can create a diversion that draws creatures' attention elsewhere. If you use a gesture or trick, this action gains the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait. If you use distracting words, it gains the [auditory](link_trait_1469) and [linguistic](link_trait_1458) traits.\n\nAttempt a single Deception check and compare it to the Perception DCs of the creatures whose attention you're trying to divert. Whether or not you succeed, creatures you attempt to divert gain a +4 circumstance bonus to their Perception DCs against your attempts to Create a Diversion for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** You become hidden to each creature whose Perception DC is less than or equal to your result. (The hidden condition allows you to [Sneak](link_action_19850) away.) This lasts until the end of your turn or until you do anything except [Step](link_action_19853) or use the Stealth skill to [Hide](link_action_19726) or [Sneak](link_action_19850). If you [Strike](link_action_19856) a creature, the creature remains off-guard against that attack, and you then become observed. If you do anything else, you become observed just before you act unless the GM determines otherwise.\n\n**Failure** You don't divert the attention of any creatures whose Perception DC exceeds your result, and those creatures are aware you were trying to trick them.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19620,"type":"action","before":{"id":19620,"cost":null,"name":"Create Forgery","type":"action","uuid":"6781948769247732","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1466,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SOCIETY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2402","book":"Player Core","page":"244"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:35:41.002077+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You create a forged document, usually over the course of a day or a week. The GM rolls a secret DC 20 Society check. If you need to forge a specific person's handwriting, you need a sample of that person's handwriting. Otherwise, you need only to have seen a similar document, and you gain up to a +4 circumstance bonus to the check (the GM determines the bonus).\n\n**Success** The forgery is of good enough quality that passive observers can't notice the fake (but see Examining Forgeries).\n\n**Failure** The forgery has some obvious signs of being a fake, potentially allowing passive observers to detect it. Each time a passive observer sees the document, the GM compares your check result to the observer's Perception DC or Society DC, whichever is higher. If your result doesn't exceed a passive observer's DC, that observer knows the document is a forgery.\n\nExamining Forgeries\n-------------------\n\nA creature on the lookout for forgeries, even one who was fooled on a passive glance, can take time to closely examine a document to see if it's a forgery. They apply different techniques and analysis methods to look beyond the surface elements and attempt a secret Perception or Society check against the forger's Society DC; any bonus you had to create the forgery initially applies to this DC. On a success, the examiner knows the document is a forgery. On a failure, they think the document is genuine and can't try again unless they get a new reason to be suspicious of the document. If a PC examines a genuine document, the GM might still pretend to roll a secret check before revealing the document is genuine.","availability":null,"requirements":"You provide the proper writing materials for your forgery.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19620,"cost":null,"name":"Create Forgery","type":"action","uuid":"6781948769247732","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1466,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SOCIETY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2402","book":"Player Core","page":"244"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:35:41.002077+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You create a forged document, usually over the course of a day or a week. The GM rolls a secret DC 20 Society check. If you need to forge a specific person's handwriting, you need a sample of that person's handwriting. Otherwise, you need only to have seen a similar document, and you gain up to a +4 circumstance bonus to the check (the GM determines the bonus).\n\n**Success** The forgery is of good enough quality that passive observers can't notice the fake (but see Examining Forgeries).\n\n**Failure** The forgery has some obvious signs of being a fake, potentially allowing passive observers to detect it. Each time a passive observer sees the document, the GM compares your check result to the observer's Perception DC or Society DC, whichever is higher. If your result doesn't exceed a passive observer's DC, that observer knows the document is a forgery.\n\nExamining Forgeries\n-------------------\n\nA creature on the lookout for forgeries, even one who was fooled on a passive glance, can take time to closely examine a document to see if it's a forgery. They apply different techniques and analysis methods to look beyond the surface elements and attempt a secret Perception or Society check against the forger's Society DC; any bonus you had to create the forgery initially applies to this DC. On a success, the examiner knows the document is a forgery. On a failure, they think the document is genuine and can't try again unless they get a new reason to be suspicious of the document. If a PC examines a genuine document, the GM might still pretend to roll a secret check before revealing the document is genuine.","availability":null,"requirements":"You provide the proper writing materials for your forgery.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19622,"type":"action","before":{"id":19622,"cost":null,"name":"Decipher Writing","type":"action","uuid":"5435930317948545","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SOCIETY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2363","book":"Player Core","page":"228"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:36:50.581089+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to decipher complicated writing or literature on an obscure topic. This usually takes 1 minute per page of text, but might take longer (typically an hour per page for decrypting ciphers or the like). The text must be in a language you can read, though the GM might allow you to attempt to decipher text written in an unfamiliar language using Society instead.\n\nThe DC is determined by the GM based on the state or complexity of the document. The GM might have you roll one check for a short text or a check for each section of a larger text.\n\nSkill\n\nTypically used for\n\n[Arcana](link_trait_1459)\n\nWriting about magic or science\n\n[Occultism](link_trait_1514)\n\nEsoteric texts about mysteries and philosophy\n\nReligion\n\nScripture\n\nSociety\n\nCoded messages or archaic documents\n\n**Critical Success** You understand the true meaning of the text.\n\n**Success** You understand the true meaning of the text. If it was a coded document, you know the general meaning but might not have a word-for-word translation.\n\n**Failure** You can't understand the text and take a –2 circumstance penalty to further checks to decipher it.\n\n**Critical Failure** You believe you understand the text on that page, but you have in fact misconstrued its message.\n\nSample Decipher Tasks\n---------------------\n\n**Trained** entry-level philosophy treatise\n\n**Expert** complex code, such as a cipher\n\n**Master** spymaster's code or advanced research notes\n\n**Legendary** esoteric planar text written in metaphor by an ancient celestial","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19622,"cost":null,"name":"Decipher Writing","type":"action","uuid":"5435930317948545","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SOCIETY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2363","book":"Player Core","page":"228"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:36:50.581089+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to decipher complicated writing or literature on an obscure topic. This usually takes 1 minute per page of text, but might take longer (typically an hour per page for decrypting ciphers or the like). The text must be in a language you can read, though the GM might allow you to attempt to decipher text written in an unfamiliar language using Society instead.\n\nThe DC is determined by the GM based on the state or complexity of the document. The GM might have you roll one check for a short text or a check for each section of a larger text.\n\nSkill\n\nTypically used for\n\n[Arcana](link_trait_1459)\n\nWriting about magic or science\n\n[Occultism](link_trait_1514)\n\nEsoteric texts about mysteries and philosophy\n\nReligion\n\nScripture\n\nSociety\n\nCoded messages or archaic documents\n\n**Critical Success** You understand the true meaning of the text.\n\n**Success** You understand the true meaning of the text. If it was a coded document, you know the general meaning but might not have a word-for-word translation.\n\n**Failure** You can't understand the text and take a –2 circumstance penalty to further checks to decipher it.\n\n**Critical Failure** You believe you understand the text on that page, but you have in fact misconstrued its message.\n\nSample Decipher Tasks\n---------------------\n\n**Trained** entry-level philosophy treatise\n\n**Expert** complex code, such as a cipher\n\n**Master** spymaster's code or advanced research notes\n\n**Legendary** esoteric planar text written in metaphor by an ancient celestial","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19624,"type":"action","before":{"id":19624,"cost":null,"name":"Demoralize","type":"action","uuid":"6544488333511565","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1486,1487,1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"INTIMIDATION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2395","book":"Player Core","page":"240"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:37:41.8577+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With a sudden shout, a well-timed taunt, or a cutting put-down, you can shake an enemy's resolve. Choose a creature within 30 feet of you who you're aware of. Attempt an Intimidation check against that target's Will DC. If the target doesn't understand the language you are speaking, or you're not speaking a language, you take a –4 circumstance penalty to the check. Regardless of your result, the target is temporarily immune to your attempts to Demoralize it for 10 minutes.\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes frightened 2.\n\n**Success** The target becomes frightened 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19624,"cost":null,"name":"Demoralize","type":"action","uuid":"6544488333511565","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1486,1487,1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"INTIMIDATION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2395","book":"Player Core","page":"240"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:37:41.8577+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With a sudden shout, a well-timed taunt, or a cutting put-down, you can shake an enemy's resolve. Choose a creature within 30 feet of you who you're aware of. Attempt an Intimidation check against that target's Will DC. If the target doesn't understand the language you are speaking, or you're not speaking a language, you take a –4 circumstance penalty to the check. Regardless of your result, the target is temporarily immune to your attempts to Demoralize it for 10 minutes.\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes frightened 2.\n\n**Success** The target becomes frightened 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19626,"type":"action","before":{"id":19626,"cost":null,"name":"Disarm","type":"action","uuid":"859200098544887","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2383","book":"Player Core","page":"236"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","value":2,"selector":"athletics","predicate":["action:disarm","target:effect:disarm-success"]}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:38:40.677115+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to knock an item out of a creature's grasp. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Reflex DC.\n\n**Critical Success** You knock the item out of the target's grasp. It falls to the ground in the target's space.\n\n**Success** You weaken your target's grasp on the item. Further attempts to Disarm the target of that item gain a +2 circumstance bonus, and the target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attacks with the item or other checks requiring a firm grasp on the item. The creature can end the effect by [Interacting](link_action_19733) to change its grip on the item; otherwise, it lasts as long as the creature holds the item.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose your balance and become off-guard until the start of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one hand free. The target can't be more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19626,"cost":null,"name":"Disarm","type":"action","uuid":"859200098544887","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2383","book":"Player Core","page":"236"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","value":2,"selector":"athletics","predicate":["action:disarm","target:effect:disarm-success"]}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:38:40.677115+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to knock an item out of a creature's grasp. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Reflex DC.\n\n**Critical Success** You knock the item out of the target's grasp. It falls to the ground in the target's space.\n\n**Success** You weaken your target's grasp on the item. Further attempts to Disarm the target of that item gain a +2 circumstance bonus, and the target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attacks with the item or other checks requiring a firm grasp on the item. The creature can end the effect by [Interacting](link_action_19733) to change its grip on the item; otherwise, it lasts as long as the creature holds the item.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose your balance and become off-guard until the start of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one hand free. The target can't be more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19627,"type":"action","before":{"id":19627,"cost":null,"name":"Dismiss","type":"action","uuid":"6610017043267456","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1437],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2311","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:38:46.674225+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You end an effect that states you can Dismiss it. Dimissing ends the entire effect unless noted otherwise.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19627,"cost":null,"name":"Dismiss","type":"action","uuid":"6610017043267456","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1437],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2311","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:38:46.674225+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You end an effect that states you can Dismiss it. Dimissing ends the entire effect unless noted otherwise.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19631,"type":"action","before":{"id":19631,"cost":null,"name":"Earn Income","type":"action","uuid":"5726317895027050","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1466,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING, PERFORMANCE, LORE","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2364","book":"Player Core","page":"228"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:42:56.811435+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can use a skill to earn money during downtime. You must be trained in the skill to do so. This takes time to set up, and your income depends on your proficiency rank and how lucrative a task you can find. Because this process requires a significant amount of time and involves tracking things outside the progress of adventures, it won't come up in every campaign. The most typical ways to earn income, detailed further in this section are:\n\n*   Crafting goods for the market (Crafting)\n    \n*   Practicing a Trade (Lore)\n    \n*   Staging a Performance (Performance)\n    \n\nIn some cases, the GM might let you use a different skill to Earn Income through specialized work. Usually, this is scholarly work, such as using Religion in a monastery to study old texts—but giving sermons at a church would still fall under Performance instead of Religion. You also might be able to use physical skills to make money, such as using Acrobatics to perform feats in a circus or Thievery to pick pockets. If you're using a skill other than Crafting, Lore, or Performance, the DC tends to be significantly higher.\n\nEarn Income\n-----------\n\n#### Downtime\n\nYou use one of your skills to make money during downtime. The GM assigns a task level representing the most lucrative job available. You can search for lower-level tasks, with the GM determining whether you find any. Sometimes you can attempt to find better work than the initial offerings, though this takes time and requires using the Diplomacy skill to Gather Information, doing some research, or socializing.\n\nWhen you take on a job, the GM secretly sets the DC of your skill check. After your first day of work, you roll to determine your earnings. You gain an amount of income based on your result, the task's level, and your proficiency rank (as listed on the Income Earned table).\n\nYou can continue working at the task on subsequent days without needing to roll again. For each day you spend after the first, you earn the same amount as the first day, up until the task's completion. The GM determines how long you can work at the task. Most tasks last a week or two, though some can take months or even years.\n\nTable 4-2: Income Earned\n------------------------\n\n| Task Level |DC|Failed|Trained|Expert|Master|Legendary|\n\n|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|\n\n| 0 |14 |1 cp |5 cp|5 cp|5 cp|5 cp|\n\n|1|15|2 cp|2 sp|2 sp|2 sp|2 sp|\n\n|2|16|4 cp|3 sp|3 sp|3 sp|3 sp|\n\n|3|18|8 cp|5 sp|5 sp|5 sp|5 sp|\n\n|4|19|1 sp|7 sp|8 sp|8 sp|8 sp|\n\n|5|20|2 sp|9 sp|1 gp|1 gp|1 gp|\n\n|6|22|3 sp|1 gp, 5 sp|2 gp|2 gp|2 gp|\n\n|7|23|4 sp|2 gp|2 gp, 5 sp|2 gp, 5 sp|2 gp, 5 sp|\n\n|8|24|5 sp|2 gp, 5 sp|3 gp|3 gp|3 gp|\n\n|9|26|6 sp|3 gp|4 gp|4 gp|4 gp|\n\n|10|27|7 sp|4 gp|5 gp|6 gp|6 gp|\n\n|11|28|8 sp|5 gp|6 gp|8 gp|8 gp|\n\n|12|30|9 sp|6 gp|8 gp|10 gp|10 gp|\n\n|13|31|1 gp|7 gp|10 gp|15 gp|15 gp|\n\n|14|32|1 gp, 5 sp|8 gp|15 gp|20 gp|20 gp|\n\n|15|34|2 gp|10 gp|20 gp|28 gp|28 gp|\n\n|16|35|2 gp, 5 sp|13 gp|25 gp|36 gp|40 gp|\n\n|17|36|3 gp|15 gp|30 gp|45 gp|55 gp|\n\n|18|38|4 gp|20 gp|45 gp|70 gp|90 gp|\n\n|19|39|6 gp|30 gp|60 gp|100 gp|130 gp|\n\n|20|40|8 gp|40 gp|75 gp|150 gp|200 gp|\n\n|20 (critical success)|—|—|50 gp|90 gp|175 gp|300 gp|\n\n**Critical Success** You do outstanding work. Gain the amount of currency listed for the task level + 1 and your proficiency rank.\n\n**Success** You do competent work. Gain the amount of currency listed for the task level and your proficiency rank.\n\n**Failure** You do shoddy work and get paid the bare minimum for your time. Gain the amount of currency listed in the failure column for the task level. The GM will likely reduce how long you can continue at the task.\n\n**Critical Failure** You earn nothing for your work and are fired immediately. You can't continue at the task. Your reputation suffers, potentially making it difficult for you to find rewarding jobs in that community in the future.\n\nSample Earn Income Tasks\n------------------------\n\nThese examples use Alcohol Lore to work in a bar or Legal Lore to perform legal work.\n\n*   **Trained** bartend, do legal research\n    \n*   **Expert** curate drink selection, present minor court cases\n    \n*   **Master** run a large brewery, present important court cases\n    \n*   **Legendary** run an international brewing franchise, present a case in Hell's courts\n    \n\nCrafting Goods for the Market Crafting\n--------------------------------------\n\nUsing Crafting, you can work at producing common items for the market. It's usually easy to find work making basic items whose level is 1 or 2 below your settlement's level.\n\nHigher-level tasks represent special commissions, which might require you to Craft a specific item using the Craft downtime activity and sell it to a buyer at full Price. These opportunities don't occur as often and might have special requirements—or serious consequences if you disappoint a prominent client.\n\nPracticing a Trade Lore\n-----------------------\n\nYou apply the practical benefits of one of your Lore specialties during downtime by practicing your trade. This is most effective for Lore specialties such as business, law, or sailing, where there's high demand for workers. The GM might increase the DC or determine only low-level tasks are available if you're attempting to use an obscure Lore skill to earn income. You might also need specialized tools to accept a job, like mining tools to work in a mine or a merchant's scale to buy and sell valuables in a market.\n\nStaging a Performance Performance\n---------------------------------\n\nYou perform for an audience to make money. The available audiences determine the level of your task, since more discerning audiences are harder to impress but provide a bigger payout. The GM determines the task level based on the audiences available. Performing for a typical audience of commoners on the street is a level 0 task, but a performance for a group of artisans with more refined tastes might be a 2nd- or 3rd-level task, and ones for merchants, nobility, and royalty are increasingly higher level.\n\nYour degree of success determines whether you moved your audience and whether you were rewarded with applause or rotten fruit.\n\nEnding or Interrupting Tasks\n----------------------------\n\nWhen a task you're doing is complete, or if you stop in the middle of one, you normally have to find a new task if you want to keep Earning Income. For instance, if you quit your job working at the docks, you'll need to find another place of employment instead of picking up where you left off. This usually takes 1 day or more of downtime looking for leads on new jobs.\n\nHowever, you might pause a task due to an adventure or event that wouldn't prevent you from returning to the old job later. The GM might decide that you can pick up where you left off, assuming the task hasn't been completed by others in your absence. Whether you roll a new skill check when you resume is also up to the GM. Generally speaking, if you had a good initial roll and want to keep it, you can, but if you had a bad initial roll, you can't try for a better one by pausing to do something else. If your statistics changed during the break—usually because you leveled up while adventuring—you can attempt a new check.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19631,"cost":null,"name":"Earn Income","type":"action","uuid":"5726317895027050","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1466,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING, PERFORMANCE, LORE","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2364","book":"Player Core","page":"228"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:42:56.811435+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can use a skill to earn money during downtime. You must be trained in the skill to do so. This takes time to set up, and your income depends on your proficiency rank and how lucrative a task you can find. Because this process requires a significant amount of time and involves tracking things outside the progress of adventures, it won't come up in every campaign. The most typical ways to earn income, detailed further in this section are:\n\n*   Crafting goods for the market (Crafting)\n    \n*   Practicing a Trade (Lore)\n    \n*   Staging a Performance (Performance)\n    \n\nIn some cases, the GM might let you use a different skill to Earn Income through specialized work. Usually, this is scholarly work, such as using Religion in a monastery to study old texts—but giving sermons at a church would still fall under Performance instead of Religion. You also might be able to use physical skills to make money, such as using Acrobatics to perform feats in a circus or Thievery to pick pockets. If you're using a skill other than Crafting, Lore, or Performance, the DC tends to be significantly higher.\n\nEarn Income\n-----------\n\n#### Downtime\n\nYou use one of your skills to make money during downtime. The GM assigns a task level representing the most lucrative job available. You can search for lower-level tasks, with the GM determining whether you find any. Sometimes you can attempt to find better work than the initial offerings, though this takes time and requires using the Diplomacy skill to Gather Information, doing some research, or socializing.\n\nWhen you take on a job, the GM secretly sets the DC of your skill check. After your first day of work, you roll to determine your earnings. You gain an amount of income based on your result, the task's level, and your proficiency rank (as listed on the Income Earned table).\n\nYou can continue working at the task on subsequent days without needing to roll again. For each day you spend after the first, you earn the same amount as the first day, up until the task's completion. The GM determines how long you can work at the task. Most tasks last a week or two, though some can take months or even years.\n\nTable 4-2: Income Earned\n------------------------\n\n| Task Level |DC|Failed|Trained|Expert|Master|Legendary|\n\n|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|\n\n| 0 |14 |1 cp |5 cp|5 cp|5 cp|5 cp|\n\n|1|15|2 cp|2 sp|2 sp|2 sp|2 sp|\n\n|2|16|4 cp|3 sp|3 sp|3 sp|3 sp|\n\n|3|18|8 cp|5 sp|5 sp|5 sp|5 sp|\n\n|4|19|1 sp|7 sp|8 sp|8 sp|8 sp|\n\n|5|20|2 sp|9 sp|1 gp|1 gp|1 gp|\n\n|6|22|3 sp|1 gp, 5 sp|2 gp|2 gp|2 gp|\n\n|7|23|4 sp|2 gp|2 gp, 5 sp|2 gp, 5 sp|2 gp, 5 sp|\n\n|8|24|5 sp|2 gp, 5 sp|3 gp|3 gp|3 gp|\n\n|9|26|6 sp|3 gp|4 gp|4 gp|4 gp|\n\n|10|27|7 sp|4 gp|5 gp|6 gp|6 gp|\n\n|11|28|8 sp|5 gp|6 gp|8 gp|8 gp|\n\n|12|30|9 sp|6 gp|8 gp|10 gp|10 gp|\n\n|13|31|1 gp|7 gp|10 gp|15 gp|15 gp|\n\n|14|32|1 gp, 5 sp|8 gp|15 gp|20 gp|20 gp|\n\n|15|34|2 gp|10 gp|20 gp|28 gp|28 gp|\n\n|16|35|2 gp, 5 sp|13 gp|25 gp|36 gp|40 gp|\n\n|17|36|3 gp|15 gp|30 gp|45 gp|55 gp|\n\n|18|38|4 gp|20 gp|45 gp|70 gp|90 gp|\n\n|19|39|6 gp|30 gp|60 gp|100 gp|130 gp|\n\n|20|40|8 gp|40 gp|75 gp|150 gp|200 gp|\n\n|20 (critical success)|—|—|50 gp|90 gp|175 gp|300 gp|\n\n**Critical Success** You do outstanding work. Gain the amount of currency listed for the task level + 1 and your proficiency rank.\n\n**Success** You do competent work. Gain the amount of currency listed for the task level and your proficiency rank.\n\n**Failure** You do shoddy work and get paid the bare minimum for your time. Gain the amount of currency listed in the failure column for the task level. The GM will likely reduce how long you can continue at the task.\n\n**Critical Failure** You earn nothing for your work and are fired immediately. You can't continue at the task. Your reputation suffers, potentially making it difficult for you to find rewarding jobs in that community in the future.\n\nSample Earn Income Tasks\n------------------------\n\nThese examples use Alcohol Lore to work in a bar or Legal Lore to perform legal work.\n\n*   **Trained** bartend, do legal research\n    \n*   **Expert** curate drink selection, present minor court cases\n    \n*   **Master** run a large brewery, present important court cases\n    \n*   **Legendary** run an international brewing franchise, present a case in Hell's courts\n    \n\nCrafting Goods for the Market Crafting\n--------------------------------------\n\nUsing Crafting, you can work at producing common items for the market. It's usually easy to find work making basic items whose level is 1 or 2 below your settlement's level.\n\nHigher-level tasks represent special commissions, which might require you to Craft a specific item using the Craft downtime activity and sell it to a buyer at full Price. These opportunities don't occur as often and might have special requirements—or serious consequences if you disappoint a prominent client.\n\nPracticing a Trade Lore\n-----------------------\n\nYou apply the practical benefits of one of your Lore specialties during downtime by practicing your trade. This is most effective for Lore specialties such as business, law, or sailing, where there's high demand for workers. The GM might increase the DC or determine only low-level tasks are available if you're attempting to use an obscure Lore skill to earn income. You might also need specialized tools to accept a job, like mining tools to work in a mine or a merchant's scale to buy and sell valuables in a market.\n\nStaging a Performance Performance\n---------------------------------\n\nYou perform for an audience to make money. The available audiences determine the level of your task, since more discerning audiences are harder to impress but provide a bigger payout. The GM determines the task level based on the audiences available. Performing for a typical audience of commoners on the street is a level 0 task, but a performance for a group of artisans with more refined tastes might be a 2nd- or 3rd-level task, and ones for merchants, nobility, and royalty are increasingly higher level.\n\nYour degree of success determines whether you moved your audience and whether you were rewarded with applause or rotten fruit.\n\nEnding or Interrupting Tasks\n----------------------------\n\nWhen a task you're doing is complete, or if you stop in the middle of one, you normally have to find a new task if you want to keep Earning Income. For instance, if you quit your job working at the docks, you'll need to find another place of employment instead of picking up where you left off. This usually takes 1 day or more of downtime looking for leads on new jobs.\n\nHowever, you might pause a task due to an adventure or event that wouldn't prevent you from returning to the old job later. The GM might decide that you can pick up where you left off, assuming the task hasn't been completed by others in your absence. Whether you roll a new skill check when you resume is also up to the GM. Generally speaking, if you had a good initial roll and want to keep it, you can, but if you had a bad initial roll, you can't try for a better one by pausing to do something else. If your statistics changed during the break—usually because you leveled up while adventuring—you can attempt a new check.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19632,"type":"action","before":{"id":19632,"cost":null,"name":"Escape","type":"action","uuid":"6836671321143633","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1437],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2296","book":"Player Core","page":"416"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:43:39.880464+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to escape from being Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained. Choose one creature, object, spell effect, hazard, or other impediment imposing any of those conditions on you. Attempt a check using your unarmed attack modifier against the DC of the effect. This is typically the Athletics DC of a creature grabbing you, the Thievery DC of a creature who tied you up, the spell DC for a spell effect, or the listed Escape DC of an object, hazard, or other impediment. You can attempt an Acrobatics or Athletics check instead of using your attack modifier if you choose (but this action still has the attack trait).\n\n**Critical Success** You get free and remove the grabbed, immobilized, and restrained conditions imposed by your chosen target. You can then Stride up to 5 feet.\n\n**Success** You get free and remove the grabbed, immobilized, and restrained conditions imposed by your chosen target.\n\n**Critical Failure** You don't get free, and you can't attempt to Escape again until your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19632,"cost":null,"name":"Escape","type":"action","uuid":"6836671321143633","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1437],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2296","book":"Player Core","page":"416"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:43:39.880464+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to escape from being Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained. Choose one creature, object, spell effect, hazard, or other impediment imposing any of those conditions on you. Attempt a check using your unarmed attack modifier against the DC of the effect. This is typically the Athletics DC of a creature grabbing you, the Thievery DC of a creature who tied you up, the spell DC for a spell effect, or the listed Escape DC of an object, hazard, or other impediment. You can attempt an Acrobatics or Athletics check instead of using your attack modifier if you choose (but this action still has the attack trait).\n\n**Critical Success** You get free and remove the grabbed, immobilized, and restrained conditions imposed by your chosen target. You can then Stride up to 5 feet.\n\n**Success** You get free and remove the grabbed, immobilized, and restrained conditions imposed by your chosen target.\n\n**Critical Failure** You don't get free, and you can't attempt to Escape again until your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19633,"type":"action","before":{"id":19633,"cost":null,"name":"Feint","type":"action","uuid":"4994199721560613","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2390","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:44:00.906855+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With a misleading flourish, you leave an opponent unprepared for your real attack. Attempt a Deception check against your target's Perception DC.\n\n**Critical Success** You throw your enemy's defenses against you entirely off. The target is off-guard against melee attacks that you attempt against it until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Success** Your foe is fooled, but only momentarily. The target is off-guard against the next melee attack that you attempt against it before the end of your current turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your feint backfires. You are off-guard against melee attacks the target attempts against you until the end of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are within melee reach of the target you attempt to Feint.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19633,"cost":null,"name":"Feint","type":"action","uuid":"4994199721560613","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2390","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T20:44:00.906855+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With a misleading flourish, you leave an opponent unprepared for your real attack. Attempt a Deception check against your target's Perception DC.\n\n**Critical Success** You throw your enemy's defenses against you entirely off. The target is off-guard against melee attacks that you attempt against it until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Success** Your foe is fooled, but only momentarily. The target is off-guard against the next melee attack that you attempt against it before the end of your current turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your feint backfires. You are off-guard against melee attacks the target attempts against you until the end of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are within melee reach of the target you attempt to Feint.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19721,"type":"action","before":{"id":19721,"cost":null,"name":"Fly","type":"action","uuid":"7192594330416424","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2312","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:24:37.866856+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move through the air up to your fly Speed. Moving upward (straight up or diagonally) uses the rules for moving through difficult terrain. You can move straight down 10 feet for every 5 feet of movement you spend. If you Fly to the ground, you don't take falling damage. You can use an action to Fly 0 feet to hover in place. If you're airborne at the end of your turn and didn't use a Fly action this round, you fall.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a fly Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19721,"cost":null,"name":"Fly","type":"action","uuid":"7192594330416424","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2312","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:24:37.866856+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move through the air up to your fly Speed. Moving upward (straight up or diagonally) uses the rules for moving through difficult terrain. You can move straight down 10 feet for every 5 feet of movement you spend. If you Fly to the ground, you don't take falling damage. You can use an action to Fly 0 feet to hover in place. If you're airborne at the end of your turn and didn't use a Fly action this round, you fall.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a fly Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19722,"type":"action","before":{"id":19722,"cost":null,"name":"Force Open","type":"action","uuid":"6604590639704314","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2375","book":"Player Core","page":"234"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:25:08.795626+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Using your body, a lever, or some other tool, you attempt to forcefully open a door, window, container or heavy gate. With a high enough result, you can even smash through walls. Without a crowbar, prying something open takes a –2 item penalty to the Athletics check to Force Open.\n\n**Critical Success** You open the door, window, container, or gate and can avoid damaging it in the process.\n\n**Success** You break the door, window, container, or gate open, and it gains the broken condition. If it's especially sturdy, the GM might have it take damage but not be broken.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your attempt jams the door, window, container, or gate shut, imposing a –2 circumstance penalty on future attempts to Force it Open.\n\nSample Force Open Tasks\n-----------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** fabric, flimsy glass\n*   **Trained** ice, sturdy glass\n*   **Expert** flimsy wooden door, wooden portcullis\n*   **Master** sturdy wooden door, iron portcullis, metal bar\n*   **Legendary** stone or iron door","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19722,"cost":null,"name":"Force Open","type":"action","uuid":"6604590639704314","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2375","book":"Player Core","page":"234"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:25:08.795626+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Using your body, a lever, or some other tool, you attempt to forcefully open a door, window, container or heavy gate. With a high enough result, you can even smash through walls. Without a crowbar, prying something open takes a –2 item penalty to the Athletics check to Force Open.\n\n**Critical Success** You open the door, window, container, or gate and can avoid damaging it in the process.\n\n**Success** You break the door, window, container, or gate open, and it gains the broken condition. If it's especially sturdy, the GM might have it take damage but not be broken.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your attempt jams the door, window, container, or gate shut, imposing a –2 circumstance penalty on future attempts to Force it Open.\n\nSample Force Open Tasks\n-----------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** fabric, flimsy glass\n*   **Trained** ice, sturdy glass\n*   **Expert** flimsy wooden door, wooden portcullis\n*   **Master** sturdy wooden door, iron portcullis, metal bar\n*   **Legendary** stone or iron door","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19723,"type":"action","before":{"id":19723,"cost":null,"name":"Gather Information","type":"action","uuid":"7658647097982892","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DIPLOMACY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2391","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:25:35.313043+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You canvass local markets, taverns, and gathering places in an attempt to learn about a specific individual or topic. The GM determines the DC of the Diplomacy check and the amount of time it takes (typically 2 hours, but sometimes more), along with any benefit you might be able to gain by spending coin on bribes, drinks, or gifts.\n\n**Success** You collect information about the individual or topic. The GM determines the specifics.\n\n**Critical Failure** You collect incorrect information about the individual or topic.\n\nSample Gather Information Tasks\n-------------------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** talk of the town\n*   **Trained** common rumor\n*   **Expert** obscure rumor, poorly guarded secret\n*   **Master** well-guarded or esoteric information\n*   **Legendary** information known only to an incredibly select few, or only to extraordinary beings","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19723,"cost":null,"name":"Gather Information","type":"action","uuid":"7658647097982892","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DIPLOMACY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2391","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:25:35.313043+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You canvass local markets, taverns, and gathering places in an attempt to learn about a specific individual or topic. The GM determines the DC of the Diplomacy check and the amount of time it takes (typically 2 hours, but sometimes more), along with any benefit you might be able to gain by spending coin on bribes, drinks, or gifts.\n\n**Success** You collect information about the individual or topic. The GM determines the specifics.\n\n**Critical Failure** You collect incorrect information about the individual or topic.\n\nSample Gather Information Tasks\n-------------------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** talk of the town\n*   **Trained** common rumor\n*   **Expert** obscure rumor, poorly guarded secret\n*   **Master** well-guarded or esoteric information\n*   **Legendary** information known only to an incredibly select few, or only to extraordinary beings","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19725,"type":"action","before":{"id":19725,"cost":null,"name":"Grapple","type":"action","uuid":"1132887528981264","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2376","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:26:31.379716+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to grab a creature or object with your free hand. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Fortitude DC. You can grapple a target you already have grabbed or restrained without having a hand free.\n\n**Critical Success** Your target is restrained until the end of your next turn unless you move or your target [Escapes](link_action_19632).\n\n**Success** Your target is grabbed until the end of your next turn unless you move or your target [Escapes](link_action_19632).\n\n**Failure** You fail to grab your target. If you already had the target grabbed or restrained using a Grapple, those conditions on the target end.\n\n**Critical Failure** If you already had the target grabbed or restrained, it breaks free. Your target can either grab you, as if it succeeded at using the Grapple action against you, or force you to fall and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one free hand and your target is no more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19725,"cost":null,"name":"Grapple","type":"action","uuid":"1132887528981264","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2376","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:26:31.379716+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to grab a creature or object with your free hand. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Fortitude DC. You can grapple a target you already have grabbed or restrained without having a hand free.\n\n**Critical Success** Your target is restrained until the end of your next turn unless you move or your target [Escapes](link_action_19632).\n\n**Success** Your target is grabbed until the end of your next turn unless you move or your target [Escapes](link_action_19632).\n\n**Failure** You fail to grab your target. If you already had the target grabbed or restrained using a Grapple, those conditions on the target end.\n\n**Critical Failure** If you already had the target grabbed or restrained, it breaks free. Your target can either grab you, as if it succeeded at using the Grapple action against you, or force you to fall and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one free hand and your target is no more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19726,"type":"action","before":{"id":19726,"cost":null,"name":"Hide","type":"action","uuid":"6465165078605128","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1463,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"STEALTH","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2404","book":"Player Core","page":"244"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:27:16.946946+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You huddle behind cover or greater cover or deeper into concealment to become Hidden, rather than Observed. The GM rolls your Stealth check in secret and compares the result to the Perception DC of each creature you're observed by but that you have cover or greater cover against or are [Concealed](link_trait_1841) from. You get a +2 circumstance bonus to your check if you have standard cover (or +4 from greater cover).\n\n**Success** If the creature could see you, you're now Hidden from it instead of Observed. If you were hidden from or Undetected by the creature, you retain that condition.\n\nIf you successfully become hidden to a creature but then cease to have cover or greater cover against it or be concealed from it, you become observed again. You cease being hidden if you do anything except Hide, Sneak, or Step. If you attempt to Strike a creature, the creature remains off-guard against that attack, and you then become observed. If you do anything else, you become observed just before you act unless the GM determines otherwise. The GM might allow you to perform a particularly unobtrusive action without being noticed, possibly requiring another Stealth check.\n\nIf a creature uses Seek to make you observed by it, you must successfully Hide to become hidden from it again.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19726,"cost":null,"name":"Hide","type":"action","uuid":"6465165078605128","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1463,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"STEALTH","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2404","book":"Player Core","page":"244"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:27:16.946946+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You huddle behind cover or greater cover or deeper into concealment to become Hidden, rather than Observed. The GM rolls your Stealth check in secret and compares the result to the Perception DC of each creature you're observed by but that you have cover or greater cover against or are [Concealed](link_trait_1841) from. You get a +2 circumstance bonus to your check if you have standard cover (or +4 from greater cover).\n\n**Success** If the creature could see you, you're now Hidden from it instead of Observed. If you were hidden from or Undetected by the creature, you retain that condition.\n\nIf you successfully become hidden to a creature but then cease to have cover or greater cover against it or be concealed from it, you become observed again. You cease being hidden if you do anything except Hide, Sneak, or Step. If you attempt to Strike a creature, the creature remains off-guard against that attack, and you then become observed. If you do anything else, you become observed just before you act unless the GM determines otherwise. The GM might allow you to perform a particularly unobtrusive action without being noticed, possibly requiring another Stealth check.\n\nIf a creature uses Seek to make you observed by it, you must successfully Hide to become hidden from it again.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19727,"type":"action","before":{"id":19727,"cost":null,"name":"High Jump","type":"action","uuid":"2894549065268087","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2377","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:27:42.817687+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You [Stride](link_action_19855), then attempt a DC 30 Athletics check to jump vertically. If you didn't [Stride](link_action_19855) at least 10 feet, you automatically fail. This DC might be increased or decreased due to the situation, as determined by the GM.\n\n**Critical Success** You [Leap](link_action_19735) up to 8 feet vertically and 10 feet horizontally.\n\n**Success** You [Leap](link_action_19735) up to 5 feet vertically and 5 feet horizontally.\n\n**Failure** You [Leap](link_action_19735) normally.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall prone in your space.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19727,"cost":null,"name":"High Jump","type":"action","uuid":"2894549065268087","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2377","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:27:42.817687+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You [Stride](link_action_19855), then attempt a DC 30 Athletics check to jump vertically. If you didn't [Stride](link_action_19855) at least 10 feet, you automatically fail. This DC might be increased or decreased due to the situation, as determined by the GM.\n\n**Critical Success** You [Leap](link_action_19735) up to 8 feet vertically and 10 feet horizontally.\n\n**Success** You [Leap](link_action_19735) up to 5 feet vertically and 5 feet horizontally.\n\n**Failure** You [Leap](link_action_19735) normally.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall prone in your space.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19728,"type":"feat","before":{"id":19728,"cost":null,"name":"Hunt Prey","type":"feat","uuid":"901840638750153","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1344],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"RollOption","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.TargetHuntedPrey","domain":"all","option":"hunted-prey","toggleable":true},{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.SeekHuntedPrey","value":2,"selector":"perception","predicate":["action:seek","hunted-prey"]},{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.TrackHuntedPrey","value":2,"selector":"survival","predicate":["action:track","hunted-prey"]},{"key":"RollOption","domain":"ranged-attack-roll","option":"ignore-range-penalty:2","predicate":["hunted-prey"]}]},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:28:05.384211+00:00","operations":[{"id":"ab9d5be4-8e23-444b-bfad-1769a60a7dc2","data":{"text":"to Seek your prey","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"ab7eaf9d-6e0a-4686-848d-1403c20fbcc9","data":{"text":"to Track your prey","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_SURVIVAL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"You designate a single creature as your prey and focus your attacks against that creature. You must be able to see or hear the prey, or you must be tracking the prey during exploration.\n\nYou gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when you [Seek](link_action_19845) your prey and a +2 circumstance bonus to Survival checks when you [Track](link_action_19861) your prey. You also ignore the penalty for making ranged attacks within your second range increment against the prey you’re hunting.\n\nYou can have only one creature designated as your prey at a time. If you use Hunt Prey against a creature when you already have a creature designated, the prior creature loses the designation and the new prey gains the designation. Your designation lasts until your next daily preparations.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":19728,"cost":null,"name":"Hunt Prey","type":"feat","uuid":"901840638750153","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1344],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"RollOption","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.TargetHuntedPrey","domain":"all","option":"hunted-prey","toggleable":true},{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.SeekHuntedPrey","value":2,"selector":"perception","predicate":["action:seek","hunted-prey"]},{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.TrackHuntedPrey","value":2,"selector":"survival","predicate":["action:track","hunted-prey"]},{"key":"RollOption","domain":"ranged-attack-roll","option":"ignore-range-penalty:2","predicate":["hunted-prey"]}]},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:28:05.384211+00:00","operations":[{"id":"ab9d5be4-8e23-444b-bfad-1769a60a7dc2","data":{"text":"to Seek your prey","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"ab7eaf9d-6e0a-4686-848d-1403c20fbcc9","data":{"text":"to Track your prey","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_SURVIVAL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"You designate a single creature as your prey and focus your attacks against that creature. You must be able to see or hear the prey, or you must be tracking the prey during exploration.\n\nYou gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when you [Seek](link_action_19845) your prey and a +2 circumstance bonus to Survival checks when you [Track](link_action_19861) your prey. You also ignore the penalty for making ranged attacks within your second range increment against the prey you’re hunting.\n\nYou can have only one creature designated as your prey at a time. If you use Hunt Prey against a creature when you already have a creature designated, the prior creature loses the designation and the new prey gains the designation. Your designation lasts until your next daily preparations.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19729,"type":"action","before":{"id":19729,"cost":null,"name":"Identify Alchemy","type":"action","uuid":"7498465223757824","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2386","book":"Player Core","page":"237"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:28:22.054006+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can identify the nature of an [alchemical item](link_trait_1529) with 10 minutes of testing using [alchemist's toolkit](link_item_6694). If your attempt is interrupted in any way, you must start over.\n\n**Success** You identify the item and the means of activating it.\n\n**Failure** You fail to identify the item but can try again.\n\n**Critical Failure** You misidentify the item as another item of the GM's choice.","availability":null,"requirements":"You're holding or wearing an Alchemist's Toolkit.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19729,"cost":null,"name":"Identify Alchemy","type":"action","uuid":"7498465223757824","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2386","book":"Player Core","page":"237"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:28:22.054006+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can identify the nature of an [alchemical item](link_trait_1529) with 10 minutes of testing using [alchemist's toolkit](link_item_6694). If your attempt is interrupted in any way, you must start over.\n\n**Success** You identify the item and the means of activating it.\n\n**Failure** You fail to identify the item but can try again.\n\n**Critical Failure** You misidentify the item as another item of the GM's choice.","availability":null,"requirements":"You're holding or wearing an Alchemist's Toolkit.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19730,"type":"action","before":{"id":19730,"cost":null,"name":"Identify Magic","type":"action","uuid":"3741081474630028","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1463],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2365","book":"Player Core","page":"230"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:28:47.629222+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Once you discover that an item, location, or ongoing effect is [magical](link_trait_1504), you can spend 10 minutes to try to identify the particulars of its magic. If your attempt is interrupted, you must start over. The GM sets the DC for your check. [Cursed](link_trait_1558) magic or esoteric subjects usually have higher DCs or might even be impossible to identify using this activity alone. Heightening a spell doesn't increase the DC to identify it.\n\n**Critical Success** You learn all the attributes of the magic, including its name (for an effect), what it does, any means of activating it (for an item or location), and whether it is cursed.\n\n**Success** For an item or location, you get a sense of what it does and learn any means of activating it. For an ongoing effect (such as a spell with a duration), you learn the effect's name and what it does. You can't try again in hopes of getting a critical success.\n\n**Failure** You fail to identify the magic and can't try again for 1 day.\n\n**Critical Failure** You misidentify the magic as something else of the GM's choice.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19730,"cost":null,"name":"Identify Magic","type":"action","uuid":"3741081474630028","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1463],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2365","book":"Player Core","page":"230"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:28:47.629222+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Once you discover that an item, location, or ongoing effect is [magical](link_trait_1504), you can spend 10 minutes to try to identify the particulars of its magic. If your attempt is interrupted, you must start over. The GM sets the DC for your check. [Cursed](link_trait_1558) magic or esoteric subjects usually have higher DCs or might even be impossible to identify using this activity alone. Heightening a spell doesn't increase the DC to identify it.\n\n**Critical Success** You learn all the attributes of the magic, including its name (for an effect), what it does, any means of activating it (for an item or location), and whether it is cursed.\n\n**Success** For an item or location, you get a sense of what it does and learn any means of activating it. For an ongoing effect (such as a spell with a duration), you learn the effect's name and what it does. You can't try again in hopes of getting a critical success.\n\n**Failure** You fail to identify the magic and can't try again for 1 day.\n\n**Critical Failure** You misidentify the magic as something else of the GM's choice.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19731,"type":"action","before":{"id":19731,"cost":null,"name":"Impersonate","type":"action","uuid":"1014257020281138","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1433,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2388","book":"Player Core","page":"238"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:29:23.397369+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You create a disguise to pass yourself off as someone or something you are not. Assembling a convincing disguise takes 10 minutes and requires a Disguise Kit, but a simpler, quicker disguise might do the job if you're not trying to imitate a specific individual, at the GM's discretion.\n\nIn most cases, creatures have a chance to detect your deception only if they use the Seek action to attempt Perception checks against your Deception DC. If you attempt to directly interact with someone while disguised, the GM rolls a secret Deception check for you against that creature's Perception DC instead.\n\nIf you're disguised as a specific individual, the GM might give creatures you interact with a circumstance bonus based on how well they know the person you're imitating, or the GM might roll a secret Deception check even if you aren't directly interacting with others.\n\n**Success** You trick the creature into thinking you're the person you're disguised as. You might have to attempt a new check if your behavior changes.\n\n**Failure** The creature can tell you're not who you claim to be.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature can tell you're not who you claim to be, and it recognizes you if it would know you without a disguise.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19731,"cost":null,"name":"Impersonate","type":"action","uuid":"1014257020281138","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1433,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2388","book":"Player Core","page":"238"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:29:23.397369+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You create a disguise to pass yourself off as someone or something you are not. Assembling a convincing disguise takes 10 minutes and requires a Disguise Kit, but a simpler, quicker disguise might do the job if you're not trying to imitate a specific individual, at the GM's discretion.\n\nIn most cases, creatures have a chance to detect your deception only if they use the Seek action to attempt Perception checks against your Deception DC. If you attempt to directly interact with someone while disguised, the GM rolls a secret Deception check for you against that creature's Perception DC instead.\n\nIf you're disguised as a specific individual, the GM might give creatures you interact with a circumstance bonus based on how well they know the person you're imitating, or the GM might roll a secret Deception check even if you aren't directly interacting with others.\n\n**Success** You trick the creature into thinking you're the person you're disguised as. You might have to attempt a new check if your behavior changes.\n\n**Failure** The creature can tell you're not who you claim to be.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature can tell you're not who you claim to be, and it recognizes you if it would know you without a disguise.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19733,"type":"action","before":{"id":19733,"cost":null,"name":"Interact","type":"action","uuid":"3402914292668269","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1433],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:29:43.563844+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You use your hand or hands to manipulate an object or the terrain. You can grab an unattended or stored object, draw a weapon, swap a held item for another, open a door, or achieve a similar effect. On rare occasions, you might have to attempt a skill check to determine if your Interact action was successful.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19733,"cost":null,"name":"Interact","type":"action","uuid":"3402914292668269","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1433],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:29:43.563844+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You use your hand or hands to manipulate an object or the terrain. You can grab an unattended or stored object, draw a weapon, swap a held item for another, open a door, or achieve a similar effect. On rare occasions, you might have to attempt a skill check to determine if your Interact action was successful.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19735,"type":"action","before":{"id":19735,"cost":null,"name":"Leap","type":"action","uuid":"5340793805957301","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2298","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:30:22.786495+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You take a short horizontal or vertical jump. Jumping a greater distance requires using the Athletics skill for a [High Jump](link_action_19727) or [Long Jump](link_action_19738).\n\n*   **Horizontal** Jump up to 10 feet horizontally if your Speed is at least 15 feet, or up to 15 feet horizontally if your speed is at least 30 feet. You land in the space where your Leap ends (meaning you can typically clear a 5-foot gap, or a 10-foot gap if your Speed is 30 feet or more). You can't make a horizontal Leap if your Speed is less than 15 feet.\n    \n*   **Vertical** Jump up to 3 feet vertically and 5 feet horizontally onto an elevated surface.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19735,"cost":null,"name":"Leap","type":"action","uuid":"5340793805957301","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2298","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:30:22.786495+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You take a short horizontal or vertical jump. Jumping a greater distance requires using the Athletics skill for a [High Jump](link_action_19727) or [Long Jump](link_action_19738).\n\n*   **Horizontal** Jump up to 10 feet horizontally if your Speed is at least 15 feet, or up to 15 feet horizontally if your speed is at least 30 feet. You land in the space where your Leap ends (meaning you can typically clear a 5-foot gap, or a 10-foot gap if your Speed is 30 feet or more). You can't make a horizontal Leap if your Speed is less than 15 feet.\n    \n*   **Vertical** Jump up to 3 feet vertically and 5 feet horizontally onto an elevated surface.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19736,"type":"action","before":{"id":19736,"cost":null,"name":"Learn a Spell","type":"action","uuid":"5702291468106036","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2366","book":"Player Core","page":"230"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:32:07.23416+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can gain access to a new spell of your tradition from someone who knows that spell or from magical writing like a spellbook or scroll. If you can cast spells of multiple traditions, you can Learn a Spell of any of those traditions, but you must use the corresponding skill to do so. For example, if you were a cleric with the bard multiclass archetype, you couldn't use Religion to add an occult spell to your bardic spell repertoire.\n\nTo learn the spell, you must do the following:\n\n*   Spend 1 hour per spell rank, during which you must remain in conversation with a person who knows the spell or have the magical writing in your possession.\n    \n*   Have materials with the Price indicated in the table below.\n    \n*   Attempt a skill check for the skill corresponding to your tradition (DC determined by the GM, often close to the DC on the Learning a Spell Table). Uncommon or rare spells have higher DCs; full guidelines for the GM appear on page 52 of GM Core.\n    \n\n**Critical Success** You expend half the materials and learn the spell.\n\n**Success** You expend the materials and learn the spell.\n\n**Failure** You fail to learn the spell but can try again after you gain a level. The materials aren't expended.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, except you expend half the materials.\n\n#### **Table 4-3: Learning a Spell**\n\n| Spell Level | Price | Typical DC |\n\n|--------------|-----------|------------|\n\n| 1st or cantrip | 2 gp | 15 |\n\n| 2nd | 6 gp | 18 |\n\n| 3rd | 16 gp | 20 |\n\n| 4th | 36 gp | 23 |\n\n| 5th | 70 gp | 26 |\n\n| 6th | 140 gp | 28 |\n\n| 7th | 300 gp | 31 |\n\n| 8th | 650 gp | 34|\n\n| 9th | 1,500 gp | 36 |\n\n| 10th | 7,000 gp | 41 |","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a spellcasting class feature, and the spell you want to learn is on your magical tradition's spell list","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19736,"cost":null,"name":"Learn a Spell","type":"action","uuid":"5702291468106036","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2366","book":"Player Core","page":"230"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:32:07.23416+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can gain access to a new spell of your tradition from someone who knows that spell or from magical writing like a spellbook or scroll. If you can cast spells of multiple traditions, you can Learn a Spell of any of those traditions, but you must use the corresponding skill to do so. For example, if you were a cleric with the bard multiclass archetype, you couldn't use Religion to add an occult spell to your bardic spell repertoire.\n\nTo learn the spell, you must do the following:\n\n*   Spend 1 hour per spell rank, during which you must remain in conversation with a person who knows the spell or have the magical writing in your possession.\n    \n*   Have materials with the Price indicated in the table below.\n    \n*   Attempt a skill check for the skill corresponding to your tradition (DC determined by the GM, often close to the DC on the Learning a Spell Table). Uncommon or rare spells have higher DCs; full guidelines for the GM appear on page 52 of GM Core.\n    \n\n**Critical Success** You expend half the materials and learn the spell.\n\n**Success** You expend the materials and learn the spell.\n\n**Failure** You fail to learn the spell but can try again after you gain a level. The materials aren't expended.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, except you expend half the materials.\n\n#### **Table 4-3: Learning a Spell**\n\n| Spell Level | Price | Typical DC |\n\n|--------------|-----------|------------|\n\n| 1st or cantrip | 2 gp | 15 |\n\n| 2nd | 6 gp | 18 |\n\n| 3rd | 16 gp | 20 |\n\n| 4th | 36 gp | 23 |\n\n| 5th | 70 gp | 26 |\n\n| 6th | 140 gp | 28 |\n\n| 7th | 300 gp | 31 |\n\n| 8th | 650 gp | 34|\n\n| 9th | 1,500 gp | 36 |\n\n| 10th | 7,000 gp | 41 |","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a spellcasting class feature, and the spell you want to learn is on your magical tradition's spell list","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19737,"type":"action","before":{"id":19737,"cost":null,"name":"Lie","type":"action","uuid":"3507031699525857","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1458,1448,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2389","book":"Player Core","page":"238"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:32:33.009768+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to fool someone with an untruth. Doing so takes at least 1 round, or longer if the lie is elaborate. You roll a single Deception check and compare it against the Perception DC of every creature you are trying to fool. The GM might give them a circumstance bonus based on the situation and the nature of the lie you are trying to tell. Elaborate or highly unbelievable lies are much harder to get a creature to believe than simpler and more believable lies, and some lies are so big that it's impossible to get anyone to believe them.\n\nAt the GM's discretion, if a creature initially believes your lie, it might attempt a Perception check later to Sense Motive against your Deception DC to realize it's a lie. This usually happens if the creature discovers enough evidence to counter your statements.\n\n**Success** The target believes your lie.\n\n**Failure** The target doesn't believe your lie and gains a +4 circumstance bonus against your attempts to Lie for the duration of your conversation. The target is also more likely to be suspicious of you in the future.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19737,"cost":null,"name":"Lie","type":"action","uuid":"3507031699525857","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1458,1448,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DECEPTION","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2389","book":"Player Core","page":"238"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:32:33.009768+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to fool someone with an untruth. Doing so takes at least 1 round, or longer if the lie is elaborate. You roll a single Deception check and compare it against the Perception DC of every creature you are trying to fool. The GM might give them a circumstance bonus based on the situation and the nature of the lie you are trying to tell. Elaborate or highly unbelievable lies are much harder to get a creature to believe than simpler and more believable lies, and some lies are so big that it's impossible to get anyone to believe them.\n\nAt the GM's discretion, if a creature initially believes your lie, it might attempt a Perception check later to Sense Motive against your Deception DC to realize it's a lie. This usually happens if the creature discovers enough evidence to counter your statements.\n\n**Success** The target believes your lie.\n\n**Failure** The target doesn't believe your lie and gains a +4 circumstance bonus against your attempts to Lie for the duration of your conversation. The target is also more likely to be suspicious of you in the future.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19738,"type":"action","before":{"id":19738,"cost":null,"name":"Long Jump","type":"action","uuid":"2295265521004504","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2378","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:32:53.06301+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You [Stride](link_action_19855), then attempt a DC 15 Athletics check to make a long jump in the direction you were [Striding](link_action_19855). If you didn't [Stride](link_action_19855) at least 10 feet, you automatically fail your check. The GM might increase or decrease this DC depending on the situation.\n\n**Success** You [Leap](link_action_19735) up to a distance equal to your check result rounded down to the nearest 5 feet. You can't jump farther than your land Speed.\n\n**Failure** You make a normal horizontal [Leap](link_action_19735).\n\n**Critical Failure** You make a normal horizontal [Leap](link_action_19735), then fall and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19738,"cost":null,"name":"Long Jump","type":"action","uuid":"2295265521004504","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2378","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:32:53.06301+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You [Stride](link_action_19855), then attempt a DC 15 Athletics check to make a long jump in the direction you were [Striding](link_action_19855). If you didn't [Stride](link_action_19855) at least 10 feet, you automatically fail your check. The GM might increase or decrease this DC depending on the situation.\n\n**Success** You [Leap](link_action_19735) up to a distance equal to your check result rounded down to the nearest 5 feet. You can't jump farther than your land Speed.\n\n**Failure** You make a normal horizontal [Leap](link_action_19735).\n\n**Critical Failure** You make a normal horizontal [Leap](link_action_19735), then fall and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19739,"type":"action","before":{"id":19739,"cost":null,"name":"Make an Impression","type":"action","uuid":"3944295765726991","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1457,1458,1448,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DIPLOMACY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2392","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:33:47.508694+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With at least 1 minute of conversation, during which you engage in charismatic overtures, flattery, and other acts of goodwill, you seek to make a good impression on someone to make them temporarily agreeable. At the end of the conversation, attempt a Diplomacy check against the Will DC of one target. You can instead choose up to five targets if you take a –2 penalty. The GM might add other bonuses or penalties based on the situation. Any impression you make lasts for only the current social interaction unless the GM decides otherwise. See Changing Attitudes below for a summary of the attitude conditions.\n\n**Critical Success** The target's attitude toward you improves by two steps.\n\n**Success** The target's attitude toward you improves by one step.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target's attitude toward you decreases by one step.\n\nChanging Attitudes\n------------------\n\nYour influence on NPCs is measured with a set of attitudes that reflect how they view your character. These are only a brief summary of a creature's disposition. The GM will supply additional nuance based on the history and beliefs of the characters you're interacting with, and their attitudes can change in accordance with the story. The attitudes are detailed in the Conditions Appendix and are summarized here.\n\n*   **Helpful:** Willing to help you and responds favorably to your requests.\n*   **Friendly:** Has a good attitude toward you, but won't necessarily stick their neck out to help you.\n*   **Indifferent:** Doesn't care about you either way. (Most NPCs start out indifferent.)\n*   **Unfriendly:** Dislikes you and doesn't want to help you.\n*   **Hostile:** Actively works against you—and might attack you just because of their dislike.\n\nNo one can ever change the attitude of a player character with these skills. You can roleplay interactions with player characters, and even use Diplomacy results if the player wants a mechanical sense of how convincing or charming a character is, but players make the ultimate decisions about how their characters respond.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19739,"cost":null,"name":"Make an Impression","type":"action","uuid":"3944295765726991","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1457,1458,1448,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DIPLOMACY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2392","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:33:47.508694+00:00","operations":null,"description":"With at least 1 minute of conversation, during which you engage in charismatic overtures, flattery, and other acts of goodwill, you seek to make a good impression on someone to make them temporarily agreeable. At the end of the conversation, attempt a Diplomacy check against the Will DC of one target. You can instead choose up to five targets if you take a –2 penalty. The GM might add other bonuses or penalties based on the situation. Any impression you make lasts for only the current social interaction unless the GM decides otherwise. See Changing Attitudes below for a summary of the attitude conditions.\n\n**Critical Success** The target's attitude toward you improves by two steps.\n\n**Success** The target's attitude toward you improves by one step.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target's attitude toward you decreases by one step.\n\nChanging Attitudes\n------------------\n\nYour influence on NPCs is measured with a set of attitudes that reflect how they view your character. These are only a brief summary of a creature's disposition. The GM will supply additional nuance based on the history and beliefs of the characters you're interacting with, and their attitudes can change in accordance with the story. The attitudes are detailed in the Conditions Appendix and are summarized here.\n\n*   **Helpful:** Willing to help you and responds favorably to your requests.\n*   **Friendly:** Has a good attitude toward you, but won't necessarily stick their neck out to help you.\n*   **Indifferent:** Doesn't care about you either way. (Most NPCs start out indifferent.)\n*   **Unfriendly:** Dislikes you and doesn't want to help you.\n*   **Hostile:** Actively works against you—and might attack you just because of their dislike.\n\nNo one can ever change the attitude of a player character with these skills. You can roleplay interactions with player characters, and even use Diplomacy results if the player wants a mechanical sense of how convincing or charming a character is, but players make the ultimate decisions about how their characters respond.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19740,"type":"action","before":{"id":19740,"cost":null,"name":"Maneuver in Flight","type":"action","uuid":"6546731887320220","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ACROBATICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2371","book":"Player Core","page":"233"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:34:11.670739+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try a difficult maneuver while flying. Attempt an Acrobatics check. The GM determines what maneuvers are possible, but they rarely allow you to move farther than your fly Speed. Success You succeed at the maneuver.\n\n**Failure** Your maneuver fails. The GM chooses if you simply can't move or if some other detrimental effect happens. The outcome should be appropriate for the maneuver you attempted (for instance, being blown off course if you were trying to fly against a strong wind).\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the consequence is more dire.\n\nSample Maneuver in Flight Tasks\n-------------------------------\n\n*   **Trained** steep ascent or descent\n*   **Expert** fly against the wind, hover midair\n*   **Master** reverse direction\n*   **Legendary** fly through gale force winds","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a fly Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19740,"cost":null,"name":"Maneuver in Flight","type":"action","uuid":"6546731887320220","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ACROBATICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2371","book":"Player Core","page":"233"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:34:11.670739+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try a difficult maneuver while flying. Attempt an Acrobatics check. The GM determines what maneuvers are possible, but they rarely allow you to move farther than your fly Speed. Success You succeed at the maneuver.\n\n**Failure** Your maneuver fails. The GM chooses if you simply can't move or if some other detrimental effect happens. The outcome should be appropriate for the maneuver you attempted (for instance, being blown off course if you were trying to fly against a strong wind).\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the consequence is more dire.\n\nSample Maneuver in Flight Tasks\n-------------------------------\n\n*   **Trained** steep ascent or descent\n*   **Expert** fly against the wind, hover midair\n*   **Master** reverse direction\n*   **Legendary** fly through gale force winds","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a fly Speed.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19743,"type":"action","before":{"id":19743,"cost":null,"name":"Palm an Object","type":"action","uuid":"8765912622111081","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"THIEVERY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2409","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:35:00.153855+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You pick up a small, unattended object and try not to be noticed. Roll a single Thievery check against the Perception DCs of all creatures who are currently observing you. You can typically only Palm Objects of negligible Bulk, though the GM might determine otherwise depending on the situation.\n\n**Success** The creature doesn't notice you Palming the Object.\n\n**Failure** The creature notices you Palming the Object.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19743,"cost":null,"name":"Palm an Object","type":"action","uuid":"8765912622111081","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"THIEVERY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2409","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:35:00.153855+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You pick up a small, unattended object and try not to be noticed. Roll a single Thievery check against the Perception DCs of all creatures who are currently observing you. You can typically only Palm Objects of negligible Bulk, though the GM might determine otherwise depending on the situation.\n\n**Success** The creature doesn't notice you Palming the Object.\n\n**Failure** The creature notices you Palming the Object.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19746,"type":"action","before":{"id":19746,"cost":null,"name":"Perform","type":"action","uuid":"6714357990070889","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"PERFORMANCE","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2401","book":"Player Core","page":"243"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:37:05.261832+00:00","operations":null,"description":"When making a brief performance-one song, a quick dance, or a few jokes-you use the Perform action. This action is most useful when you want to prove your capability or impress someone quickly. Performing rarely has an impact on its own, but it might influence the DCs of subsequent Diplomacy checks against the observers, or even change their attitudes if the GM sees fit.\n\n**Critical Success** Your performance impresses the observers, and they're likely to share stories of your ability.\n\n**Success** You prove yourself, and observers appreciate the quality of your performance.\n\n**Failure** Your performance falls flat.\n\n**Critical Failure** You demonstrate only incompetence.\n\nSample Perform Tasks\n--------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** audience of commoners\n    \n*   **Trained** audience of artisans\n    \n*   **Expert** audience of merchants or minor nobles\n    \n*   **Master** audience of high nobility or minor royalty\n    \n*   **Legendary** audience of major royalty or otherworldly beings\n    \n\n#### Performance Traits\n\nWhen you use an action that utilizes the Performance skill, it gains one or more traits relevant to the type of performance. The GM might change these depending on the circumstances, but the most common performance-based traits are listed below.\n\nIf you want to be particularly skilled with one type of performance, you can select the [Virtuosic Performer](link_feat_20690) skill feat. That feat breaks down some of the performance listed above into specific instrument types, and your GM might allow you to add your own type.\n\n| Performance | Additional Traits |\n\n|---|---|\n\n| Act or perform comedy | [Auditory](link_trait_1469), [linguistic](link_trait_1458), and [visual](link_trait_1479) |\n\n| Dance | [Move](link_trait_1505) and [visual](link_trait_1479) |\n\n| Play an instrument | [Auditory](link_trait_1469) and [manipulate](link_trait_1433) |\n\n| Orate or sing | [Auditory](link_trait_1469) and [linguistic](link_trait_1458) |","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19746,"cost":null,"name":"Perform","type":"action","uuid":"6714357990070889","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"PERFORMANCE","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2401","book":"Player Core","page":"243"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:37:05.261832+00:00","operations":null,"description":"When making a brief performance-one song, a quick dance, or a few jokes-you use the Perform action. This action is most useful when you want to prove your capability or impress someone quickly. Performing rarely has an impact on its own, but it might influence the DCs of subsequent Diplomacy checks against the observers, or even change their attitudes if the GM sees fit.\n\n**Critical Success** Your performance impresses the observers, and they're likely to share stories of your ability.\n\n**Success** You prove yourself, and observers appreciate the quality of your performance.\n\n**Failure** Your performance falls flat.\n\n**Critical Failure** You demonstrate only incompetence.\n\nSample Perform Tasks\n--------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** audience of commoners\n    \n*   **Trained** audience of artisans\n    \n*   **Expert** audience of merchants or minor nobles\n    \n*   **Master** audience of high nobility or minor royalty\n    \n*   **Legendary** audience of major royalty or otherworldly beings\n    \n\n#### Performance Traits\n\nWhen you use an action that utilizes the Performance skill, it gains one or more traits relevant to the type of performance. The GM might change these depending on the circumstances, but the most common performance-based traits are listed below.\n\nIf you want to be particularly skilled with one type of performance, you can select the [Virtuosic Performer](link_feat_20690) skill feat. That feat breaks down some of the performance listed above into specific instrument types, and your GM might allow you to add your own type.\n\n| Performance | Additional Traits |\n\n|---|---|\n\n| Act or perform comedy | [Auditory](link_trait_1469), [linguistic](link_trait_1458), and [visual](link_trait_1479) |\n\n| Dance | [Move](link_trait_1505) and [visual](link_trait_1479) |\n\n| Play an instrument | [Auditory](link_trait_1469) and [manipulate](link_trait_1433) |\n\n| Orate or sing | [Auditory](link_trait_1469) and [linguistic](link_trait_1458) |","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19747,"type":"action","before":{"id":19747,"cost":null,"name":"Pick a Lock","type":"action","uuid":"3443266719861245","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1438],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"THIEVERY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2412","book":"Player Core","page":"247"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:37:33.160647+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Opening a lock without a key is very similar to [Disable a Device](link_action_19625), but the DC of the Thievery check is determined by the complexity and construction of the lock you are attempting to pick (locks and their DCs are found in their description). Locks of higher qualities might require multiple successes to unlock, since otherwise even an unskilled burglar could easily crack the lock by attempting the check until they rolled a natural 20. If you lack the proper tools, the GM might let you used improvised picks, which are treated as shoddy tools, depending on the specifics of the lock.\n\n**Critical Success** You unlock the lock, or you achieve two successes toward opening a complex lock. You leave no trace of your tampering.\n\n**Success** You open the lock, or you achieve one success toward opening a complex lock.\n\n**Critical Failure** You break your tools. Fixing them requires using Crafting to [Repair](link_action_19756) them or else swapping in [Thieves' Toolkit Replacement Picks](link_item_7886).","availability":null,"requirements":"You're wearing or holding Thieves' Tools","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19747,"cost":null,"name":"Pick a Lock","type":"action","uuid":"3443266719861245","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1438],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"THIEVERY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2412","book":"Player Core","page":"247"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:37:33.160647+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Opening a lock without a key is very similar to [Disable a Device](link_action_19625), but the DC of the Thievery check is determined by the complexity and construction of the lock you are attempting to pick (locks and their DCs are found in their description). Locks of higher qualities might require multiple successes to unlock, since otherwise even an unskilled burglar could easily crack the lock by attempting the check until they rolled a natural 20. If you lack the proper tools, the GM might let you used improvised picks, which are treated as shoddy tools, depending on the specifics of the lock.\n\n**Critical Success** You unlock the lock, or you achieve two successes toward opening a complex lock. You leave no trace of your tampering.\n\n**Success** You open the lock, or you achieve one success toward opening a complex lock.\n\n**Critical Failure** You break your tools. Fixing them requires using Crafting to [Repair](link_action_19756) them or else swapping in [Thieves' Toolkit Replacement Picks](link_item_7886).","availability":null,"requirements":"You're wearing or holding Thieves' Tools","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19750,"type":"action","before":{"id":19750,"cost":null,"name":"Raise a Shield","type":"action","uuid":"1182629222392591","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2316","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:38:12.947104+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You position your shield to protect yourself. When you have Raised a Shield, you gain its listed circumstance bonus to AC. Your shield remains raised until the start of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are wielding a shield.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19750,"cost":null,"name":"Raise a Shield","type":"action","uuid":"1182629222392591","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2316","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:38:12.947104+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You position your shield to protect yourself. When you have Raised a Shield, you gain its listed circumstance bonus to AC. Your shield remains raised until the start of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are wielding a shield.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19751,"type":"feat","before":{"id":19751,"cost":null,"name":"Reactive Strike","type":"feat","uuid":"4548156761295409","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1339],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"A creature within your reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it’s using.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:38:26.762767+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You lash out at a foe that leaves an opening. Make a melee [Strike](link_action_19856) against the triggering creature. If your attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a [manipulate](link_trait_1433) action, you disrupt that action. This [Strike](link_action_19856) doesn’t count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn’t apply to this [Strike](link_action_19856).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":19751,"cost":null,"name":"Reactive Strike","type":"feat","uuid":"4548156761295409","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1339],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"A creature within your reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it’s using.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:38:26.762767+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You lash out at a foe that leaves an opening. Make a melee [Strike](link_action_19856) against the triggering creature. If your attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a [manipulate](link_trait_1433) action, you disrupt that action. This [Strike](link_action_19856) doesn’t count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn’t apply to this [Strike](link_action_19856).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19752,"type":"action","before":{"id":19752,"cost":null,"name":"Ready","type":"action","uuid":"261383067931154","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2299","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:38:42.252756+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You prepare to use an action that will occur outside your turn. Choose a single action or free action you can use, and designate a trigger. Your turn then ends. If the trigger you designated occurs before the start of your next turn, you can use the chosen action as a reaction (provided you still meet the requirements to use it). You can't Ready a free action that already has a trigger.\n\nIf you have a multiple attack penalty and your readied action is an attack action, your readied attack takes the multiple attack penalty you had at the time you used Ready. This is one of the few times the multiple attack penalty applies when it's not your turn.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19752,"cost":null,"name":"Ready","type":"action","uuid":"261383067931154","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2299","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:38:42.252756+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You prepare to use an action that will occur outside your turn. Choose a single action or free action you can use, and designate a trigger. Your turn then ends. If the trigger you designated occurs before the start of your next turn, you can use the chosen action as a reaction (provided you still meet the requirements to use it). You can't Ready a free action that already has a trigger.\n\nIf you have a multiple attack penalty and your readied action is an attack action, your readied attack takes the multiple attack penalty you had at the time you used Ready. This is one of the few times the multiple attack penalty applies when it's not your turn.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19753,"type":"action","before":{"id":19753,"cost":null,"name":"Recall Knowledge","type":"action","uuid":"5986656125609599","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1463,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":["LORE","ARCANA","CRAFTING","MEDICINE","NATURE","OCCULTISM","RELIGION","SOCIETY"],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2367","book":"Player Core","page":"231"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:39:00.604375+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt a skill check to try to remember a bit of knowledge regarding a topic related to that skill. Suggest which skill you'd like to use and ask the GM one question. The GM determines the DC. You might need to collaborate with the GM to narrow down the question or skills, and you can decide not to Recall Knowledge before committing to the action if you don't like your options.\n\n**Critical Success** You recall the knowledge accurately. The GM answers your question truthfully and either tells you additional information or context, or answers one follow-up question.\n\n**Success** You recall the knowledge accurately. The GM answers your question truthfully.\n\n**Critical Failure** You recall incorrect information. The GM answers your question falsely (or decides to give you no information, as on a failure).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19753,"cost":null,"name":"Recall Knowledge","type":"action","uuid":"5986656125609599","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1463,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":["LORE","ARCANA","CRAFTING","MEDICINE","NATURE","OCCULTISM","RELIGION","SOCIETY"],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2367","book":"Player Core","page":"231"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:39:00.604375+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt a skill check to try to remember a bit of knowledge regarding a topic related to that skill. Suggest which skill you'd like to use and ask the GM one question. The GM determines the DC. You might need to collaborate with the GM to narrow down the question or skills, and you can decide not to Recall Knowledge before committing to the action if you don't like your options.\n\n**Critical Success** You recall the knowledge accurately. The GM answers your question truthfully and either tells you additional information or context, or answers one follow-up question.\n\n**Success** You recall the knowledge accurately. The GM answers your question truthfully.\n\n**Critical Failure** You recall incorrect information. The GM answers your question falsely (or decides to give you no information, as on a failure).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19754,"type":"action","before":{"id":19754,"cost":null,"name":"Refocus","type":"action","uuid":"4729143181611045","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2621","book":"Player Core","page":"298"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:39:16.278155+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You spend 10 minutes performing deeds to restore your magical connection. This restores 1 [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) to your focus pool. The deeds you need to perform are specified in the class or ability that gives you your focus spells. These deeds can usually overlap with other tasks that relate to the source of your focus spells. For instance, a cleric with focus spells from a holy deity can usually [Refocus](link_trait_1526) while tending the wounds of their allies.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a focus pool.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19754,"cost":null,"name":"Refocus","type":"action","uuid":"4729143181611045","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2621","book":"Player Core","page":"298"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:39:16.278155+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You spend 10 minutes performing deeds to restore your magical connection. This restores 1 [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) to your focus pool. The deeds you need to perform are specified in the class or ability that gives you your focus spells. These deeds can usually overlap with other tasks that relate to the source of your focus spells. For instance, a cleric with focus spells from a holy deity can usually [Refocus](link_trait_1526) while tending the wounds of their allies.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a focus pool.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19755,"type":"action","before":{"id":19755,"cost":null,"name":"Release","type":"action","uuid":"5294490165983551","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1433],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2300","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:39:31.668247+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You release something you're holding in your hand or hands. This might mean dropping an item, removing one hand from your weapon while continuing to hold it in another hand, releasing a rope suspending a chandelier, or performing a similar action. Unlike most manipulate actions, Release does not trigger reactions that can be triggered by actions with the manipulate trait (such as [Reactive Strike](link_class-feature_19201)).\n\nIf you want to prepare to Release something outside of your turn, use the Ready activity.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19755,"cost":null,"name":"Release","type":"action","uuid":"5294490165983551","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1433],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2300","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:39:31.668247+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You release something you're holding in your hand or hands. This might mean dropping an item, removing one hand from your weapon while continuing to hold it in another hand, releasing a rope suspending a chandelier, or performing a similar action. Unlike most manipulate actions, Release does not trigger reactions that can be triggered by actions with the manipulate trait (such as [Reactive Strike](link_class-feature_19201)).\n\nIf you want to prepare to Release something outside of your turn, use the Ready activity.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19756,"type":"action","before":{"id":19756,"cost":null,"name":"Repair","type":"action","uuid":"7404902297519588","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457,1433,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2384","book":"Player Core","page":"236"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:40:09.826495+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You spend 10 minutes attempting to fix a damaged item, placing the item on a stable surface and using the [repair toolkit](link_item_7700) with both hands. The GM sets the DC, but it's usually about the same DC to Repair a given item as it is to [Craft](link_action_19617) it in the first place. You can't Repair a destroyed item.\n\n**Critical Success** You restore 10 Hit Points to the item, plus an additional 10 Hit Points per proficiency rank you have in Crafting (a total of 20 HP if you're trained, 30 HP if you're an expert, 40 HP if you're a master, or 50 HP if you're legendary).\n\n**Success** You restore 5 Hit Points to the item, plus an additional 5 per proficiency rank you have in Crafting (for a total of 10 HP if you are trained, 15 HP if you're an expert, 20 HP if you're a master, or 25 HP if you're legendary).\n\n**Critical Failure** You deal 2d6 damage to the item. Apply the item's Hardness to this damage.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are holding or wearing a repair toolkit","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19756,"cost":null,"name":"Repair","type":"action","uuid":"7404902297519588","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457,1433,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"CRAFTING","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2384","book":"Player Core","page":"236"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-13T22:40:09.826495+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You spend 10 minutes attempting to fix a damaged item, placing the item on a stable surface and using the [repair toolkit](link_item_7700) with both hands. The GM sets the DC, but it's usually about the same DC to Repair a given item as it is to [Craft](link_action_19617) it in the first place. You can't Repair a destroyed item.\n\n**Critical Success** You restore 10 Hit Points to the item, plus an additional 10 Hit Points per proficiency rank you have in Crafting (a total of 20 HP if you're trained, 30 HP if you're an expert, 40 HP if you're a master, or 50 HP if you're legendary).\n\n**Success** You restore 5 Hit Points to the item, plus an additional 5 per proficiency rank you have in Crafting (for a total of 10 HP if you are trained, 15 HP if you're an expert, 20 HP if you're a master, or 25 HP if you're legendary).\n\n**Critical Failure** You deal 2d6 damage to the item. Apply the item's Hardness to this damage.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are holding or wearing a repair toolkit","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19844,"type":"action","before":{"id":19844,"cost":null,"name":"Request","type":"action","uuid":"8121201913501594","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1458,1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DIPLOMACY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2393","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:21:15.627033+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can make a request of a creature that's friendly or helpful to you. You must couch the request in terms that the target would accept given their current attitude toward you. The GM sets the DC of the Diplomacy check based on the difficulty of the request. Some requests are unsavory or impossible, and even a helpful NPC would never agree to them.\n\n**Critical Success** The target agrees to your request without qualifications.\n\n**Success** The target agrees to your request, but they might demand added provisions or alterations to the request.\n\n**Failure** The target refuses the request, though they might propose an alternative that is less extreme.\n\n**Critical Failure** Not only does the target refuse the request, but their attitude toward you decreases by one step due to the temerity of the request.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19844,"cost":null,"name":"Request","type":"action","uuid":"8121201913501594","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1458,1448,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"DIPLOMACY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2393","book":"Player Core","page":"239"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:21:15.627033+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can make a request of a creature that's friendly or helpful to you. You must couch the request in terms that the target would accept given their current attitude toward you. The GM sets the DC of the Diplomacy check based on the difficulty of the request. Some requests are unsavory or impossible, and even a helpful NPC would never agree to them.\n\n**Critical Success** The target agrees to your request without qualifications.\n\n**Success** The target agrees to your request, but they might demand added provisions or alterations to the request.\n\n**Failure** The target refuses the request, though they might propose an alternative that is less extreme.\n\n**Critical Failure** Not only does the target refuse the request, but their attitude toward you decreases by one step due to the temerity of the request.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19845,"type":"action","before":{"id":19845,"cost":null,"name":"Seek","type":"action","uuid":"2039728856448174","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1463],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2301","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:22:00.59033+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You scan an area for signs of creatures or objects, possibly including secret doors or hazards. Choose an area to scan. The GM determines the area you can scan with one Seek action--almost always 30 feet or less in any dimension. The GM might impose a penalty if you search far away from you or adjust the number of actions it takes to Seek a particularly cluttered area.\n\nThe GM attempts a single secret Perception check for you and compares the result to the Stealth DCs of any undetected or hidden creatures in the area, or the DC to detect each object in the area (as determined by the GM or by someone [Concealing the Object](link_action_19615)). A creature you detect might remain hidden, rather than becoming observed, if you're using an imprecise sense or if an effect (such as [invisibility](link_spell_4689)) prevents the subject from being observed.\n\n**Critical Success** Any undetected or hidden creature you critically succeeded against becomes observed by you. You learn the location of objects in the area you critically succeeded against.\n\n**Success** Any undetected creature you suceeded against becomes hidden from you instead of undetected, and any hidden creature you succeeded against becomes observed by you. You learn the location of any object or get a clue to its whereabouts, as determined by the GM.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19845,"cost":null,"name":"Seek","type":"action","uuid":"2039728856448174","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1463],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2301","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:22:00.59033+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You scan an area for signs of creatures or objects, possibly including secret doors or hazards. Choose an area to scan. The GM determines the area you can scan with one Seek action--almost always 30 feet or less in any dimension. The GM might impose a penalty if you search far away from you or adjust the number of actions it takes to Seek a particularly cluttered area.\n\nThe GM attempts a single secret Perception check for you and compares the result to the Stealth DCs of any undetected or hidden creatures in the area, or the DC to detect each object in the area (as determined by the GM or by someone [Concealing the Object](link_action_19615)). A creature you detect might remain hidden, rather than becoming observed, if you're using an imprecise sense or if an effect (such as [invisibility](link_spell_4689)) prevents the subject from being observed.\n\n**Critical Success** Any undetected or hidden creature you critically succeeded against becomes observed by you. You learn the location of objects in the area you critically succeeded against.\n\n**Success** Any undetected creature you suceeded against becomes hidden from you instead of undetected, and any hidden creature you succeeded against becomes observed by you. You learn the location of any object or get a clue to its whereabouts, as determined by the GM.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19846,"type":"action","before":{"id":19846,"cost":null,"name":"Sense Direction","type":"action","uuid":"8442254037380496","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SURVIVAL","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2406","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:22:31.542527+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Using the stars, the position of the sun, traits of the geography or flora, or the behavior of fauna, you can stay oriented in the wild. Typically, you attempt a Survival check only once per day, but some environments or changes might necessitate rolling more often. The GM determines the DC and how long this activity takes (usually just a minute or so). More unusual locales or those you're unfamiliar with might require you to have a minimum proficiency rank to Sense Direction. Without a Compass, you take a -2 item penalty to checks to Sense Direction.\n\n**Critical Success** You get an excellent sense of where you are. If you are in an environment with cardinal directions, you know them exactly.\n\n**Success** You gain enough orientation to avoid becoming hopelessly lost. If you are in an environment with cardinal directions, you have a sense of those directions.\n\nSense Direction Tasks\n---------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** determine a cardinal direction using the sun\n*   **Trained** find an overgrown path in a forest\n*   **Expert** navigate a hedge maze\n*   **Master** navigate a byzantine labyrinth or relatively featureless desert\n*   **Legendary** navigate an ever-changing dream realm","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19846,"cost":null,"name":"Sense Direction","type":"action","uuid":"8442254037380496","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457,1463,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SURVIVAL","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2406","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:22:31.542527+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Using the stars, the position of the sun, traits of the geography or flora, or the behavior of fauna, you can stay oriented in the wild. Typically, you attempt a Survival check only once per day, but some environments or changes might necessitate rolling more often. The GM determines the DC and how long this activity takes (usually just a minute or so). More unusual locales or those you're unfamiliar with might require you to have a minimum proficiency rank to Sense Direction. Without a Compass, you take a -2 item penalty to checks to Sense Direction.\n\n**Critical Success** You get an excellent sense of where you are. If you are in an environment with cardinal directions, you know them exactly.\n\n**Success** You gain enough orientation to avoid becoming hopelessly lost. If you are in an environment with cardinal directions, you have a sense of those directions.\n\nSense Direction Tasks\n---------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** determine a cardinal direction using the sun\n*   **Trained** find an overgrown path in a forest\n*   **Expert** navigate a hedge maze\n*   **Master** navigate a byzantine labyrinth or relatively featureless desert\n*   **Legendary** navigate an ever-changing dream realm","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19847,"type":"action","before":{"id":19847,"cost":null,"name":"Sense Motive","type":"action","uuid":"6909398769181112","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1437,1463],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2302","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:22:53.146153+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to tell whether a creature's behavior is abnormal. Choose one creature and assess it for odd body language, signs of nervousness, and other indicators that it might be trying to deceive someone. The GM attempts a single secret Perception check for you and compares the result to the Deception DC of the creature, the DC of a spell affecting the creature's mental state, or another appropriate DC determined by the GM. You typically can't try to Sense the Motive of the same creature again until the situation changes significantly.\n\n**Critical Success** You determine the creature's true intentions and get a solid idea of any mental magic affecting it.\n\n**Success** You can tell whether the creature is behaving normally, but you don't know its exact intentions or what magic might be affecting it.\n\n**Failure** You detect what a deceptive creature wants you to believe. If they're not being deceptive, you believe they're behaving normally.\n\n**Critical Failure** You get a false sense of the creature's intentions.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19847,"cost":null,"name":"Sense Motive","type":"action","uuid":"6909398769181112","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1437,1463],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2302","book":"Player Core","page":"417"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:22:53.146153+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to tell whether a creature's behavior is abnormal. Choose one creature and assess it for odd body language, signs of nervousness, and other indicators that it might be trying to deceive someone. The GM attempts a single secret Perception check for you and compares the result to the Deception DC of the creature, the DC of a spell affecting the creature's mental state, or another appropriate DC determined by the GM. You typically can't try to Sense the Motive of the same creature again until the situation changes significantly.\n\n**Critical Success** You determine the creature's true intentions and get a solid idea of any mental magic affecting it.\n\n**Success** You can tell whether the creature is behaving normally, but you don't know its exact intentions or what magic might be affecting it.\n\n**Failure** You detect what a deceptive creature wants you to believe. If they're not being deceptive, you believe they're behaving normally.\n\n**Critical Failure** You get a false sense of the creature's intentions.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19849,"type":"action","before":{"id":19849,"cost":null,"name":"Shove","type":"action","uuid":"6615194763019592","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2380","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:23:27.105996+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You push a creature away from you. Attempt an Athletics check against your target's Fortitude DC.\n\n**Critical Success** You push your target up to 10 feet away from you. You can [Stride](link_action_19855) after it, but you must move the same distance and in the same direction.\n\n**Success** You push your target back 5 feet. You can [Stride](link_action_19855) after it, but you must move the same distance and in the same direction.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose your balance, fall, and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one hand free. The target can't be more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19849,"cost":null,"name":"Shove","type":"action","uuid":"6615194763019592","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2380","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:23:27.105996+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You push a creature away from you. Attempt an Athletics check against your target's Fortitude DC.\n\n**Critical Success** You push your target up to 10 feet away from you. You can [Stride](link_action_19855) after it, but you must move the same distance and in the same direction.\n\n**Success** You push your target back 5 feet. You can [Stride](link_action_19855) after it, but you must move the same distance and in the same direction.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose your balance, fall, and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one hand free. The target can't be more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19850,"type":"action","before":{"id":19850,"cost":null,"name":"Sneak","type":"action","uuid":"5103370009778602","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1463,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"STEALTH","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2405","book":"Player Core","page":"245"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:24:29.519666+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to move to another place while becoming or staying undetected. Stride up to half your Speed. (You can use Sneak while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type; you must move at half that Speed.)\n\nAt the end of your movement, the GM rolls your Stealth check in secret and compares the result to the Perception DC of each creature you were Hidden from or Undetected by at the start of your movement. If you have cover or greater cover from the creature throughout your Stride, you gain the +2 circumstance bonus from cover (or +4 from greater cover) to your Stealth check. Because you're moving, the bonus increase from Taking Cover doesn't apply. You don't get to roll against a creature if, at the end of your movement, you neither are [Concealed](link_trait_1841) from it nor have cover or greater cover against it. You automatically become observed by such a creature.\n\n**Success** You're undetected by the creature during your movement and remain undetected by the creature at the end of it.\n\nYou become observed as soon as you do anything other than Hide, Sneak, or Step. If you attempt to Strike a creature, the creature remains Off-Guard against that attack, and you then become observed. If you do anything else, you become observed just before you act unless the GM determines otherwise. The GM might allow you to perform a particularly unobtrusive action without being noticed, possibly requiring another Stealth check. If you speak or make a deliberate loud noise, you become hidden instead of undetected.\n\nIf a creature uses Seek and you become hidden to it as a result, you must Sneak if you want to become undetected by that creature again.\n\n**Failure** A telltale sound or other sign gives your position away, though you still remain unseen. You're hidden from the creature throughout your movement and remain so.\n\n**Critical Failure** You're spotted! You're observed by the creature throughout your movement and remain so. If you're Invisible and were hidden from the creature, instead of being observed you're hidden throughout your movement and remain so.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19850,"cost":null,"name":"Sneak","type":"action","uuid":"5103370009778602","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1463,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"STEALTH","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2405","book":"Player Core","page":"245"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:24:29.519666+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt to move to another place while becoming or staying undetected. Stride up to half your Speed. (You can use Sneak while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type; you must move at half that Speed.)\n\nAt the end of your movement, the GM rolls your Stealth check in secret and compares the result to the Perception DC of each creature you were Hidden from or Undetected by at the start of your movement. If you have cover or greater cover from the creature throughout your Stride, you gain the +2 circumstance bonus from cover (or +4 from greater cover) to your Stealth check. Because you're moving, the bonus increase from Taking Cover doesn't apply. You don't get to roll against a creature if, at the end of your movement, you neither are [Concealed](link_trait_1841) from it nor have cover or greater cover against it. You automatically become observed by such a creature.\n\n**Success** You're undetected by the creature during your movement and remain undetected by the creature at the end of it.\n\nYou become observed as soon as you do anything other than Hide, Sneak, or Step. If you attempt to Strike a creature, the creature remains Off-Guard against that attack, and you then become observed. If you do anything else, you become observed just before you act unless the GM determines otherwise. The GM might allow you to perform a particularly unobtrusive action without being noticed, possibly requiring another Stealth check. If you speak or make a deliberate loud noise, you become hidden instead of undetected.\n\nIf a creature uses Seek and you become hidden to it as a result, you must Sneak if you want to become undetected by that creature again.\n\n**Failure** A telltale sound or other sign gives your position away, though you still remain unseen. You're hidden from the creature throughout your movement and remain so.\n\n**Critical Failure** You're spotted! You're observed by the creature throughout your movement and remain so. If you're Invisible and were hidden from the creature, instead of being observed you're hidden throughout your movement and remain so.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19851,"type":"action","before":{"id":19851,"cost":null,"name":"Stand","type":"action","uuid":"4574741108871677","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2303","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:24:36.576811+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You stand up from Prone.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19851,"cost":null,"name":"Stand","type":"action","uuid":"4574741108871677","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2303","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:24:36.576811+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You stand up from Prone.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19852,"type":"action","before":{"id":19852,"cost":null,"name":"Steal","type":"action","uuid":"7030387941264189","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"THIEVERY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2410","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:25:11.235548+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to take a small object from another creature without being noticed. Typically, you can Steal only an object of negligible Bulk, you must have a free hand, and you automatically fail if the creature who has the object is in combat or on guard.\n\nAttempt a Thievery check to determine if you successfully Steal the object. The DC is usually the Perception DC of the creature wearing the object. It's easiest to steal an object that is worn but not closely guarded (like a loosely carried pouch filled with coins, or an object within such a pouch). The GM might increase the DC if the object is protected or if the nature of the object makes it harder to steal (such as a very small item in a large pack, or a sheet of parchment mixed in with other documents). For instance, the DC is typically 5 higher if the object is in a pocket, held in a creature's hand, or similarly protected.\n\nYou might also need to compare your Thievery check result against the Perception DCs of observers other than the person wearing the object. The GM might impose a circumstance penalty to the DCs of observers who are distracted.\n\n**Success** You steal the item without the bearer noticing, or an observer doesn't see you take or attempt to take the item.\n\n**Failure** The item's bearer notices your attempt before you can take the object, or an observer sees you take or attempt to take the item. The GM determines the response of any creature that notices your theft.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19852,"cost":null,"name":"Steal","type":"action","uuid":"7030387941264189","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"THIEVERY","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2410","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:25:11.235548+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to take a small object from another creature without being noticed. Typically, you can Steal only an object of negligible Bulk, you must have a free hand, and you automatically fail if the creature who has the object is in combat or on guard.\n\nAttempt a Thievery check to determine if you successfully Steal the object. The DC is usually the Perception DC of the creature wearing the object. It's easiest to steal an object that is worn but not closely guarded (like a loosely carried pouch filled with coins, or an object within such a pouch). The GM might increase the DC if the object is protected or if the nature of the object makes it harder to steal (such as a very small item in a large pack, or a sheet of parchment mixed in with other documents). For instance, the DC is typically 5 higher if the object is in a pocket, held in a creature's hand, or similarly protected.\n\nYou might also need to compare your Thievery check result against the Perception DCs of observers other than the person wearing the object. The GM might impose a circumstance penalty to the DCs of observers who are distracted.\n\n**Success** You steal the item without the bearer noticing, or an observer doesn't see you take or attempt to take the item.\n\n**Failure** The item's bearer notices your attempt before you can take the object, or an observer sees you take or attempt to take the item. The GM determines the response of any creature that notices your theft.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19853,"type":"action","before":{"id":19853,"cost":null,"name":"Step","type":"action","uuid":"567734121479914","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2304","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:25:25.366071+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You carefully move 5 feet. Unlike most types of movement, Stepping doesn't trigger reactions, such as [Reactive Strike](link_class-feature_19201), that can be triggered by move actions or upon leaving or entering a square.\n\nYou can't Step into difficult terrain, and you can't Step using a Speed other than your land Speed.","availability":null,"requirements":"Your Speed is at least 10 feet.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19853,"cost":null,"name":"Step","type":"action","uuid":"567734121479914","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2304","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:25:25.366071+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You carefully move 5 feet. Unlike most types of movement, Stepping doesn't trigger reactions, such as [Reactive Strike](link_class-feature_19201), that can be triggered by move actions or upon leaving or entering a square.\n\nYou can't Step into difficult terrain, and you can't Step using a Speed other than your land Speed.","availability":null,"requirements":"Your Speed is at least 10 feet.","prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19855,"type":"action","before":{"id":19855,"cost":null,"name":"Stride","type":"action","uuid":"3622379426522088","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2305","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:25:49.42181+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move up to your Speed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19855,"cost":null,"name":"Stride","type":"action","uuid":"3622379426522088","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2305","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:25:49.42181+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You move up to your Speed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19856,"type":"action","before":{"id":19856,"cost":null,"name":"Strike","type":"action","uuid":"2549047613995403","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2306","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:26:07.449536+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attack with a weapon you're wielding or with an unarmed attack, targeting one creature within your reach (for a melee attack) or within range (for a ranged attack). Roll an attack roll using the attack modifier for the weapon or unarmed attack you're using, and compare the result to the target creature's AC to determine the effect.\n\n**Critical Success** You make a damage roll according to the weapon or unarmed attack and deal double damage.\n\n**Success** You make a damage roll according to the weapon or unarmed attack and deal damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19856,"cost":null,"name":"Strike","type":"action","uuid":"2549047613995403","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2306","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:26:07.449536+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attack with a weapon you're wielding or with an unarmed attack, targeting one creature within your reach (for a melee attack) or within range (for a ranged attack). Roll an attack roll using the attack modifier for the weapon or unarmed attack you're using, and compare the result to the target creature's AC to determine the effect.\n\n**Critical Success** You make a damage roll according to the weapon or unarmed attack and deal double damage.\n\n**Success** You make a damage roll according to the weapon or unarmed attack and deal damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19858,"type":"action","before":{"id":19858,"cost":null,"name":"Sustain","type":"action","uuid":"7845751305633010","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2317","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:27:10.903097+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Choose one of your effects that has a sustained duration or lists a special benefit when you Sustain it. Most such effects come from spells or magic item activations. If the effect has a sustained duration, its duration extends until the end of your next turn. (Sustaining more than once in the same turn doesn't extend the duration to subsequent turns.) If an ability can be sustained but doesn't list how long, it can be sustained up to 10 minutes.\n\nAn effect might list an additional benefit that occurs if you Sustain it, and this can even appear on effects that don't have a sustained duration. If the effect has both a special benefit and a sustained duration, your Sustain action extends the duration as well as having the special benefit.\n\nIf your Sustain action is disrupted, the ability ends.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19858,"cost":null,"name":"Sustain","type":"action","uuid":"7845751305633010","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2317","book":"Player Core","page":"419"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:27:10.903097+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Choose one of your effects that has a sustained duration or lists a special benefit when you Sustain it. Most such effects come from spells or magic item activations. If the effect has a sustained duration, its duration extends until the end of your next turn. (Sustaining more than once in the same turn doesn't extend the duration to subsequent turns.) If an ability can be sustained but doesn't list how long, it can be sustained up to 10 minutes.\n\nAn effect might list an additional benefit that occurs if you Sustain it, and this can even appear on effects that don't have a sustained duration. If the effect has both a special benefit and a sustained duration, your Sustain action extends the duration as well as having the special benefit.\n\nIf your Sustain action is disrupted, the ability ends.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19859,"type":"action","before":{"id":19859,"cost":null,"name":"Swim","type":"action","uuid":"8987806645938531","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2381","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:27:39.809223+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt an Athletics check to move a maximum distance of 10 feet through water. The GM determines the DC based on the turbulence or danger of the water; in most instances of calm water, you get an automatic critical success. If your land Speed is 40 feet or higher, increase the maximum possible distance by 5 feet for every 20 feet of Speed above 20 feet.\n\nIf you end your turn in water and haven't succeeded at a Swim action that turn, you sink 10 feet or get moved by the current, as determined by the GM. This doesn't apply if your last action on your turn was to enter the water.\n\n**Critical Success** You move through the water, increasing the maximum distance by 5 feet.\n\n**Success** You move through the water.\n\n**Critical Failure** You make no progress. If you're holding your breath, you lose 1 round of air.\n\nSample Swim Tasks\n-----------------\n\n**Untrained** lake or other still water\n\n**Trained** flowing water, like a river\n\n**Expert** swiftly flowing river\n\n**Master** stormy sea Legendary maelstrom, waterfall","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19859,"cost":null,"name":"Swim","type":"action","uuid":"8987806645938531","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2381","book":"Player Core","page":"235"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:27:39.809223+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You attempt an Athletics check to move a maximum distance of 10 feet through water. The GM determines the DC based on the turbulence or danger of the water; in most instances of calm water, you get an automatic critical success. If your land Speed is 40 feet or higher, increase the maximum possible distance by 5 feet for every 20 feet of Speed above 20 feet.\n\nIf you end your turn in water and haven't succeeded at a Swim action that turn, you sink 10 feet or get moved by the current, as determined by the GM. This doesn't apply if your last action on your turn was to enter the water.\n\n**Critical Success** You move through the water, increasing the maximum distance by 5 feet.\n\n**Success** You move through the water.\n\n**Critical Failure** You make no progress. If you're holding your breath, you lose 1 round of air.\n\nSample Swim Tasks\n-----------------\n\n**Untrained** lake or other still water\n\n**Trained** flowing water, like a river\n\n**Expert** swiftly flowing river\n\n**Master** stormy sea Legendary maelstrom, waterfall","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19860,"type":"action","before":{"id":19860,"cost":null,"name":"Take Cover","type":"action","uuid":"4488978688595915","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2307","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:28:00.476716+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You press yourself against a wall or duck behind an obstacle to take better advantage of cover. If you would have standard cover, you instead gain greater cover, which provides a +4 circumstance bonus to AC; to Reflex saves against area effects; and to Stealth checks to [Hide](link_action_19726), [Sneak](link_action_19850), or otherwise avoid detection. Otherwise, you gain standard cover (a +2 circumstance bonus instead). If you’re prone, you gain greater cover against ranged attacks. Take Cover lasts until you move from your current space, use an [attack](link_trait_1520) action, become unconscious, or end it as a free action.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are benefiting from standard cover, are near a feature that allows you to take cover, or are prone.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19860,"cost":null,"name":"Take Cover","type":"action","uuid":"4488978688595915","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2307","book":"Player Core","page":"418"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:28:00.476716+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You press yourself against a wall or duck behind an obstacle to take better advantage of cover. If you would have standard cover, you instead gain greater cover, which provides a +4 circumstance bonus to AC; to Reflex saves against area effects; and to Stealth checks to [Hide](link_action_19726), [Sneak](link_action_19850), or otherwise avoid detection. Otherwise, you gain standard cover (a +2 circumstance bonus instead). If you’re prone, you gain greater cover against ranged attacks. Take Cover lasts until you move from your current space, use an [attack](link_trait_1520) action, become unconscious, or end it as a free action.","availability":null,"requirements":"You are benefiting from standard cover, are near a feature that allows you to take cover, or are prone.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19861,"type":"action","before":{"id":19861,"cost":null,"name":"Track","type":"action","uuid":"4205562911072053","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1505,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SURVIVAL","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2408","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:28:44.507523+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You follow tracks, moving at up to half your travel Speed, using the Travel Speed rules. After a successful check to Track, you can continue following the tracks at half your Speed without attempting additional checks for up to 1 hour.\n\nIn some cases, you might Track in an encounter. In this case, Track is a single action and doesn't have the exploration trait, but you might need to roll more often because you're in a tense situation. The GM determines how often you must attempt this check.\n\nYou attempt your Survival check when you start Tracking, once every hour you continue tracking, and any time something significant changes in the trail. The GM determines the DCs for such checks, depending on the freshness of the trail, the weather, and the type of ground.\n\n**Success** You find the trail or continue to follow the one you're already following.\n\n**Failure** You lose the trail but can try again after a 1-hour delay.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose the trail and can't try again for 24 hours.\n\nSample Track Tasks\n------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** the path of a large army following a road\n    \n*   **Trained** relatively fresh tracks of a rampaging bear through the plains\n    \n*   **Expert** a nimble panther's tracks through a jungle, tracks obscured by rainfall\n    \n*   **Master** tracks obscured by winter snow, tracks of a mouse or smaller creature, tracks left on surfaces that can't hold prints like bare rock\n    \n*   **Legendary** old tracks through a windy desert's sands, tracks obscured by a major blizzard or hurricane","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19861,"cost":null,"name":"Track","type":"action","uuid":"4205562911072053","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,1505,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"SURVIVAL","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2408","book":"Player Core","page":"246"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:28:44.507523+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You follow tracks, moving at up to half your travel Speed, using the Travel Speed rules. After a successful check to Track, you can continue following the tracks at half your Speed without attempting additional checks for up to 1 hour.\n\nIn some cases, you might Track in an encounter. In this case, Track is a single action and doesn't have the exploration trait, but you might need to roll more often because you're in a tense situation. The GM determines how often you must attempt this check.\n\nYou attempt your Survival check when you start Tracking, once every hour you continue tracking, and any time something significant changes in the trail. The GM determines the DCs for such checks, depending on the freshness of the trail, the weather, and the type of ground.\n\n**Success** You find the trail or continue to follow the one you're already following.\n\n**Failure** You lose the trail but can try again after a 1-hour delay.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose the trail and can't try again for 24 hours.\n\nSample Track Tasks\n------------------\n\n*   **Untrained** the path of a large army following a road\n    \n*   **Trained** relatively fresh tracks of a rampaging bear through the plains\n    \n*   **Expert** a nimble panther's tracks through a jungle, tracks obscured by rainfall\n    \n*   **Master** tracks obscured by winter snow, tracks of a mouse or smaller creature, tracks left on surfaces that can't hold prints like bare rock\n    \n*   **Legendary** old tracks through a windy desert's sands, tracks obscured by a major blizzard or hurricane","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19865,"type":"action","before":{"id":19865,"cost":null,"name":"Trip","type":"action","uuid":"3705909069281200","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2382","book":"Player Core","page":"236"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:30:28.045407+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to knock a creature to the ground. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Reflex DC.\n\n**Critical Success** The target falls, lands prone, and takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage.\n\n**Success** The target falls and lands prone.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose your balance, fall, and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one hand free. Your target can't be more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19865,"cost":null,"name":"Trip","type":"action","uuid":"3705909069281200","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ATHLETICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2382","book":"Player Core","page":"236"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:30:28.045407+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You try to knock a creature to the ground. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Reflex DC.\n\n**Critical Success** The target falls, lands prone, and takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage.\n\n**Success** The target falls and lands prone.\n\n**Critical Failure** You lose your balance, fall, and land prone.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have at least one hand free. Your target can't be more than one size larger than you.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19867,"type":"action","before":{"id":19867,"cost":null,"name":"Tumble Through","type":"action","uuid":"2898904612729056","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ACROBATICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2370","book":"Player Core","page":"233"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:31:00.053818+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You Stride up to your Speed. During this movement, you can try to move through the space of one enemy. Attempt an Acrobatics check against the enemy's Reflex DC as soon as you try to enter its space. You can Tumble Through using Climb, Fly, Swim, or another action instead of Stride in the appropriate environment.\n\n**Success** You move through the enemy's space, treating the squares in its space as difficult terrain (every 5 feet costs 10 feet of movement). If you don't have enough Speed to move all the way through its space, you get the same effect as a failure.\n\n**Failure** Your movement ends, and you trigger reactions as if you had moved out of the square you started in.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19867,"cost":null,"name":"Tumble Through","type":"action","uuid":"2898904612729056","level":null,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1505,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"skill":"ACROBATICS","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2370","book":"Player Core","page":"233"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:31:00.053818+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You Stride up to your Speed. During this movement, you can try to move through the space of one enemy. Attempt an Acrobatics check against the enemy's Reflex DC as soon as you try to enter its space. You can Tumble Through using Climb, Fly, Swim, or another action instead of Stride in the appropriate environment.\n\n**Success** You move through the enemy's space, treating the squares in its space as difficult terrain (every 5 feet costs 10 feet of movement). If you don't have enough Speed to move all the way through its space, you get the same effect as a failure.\n\n**Failure** Your movement ends, and you trigger reactions as if you had moved out of the square you started in.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19894,"type":"feat","before":{"id":19894,"cost":null,"name":"Alchemical Crafting","type":"feat","uuid":"875713794774102","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5117","book":"Player Core","page":"252"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:07:40.675984+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You can use the [Craft](link_action_19617) activity to create [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level alchemical items to your [formula book](link_item_6972).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["trained in Crafting"],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":19894,"cost":null,"name":"Alchemical Crafting","type":"feat","uuid":"875713794774102","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5117","book":"Player Core","page":"252"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:07:40.675984+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You can use the [Craft](link_action_19617) activity to create [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level alchemical items to your [formula book](link_item_6972).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["trained in Crafting"],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19908,"type":"feat","before":{"id":19908,"cost":null,"name":"Animal Empathy (Druid)","type":"feat","uuid":"5291244091667893","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1343],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4709","book":"Player Core","page":"127"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:10:20.796814+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You have a connection to the creatures of the natural world that allows you to communicate with them on a rudimentary level. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals. In most cases, wild animals will give you time to make your case.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":19908,"cost":null,"name":"Animal Empathy (Druid)","type":"feat","uuid":"5291244091667893","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1343],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4709","book":"Player Core","page":"127"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:10:20.796814+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You have a connection to the creatures of the natural world that allows you to communicate with them on a rudimentary level. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals. In most cases, wild animals will give you time to make your case.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19945,"type":"feat","before":{"id":19945,"cost":null,"name":"Battle Cry","type":"feat","uuid":"7707387564647235","level":7,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5124","book":"Player Core","page":"252"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"Note","text":"{item|system.description.value}","title":"{item|name}","outcome":[],"selector":"initiative"},{"key":"Note","text":"{item|system.description.value}","title":"{item|name}","outcome":["criticalSuccess"],"selector":"attack","predicate":["skill:itm:rank:4"]}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:17:33.775824+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b3e8876e-b627-4c51-9c46-1bad6ad2134f","data":{"id":19624,"text":"**Battle Cry** When you roll initiative, you can yell a mighty battle cry and Demoralize an observed foe as a free action. If you're legendary in Intimidation, you can use a reaction to Demoralize your foe when you critically succeed at an attack roll.","type":"action"},"type":"injectText"}],"description":"When you roll initiative, you can yell a mighty battle cry and [Demoralize](link_action_19624) an observed foe as a free action. If you're legendary in Intimidation, you can use a reaction to [Demoralize](link_action_19624) your foe when you critically succeed at an attack roll.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["master in Intimidation"],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19945,"cost":null,"name":"Battle Cry","type":"feat","uuid":"7707387564647235","level":7,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5124","book":"Player Core","page":"252"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"Note","text":"{item|system.description.value}","title":"{item|name}","outcome":[],"selector":"initiative"},{"key":"Note","text":"{item|system.description.value}","title":"{item|name}","outcome":["criticalSuccess"],"selector":"attack","predicate":["skill:itm:rank:4"]}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:17:33.775824+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b3e8876e-b627-4c51-9c46-1bad6ad2134f","data":{"id":19624,"text":"**Battle Cry** When you roll initiative, you can yell a mighty battle cry and Demoralize an observed foe as a free action. If you're legendary in Intimidation, you can use a reaction to Demoralize your foe when you critically succeed at an attack roll.","type":"action"},"type":"injectText"}],"description":"When you roll initiative, you can yell a mighty battle cry and [Demoralize](link_action_19624) an observed foe as a free action. If you're legendary in Intimidation, you can use a reaction to [Demoralize](link_action_19624) your foe when you critically succeed at an attack roll.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["master in Intimidation"],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":19946,"type":"feat","before":{"id":19946,"cost":null,"name":"Battle Medicine","type":"feat","uuid":"6504518758038491","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1442,1433,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5125","book":"Player Core","page":"253"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:17:47.720099+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can patch up wounds, even in combat. Attempt a Medicine check with the same DC as for [Treat Wounds](link_action_19864) and restore the corresponding amount of HP; this doesn’t remove the wounded condition. As with [Treat Wounds](link_action_19864), you can attempt checks against higher DCs if you have the minimum proficiency rank. The target is then immune to your Battle Medicine for 1 day. This does not make them immune to, or otherwise count as, [Treat Wounds](link_action_19864).","availability":null,"requirements":"You're holding or wearing a healer's toolkit.","prerequisites":["trained in Medicine"],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":19946,"cost":null,"name":"Battle Medicine","type":"feat","uuid":"6504518758038491","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1442,1433,1438],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5125","book":"Player Core","page":"253"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:17:47.720099+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can patch up wounds, even in combat. Attempt a Medicine check with the same DC as for [Treat Wounds](link_action_19864) and restore the corresponding amount of HP; this doesn’t remove the wounded condition. As with [Treat Wounds](link_action_19864), you can attempt checks against higher DCs if you have the minimum proficiency rank. The target is then immune to your Battle Medicine for 1 day. This does not make them immune to, or otherwise count as, [Treat Wounds](link_action_19864).","availability":null,"requirements":"You're holding or wearing a healer's toolkit.","prerequisites":["trained in Medicine"],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20077,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20077,"cost":null,"name":"Domain Initiate","type":"feat","uuid":"8500877353716213","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1342],"actions":null,"special":"You can select this feat multiple times, selecting a different domain each time and gaining its domain spell.","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4644","book":"Player Core","page":"113"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"ChoiceSet","flag":"domainInitiate","prompt":"PF2E.SpecificRule.Prompt.DeitysDomain","choices":"system.details.deities.domains"}]},"can_select_multiple_times":true},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:48:18.944764+00:00","operations":[{"id":"dcd9ca64-97c7-4f20-90ec-80ac1d3d7375","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":21087},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"3428b811-81f9-4fca-a0d0-a7bf2066d29b","data":{"title":"Select an Initial Domain Spell","modeType":"FILTERED","optionType":"SPELL","optionsFilters":{"id":"0e1eecdd-f5d7-49e8-ac20-e8d9fe33f14b","type":"SPELL","level":{"max":1},"traits":["Domain"],"spellData":{"rank":null,"type":"FOCUS","castingSource":"CLERIC"},"traditions":[]},"optionsPredefined":[]},"type":"select"}],"description":"Your deity bestows a special spell related to their powers. Select one domain—a subject of particular interest to you within your religion—from your deity's list. You gain an initial domain spell for that domain, a spell unique to the domain and not available to other clerics.\n\nDomain spells are a type of focus spell. It costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell, and you start with a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you can regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the [Refocus](link_action_19754) activity to pray to your deity or do service toward their causes.\n\nFocus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up, much like cantrips. Focus spells don't require spell slots, and can't be cast using spell slots. Your focus pool can hold one Focus Point for each focus spell you have, up to 3 points.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20077,"cost":null,"name":"Domain Initiate","type":"feat","uuid":"8500877353716213","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1342],"actions":null,"special":"You can select this feat multiple times, selecting a different domain each time and gaining its domain spell.","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4644","book":"Player Core","page":"113"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"ChoiceSet","flag":"domainInitiate","prompt":"PF2E.SpecificRule.Prompt.DeitysDomain","choices":"system.details.deities.domains"}]},"can_select_multiple_times":true},"created_at":"2023-12-14T01:48:18.944764+00:00","operations":[{"id":"dcd9ca64-97c7-4f20-90ec-80ac1d3d7375","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":21087},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"3428b811-81f9-4fca-a0d0-a7bf2066d29b","data":{"title":"Select an Initial Domain Spell","modeType":"FILTERED","optionType":"SPELL","optionsFilters":{"id":"0e1eecdd-f5d7-49e8-ac20-e8d9fe33f14b","type":"SPELL","level":{"max":1},"traits":["Domain"],"spellData":{"rank":null,"type":"FOCUS","castingSource":"CLERIC"},"traditions":[]},"optionsPredefined":[]},"type":"select"}],"description":"Your deity bestows a special spell related to their powers. Select one domain—a subject of particular interest to you within your religion—from your deity's list. You gain an initial domain spell for that domain, a spell unique to the domain and not available to other clerics.\n\nDomain spells are a type of focus spell. It costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell, and you start with a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you can regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the [Refocus](link_action_19754) activity to pray to your deity or do service toward their causes.\n\nFocus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up, much like cantrips. Focus spells don't require spell slots, and can't be cast using spell slots. Your focus pool can hold one Focus Point for each focus spell you have, up to 3 points.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20136,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20136,"cost":null,"name":"Familiar","type":"feat","uuid":"6591588092432893","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1346],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Pet"}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:04:02.906391+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7854cbd5-5eca-43bf-9756-a3b584c23718","data":{"value":"companions","variable":"PRIMARY_SHEET_TABS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You make a pact with a creature that serves you and assists your spellcasting. You gain a [familiar](link_trait_3843).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20136,"cost":null,"name":"Familiar","type":"feat","uuid":"6591588092432893","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1346],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Pet"}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:04:02.906391+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7854cbd5-5eca-43bf-9756-a3b584c23718","data":{"value":"companions","variable":"PRIMARY_SHEET_TABS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You make a pact with a creature that serves you and assists your spellcasting. You gain a [familiar](link_trait_3843).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20141,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20141,"cost":null,"name":"Fascinating Performance","type":"feat","uuid":"6753781171706528","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5147","book":"Player Core","page":"255"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:05:09.653289+00:00","operations":null,"description":"When you Perform, compare your result to the Will DC of one observer. If you succeed, the target is fascinated by you for 1 round. If the observer is in a situation that demands immediate attention, such as combat, you must critically succeed to fascinate it and the [Perform](link_action_19746) action gains the [incapacitation](link_trait_1481) trait. You must choose which creature you're trying to fascinate before you roll your check, and the target is then temporarily immune for 1 hour.\n\nIf you're an expert in Performance, you can fascinate up to four observers; if you're a master, you can fascinate up to 10 observers; and if you're legendary, you can fascinate any number of observers at the same time.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["trained in Performance"],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20141,"cost":null,"name":"Fascinating Performance","type":"feat","uuid":"6753781171706528","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5147","book":"Player Core","page":"255"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:05:09.653289+00:00","operations":null,"description":"When you Perform, compare your result to the Will DC of one observer. If you succeed, the target is fascinated by you for 1 round. If the observer is in a situation that demands immediate attention, such as combat, you must critically succeed to fascinate it and the [Perform](link_action_19746) action gains the [incapacitation](link_trait_1481) trait. You must choose which creature you're trying to fascinate before you roll your check, and the target is then temporarily immune for 1 hour.\n\nIf you're an expert in Performance, you can fascinate up to four observers; if you're a master, you can fascinate up to 10 observers; and if you're legendary, you can fascinate any number of observers at the same time.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["trained in Performance"],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20206,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20206,"cost":null,"name":"Halfling Weapon Familiarity","type":"feat","uuid":"1736040234981456","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1474],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4459","book":"Player Core","page":"60"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"MartialProficiency","slug":"martial-halfling-weapons","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.MartialProficiency.MartialHalflingWeapons","sameAs":"simple","definition":[{"or":[{"and":["item:trait:halfling","item:category:martial"]},"item:base:shortsword"]}]},{"key":"MartialProficiency","slug":"advanced-halfling-weapons","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.MartialProficiency.AdvancedHalflingWeapons","sameAs":"martial","definition":["item:trait:halfling","item:category:advanced"]},{"key":"CriticalSpecialization","predicate":[{"gte":["self:level",5]},{"or":["item:trait:halfling","item:base:sling","item:base:shortsword"]}]}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:21:25.815568+00:00","operations":[{"id":"9ca2f3bb-6e2b-4e94-aa7d-7be6753a20f2","data":{"value":"1474","variable":"WEAPON_FAMILIARITY"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"8c27f93b-729e-483f-9f87-e0012aef10a2","data":{"value":"sling","variable":"WEAPON_FAMILIARITY"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"03aac770-f493-4dde-b48d-c771c1546d29","data":{"value":"shortsword","variable":"WEAPON_FAMILIARITY"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You favor traditional halfling weapons, so you've learned how to use them more effectively. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the [halfling](link_trait_1474) trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the [halfling](link_trait_1474) trait plus the [sling](link_item_7786) and [shortsword](link_item_7764)—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20206,"cost":null,"name":"Halfling Weapon Familiarity","type":"feat","uuid":"1736040234981456","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1474],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4459","book":"Player Core","page":"60"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"MartialProficiency","slug":"martial-halfling-weapons","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.MartialProficiency.MartialHalflingWeapons","sameAs":"simple","definition":[{"or":[{"and":["item:trait:halfling","item:category:martial"]},"item:base:shortsword"]}]},{"key":"MartialProficiency","slug":"advanced-halfling-weapons","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.MartialProficiency.AdvancedHalflingWeapons","sameAs":"martial","definition":["item:trait:halfling","item:category:advanced"]},{"key":"CriticalSpecialization","predicate":[{"gte":["self:level",5]},{"or":["item:trait:halfling","item:base:sling","item:base:shortsword"]}]}]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:21:25.815568+00:00","operations":[{"id":"9ca2f3bb-6e2b-4e94-aa7d-7be6753a20f2","data":{"value":"1474","variable":"WEAPON_FAMILIARITY"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"8c27f93b-729e-483f-9f87-e0012aef10a2","data":{"value":"sling","variable":"WEAPON_FAMILIARITY"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"03aac770-f493-4dde-b48d-c771c1546d29","data":{"value":"shortsword","variable":"WEAPON_FAMILIARITY"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You favor traditional halfling weapons, so you've learned how to use them more effectively. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the [halfling](link_trait_1474) trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the [halfling](link_trait_1474) trait plus the [sling](link_item_7786) and [shortsword](link_item_7764)—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20319,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20319,"cost":null,"name":"Magical Crafting","type":"feat","uuid":"876262790556551","level":2,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5178","book":"Player Core","page":"258"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:45:33.533498+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can [Craft](link_action_19617) magic items, though some have other requirements. When you select this feat, you gain formulas for four common magic items of 2nd level or lower.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["expert in Crafting"],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20319,"cost":null,"name":"Magical Crafting","type":"feat","uuid":"876262790556551","level":2,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=5178","book":"Player Core","page":"258"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:45:33.533498+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You can [Craft](link_action_19617) magic items, though some have other requirements. When you select this feat, you gain formulas for four common magic items of 2nd level or lower.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":["expert in Crafting"],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20379,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20379,"cost":null,"name":"Orc Ferocity","type":"feat","uuid":"2719532749655939","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1461],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed.","version":"1.0","frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4514","book":"Player Core","page":"72"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:58:15.187583+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Fierceness in battle runs through your blood, and you refuse to fall from your injuries no matter how terrible they may be. You avoid being knocked out and remain at 1 Hit Point, and your wounded condition increases by 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20379,"cost":null,"name":"Orc Ferocity","type":"feat","uuid":"2719532749655939","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1461],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed.","version":"1.0","frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4514","book":"Player Core","page":"72"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T02:58:15.187583+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Fierceness in battle runs through your blood, and you refuse to fall from your injuries no matter how terrible they may be. You avoid being knocked out and remain at 1 Hit Point, and your wounded condition increases by 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20412,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20412,"cost":null,"name":"Plant Empathy","type":"feat","uuid":"6021249750161657","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1343],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4711","book":"Player Core","page":"127"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:06:30.610437+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You have a connection to flora that allows you to communicate with them on a rudimentary level. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with plants and fungus.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20412,"cost":null,"name":"Plant Empathy","type":"feat","uuid":"6021249750161657","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1343],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4711","book":"Player Core","page":"127"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:06:30.610437+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You have a connection to flora that allows you to communicate with them on a rudimentary level. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with plants and fungus.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20441,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20441,"cost":null,"name":"Quick Draw","type":"feat","uuid":"4392539903580209","level":2,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1344,1345],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4869","book":"Player Core","page":"159"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:11:58.625827+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You draw your weapon and attack with the same motion. You [Interact](link_action_19733) to draw a weapon, then [Strike](link_action_19856) with that weapon.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20441,"cost":null,"name":"Quick Draw","type":"feat","uuid":"4392539903580209","level":2,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1344,1345],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4869","book":"Player Core","page":"159"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:11:58.625827+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You draw your weapon and attack with the same motion. You [Interact](link_action_19733) to draw a weapon, then [Strike](link_action_19856) with that weapon.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20534,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20534,"cost":null,"name":"Shield Block","type":"feat","uuid":"4880963151232844","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"While you have your shield raised, you would take physical damage (bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing) from an attack.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:34:10.797344+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You snap your shield in place to ward off a blow. Your shield prevents you from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. You and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20534,"cost":null,"name":"Shield Block","type":"feat","uuid":"4880963151232844","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":"REACTION","special":null,"trigger":"While you have your shield raised, you would take physical damage (bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing) from an attack.","version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:34:10.797344+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You snap your shield in place to ward off a blow. Your shield prevents you from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. You and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20546,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20546,"cost":null,"name":"Skillful Tail","type":"feat","uuid":"6007591741268121","level":5,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1451],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4557","book":"Player Core","page":"80"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:36:30.397004+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You've always had a tail, but with practice, you've learned to use it for more than signaling your mood. You can perform simple [Interact](link_action_19733) actions with your tail, such as opening an unlocked door. Your tail can't perform actions that require fingers or significant manual dexterity, including any action that would require a check to accomplish, and you can't use it to hold items.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20546,"cost":null,"name":"Skillful Tail","type":"feat","uuid":"6007591741268121","level":5,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1451],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4557","book":"Player Core","page":"80"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T03:36:30.397004+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You've always had a tail, but with practice, you've learned to use it for more than signaling your mood. You can perform simple [Interact](link_action_19733) actions with your tail, such as opening an unlocked door. Your tail can't perform actions that require fingers or significant manual dexterity, including any action that would require a check to accomplish, and you can't use it to hold items.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20709,"type":"feat","before":{"id":20709,"cost":null,"name":"Widen Spell","type":"feat","uuid":"6648038279965359","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1343,1433,1465,1347,1346],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4715","book":"Player Core","page":"128"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T04:34:45.808825+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You manipulate the energy of your spell, causing it to spread out and affect a wider area. If the next action you use is to [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) that has an area of a burst, cone, or line and does not have a duration, increase the area of that spell. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius is not affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that is normally 15 feet long or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20709,"cost":null,"name":"Widen Spell","type":"feat","uuid":"6648038279965359","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1343,1433,1465,1347,1346],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4715","book":"Player Core","page":"128"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-14T04:34:45.808825+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You manipulate the energy of your spell, causing it to spread out and affect a wider area. If the next action you use is to [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) that has an area of a burst, cone, or line and does not have a duration, increase the area of that spell. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius is not affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that is normally 15 feet long or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20733,"type":"heritage","before":{"id":20733,"cost":null,"name":"Dromaar","type":"heritage","uuid":"5234135922972659","level":-1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Heritages.aspx?ID=282","book":"Player Core","page":"83"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"Sense","selector":"lowLightVision"},{"add":["orc","dromaar"],"key":"ActorTraits"},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"override","path":"system.details.ancestry.versatile","value":"orc"},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"add","path":"system.details.ancestry.countsAs","value":"dromaar"},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"add","path":"system.details.ancestry.countsAs","value":"orc"}]},"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Dromaar_Mountaineer.webp"},"created_at":"2023-12-14T04:50:13.964281+00:00","operations":[{"id":"4dedf1b0-2515-48ba-9d88-195e68f1e628","data":{"traitId":1512},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"58709993-998e-4885-9390-f708712195d7","data":{"traitId":1461},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"4b1a81f8-4024-4f6d-ab8e-71fb7e9a6531","data":{"type":"sense","abilityBlockId":19330},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"Orcish strength emboldens your bloodline. You have a green tinge to your skin and other indicators of orc heritage. You gain the [orc](link_trait_1461) trait, the [dromaar](link_trait_1512) trait, and [low-light vision](link_sense_19330). When you gain an ancestry feat, you can choose from dromaar and orc feats in addition to those from your ancestry.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":20733,"cost":null,"name":"Dromaar","type":"heritage","uuid":"5234135922972659","level":-1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Heritages.aspx?ID=282","book":"Player Core","page":"83"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"Sense","selector":"lowLightVision"},{"add":["orc","dromaar"],"key":"ActorTraits"},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"override","path":"system.details.ancestry.versatile","value":"orc"},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"add","path":"system.details.ancestry.countsAs","value":"dromaar"},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"add","path":"system.details.ancestry.countsAs","value":"orc"}]},"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Dromaar_Mountaineer.webp"},"created_at":"2023-12-14T04:50:13.964281+00:00","operations":[{"id":"4dedf1b0-2515-48ba-9d88-195e68f1e628","data":{"traitId":1512},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"58709993-998e-4885-9390-f708712195d7","data":{"traitId":1461},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"4b1a81f8-4024-4f6d-ab8e-71fb7e9a6531","data":{"type":"sense","abilityBlockId":19330},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"Orcish strength emboldens your bloodline. You have a green tinge to your skin and other indicators of orc heritage. You gain the [orc](link_trait_1461) trait, the [dromaar](link_trait_1512) trait, and [low-light vision](link_sense_19330). When you gain an ancestry feat, you can choose from dromaar and orc feats in addition to those from your ancestry.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20769,"type":"sense","before":{"id":20769,"cost":"","name":"Darkvision","type":"sense","uuid":"990708369957964","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Familiars.aspx?ID=142","book":"Player Core","page":"259"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-14T23:25:55.882053+00:00","operations":[{"id":"85ad67ec-6db0-407a-a46c-a5477825b724","data":{"value":"darkvision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"A creature with darkvision can see perfectly well in areas of darkness and dim light, though such vision is in black and white only. Some forms of magical darkness, such as a 4th-rank [darkness](link_spell_4552) spell, block normal darkvision.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20769,"cost":"","name":"Darkvision","type":"sense","uuid":"990708369957964","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Familiars.aspx?ID=142","book":"Player Core","page":"259"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-14T23:25:55.882053+00:00","operations":[{"id":"85ad67ec-6db0-407a-a46c-a5477825b724","data":{"value":"darkvision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"A creature with darkvision can see perfectly well in areas of darkness and dim light, though such vision is in black and white only. Some forms of magical darkness, such as a 4th-rank [darkness](link_spell_4552) spell, block normal darkvision.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20772,"type":"sense","before":{"id":20772,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 20 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"6089415867960565","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-15T01:34:10.642971+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7ab72b32-d821-4766-93a8-c224fdc3d40a","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 20","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20772,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 20 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"6089415867960565","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-15T01:34:10.642971+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7ab72b32-d821-4766-93a8-c224fdc3d40a","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 20","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20773,"type":"sense","before":{"id":20773,"cost":"","name":"Scent (imprecise 30 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"987176158247911","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-15T02:59:38.851639+00:00","operations":[{"id":"f5bdde27-0128-4c78-9b0b-052461f323e5","data":{"text":"whenever you’re trying to locate an undetected creature that is within the range of your scent","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"1e04f745-f127-4ff1-a75c-710538bd8c6d","data":{"value":"scent, 30","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can use your sense of smell to determine the location of a creature. The GM will usually double the range if you’re downwind from the creature or halve the range if you’re upwind.\n\nIn addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks whenever you’re trying to locate an undetected creature that is within the range of your scent.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20773,"cost":"","name":"Scent (imprecise 30 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"987176158247911","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2023-12-15T02:59:38.851639+00:00","operations":[{"id":"f5bdde27-0128-4c78-9b0b-052461f323e5","data":{"text":"whenever you’re trying to locate an undetected creature that is within the range of your scent","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"1e04f745-f127-4ff1-a75c-710538bd8c6d","data":{"value":"scent, 30","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can use your sense of smell to determine the location of a creature. The GM will usually double the range if you’re downwind from the creature or halve the range if you’re upwind.\n\nIn addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks whenever you’re trying to locate an undetected creature that is within the range of your scent.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20775,"type":"action","before":{"id":20775,"cost":null,"name":"Invest an Item","type":"action","uuid":"6963090982673237","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2799","book":"GM Core","page":"219"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-17T20:58:50.873666+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You invest your energy in an item with the [invested](link_trait_1527) trait as you don it. This process requires 1 or more [Interact](link_action_19733) actions, usually taking the same amount of time it takes to don the item. Once you’ve Invested the Item, you benefit from its constant [magical](link_trait_1504) abilities as long as you meet its other requirements (for most invested items, the only other requirement is that you must be wearing the item). This investiture lasts until you remove the item.\n\nYou can invest no more than 10 items per day. If you remove an invested item, it loses its investiture. The item still counts against your daily limit after it loses its investiture. You reset the limit during your daily preparations, at which point you Invest your Items anew. If you’re still wearing items you had invested the previous day, you can typically keep them invested on the new day, but they still count against your limit.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20775,"cost":null,"name":"Invest an Item","type":"action","uuid":"6963090982673237","level":1,"access":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437],"actions":null,"special":null,"trigger":null,"version":"1.0","frequency":null,"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2799","book":"GM Core","page":"219"},"foundry":{"rules":[]}},"created_at":"2023-12-17T20:58:50.873666+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You invest your energy in an item with the [invested](link_trait_1527) trait as you don it. This process requires 1 or more [Interact](link_action_19733) actions, usually taking the same amount of time it takes to don the item. Once you’ve Invested the Item, you benefit from its constant [magical](link_trait_1504) abilities as long as you meet its other requirements (for most invested items, the only other requirement is that you must be wearing the item). This investiture lasts until you remove the item.\n\nYou can invest no more than 10 items per day. If you remove an invested item, it loses its investiture. The item still counts against your daily limit after it loses its investiture. You reset the limit during your daily preparations, at which point you Invest your Items anew. If you’re still wearing items you had invested the previous day, you can typically keep them invested on the new day, but they still count against your limit.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":20776,"type":"sense","before":{"id":20776,"cost":"","name":"Normal Vision","type":"sense","uuid":"423202486919968","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-03-23T17:24:22.611991+00:00","operations":[{"id":"1c98e2a2-5228-4d57-bb09-d0c87d3d055a","data":{"value":"normal vision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"In bright light, such as sunlight, you can observe things clearly. However, creatures and objects in areas of dim light have the concealed condition for you and, in darkness, they're hidden or undetected.  \n  \nYou have the blinded condition while in darkness, though you may be able to see illuminated areas beyond the darkness. If you can see into an illuminated area, it can observe creatures within that illuminated area normally. After being in darkness, sudden exposure to bright light might make you dazzled for a short time, as determined by the GM.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":20776,"cost":"","name":"Normal Vision","type":"sense","uuid":"423202486919968","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-03-23T17:24:22.611991+00:00","operations":[{"id":"1c98e2a2-5228-4d57-bb09-d0c87d3d055a","data":{"value":"normal vision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"In bright light, such as sunlight, you can observe things clearly. However, creatures and objects in areas of dim light have the concealed condition for you and, in darkness, they're hidden or undetected.  \n  \nYou have the blinded condition while in darkness, though you may be able to see illuminated areas beyond the darkness. If you can see into an illuminated area, it can observe creatures within that illuminated area normally. After being in darkness, sudden exposure to bright light might make you dazzled for a short time, as determined by the GM.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21077,"type":"sense","before":{"id":21077,"cost":"","name":"Scent (imprecise 20 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"4733528473790085","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T20:33:32.049735+00:00","operations":[{"id":"f5bdde27-0128-4c78