u’re upwind.\n\nIn addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks whenever you’re trying to locate an undetected creature that is within the range of your scent.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21079,"type":"sense","before":{"id":21079,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 30 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"2474907230971847","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T20:35:16.559698+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7ab72b32-d821-4766-93a8-c224fdc3d40a","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 30","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":21079,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 30 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"2474907230971847","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T20:35:16.559698+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7ab72b32-d821-4766-93a8-c224fdc3d40a","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 30","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21080,"type":"sense","before":{"id":21080,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 40 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"654505062377155","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T20:35:34.806374+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7ab72b32-d821-4766-93a8-c224fdc3d40a","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 40","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":21080,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 40 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"654505062377155","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T20:35:34.806374+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7ab72b32-d821-4766-93a8-c224fdc3d40a","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 40","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21081,"type":"sense","before":{"id":21081,"cost":"","name":"Hearing","type":"sense","uuid":"7294419213926000","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T21:29:53.369732+00:00","operations":[{"id":"d093403b-7e30-48b0-865b-d823f756f54c","data":{"value":"hearing","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"Hearing is the ability to perceive sound by detecting vibrations through an organ such as the ear. A creature might be undetected by you if it’s in an environment that distorts the sense, such as a noisy room. In those cases, you have to use the [Seek](link_action_19845) basic action to detect the creature.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":21081,"cost":"","name":"Hearing","type":"sense","uuid":"7294419213926000","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-05T21:29:53.369732+00:00","operations":[{"id":"d093403b-7e30-48b0-865b-d823f756f54c","data":{"value":"hearing","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"Hearing is the ability to perceive sound by detecting vibrations through an organ such as the ear. A creature might be undetected by you if it’s in an environment that distorts the sense, such as a noisy room. In those cases, you have to use the [Seek](link_action_19845) basic action to detect the creature.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21145,"type":"action","before":{"id":21145,"cost":"","name":"Follow the Expert","type":"action","uuid":"779472612461757","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1457,1479],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2625","book":"Player Core","page":"438"}},"created_at":"2024-04-07T01:55:25.338101+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Choose an ally attempting a recurring skill check while exploring, such as climbing, or performing a different [exploration](link_trait_1457) tactic that requires a skill check (like [Avoiding Notice](link_action_21146)). The ally must be at least an expert in that skill and must be willing to provide assistance. While Following the Expert, you match their tactic or attempt similar skill checks.  \nThanks to your ally's assistance, you can add your level as a proficiency bonus to the associated skill check, even if you're untrained. Additionally, you gain a circumstance bonus to your skill check based on your ally's proficiency (+2 for expert, +3 for master, and +4 for legendary).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":21145,"cost":"","name":"Follow the Expert","type":"action","uuid":"779472612461757","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1457,1479],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2625","book":"Player Core","page":"438"}},"created_at":"2024-04-07T01:55:25.338101+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Choose an ally attempting a recurring skill check while exploring, such as climbing, or performing a different [exploration](link_trait_1457) tactic that requires a skill check (like [Avoiding Notice](link_action_21146)). The ally must be at least an expert in that skill and must be willing to provide assistance. While Following the Expert, you match their tactic or attempt similar skill checks.  \nThanks to your ally's assistance, you can add your level as a proficiency bonus to the associated skill check, even if you're untrained. Additionally, you gain a circumstance bonus to your skill check based on your ally's proficiency (+2 for expert, +3 for master, and +4 for legendary).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21146,"type":"action","before":{"id":21146,"cost":"","name":"Avoid Notice","type":"action","uuid":"3428789436847928","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2622","book":"Player Core","page":"438"}},"created_at":"2024-04-07T01:56:13.979282+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You attempt a Stealth check to avoid notice while traveling at half speed. If you're Avoiding Notice at the start of an encounter, you usually roll a Stealth check instead of a Perception check both to determine your initiative and to see if the enemies notice you (based on their Perception DCs, as normal for [Sneak](link_action_19850), regardless of their initiative check results).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":21146,"cost":"","name":"Avoid Notice","type":"action","uuid":"3428789436847928","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1457],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2622","book":"Player Core","page":"438"}},"created_at":"2024-04-07T01:56:13.979282+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You attempt a Stealth check to avoid notice while traveling at half speed. If you're Avoiding Notice at the start of an encounter, you usually roll a Stealth check instead of a Perception check both to determine your initiative and to see if the enemies notice you (based on their Perception DCs, as normal for [Sneak](link_action_19850), regardless of their initiative check results).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":21194,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":21194,"cost":"","name":"Divine Font","type":"class-feature","uuid":"1062104322655385","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1342],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=33","book":"Player Core","page":"108"}},"created_at":"2024-04-13T01:22:08.919292+00:00","operations":[{"id":"39a7d4b6-d78c-4e6d-a3dc-cd260c69d6be","data":{"value":"CLERIC_DIVINE_FONT:::PREPARED-LIST:::DIVINE:::ATTRIBUTE_WIS","variable":"CASTING_SOURCES"},"type":"defineCastingSource"},{"id":"e4b27cea-3a1d-47e4-9002-4b57ceca4088","data":{"title":"Select Divine Font","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"CUSTOM","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"731b2c39-4f6e-4b42-885d-23b26fc82fc2","type":"CUSTOM","title":"Healing Font","operations":[{"id":"01f7ceb2-2a2c-43ee-97b3-7824f05eaa79","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":34054},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You gain 4 additional spell slots each day at your highest rank of cleric spell slots. You can prepare only [_heal_](link_spell_4656) spells in these slots. At 5th level, the number of additional slots increases to 5, and at 15th level, the total number of additional slots increases to 6."},{"id":"a9ee8bed-c215-458e-8a2b-abbfa9bc2c7a","type":"CUSTOM","title":"Harmful Font","operations":[{"id":"de215472-137a-409d-8395-caeadb3ec51a","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":34055},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You gain 4 additional spell slots each day at your highest rank of cleric spell slots. You can prepare only [_harm_](link_spell_4653) spells in these slots. At 5th level, the number of additional slots increases to 5, and at 15th level, the total number of additional slots increases to 6."}]},"type":"select"},{"id":"986d79b5-292d-43f2-92a1-8877ed1e1aa8","data":{"slots":[{"amt":4,"lvl":1,"rank":1},{"amt":4,"lvl":2,"rank":1},{"amt":4,"lvl":3,"rank":2},{"amt":4,"lvl":4,"rank":2},{"amt":5,"lvl":5,"rank":3},{"amt":5,"lvl":6,"rank":3},{"amt":5,"lvl":7,"rank":4},{"amt":5,"lvl":8,"rank":4},{"amt":5,"lvl":9,"rank":5},{"amt":5,"lvl":10,"rank":5},{"amt":5,"lvl":11,"rank":6},{"amt":5,"lvl":12,"rank":6},{"amt":5,"lvl":13,"rank":7},{"amt":5,"lvl":14,"rank":7},{"amt":6,"lvl":15,"rank":8},{"amt":6,"lvl":16,"rank":8},{"amt":6,"lvl":17,"rank":9},{"amt":6,"lvl":18,"rank":9},{"amt":6,"lvl":19,"rank":10},{"amt":6,"lvl":20,"rank":10}],"castingSource":"CLERIC_DIVINE_FONT"},"type":"giveSpellSlot"}],"description":"Through your deity’s blessing, you gain additional spells that channel either the life force called [vitality](link_trait_1478) or its counterforce, the [void](link_trait_1485). When you prepare your spells each day, you can prepare additional [_heal_](link_spell_4656) or [_harm_](link_spell_4653) spells, depending on your deity. The divine font spell your deity provides is listed in the Divine Font entry for your deity on pages 35–39; if both are listed, you can choose between [_heal_](link_spell_4656) or [_harm_](link_spell_4653). Once you choose, you can’t change your choice short of divine intervention.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":21194,"cost":"","name":"Divine Font","type":"class-feature","uuid":"1062104322655385","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1342],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":"1.0","frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=33","book":"Player Core","page":"108"}},"created_at":"2024-04-13T01:22:08.919292+00:00","operations":[{"id":"39a7d4b6-d78c-4e6d-a3dc-cd260c69d6be","data":{"value":"CLERIC_DIVINE_FONT:::PREPARED-LIST:::DIVINE:::ATTRIBUTE_WIS","variable":"CASTING_SOURCES"},"type":"defineCastingSource"},{"id":"e4b27cea-3a1d-47e4-9002-4b57ceca4088","data":{"title":"Select Divine Font","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"CUSTOM","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"731b2c39-4f6e-4b42-885d-23b26fc82fc2","type":"CUSTOM","title":"Healing Font","operations":[{"id":"01f7ceb2-2a2c-43ee-97b3-7824f05eaa79","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":34054},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You gain 4 additional spell slots each day at your highest rank of cleric spell slots. You can prepare only [_heal_](link_spell_4656) spells in these slots. At 5th l