e":"sense","uuid":"8696534592770189","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-20T19:59:07.612585+00:00","operations":[{"id":"1e04f745-f127-4ff1-a75c-710538bd8c6d","data":{"value":"motion sense, 60","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":22887,"type":"feat","before":{"id":22887,"cost":"","name":"Quick Setup","type":"feat","uuid":"1254644713225328","level":7,"access":"","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4085","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"159"}},"created_at":"2024-04-20T20:17:11.556193+00:00","operations":[],"description":"If you reduce the setup time for a batch of [consumables](link_trait_1531) at least 6 levels lower than you to less than 1 day, you can set it up in just 2 hours (allowing you to do so during an adventuring day if you have access to your tools and materials). If you rush the setup of a permanent item at least 6 levels lower than you and reduce the setup time to less than 1 day, you can perform the setup in 4 hours.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["master in Crafting"],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":22887,"cost":"","name":"Quick Setup","type":"feat","uuid":"1254644713225328","level":7,"access":"","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4085","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"159"}},"created_at":"2024-04-20T20:17:11.556193+00:00","operations":[],"description":"If you reduce the setup time for a batch of [consumables](link_trait_1531) at least 6 levels lower than you to less than 1 day, you can set it up in just 2 hours (allowing you to do so during an adventuring day if you have access to your tools and materials). If you rush the setup of a permanent item at least 6 levels lower than you and reduce the setup time to less than 1 day, you can perform the setup in 4 hours.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["master in Crafting"],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":23655,"type":"heritage","before":{"id":23655,"cost":"","name":"Draxie","type":"heritage","uuid":"8620077481020255","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3042],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Heritages.aspx?ID=140","book":"Ancestry Guide","page":"129"}},"created_at":"2024-04-25T23:29:56.289966+00:00","operations":[{"id":"6bb2c13c-fdb6-4738-9ac7-d6747ce5681e","data":{"type":"physical-feature","abilityBlockId":23656},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You are kin to faerie dragons, tracing your heritage back to the death of the mightiest faerie dragon in the First World. You gain touch telepathy, allowing you to communicate silently and purely mentally with any creature you're touching, as long as you share a language.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":18},"after":{"id":23655,"cost":"","name":"Draxie","type":"heritage","uuid":"8620077481020255","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3042],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Heritages.aspx?ID=140","book":"Ancestry Guide","page":"129"}},"created_at":"2024-04-25T23:29:56.289966+00:00","operations":[{"id":"6bb2c13c-fdb6-4738-9ac7-d6747ce5681e","data":{"type":"physical-feature","abilityBlockId":23656},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You are kin to faerie dragons, tracing your heritage back to the death of the mightiest faerie dragon in the First World. You gain touch telepathy, allowing you to communicate silently and purely mentally with any creature you're touching, as long as you share a language.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":18},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":24727,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":24727,"cost":"","name":"Psi Cantrips and Amps","type":"class-feature","uuid":"7369075130610236","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2951],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=21","book":"Dark Archive","page":"8"}},"created_at":"2024-04-29T02:55:57.811456+00:00","operations":[{"id":"007c55e7-3779-43fa-b395-da18cfe1bce8","data":{"value":2,"variable":"FOCUS_POINT_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"The magic of your mind manifests as psi cantrips, which you can modify by spending Focus Points. Like other cantrips, you can cast psi cantrips as often as you like, and they are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up. Your psi cantrips are in addition to the cantrips you choose from the occult list as part of your psychic spellcasting. Generally, only feats can give you more psi cantrips. Unlike other cantrips, you can't swap out psi cantrips gained from psychic feats at a later level, unless you swap out the specific feat via retraining.\n\nAt 1st level, you learn three psi cantrips determined by your choice of conscious mind; one is a unique psi cantrip and two are common cantrips, typically from the occult spellcasting tradition, that you always cast as psi cantrips. You automatically gain more psi cantrips as you progress in your career as a psychic.\n\nYou start with a focus pool of 2 Focus Points. However, unlike other spellcasters, you don't gain focus spells that cost Focus Points to cast. Instead, you use your Focus Points to boost or modify your psi cantrips by applying amps—specialized thoughtforms that alter the expression of your psychic power. Each of your psi cantrips has a special amp heading. Whenever you cast a psi cantrip, you can amp it by spending 1 Focus Point as a free action. If the next action you take is to cast the psi cantrip, you add the amp effect. If the spell is a reaction or triggered free action, instead spend the Focus Point as part of that action to add the amped effect. You can also gain additional amps through feats, allowing you to substitute a psi cantrip's normal amp effect for another one. You choose which amp to use, if you choose to use any, each time you cast a psi cantrip. Unless otherwise noted, you can apply only one amp to a given psi cantrip.\n\nYou refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you can regain Focus Points by spending 10 minutes using the Refocus activity to explore your mind, whether via meditation, practicing a craft or activity that gives you the mental space to self-reflect, or talking through your thoughts and feelings with yourself or another. If you’ve spent Focus Points only to amp psi cantrips or fuel psychic abilities since the last time you Refocused, you regain 2 Focus Points instead of 1. If you've spent Focus Points on focus spells or abilities other than those from the psychic class (for instance, to cast a focus spell you gained from an archetype), you regain only 1 Focus Point.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":12},"after":{"id":24727,"cost":"","name":"Psi Cantrips and Amps","type":"class-feature","uuid":"7369075130610236","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2951],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=21","book":"Dark Archive","page":"8"}},"created_at":"2024-04-29T02:55:57.811456+00:00","operations":[{"id":"007c55e7-3779-43fa-b395-da18cfe1bce8","data":{"value":2,"variable":"FOCUS_POINT_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"The magic of your mind manifests as psi cantrips, which you can modify by spending Focus Points. Like other cantrips, you can cast psi cantrips as often as you like, and they are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up. Your psi cantrips are in addition to the cantrips you choose from the occult list as part of your psychic spellcasting. Generally, only feats can give you more psi cantrips. Unlike other cantrips, you can't swap out psi cantrips gained from psychic feats at a later level, unless you swap out the specific feat via retraining.\n\nAt 1st level, you learn three psi cantrips determined by your choice of conscious mind; one is a unique psi cantrip and two are common cantrips, typically from the occult spellcasting tradition, that you always cast as psi cantrips. You automatically gain more psi cantrips as you progress in your career as a psychic.\n\nYou start with a focus pool of 2 Focus Points. However, unlike other spellcasters, you don't gain focus spells that cost Focus Points to cast. Instead, you use your Focus Points to boost or modify your psi cantrips by applying amps—specialized thoughtforms that alter the expression of your psychic power. Each of your psi cantrips has a special amp heading. Whenever you cast a psi cantrip, you can amp it by spending 1 Focus Point as a free action. If the next action you take is to cast the psi cantrip, you add the amp effect. If the spell is a reaction or triggered free action, instead spend the Focus Point as part of that action to add the amped effect. You can also gain additional amps through feats, allowing you to substitute a psi cantrip's normal amp effect for another one. You choose which amp to use, if you choose to use any, each time you cast a psi cantrip. Unless otherwise noted, you can apply only one amp to a given psi cantrip.\n\nYou refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you can regain Focus Points by spending 10 minutes using the Refocus activity to explore your mind, whether via meditation, practicing a craft or activity that gives you the mental space to self-reflect, or talking through your thoughts and feelings with yourself or another. If you’ve spent Focus Points only to amp psi cantrips or fuel psychic abilities since the last time you Refocused, you regain 2 Focus Points instead of 1. If you've spent Focus Points on focus spells or abilities other than those from the psychic class (for instance, to cast a focus spell you gained from an archetype), you regain only 1 Focus Point.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":12},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":24796,"type":"feat","before":{"id":24796,"cost":"","name":"Expert Spellcasting","type":"feat","uuid":"6098741549104665","level":12,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-29T03:07:53.194763+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Typically taken at 12th level, these feats make you an expert in spell attack modifiers and spell DCs and grant you a 4th-rank spell slot. If you have a spell repertoire, you can select a second spell from your repertoire as a signature spell. At 14th level, they grant you a 5th-rank spell slot, and at 16th level, they grant you a 6th-rank spell slot. Archetypes refer to these benefits as the “expert spellcasting benefits.”","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":24796,"cost":"","name":"Expert Spellcasting","type":"feat","uuid":"6098741549104665","level":12,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-04-29T03:07:53.194763+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Typically taken at 12th level, these feats make you an expert in spell attack modifiers and spell DCs and grant you a 4th-rank spell slot. If you have a spell repertoire, you can select a second spell from your repertoire as a signature spell. At 14th level, they grant you a 5th-rank spell slot, and at 16th level, they grant you a 6th-rank spell slot. Archetypes refer to these benefits as the “expert spellcasting benefits.”","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":25595,"type":"feat","before":{"id":25595,"cost":"","name":"Spellstrike","type":"feat","uuid":"639662204617111","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2940],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"until recharged (see below)","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-05-04T08:10:28.409393+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You channel a spell into a punch or sword thrust to deliver a combined attack. You cast a spell that takes 1 or 2 actions to cast and requires either a spell attack roll or a saving throw. You imbue its effects into an attack instead of executing the spell normally. Make a melee [Strike](link_action_19856) with a weapon or unarmed attack. This counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty, but you don’t apply the penalty until after you’ve completed the Spellstrike. The infusion of spell energy grants your [Strike](link_action_19856) the [arcane](link_trait_1459) trait, making it [magical](link_trait_1504). If the spell required a spell attack roll, use your [Strike's](link_action_19856) results to determine the effects of both the [Strike](link_action_19856) and the spell. If the spell required a save, the target of the [Strike](link_action_19856) rolls its saving throw normally regardless of your attack roll’s result unless your [Strike](link_action_19856) was a critical failure, in which case your spell is disrupted. Combine the [Strike](link_action_19856) and spell’s damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses.\n\nAfter you use Spellstrike, you can’t do so again until you recharge your Spellstrike as a single action, which has the [concentrate](link_trait_1432) trait. You also recharge your Spellstrike when you cast a [conflux spell](link_class-feature_25596) that takes at least 1 action to cast; casting a focus spell of another type doesn’t recharge your Spellstrike.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":842},"after":{"id":25595,"cost":"","name":"Spellstrike","type":"feat","uuid":"639662204617111","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2940],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"until recharged (see below)","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-05-04T08:10:28.409393+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You channel a spell into a punch or sword thrust to deliver a combined attack. You cast a spell that takes 1 or 2 actions to cast and requires either a spell attack roll or a saving throw. You imbue its effects into an attack instead of executing the spell normally. Make a melee [Strike](link_action_19856) with a weapon or unarmed attack. This counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty, but you don’t apply the penalty until after you’ve completed the Spellstrike. The infusion of spell energy grants your [Strike](link_action_19856) the [arcane](link_trait_1459) trait, making it [magical](link_trait_1504). If the spell required a spell attack roll, use your [Strike's](link_action_19856) results to determine the effects of both the [Strike](link_action_19856) and the spell. If the spell required a save, the target of the [Strike](link_action_19856) rolls its saving throw normally regardless of your attack roll’s result unless your [Strike](link_action_19856) was a critical failure, in which case your spell is disrupted. Combine the [Strike](link_action_19856) and spell’s damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses.\n\nAfter you use Spellstrike, you can’t do so again until you recharge your Spellstrike as a single action, which has the [concentrate](link_trait_1432) trait. You also recharge your Spellstrike when you cast a [conflux spell](link_class-feature_25596) that takes at least 1 action to cast; casting a focus spell of another type doesn’t recharge your Spellstrike.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":842},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":25718,"type":"feat","before":{"id":25718,"cost":"","name":"Firework Technician Dedication","type":"feat","uuid":"7101724702598066","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1445,3298],"actions":null,"special":"You can't select another dedication feat until you've gained two other feats from the fireworks technician archetype.","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=8750","book":"Guns & Gears","page":"134"}},"created_at":"2024-05-06T10:22:57.511771+00:00","operations":[{"id":"24a73c87-5ec4-4893-a168-1f6668b8c21e","data":{"type":"prof","value":{"value":"U","attribute":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"variable":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS"},"type":"createValue"},{"id":"6129bbf2-0629-4bb9-a239-4c45e11b3624","data":{"conditions":[{"id":"12161a1a-10b4-4295-a019-82bba8006160","data":{"name":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS","type":"prof","value":{"value":"U","attribute":"ATTRIBUTE_INT","increases":0}},"name":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS","type":"prof","value":"T","operator":"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"42179b35-6894-4838-8361-92a4dee955ea","data":{"value":{"value":"E"},"variable":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"falseOperations":[{"id":"05480432-48ac-491d-97ab-b55766bb8fe8","data":{"value":{"value":"E"},"variable":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS"},"type":"adjValue"}]},"type":"conditional"},{"id":"609e13f2-8390-4fe8-86cd-1c0a97193e54","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":33683},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"ce6323f3-bb77-4054-9ed5-8500b092db85","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":25719},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"4b15f1a7-14fb-4b80-8303-469540b05568","data":{"itemId":22504},"type":"giveItem"}],"description":"You’ve learned the secrets of making fire and sound bloom using black powder, metals, and paper. You most likely came by this knowledge through formal training with a fireworks house in Tian Xia or a fireworks company from Vudra, though perhaps you mastered fireworks completely by yourself after finding a secret stash in an old shipwreck.\n\nYou become trained in Fireworks Lore or become an expert if you were already trained in it. You gain the [Quick Alchemy benefits](link_feat_33683), creating up to 4 [pyrotechnic versatile vials](link_item_22504) during your daily preparations. These vials have the [fire](link_trait_1542) trait and deal [fire](link_trait_1542) damage instead of [acid](link_trait_1528). You can use [pyrotechnic versatile vials](link_item_22504) only to throw as [bombs](link_trait_1530), for the [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719) action**,** or with [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) to create fireworks consumables, including doses or rounds of [black powder](link_item_13495), the [sparkler](link_item_12438) item, and other items determined by the GM. You can replenish your pyrotechnic versatile vials during exploration the same way an alchemist can.\n\nYou can create fireworks displays to have distinctive effects you can use to make onlookers marvel and even to gain an advantage in combat. You gain the [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719) action and learn some basic effects. You can learn additional, more complex displays through other firework technician feats. These add a new fireworks display to your options for [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719), each of which lists its number of actions and effects. The DC for [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719) is equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["trained in Crafting"],"content_source_id":17},"after":{"id":25718,"cost":"","name":"Firework Technician Dedication","type":"feat","uuid":"7101724702598066","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1445,3298],"actions":null,"special":"You can't select another dedication feat until you've gained two other feats from the fireworks technician archetype.","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=8750","book":"Guns & Gears","page":"134"}},"created_at":"2024-05-06T10:22:57.511771+00:00","operations":[{"id":"24a73c87-5ec4-4893-a168-1f6668b8c21e","data":{"type":"prof","value":{"value":"U","attribute":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"variable":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS"},"type":"createValue"},{"id":"6129bbf2-0629-4bb9-a239-4c45e11b3624","data":{"conditions":[{"id":"12161a1a-10b4-4295-a019-82bba8006160","data":{"name":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS","type":"prof","value":{"value":"U","attribute":"ATTRIBUTE_INT","increases":0}},"name":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS","type":"prof","value":"T","operator":"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"42179b35-6894-4838-8361-92a4dee955ea","data":{"value":{"value":"E"},"variable":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"falseOperations":[{"id":"05480432-48ac-491d-97ab-b55766bb8fe8","data":{"value":{"value":"E"},"variable":"SKILL_LORE_FIREWORKS"},"type":"adjValue"}]},"type":"conditional"},{"id":"609e13f2-8390-4fe8-86cd-1c0a97193e54","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":33683},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"ce6323f3-bb77-4054-9ed5-8500b092db85","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":25719},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"4b15f1a7-14fb-4b80-8303-469540b05568","data":{"itemId":22504},"type":"giveItem"}],"description":"You’ve learned the secrets of making fire and sound bloom using black powder, metals, and paper. You most likely came by this knowledge through formal training with a fireworks house in Tian Xia or a fireworks company from Vudra, though perhaps you mastered fireworks completely by yourself after finding a secret stash in an old shipwreck.\n\nYou become trained in Fireworks Lore or become an expert if you were already trained in it. You gain the [Quick Alchemy benefits](link_feat_33683), creating up to 4 [pyrotechnic versatile vials](link_item_22504) during your daily preparations. These vials have the [fire](link_trait_1542) trait and deal [fire](link_trait_1542) damage instead of [acid](link_trait_1528). You can use [pyrotechnic versatile vials](link_item_22504) only to throw as [bombs](link_trait_1530), for the [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719) action**,** or with [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) to create fireworks consumables, including doses or rounds of [black powder](link_item_13495), the [sparkler](link_item_12438) item, and other items determined by the GM. You can replenish your pyrotechnic versatile vials during exploration the same way an alchemist can.\n\nYou can create fireworks displays to have distinctive effects you can use to make onlookers marvel and even to gain an advantage in combat. You gain the [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719) action and learn some basic effects. You can learn additional, more complex displays through other firework technician feats. These add a new fireworks display to your options for [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719), each of which lists its number of actions and effects. The DC for [Launch Fireworks](link_feat_25719) is equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["trained in Crafting"],"content_source_id":17},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":25723,"type":"feat","before":{"id":25723,"cost":"","name":"First Frost","type":"feat","uuid":"1886338270451949","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3295],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4096","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"185"}},"created_at":"2024-05-06T10:29:17.657994+00:00","operations":[{"id":"37fc7e3e-146e-4cb6-8fc0-315a1c3ebb3f","data":{"value":"GELID_SHARD:::SPONTANEOUS-REPERTOIRE:::ARCANE:::ATTRIBUTE_CHA","variable":"CASTING_SOURCES"},"type":"defineCastingSource"},{"id":"12e6d71a-540f-49db-a115-7f78a22677b5","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SPELL_ATTACK"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9e91ce4f-0139-4413-93c2-929a69222747","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SPELL_DC"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9cb8046c-4292-4be4-97d4-bec99edc52e1","data":{"rank":0,"type":"NORMAL","spellId":4636,"castingSource":"GELID_SHARD"},"type":"giveSpell"},{"id":"a623f17c-6486-4646-a5f2-9585fd3d2df0","data":{"rank":0,"type":"NORMAL","spellId":5829,"castingSource":"GELID_SHARD"},"type":"giveSpell"}],"description":"The [_gelid shard_](link_item_12041) within your heart may sap your ability to feel and experience emotion, but it also lets you create and manipulate cold. You learn to cast spontaneous spells and gain the [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) activity. You gain a spell repertoire with the [_frost's touch_](link_spell_5829) and [_frostbite_](link_spell_4636) [cantrips](link_trait_1858). You're trained in spell attack rolls and spell DCs for [arcane](link_trait_1459) spells. Your key spellcasting ability is Charisma.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["Gelid Shard Dedication"],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":25723,"cost":"","name":"First Frost","type":"feat","uuid":"1886338270451949","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3295],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4096","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"185"}},"created_at":"2024-05-06T10:29:17.657994+00:00","operations":[{"id":"37fc7e3e-146e-4cb6-8fc0-315a1c3ebb3f","data":{"value":"GELID_SHARD:::SPONTANEOUS-REPERTOIRE:::ARCANE:::ATTRIBUTE_CHA","variable":"CASTING_SOURCES"},"type":"defineCastingSource"},{"id":"12e6d71a-540f-49db-a115-7f78a22677b5","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SPELL_ATTACK"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9e91ce4f-0139-4413-93c2-929a69222747","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SPELL_DC"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9cb8046c-4292-4be4-97d4-bec99edc52e1","data":{"rank":0,"type":"NORMAL","spellId":4636,"castingSource":"GELID_SHARD"},"type":"giveSpell"},{"id":"a623f17c-6486-4646-a5f2-9585fd3d2df0","data":{"rank":0,"type":"NORMAL","spellId":5829,"castingSource":"GELID_SHARD"},"type":"giveSpell"}],"description":"The [_gelid shard_](link_item_12041) within your heart may sap your ability to feel and experience emotion, but it also lets you create and manipulate cold. You learn to cast spontaneous spells and gain the [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) activity. You gain a spell repertoire with the [_frost's touch_](link_spell_5829) and [_frostbite_](link_spell_4636) [cantrips](link_trait_1858). You're trained in spell attack rolls and spell DCs for [arcane](link_trait_1459) spells. Your key spellcasting ability is Charisma.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["Gelid Shard Dedication"],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":26030,"type":"feat","before":{"id":26030,"cost":"","name":"Ursine Avenger Form","type":"feat","uuid":"1788057276209300","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"UNIQUE","traits":[1568,1456,1454,1445,3351],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4086","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"183"}},"created_at":"2024-05-08T21:51:42.376651+00:00","operations":[{"id":"88233209-3b95-4aed-8497-fe1809421b8a","data":{"itemId":13667},"type":"giveItem"},{"id":"fd429a17-7805-4ecf-8db5-2e09a112dbe8","data":{"itemId":13666},"type":"giveItem"}],"description":"You draw the [_Ursine Avenger Hood_](link_item_12573) over your head and its fur over your arms, assuming an ursine form that has traits of your original form as well as that of a bear. In your ursine form, you gain a jaws [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack that deals 1d8 piercing damage and a claws [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack that deals 1d6 slashing damage and has the [agile](link_trait_1569) trait. Both [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks are in the brawling group. You lose the ability to speak complex sentences while transformed and can only communicate through grunts and gestures; this prevents you from using effects that require a shared or spoken language until you revert back to your non-hybrid form. You can use this action while transformed to remove the hood and return to your original form.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":26030,"cost":"","name":"Ursine Avenger Form","type":"feat","uuid":"1788057276209300","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"UNIQUE","traits":[1568,1456,1454,1445,3351],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=4086","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"183"}},"created_at":"2024-05-08T21:51:42.376651+00:00","operations":[{"id":"88233209-3b95-4aed-8497-fe1809421b8a","data":{"itemId":13667},"type":"giveItem"},{"id":"fd429a17-7805-4ecf-8db5-2e09a112dbe8","data":{"itemId":13666},"type":"giveItem"}],"description":"You draw the [_Ursine Avenger Hood_](link_item_12573) over your head and its fur over your arms, assuming an ursine form that has traits of your original form as well as that of a bear. In your ursine form, you gain a jaws [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack that deals 1d8 piercing damage and a claws [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack that deals 1d6 slashing damage and has the [agile](link_trait_1569) trait. Both [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks are in the brawling group. You lose the ability to speak complex sentences while transformed and can only communicate through grunts and gestures; this prevents you from using effects that require a shared or spoken language until you revert back to your non-hybrid form. You can use this action while transformed to remove the hood and return to your original form.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":26840,"type":"heritage","before":{"id":26840,"cost":"","name":"Tailed Goblin","type":"heritage","uuid":"6194771115227859","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1468],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Heritages.aspx?ID=37","book":"Character Guide","page":"37"}},"created_at":"2024-05-13T17:12:56.178229+00:00","operations":[{"id":"06f3c4fd-f67f-4adb-9cc1-5e7e27842095","data":{"text":"bonus to Climb.","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"43d0ab23-310d-43d9-a386-33da050c14ec","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":20007},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You have a powerful tail, likely because you descend from a community of monkey goblins. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to [Climb](link_action_19612), you gain [Combat Climber](link_feat_20007) as a bonus feat, and you reduce the number of free hands required to [Climb](link_action_19612) or [Trip](link_action_19865) by one.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":19},"after":{"id":26840,"cost":"","name":"Tailed Goblin","type":"heritage","uuid":"6194771115227859","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1468],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Heritages.aspx?ID=37","book":"Character Guide","page":"37"}},"created_at":"2024-05-13T17:12:56.178229+00:00","operations":[{"id":"06f3c4fd-f67f-4adb-9cc1-5e7e27842095","data":{"text":"bonus to Climb.","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"43d0ab23-310d-43d9-a386-33da050c14ec","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":20007},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You have a powerful tail, likely because you descend from a community of monkey goblins. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to [Climb](link_action_19612), you gain [Combat Climber](link_feat_20007) as a bonus feat, and you reduce the number of free hands required to [Climb](link_action_19612) or [Trip](link_action_19865) by one.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":19},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":27032,"type":"feat","before":{"id":27032,"cost":"","name":"Tattoo Artist","type":"feat","uuid":"4821147126115202","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=2962","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"118"}},"created_at":"2024-05-14T18:54:17.403603+00:00","operations":[{"id":"2821ca0f-1ef1-430c-8297-ebabcca217f3","data":{"conditions":[{"id":"699bb13d-0503-4808-916d-ab3f7ed6ab33","data":{"name":"SKILL_CRAFTING","type":"prof","value":{"value":"U","attribute":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"}},"name":"SKILL_CRAFTING","type":"prof","value":"M","operator":"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"c8e7feba-b885-48fe-8293-ad0c71a945e2","data":{"text":"to craft tattoos","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_CRAFTING"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"falseOperations":[{"id":"dcadbc58-408a-4999-a458-81c5ea5e2a6b","data":{"text":"to craft tattoos","type":"circumstance","value":1,"variable":"SKILL_CRAFTING"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}]},"type":"conditional"}],"description":"You can [craft](link_action_19617) tattoos, including [magical tattoos](link_trait_2857). When you select this feat, you gain the formulas for four common [magical tattoos](link_trait_2857) of 2nd level or lower. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to [Craft](link_action_19617) tattoos. If you're a master in Crafting, this bonus increases to +2 and you gain the formulas for four common [magical tattoos](link_trait_2857) of 7th level or lower.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["trained in Crafting"],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":27032,"cost":"","name":"Tattoo Artist","type":"feat","uuid":"4821147126115202","level":2,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1437,1438],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=2962","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"118"}},"created_at":"2024-05-14T18:54:17.403603+00:00","operations":[{"id":"2821ca0f-1ef1-430c-8297-ebabcca217f3","data":{"conditions":[{"id":"699bb13d-0503-4808-916d-ab3f7ed6ab33","data":{"name":"SKILL_CRAFTING","type":"prof","value":{"value":"U","attribute":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"}},"name":"SKILL_CRAFTING","type":"prof","value":"M","operator":"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"c8e7feba-b885-48fe-8293-ad0c71a945e2","data":{"text":"to craft tattoos","type":"circumstance","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_CRAFTING"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"falseOperations":[{"id":"dcadbc58-408a-4999-a458-81c5ea5e2a6b","data":{"text":"to craft tattoos","type":"circumstance","value":1,"variable":"SKILL_CRAFTING"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}]},"type":"conditional"}],"description":"You can [craft](link_action_19617) tattoos, including [magical tattoos](link_trait_2857). When you select this feat, you gain the formulas for four common [magical tattoos](link_trait_2857) of 2nd level or lower. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to [Craft](link_action_19617) tattoos. If you're a master in Crafting, this bonus increases to +2 and you gain the formulas for four common [magical tattoos](link_trait_2857) of 7th level or lower.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["trained in Crafting"],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":27438,"type":"physical-feature","before":{"id":27438,"cost":"","name":"Void Healing","type":"physical-feature","uuid":"1660634238027964","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-05-19T18:12:28.016264+00:00","operations":[],"description":"A creature with [void](link_trait_1485) healing draws health from [void](link_trait_1485) energy rather than [vitality](link_trait_1478) energy. It is damaged by [vitality](link_trait_1478) damage and is not healed by [vitality](link_trait_1478) healing effects. It does not take [void](link_trait_1485) damage, and it is healed by [void](link_trait_1485) effects that heal [undead](link_trait_2425).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":27438,"cost":"","name":"Void Healing","type":"physical-feature","uuid":"1660634238027964","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-05-19T18:12:28.016264+00:00","operations":[],"description":"A creature with [void](link_trait_1485) healing draws health from [void](link_trait_1485) energy rather than [vitality](link_trait_1478) energy. It is damaged by [vitality](link_trait_1478) damage and is not healed by [vitality](link_trait_1478) healing effects. It does not take [void](link_trait_1485) damage, and it is healed by [void](link_trait_1485) effects that heal [undead](link_trait_2425).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":27519,"type":"action","before":{"id":27519,"cost":"","name":"Counteract","type":"action","uuid":"5801842492515756","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-05-21T17:05:26.731011+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Some effects try to counteract spells, afflictions, conditions, or other effects. Counteract checks compare the power of two forces and determine which defeats the other. Successfully counteracting an effect disrupts it, preventing it from having any effect, unless noted otherwise.\n\nWhen attempting a counteract check, add the relevant skill modifier or other appropriate modifier to your check against the target's DC. If you're counteracting an affliction, the DC is in the affliction's stat block. If it's a spell, use the caster's DC. The GM can also calculate a DC based on the target effect's level. For spells, the counteract check modifier is your spellcasting attribute modifier plus your spellcasting proficiency bonus, plus any bonuses and penalties that specifically apply to counteract checks.\n\nWhat you can counteract depends on the check result and the target's counteract rank. If an effect is a spell, its rank is the counteract rank. Otherwise, halve its level and round up to determine its counteract rank (minimum counteract rank 0). If an effect's level is unclear and it came from a creature, halve and round up the creature's level.\n\n**Critical Success** Counteract the target if its counteract rank is no more than 3 higher than your effect's counteract rank.\n\n**Success** Counteract the target if its counteract rank is no more than 1 higher than your effect's counteract rank.\n\n**Failure** Counteract the target if its counteract rank is lower than your effect's counteract rank.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fail to counteract the target.\n\n**Counteract Table**\n\nThis table provides a reference for what an effect can counteract based on its rank and the check result. The first number in each column is the counteract rank at which you can counteract an effect based on your degree of success. The numbers in parentheses are the typical level range corresponding to that rank.\n\n**Counteract**\n\n| Counteract Rank | Failure | Success | Critical Success |\n\n|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|\n\n| 0 | - | 1 ( 1 to 2) | 3 (5 to 6)|\n\n| 1 | 0 (-1 to 0) | 2 (3 to 4) | 4 (7 to 8)|\n\n| 2 | 1 (1 to 2) | 3 (5 to 6) | 5 (9 to 10)|\n\n| 3 | 2 (2 to 4) | 4 (7 to 8) | 6 (11 to 12)|\n\n| 4 | 3 (3 to 6) | 5 (9 to 10) | 7 (13 to 14)|\n\n| 5 | 4 (4 to 8) | 6 (11 to 12) | 8 (15 to 16)|\n\n| 6 | 5 (5 to 10) | 7 (13 to 14) | 9 (17 to 18)|\n\n| 7 | 6 (6 to 12) | 8 (15 to 16) | 10 (19 to 20)|\n\n| 8 | 7 (7 to 14) | 9 (17 to 18) | 11 (21 to 22)|\n\n| 9 | 8 (8 to 16) | 10 (19 to 20) | 12 (23 to 24)|\n\n| 10 | 9 (9 to 18) | 11 (21 to 22) | 13 (25 to 26)|","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":27519,"cost":"","name":"Counteract","type":"action","uuid":"5801842492515756","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-05-21T17:05:26.731011+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Some effects try to counteract spells, afflictions, conditions, or other effects. Counteract checks compare the power of two forces and determine which defeats the other. Successfully counteracting an effect disrupts it, preventing it from having any effect, unless noted otherwise.\n\nWhen attempting a counteract check, add the relevant skill modifier or other appropriate modifier to your check against the target's DC. If you're counteracting an affliction, the DC is in the affliction's stat block. If it's a spell, use the caster's DC. The GM can also calculate a DC based on the target effect's level. For spells, the counteract check modifier is your spellcasting attribute modifier plus your spellcasting proficiency bonus, plus any bonuses and penalties that specifically apply to counteract checks.\n\nWhat you can counteract depends on the check result and the target's counteract rank. If an effect is a spell, its rank is the counteract rank. Otherwise, halve its level and round up to determine its counteract rank (minimum counteract rank 0). If an effect's level is unclear and it came from a creature, halve and round up the creature's level.\n\n**Critical Success** Counteract the target if its counteract rank is no more than 3 higher than your effect's counteract rank.\n\n**Success** Counteract the target if its counteract rank is no more than 1 higher than your effect's counteract rank.\n\n**Failure** Counteract the target if its counteract rank is lower than your effect's counteract rank.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fail to counteract the target.\n\n**Counteract Table**\n\nThis table provides a reference for what an effect can counteract based on its rank and the check result. The first number in each column is the counteract rank at which you can counteract an effect based on your degree of success. The numbers in parentheses are the typical level range corresponding to that rank.\n\n**Counteract**\n\n| Counteract Rank | Failure | Success | Critical Success |\n\n|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:|\n\n| 0 | - | 1 ( 1 to 2) | 3 (5 to 6)|\n\n| 1 | 0 (-1 to 0) | 2 (3 to 4) | 4 (7 to 8)|\n\n| 2 | 1 (1 to 2) | 3 (5 to 6) | 5 (9 to 10)|\n\n| 3 | 2 (2 to 4) | 4 (7 to 8) | 6 (11 to 12)|\n\n| 4 | 3 (3 to 6) | 5 (9 to 10) | 7 (13 to 14)|\n\n| 5 | 4 (4 to 8) | 6 (11 to 12) | 8 (15 to 16)|\n\n| 6 | 5 (5 to 10) | 7 (13 to 14) | 9 (17 to 18)|\n\n| 7 | 6 (6 to 12) | 8 (15 to 16) | 10 (19 to 20)|\n\n| 8 | 7 (7 to 14) | 9 (17 to 18) | 11 (21 to 22)|\n\n| 9 | 8 (8 to 16) | 10 (19 to 20) | 12 (23 to 24)|\n\n| 10 | 9 (9 to 18) | 11 (21 to 22) | 13 (25 to 26)|","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":28849,"type":"feat","before":{"id":28849,"cost":"","name":"Fascinating","ty