ata":{"conditions":[{"id":"fb08625f-0678-4fcb-9325-8213f3ec0a27","data":{"name":"LEVEL","type":"num","value":3},"name":"LEVEL","type":"num","value":17,"operator":"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"e907bb08-1951-4c07-92ef-dadb4303be3c","data":{"title":"Select a Lore","modeType":"FILTERED","optionType":"ADJ_VALUE","optionsFilters":{"id":"daeeda4d-86ec-411f-a0b6-11afc1b3166b","type":"ADJ_VALUE","group":"ADD-LORE","value":{"value":"M"}},"optionsPredefined":[],"selectionAliases":["12b99a0e-78fe-4f25-bd69-2d5f48b94953","8bffc37b-eb2e-47e2-ac49-3ef1328ecf43"]},"type":"select"},{"id":"95bce3da-e60f-4e8c-ac3d-8a1785346917","data":{"title":"Select a Lore","modeType":"FILTERED","optionType":"ADJ_VALUE","optionsFilters":{"id":"b0d2083b-d06f-48ec-89a3-76a016b07d8d","type":"ADJ_VALUE","group":"ADD-LORE","value":{"value":"M"}},"optionsPredefined":[],"selectionAliases":["b1d1ddf2-4d94-43bb-8fa9-8b8280ce0f6f","70fed59d-09e9-4ad0-a8df-05df08d79040"]},"type":"select"},{"id":"4b406c3a-6196-42e3-a9bd-893dae19e992","data":{"title":"Select a Lore","modeType":"FILTERED","optionType":"ADJ_VALUE","optionsFilters":{"id":"67213601-6ad0-410b-8c17-241dacc70473","type":"ADJ_VALUE","group":"ADD-LORE","value":{"value":"M"}},"optionsPredefined":[],"selectionAliases":["dba4429c-31af-4eb1-9de5-4a5a38381189","7a8bd1c3-7a0b-4540-a09f-8e6c72fcafe2"]},"type":"select"}],"falseOperations":[]},"type":"conditional"}],"description":"**Gift Type** Minor\n\n**Aspect** mind\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) is imbued with the psychic impressions of ages past. While the [relic](link_trait_3460) is on your person, you are trained in 3 additional Lore skills of the GM's choice that fit the [relic's](link_trait_3460) history, decided at the time of gaining this gift. If the [relic](link_trait_3460) is 9th level, you instead have expert proficiency in these Lore skills, and if the relic is 17th level, you have master proficiency in these Lore skills.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":7},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29712,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29712,"cost":"","name":"Perception Filter","type":"feat","uuid":"4290480895077864","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3497,3480,1448,1432],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=175","book":"GM Core","page":"316"}},"created_at":"2024-06-19T10:03:02.732448+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** mind\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) reaches into the minds of nearby creatures and blocks your presence from their perceptions. For the next 10 minutes, a creature that enters a 120-foot-radius emanation, centered on you, must attempt a secret Will save, after which the creature is then temporarily immune for 1 day.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes a –2 status penalty to Perception checks to [Seek](link_action_19845) or otherwise detect you.\n\n**Failure** You filter all of the creature's senses, making it difficult for it to notice you. When you are hidden or undetected from the creature, it doesn't observe you as soon as you do anything other than [Hide](link_action_19726), [Sneak](link_action_19850), or [Step](link_action_19853). If it rolls a Perception check to [Seek](link_action_19845) or otherwise detect you, it gets the outcome one degree of success worse than what it rolled, and if you roll a Stealth check to [Hide](link_action_19726), [Sneak](link_action_19850), or otherwise escape its attention, you get the outcome one degree of success better than what you rolled against the creature. If you use a hostile action toward the creature, the effect ends for that creature after your hostile action is completed.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the effect doesn't end for that creature if you use a hostile action against it.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":7},"after":{"id":29712,"cost":"","name":"Perception Filter","type":"feat","uuid":"4290480895077864","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3497,3480,1448,1432],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=175","book":"GM Core","page":"316"}},"created_at":"2024-06-19T10:03:02.732448+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** mind\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) reaches into the minds of nearby creatures and blocks your presence from their perceptions. For the next 10 minutes, a creature that enters a 120-foot-radius emanation, centered on you, must attempt a secret Will save, after which the creature is then temporarily immune for 1 day.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes a –2 status penalty to Perception checks to [Seek](link_action_19845) or otherwise detect you.\n\n**Failure** You filter all of the creature's senses, making it difficult for it to notice you. When you are hidden or undetected from the creature, it doesn't observe you as soon as you do anything other than [Hide](link_action_19726), [Sneak](link_action_19850), or [Step](link_action_19853). If it rolls a Perception check to [Seek](link_action_19845) or otherwise detect you, it gets the outcome one degree of success worse than what it rolled, and if you roll a Stealth check to [Hide](link_action_19726), [Sneak](link_action_19850), or otherwise escape its attention, you get the outcome one degree of success better than what you rolled against the creature. If you use a hostile action toward the creature, the effect ends for that creature after your hostile action is completed.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the effect doesn't end for that creature if you use a hostile action against it.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":7},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29714,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29714,"cost":"","name":"Mental Bastion","type":"feat","uuid":"5890704694499090","level":17,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3497,3481,1448],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=177","book":"GM Core","page":"316"}},"created_at":"2024-06-19T10:06:01.781657+00:00","operations":[{"id":"107248cb-1393-4005-ba5d-e363a9be6f50","data":{"type":"physical-feature","abilityBlockId":28884},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"**Gift Type** Grand\n\n**Aspect** mind\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) takes over some of your mental processes and enhances others. You gain [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884); if you already have [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884), you instead increase its range by 30 feet. Whenever you would become stupefied, reduce the value by 1. You are permanently quickened and can use the additional action to [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":7},"after":{"id":29714,"cost":"","name":"Mental Bastion","type":"feat","uuid":"5890704694499090","level":17,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3497,3481,1448],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=177","book":"GM Core","page":"316"}},"created_at":"2024-06-19T10:06:01.781657+00:00","operations":[{"id":"107248cb-1393-4005-ba5d-e363a9be6f50","data":{"type":"physical-feature","abilityBlockId":28884},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"**Gift Type** Grand\n\n**Aspect** mind\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) takes over some of your mental processes and enhances others. You gain [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884); if you already have [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884), you instead increase its range by 30 feet. Whenever you would become stupefied, reduce the value by 1. You are permanently quickened and can use the additional action to [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753).","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":7},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29805,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29805,"cost":"","name":"Borrow Time","type":"feat","uuid":"611344786572040","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3479,1432,1433],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=103","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T09:58:22.190527+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Minor\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou point the [relic](link_trait_3460) at a creature within 30 feet, imbuing it with urgency. The creature gains the quickened condition for 1 round. After the condition ends, the creature is slowed 1 for 1 round and temporarily immune to this gift until you next perform your daily preparations.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":29805,"cost":"","name":"Borrow Time","type":"feat","uuid":"611344786572040","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3479,1432,1433],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=103","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T09:58:22.190527+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Minor\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou point the [relic](link_trait_3460) at a creature within 30 feet, imbuing it with urgency. The creature gains the quickened condition for 1 round. After the condition ends, the creature is slowed 1 for 1 round and temporarily immune to this gift until you next perform your daily preparations.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29806,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29806,"cost":"","name":"Sands of the Hourglass","type":"feat","uuid":"874046999605701","level":5,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3479,1432,1433],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per hour","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=104","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T09:59:58.082658+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Minor\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou target one creature within 30 feet, temporarily imposing the decrepitude of time on it. The target must attempt a Fortitude saving throw. The clumsy and enfeebled conditions last 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target becomes clumsy 1 and enfeebled 1.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes clumsy 2, enfeebled 2, and drained 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target becomes clumsy 3, enfeebled 3, and drained 2.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["The relic is 5th level or higher"],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":29806,"cost":"","name":"Sands of the Hourglass","type":"feat","uuid":"874046999605701","level":5,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3479,1432,1433],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per hour","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=104","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T09:59:58.082658+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Minor\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou target one creature within 30 feet, temporarily imposing the decrepitude of time on it. The target must attempt a Fortitude saving throw. The clumsy and enfeebled conditions last 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target becomes clumsy 1 and enfeebled 1.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes clumsy 2, enfeebled 2, and drained 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target becomes clumsy 3, enfeebled 3, and drained 2.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["The relic is 5th level or higher"],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29807,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29807,"cost":"","name":"Precognition","type":"feat","uuid":"8977415883265950","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3480,1432,1896],"actions":"REACTION","special":"","trigger":"Your turn starts","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=105","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:02:43.401438+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou analyze diverging time streams to determine the best course of action. Resolve two turns as if they occurred, then choose which one happens. The other does not occur.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":29807,"cost":"","name":"Precognition","type":"feat","uuid":"8977415883265950","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3480,1432,1896],"actions":"REACTION","special":"","trigger":"Your turn starts","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=105","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:02:43.401438+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou analyze diverging time streams to determine the best course of action. Resolve two turns as if they occurred, then choose which one happens. The other does not occur.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29808,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29808,"cost":"","name":"Temporal Pulse","type":"feat","uuid":"3548091260347380","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3480,1432],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=106","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:03:48.216558+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou make time shudder around you, stealing it from enemies and granting it to allies. Creatures of your choice within 30 feet must attempt a Will save. For each creature you render slowed with this gift, you can render one ally within 30 feet, including you, quickened for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is slowed 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is slowed 2.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":29808,"cost":"","name":"Temporal Pulse","type":"feat","uuid":"3548091260347380","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3480,1432],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=106","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:03:48.216558+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYou make time shudder around you, stealing it from enemies and granting it to allies. Creatures of your choice within 30 feet must attempt a Will save. For each creature you render slowed with this gift, you can render one ally within 30 feet, including you, quickened for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is slowed 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is slowed 2.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29809,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29809,"cost":"","name":"Time Jump","type":"feat","uuid":"5046928951437424","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3480,1432],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=107","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:04:42.550913+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) [casts](link_action_19611) [_time jump_](link_spell_9051) on you to your specifications.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":29809,"cost":"","name":"Time Jump","type":"feat","uuid":"5046928951437424","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3460,3501,3480,1432],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=107","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:04:42.550913+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Major\n\n**Aspect** time\n\nYour [relic](link_trait_3460) [casts](link_action_19611) [_time jump_](link_spell_9051) on you to your specifications.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29810,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29810,"cost":"","name":"Time Reversal","type":"feat","uuid":"8749976762768099","level":17,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3501,1432,3481,3460],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=108","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:05:35.223733+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Grand\n\n**Aspect** time\n\n* * *\n\nThe [relic](link_trait_3460) casts *[time beacon](link_spell_7373)* on you.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":29810,"cost":"","name":"Time Reversal","type":"feat","uuid":"8749976762768099","level":17,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3501,1432,3481,3460],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Relics.aspx?ID=108","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"200"}},"created_at":"2024-06-22T10:05:35.223733+00:00","operations":[],"description":"**Gift Type** Grand\n\n**Aspect** time\n\n* * *\n\nThe [relic](link_trait_3460) casts *[time beacon](link_spell_7373)* on you.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":29938,"type":"feat","before":{"id":29938,"cost":"1 batch of infused reagents","name":"Quick Alchemy (legacy)","type":"feat","uuid":"7524650515329488","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3530,1433],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-06-23T01:29:33.132716+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You swiftly mix up a short-lived alchemical item to use at a moment's notice. You create a single [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) item of your advanced alchemy level or lower that's in your [formula book](link_item_6972) without having to spend the normal monetary cost in [alchemical](link_trait_1529) reagents or needing to attempt a Crafting check. This item has the [infused](link_trait_3540) trait, but it remains potent only until the start of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have the formula for the alchemical item you're creating, and you're either holding or wearing alchemist's tools.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":11},"after":{"id":29938,"cost":"1 batch of infused reagents","name":"Quick Alchemy (legacy)","type":"feat","uuid":"7524650515329488","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3530,1433],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-06-23T01:29:33.132716+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You swiftly mix up a short-lived alchemical item to use at a moment's notice. You create a single [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) item of your advanced alchemy level or lower that's in your [formula book](link_item_6972) without having to spend the normal monetary cost in [alchemical](link_trait_1529) reagents or needing to attempt a Crafting check. This item has the [infused](link_trait_3540) trait, but it remains potent only until the start of your next turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have the formula for the alchemical item you're creating, and you're either holding or wearing alchemist's tools.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":11},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30026,"type":"sense","before":{"id":30026,"cost":"","name":"Thoughtsense (imprecise 30 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"7711126808857361","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-06-25T03:18:52.1966+00:00","operations":[{"id":"83bc013f-00ed-4023-affb-7a8973c60af8","data":{"value":"thoughtsense, 30","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can detect the flickers of mental activity let off by all thinking creatures. Your thoughtsense detects only thinking creatures, so a creature that is unthinking or otherwise immune to [mental](link_trait_1448) effects (such as many constructs and oozes) can't be perceived using your thoughtsense, regardless of how precise it is.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":30026,"cost":"","name":"Thoughtsense (imprecise 30 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"7711126808857361","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-06-25T03:18:52.1966+00:00","operations":[{"id":"83bc013f-00ed-4023-affb-7a8973c60af8","data":{"value":"thoughtsense, 30","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can detect the flickers of mental activity let off by all thinking creatures. Your thoughtsense detects only thinking creatures, so a creature that is unthinking or otherwise immune to [mental](link_trait_1448) effects (such as many constructs and oozes) can't be perceived using your thoughtsense, regardless of how precise it is.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30027,"type":"feat","before":{"id":30027,"cost":"","name":"Manifest Eidolon","type":"feat","uuid":"8151498550851973","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,2939,1470],"actions":"THREE-ACTIONS","special":"This activity has the trait matching your eidolon's tradition (arcane, divine, occult, or primal).","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=4267","book":"Impossible Magic","page":"64"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-06-25T03:21:48.413876+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Your [eidolon](link_trait_2937) appears in an open space adjacent to you, and can then take a single action. If your eidolon was already manifested, you unmanifest it instead.\n\nThe conduit that allows your eidolon to manifest is also a tether between you. Your eidolon must remain within 100 feet of you at all times and can’t willingly go beyond that limit. If forced beyond this distance, or if you are reduced to 0 Hit Points or your eidolon were to die, your eidolon’s physical form unmanifests, and you need to use Manifest Eidolon to manifest them again.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":842},"after":{"id":30027,"cost":"","name":"Manifest Eidolon","type":"feat","uuid":"8151498550851973","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,2939,1470],"actions":"THREE-ACTIONS","special":"This activity has the trait matching your eidolon's tradition (arcane, divine, occult, or primal).","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=4267","book":"Impossible Magic","page":"64"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-06-25T03:21:48.413876+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Your [eidolon](link_trait_2937) appears in an open space adjacent to you, and can then take a single action. If your eidolon was already manifested, you unmanifest it instead.\n\nThe conduit that allows your eidolon to manifest is also a tether between you. Your eidolon must remain within 100 feet of you at all times and can’t willingly go beyond that limit. If forced beyond this distance, or if you are reduced to 0 Hit Points or your eidolon were to die, your eidolon’s physical form unmanifests, and you need to use Manifest Eidolon to manifest them again.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":842},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30186,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":30186,"cost":"","name":"Powerful Alchemy (legacy)","type":"class-feature","uuid":"1361124856464749","level":5,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3530],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=1","book":"Core Rulebook","page":"66"}},"created_at":"2024-07-01T18:25:29.034868+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Alchemical items you create on the fly are particularly potent. When you use [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_29938) to create an [infused](link_trait_3540) [alchemical](link_trait_1529) item that allows a saving throw, you can change its DC to your class DC.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":11},"after":{"id":30186,"cost":"","name":"Powerful Alchemy (legacy)","type":"class-feature","uuid":"1361124856464749","level":5,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3530],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=1","book":"Core Rulebook","page":"66"}},"created_at":"2024-07-01T18:25:29.034868+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Alchemical items you create on the fly are particularly potent. When you use [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_29938) to create an [infused](link_trait_3540) [alchemical](link_trait_1529) item that allows a saving throw, you can change its DC to your class DC.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":11},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30188,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":30188,"cost":"","name":"Double Brew (legacy)","type":"class-feature","uuid":"727158101771952","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3530],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=1","book":"Core Rulebook","page":"66"}},"created_at":"2024-07-01T18:27:53.432509+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b8d99971-84ff-4da4-8fdc-79304acb8dd8","data":{"id":29938,"text":"**Double Brew**\n\nInstead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to two batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"},{"id":"8a5c5da0-1d0d-4fcc-b3f3-655410dde7fc","data":{"conditions":[{"id":"ca903676-d735-4afc-ae50-381a0422d9d1","data":{"name":"FEAT_NAMES","type":"list-str","value":[]},"name":"FEAT_NAMES","type":"list-str","value":"alchemical alacrity","operator":"INCLUDES"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"1ba33378-284e-4acb-a451-9da4456bf846","data":{"id":29938,"text":"[**Alchemical Alacrity**](link_class-feature_30191)\n\nInstead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to three batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same, and you automatically stow one of these new items as you create them.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"}],"falseOperations":[{"id":"022846e8-d38b-499f-b59d-9548066d5847","data":{"id":29938,"text":"[**Double Brew**](link_class-feature_30188)\n\nInstead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to two batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"}]},"type":"conditional"}],"description":"You know your formulas so well that you can concoct two items at once. When using the [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_29938) action, instead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to two batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":11},"after":{"id":30188,"cost":"","name":"Double Brew (legacy)","type":"class-feature","uuid":"727158101771952","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3530],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=1","book":"Core Rulebook","page":"66"}},"created_at":"2024-07-01T18:27:53.432509+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b8d99971-84ff-4da4-8fdc-79304acb8dd8","data":{"id":29938,"text":"**Double Brew**\n\nInstead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to two batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"},{"id":"8a5c5da0-1d0d-4fcc-b3f3-655410dde7fc","data":{"conditions":[{"id":"ca903676-d735-4afc-ae50-381a0422d9d1","data":{"name":"FEAT_NAMES","type":"list-str","value":[]},"name":"FEAT_NAMES","type":"list-str","value":"alchemical alacrity","operator":"INCLUDES"}],"trueOperations":[{"id":"1ba33378-284e-4acb-a451-9da4456bf846","data":{"id":29938,"text":"[**Alchemical Alacrity**](link_class-feature_30191)\n\nInstead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to three batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same, and you automatically stow one of these new items as you create them.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"}],"falseOperations":[{"id":"022846e8-d38b-499f-b59d-9548066d5847","data":{"id":29938,"text":"[**Double Brew**](link_class-feature_30188)\n\nInstead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to two batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"}]},"type":"conditional"}],"description":"You know your formulas so well that you can concoct two items at once. When using the [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_29938) action, instead of spending one batch of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to create a single item, you can spend up to two batches of [infused](link_trait_3540) reagents to make up to two [alchemical](link_trait_1529) items as described in that action. These items do not have to be the same.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":11},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30274,"type":"sense","before":{"id":30274,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 10 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"3006600167159925","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-07-10T23:02:26.122294+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b9da4888-dd9f-42da-91df-1572b4cd8d89","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 10","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":30274,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 10 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"3006600167159925","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-07-10T23:02:26.122294+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b9da4888-dd9f-42da-91df-1572b4cd8d89","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 10","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30275,"type":"sense","before":{"id":30275,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 15 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"3399939673415076","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-07-10T23:02:26.658382+00:00","operations":[{"id":"c4d056bf-e7e7-47e0-aaed-360e0d44e5d0","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 15","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":30275,"cost":"","name":"Tremorsense (imprecise 15 ft)","type":"sense","uuid":"3399939673415076","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-07-10T23:02:26.658382+00:00","operations":[{"id":"c4d056bf-e7e7-47e0-aaed-360e0d44e5d0","data":{"value":"tremorsense, 15","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"You can feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. This functions only if you are on the same surface as the subject you're detecting, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30995,"type":"feat","before":{"id":30995,"cost":"","name":"Pursue a Lead","type":"feat","uuid":"7863826135270286","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,3629],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2811","book":"Player Core 2","page":"102"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-27T20:29:39.382206+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You name one detail you’ve identified that you think is part of a larger mystery, then spend 1 minute examining it. The detail is typically either obvious or something you’ve already discovered using [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753), [Sense Motive](link_action_19847), [Gather Information](link_action_19723), or a similar action. After the minute passes, the GM either confirms there’s a larger mystery or tells you there’s nothing more to learn (the detail is inconsequential or you know all the information already). If there is in fact a larger mystery at play, you can’t Pursue a Lead again for 10 minutes, but you can choose to open an investigation. To do so, define the question at the heart of the mystery, such as “Where has the priceless work of art that was supposed to hang here been taken?” or “Who or what killed this priest?” Work with your GM to refine the question if need be. You can also give your investigation a name to better keep track of it (such as “The Case of the Cheated Goblin” or “The Skinsaw Murders”).\n\n**Investigation Bonus** Whenever you attempt a Perception check or skill check to attempt to get closer to answering the question at the heart of an active investigation, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the check. The exact checks this applies to depend on the actions you use to investigate and are determined by the GM, but checks to investigate are typically Perception checks or skill checks that use Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma.\n\n**Active Investigations** You can maintain two active investigations at a time. If you Pursue another Lead after that, the case must be different from any of your current investigations (as far as you are aware), and you give up on a current investigation of your choice. Once you’ve given up pursuit of an investigation, you can’t Pursue a Lead into it again until after the next time you make your daily preparations.\n\n**Solving an Investigation** If you answer the question at the heart of your investigation, the GM tells you that you’ve done so. You don’t lose the bonus or other benefits until you choose to close the investigation by Pursuing a Lead again or voluntarily [Dismissing](link_action_19627) it. If what you discover points to an even larger mystery, you can work with the GM to adapt the question and name of the investigation to the new information.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":30995,"cost":"","name":"Pursue a Lead","type":"feat","uuid":"7863826135270286","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1457,3629],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2811","book":"Player Core 2","page":"102"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-27T20:29:39.382206+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You name one detail you’ve identified that you think is part of a larger mystery, then spend 1 minute examining it. The detail is typically either obvious or something you’ve already discovered using [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753), [Sense Motive](link_action_19847), [Gather Information](link_action_19723), or a similar action. After the minute passes, the GM either confirms there’s a larger mystery or tells you there’s nothing more to learn (the detail is inconsequential or you know all the information already). If there is in fact a larger mystery at play, you can’t Pursue a Lead again for 10 minutes, but you can choose to open an investigation. To do so, define the question at the heart of the mystery, such as “Where has the priceless work of art that was supposed to hang here been taken?” or “Who or what killed this priest?” Work with your GM to refine the question if need be. You can also give your investigation a name to better keep track of it (such as “The Case of the Cheated Goblin” or “The Skinsaw Murders”).\n\n**Investigation Bonus** Whenever you attempt a Perception check or skill check to attempt to get closer to answering the question at the heart of an active investigation, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the check. The exact checks this applies to depend on the actions you use to investigate and are determined by the GM, but checks to investigate are typically Perception checks or skill checks that use Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma.\n\n**Active Investigations** You can maintain two active investigations at a time. If you Pursue another Lead after that, the case must be different from any of your current investigations (as far as you are aware), and you give up on a current investigation of your choice. Once you’ve given up pursuit of an investigation, you can’t Pursue a Lead into it again until after the next time you make your daily preparations.\n\n**Solving an Investigation** If you answer the question at the heart of your investigation, the GM tells you that you’ve done so. You don’t lose the bonus or other benefits until you choose to close the investigation by Pursuing a Lead again or voluntarily [Dismissing](link_action_19627) it. If what you discover points to an even larger mystery, you can work with the GM to adapt the question and name of the investigation to the new information.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":30999,"type":"feat","before":{"id":30999,"cost":"","name":"Flurry of Blows","type":"feat","uuid":"1391548415062148","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1462,3630],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-27T20:36:45.483752+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Make two unarmed [Strikes](link_action_19856). If both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses. Apply your multiple attack penalty to the [Strikes](link_action_19856) normally. As a [flourish](link_trait_1462) ability, you can use Flurry of Blows only once per turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":30999,"cost":"","name":"Flurry of Blows","type":"feat","uuid":"1391548415062148","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1462,3630],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-27T20:36:45.483752+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Make two unarmed [Strikes](link_action_19856). If both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses. Apply your multiple attack penalty to the [Strikes](link_action_19856) normally. As a [flourish](link_trait_1462) ability, you can use Flurry of Blows only once per turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31174,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":31174,"cost":"","name":"Double Brew","type":"class-feature","uuid":"3436336554382249","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3626],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=56","book":"Player Core 2","page":"56"}},"created_at":"2024-07-30T17:04:33.924601+00:00","operations":[{"id":"26166b94-0e4e-4753-81bf-783948e10664","data":{"id":31176,"text":"**Double Brew** You can create two items. These items don’t have to be the same. If you create two consumables, you have to expend a versatile vial for each one.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"}],"description":"You know your formulas so well that you can concoct two items at once. When using the [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) action, you can create two items. These items don’t have to be the same. If you create two consumables, you have to expend a versatile vial for each one.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31174,"cost":"","name":"Double Brew","type":"class-feature","uuid":"3436336554382249","level":9,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3626],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=56","book":"Player Core 2","page":"56"}},"created_at":"2024-07-30T17:04:33.924601+00:00","operations":[{"id":"26166b94-0e4e-4753-81bf-783948e10664","data":{"id":31176,"text":"**Double Brew** You can create two items. These items don’t have to be the same. If you create two consumables, you have to expend a versatile vial for each one.","type":"feat"},"type":"injectText"}],"description":"You know your formulas so well that you can concoct two items at once. When using the [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) action, you can create two items. These items don’t have to be the same. If you create two consumables, you have to expend a versatile vial for each one.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31176,"type":"feat","before":{"id":31176,"cost":"","name":"Quick Alchemy","type":"feat","uuid":"3378041843631222","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3626,1433],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2801","book":"Player Core 2","page":"59"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-30T17:05:52.36043+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You can either use up a versatile vial to make another [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) at a moment’s notice or create an especially short-lived versatile vial. Any effect created by an item made with Quick Alchemy that would have a duration longer than 10 minutes lasts for 10 minutes instead.\n\n*   **Create Consumable** You expend one of your versatile vials to create a single [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) item of your level or lower that’s in your [formula book](link_item_6972). You don’t have to spend the normal monetary cost in [alchemical](link_trait_1529) raw materials or need to attempt a Crafting check. This item has the [infused](link_trait_3540) trait, but it remains potent only until the start of your next turn. (As normal, you need only one formula for an item to create any level of that item.)\n    \n*   **Quick Vial** You create a versatile vial that can be used only as a [bomb](link_trait_1530) or for the versatile vial option from your research field (it can’t be used to create a [consumable](link_trait_1531), for example). This item has the [infused](link_trait_3540) trait, but it remains potent only until the end of your current turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You're either holding or wearing an alchemist's toolkit and you have a free hand.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31176,"cost":"","name":"Quick Alchemy","type":"feat","uuid":"3378041843631222","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3626,1433],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Actions.aspx?ID=2801","book":"Player Core 2","page":"59"},"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-30T17:05:52.36043+00:00","operations":[],"description":"You can either use up a versatile vial to make another [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) at a moment’s notice or create an especially short-lived versatile vial. Any effect created by an item made with Quick Alchemy that would have a duration longer than 10 minutes lasts for 10 minutes instead.\n\n*   **Create Consumable** You expend one of your versatile vials to create a single [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) item of your level or lower that’s in your [formula book](link_item_6972). You don’t have to spend the normal monetary cost in [alchemical](link_trait_1529) raw materials or need to attempt a Crafting check. This item has the [infused](link_trait_3540) trait, but it remains potent only until the start of your next turn. (As normal, you need only one formula for an item to create any level of that item.)\n    \n*   **Quick Vial** You create a versatile vial that can be used only as a [bomb](link_trait_1530) or for the versatile vial option from your research field (it can’t be used to create a [consumable](link_trait_1531), for example). This item has the [infused](link_trait_3540) trait, but it remains potent only until the end of your current turn.","availability":null,"requirements":"You're either holding or wearing an alchemist's toolkit and you have a free hand.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31184,"type":"feat","before":{"id":31184,"cost":"","name":"Rage","type":"feat","uuid":"952294454471782","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3627,1432,1486,1448],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-30T17:16:02.496724+00:00","operations":[{"id":"1c787182-763c-4b65-a5b7-4b518f929bd9","data":{"type":"mode","abilityBlockId":31008},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"954a59d3-13d3-40a9-a456-321f12602080","data":{"type":"num","value":2,"variable":"RAGE_DAMAGE"},"type":"createValue"},{"id":"d13045d5-11c3-4897-83ee-660116a1cf84","data":{"type":"str","value":"","variable":"RAGE_DAMAGE_TYPE"},"type":"createValue"}],"description":"You tap into your inner fury and begin raging. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level plus your Constitution modifier (⬆️{{level+attribute\\_con}}). While you are raging:\n\n*   You deal 2 additional damage on melee [Strikes](link_action_19856). This additional damage is halved if your weapon or [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack is [agile](link_trait_1569).\n    \n*   You can’t use actions with the [concentrate](link_trait_1432) trait unless they also have the [rage](link_trait_1455) trait. You can [Seek](link_action_19845) while raging.\n    \n\nRage lasts for 1 minute, until you fall unconscious, or until the encounter ends, whichever comes first. You can’t voluntarily stop raging. When you stop raging, you lose any remaining temporary Hit Points from Rage, and can’t gain temporary Hit Points from using the Rage action again for 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":"You aren’t fatigued or raging.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31184,"cost":"","name":"Rage","type":"feat","uuid":"952294454471782","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3627,1432,1486,1448],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-30T17:16:02.496724+00:00","operations":[{"id":"1c787182-763c-4b65-a5b7-4b518f929bd9","data":{"type":"mode","abilityBlockId":31008},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"},{"id":"954a59d3-13d3-40a9-a456-321f12602080","data":{"type":"num","value":2,"variable":"RAGE_DAMAGE"},"type":"createValue"},{"id":"d13045d5-11c3-4897-83ee-660116a1cf84","data":{"type":"str","value":"","variable":"RAGE_DAMAGE_TYPE"},"type":"createValue"}],"description":"You tap into your inner fury and begin raging. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level plus your Constitution modifier (⬆️{{level+attribute\\_con}}). While you are raging:\n\n*   You deal 2 additional damage on melee [Strikes](link_action_19856). This additional damage is halved if your weapon or [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack is [agile](link_trait_1569).\n    \n*   You can’t use actions with the [concentrate](link_trait_1432) trait unless they also have the [rage](link_trait_1455) trait. You can [Seek](link_action_19845) while raging.\n    \n\nRage lasts for 1 minute, until you fall unconscious, or until the encounter ends, whichever comes first. You can’t voluntarily stop raging. When you stop raging, you lose any remaining temporary Hit Points from Rage, and can’t gain temporary Hit Points from using the Rage action again for 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":"You aren’t fatigued or raging.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31200,"type":"feat","before":{"id":31200,"cost":"","name":"Quick-Tempered","type":"feat","uuid":"8555482895940595","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3627],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"You roll initiative.","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-30T22:14:22.939532+00:00","operations":[],"description":"So long as you are able to move freely, your fury is instinctive and instantaneous. You [Rage](link_feat_31184).","availability":null,"requirements":"You are not encumbered or wearing heavy armor.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31200,"cost":"","name":"Quick-Tempered","type":"feat","uuid":"8555482895940595","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3627],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"You roll initiative.","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"unselectable":true},"created_at":"2024-07-30T22:14:22.939532+00:00","operations":[],"description":"So long as you are able to move freely, your fury is instinctive and instantaneous. You [Rage](link_feat_31184).","availability":null,"requirements":"You are not encumbered or wearing heavy armor.","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31201,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":31201,"cost":"","name":"Quick-Tempered","type":"class-feature","uuid":"8795569301966040","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3627],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-07-30T22:16:27.100222+00:00","operations":[{"id":"8540159b-5346-457d-8364-1aab5ec26a74","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":31200},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You gain the [Quick-Tempered](link_feat_31200) free action, which lets you [Rage](link_feat_31184) at the slightest provocation.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31201,"cost":"","name":"Quick-Tempered","type":"class-feature","uuid":"8795569301966040","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3627],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{},"created_at":"2024-07-30T22:16:27.100222+00:00","operations":[{"id":"8540159b-5346-457d-8364-1aab5ec26a74","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":31200},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}],"description":"You gain the [Quick-Tempered](link_feat_31200) free action, which lets you [Rage](link_feat_31184) at the slightest provocation.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31209,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":31209,"cost":"","name":"Devotion Spells","type":"class-feature","uuid":"3463497906508001","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3628],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=58","book":"Player Core 2","page":"86"}},"created_at":"2024-07-31T22:22:50.623487+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b5c85c3b-9902-46a3-b206-2a7b7eb87186","data":{"value":"CHAMPION:::-:::DIVINE:::ATTRIBUTE_CHA","variable":"CASTING_SOURCES"},"type":"defineCastingSource"},{"id":"80942acd-c988-4189-af47-e264e74a8373","data":{"title":"Select a Devotion Spell","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"SPELL","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"7a0d915b-e884-4207-b0fc-34901fff207e","type":"SPELL","operation":{"id":"977eba17-b6a6-47a7-b1b1-5eda3766e0fc","data":{"type":"FOCUS","spellId":6381,"castingSource":"CHAMPION"},"type":"giveSpell"}},{"id":"e413ea6c-bf6f-4d51-8b29-860650d1cc5a","type":"SPELL","operation":{"id":"6a460a13-6180-4cf5-a49b-e2d0e25032fc","data":{"type":"NORMAL","spellId":6379},"type":"giveSpell"}},{"id":"f24ce9e8-acae-44a5-b10e-e88911dee637","type":"SPELL","operation":{"id":"1543470e-9a84-4d3c-9f8f-8064f66235b6","data":{"type":"NORMAL","spellId":6380},"type":"giveSpell"}}]},"type":"select"},{"id":"fda85cb0-eb8f-4944-a2eb-69708a36e6fa","data":{"value":"spells","variable":"PRIMARY_SHEET_TABS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"Your deity’s power grants you special divine spells called devotion spells, which are a type of focus spell. Choose either [shields of the spirit](link_spell_6381) or a spell based on your deity’s divine font ([lay on hands](link_spell_6379) if your deity allows [heal](link_spell_4656), [touch of the void](link_spell_6380) if your deity allows [harm](link_spell_4653)).\n\nIt costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell. When you gain your first devotion spell, you also gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the [Refocus](link_action_19754) activity to pray to your deity or do service toward their causes.\n\nYour devotion spells are [divine](link_trait_1475) spells. Your spellcasting attribute is Charisma.\n\nFocus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up. Certain feats give you more focus spells. The maximum Focus Points your focus pool can hold is equal to the number of focus spells you have, but can never be more than 3 points.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31209,"cost":"","name":"Devotion Spells","type":"class-feature","uuid":"3463497906508001","level":1,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3628],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=58","book":"Player Core 2","page":"86"}},"created_at":"2024-07-31T22:22:50.623487+00:00","operations":[{"id":"b5c85c3b-9902-46a3-b206-2a7b7eb87186","data":{"value":"CHAMPION:::-:::DIVINE:::ATTRIBUTE_CHA","variable":"CASTING_SOURCES"},"type":"defineCastingSource"},{"id":"80942acd-c988-4189-af47-e264e74a8373","data":{"title":"Select a Devotion Spell","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"SPELL","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"7a0d915b-e884-4207-b0fc-34901fff207e","type":"SPELL","operation":{"id":"977eba17-b6a6-47a7-b1b1-5eda3766e0fc","data":{"type":"FOCUS","spellId":6381,"castingSource":"CHAMPION"},"type":"giveSpell"}},{"id":"e413ea6c-bf6f-4d51-8b29-860650d1cc5a","type":"SPELL","operation":{"id":"6a460a13-6180-4cf5-a49b-e2d0e25032fc","data":{"type":"NORMAL","spellId":6379},"type":"giveSpell"}},{"id":"f24ce9e8-acae-44a5-b10e-e88911dee637","type":"SPELL","operation":{"id":"1543470e-9a84-4d3c-9f8f-8064f66235b6","data":{"type":"NORMAL","spellId":6380},"type":"giveSpell"}}]},"type":"select"},{"id":"fda85cb0-eb8f-4944-a2eb-69708a36e6fa","data":{"value":"spells","variable":"PRIMARY_SHEET_TABS"},"type":"adjValue"}],"description":"Your deity’s power grants you special divine spells called devotion spells, which are a type of focus spell. Choose either [shields of the spirit](link_spell_6381) or a spell based on your deity’s divine font ([lay on hands](link_spell_6379) if your deity allows [heal](link_spell_4656), [touch of the void](link_spell_6380) if your deity allows [harm](link_spell_4653)).\n\nIt costs 1 Focus Point to cast a focus spell. When you gain your first devotion spell, you also gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point. You refill your focus pool during your daily preparations, and you regain 1 Focus Point by spending 10 minutes using the [Refocus](link_action_19754) activity to pray to your deity or do service toward their causes.\n\nYour devotion spells are [divine](link_trait_1475) spells. Your spellcasting attribute is Charisma.\n\nFocus spells are automatically heightened to half your level rounded up. Certain feats give you more focus spells. The maximum Focus Points your focus pool can hold is equal to the number of focus spells you have, but can never be more than 3 points.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31232,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":31232,"cost":"","name":"Powerful Alchemy","type":"class-feature","uuid":"313870151190288","level":5,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3626],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=56","book":"Player Core 2","page":"56"}},"created_at":"2024-08-01T06:24:09.557776+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Alchemical items you infuse are particularly potent. When you create an [infused](link_trait_3540) [alchemical](link_trait_1529) item that allows a saving throw, you can change its DC to your class DC.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31232,"cost":"","name":"Powerful Alchemy","type":"class-feature","uuid":"313870151190288","level":5,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3626],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=56","book":"Player Core 2","page":"56"}},"created_at":"2024-08-01T06:24:09.557776+00:00","operations":[],"description":"Alchemical items you infuse are particularly potent. When you create an [infused](link_trait_3540) [alchemical](link_trait_1529) item that allows a saving throw, you can change its DC to your class DC.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":31244,"type":"class-feature","before":{"id":31244,"cost":"","name":"Blessing of the Devoted","type":"class-feature","uuid":"5840604374345909","level":3,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3628],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=58","book":"Player Core 2","page":"86"}},"created_at":"2024-08-01T06:26:50.21267+00:00","operations":[{"id":"e429f4d2-b36f-42fc-8c87-8fa2532928e1","data":{"title":"Select a Blessing","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"ABILITY_BLOCK","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"c0d2b001-1876-45b1-b0d4-204f6d6b3283","type":"ABILITY_BLOCK","operation":{"id":"53d128c3-1583-4490-b849-2d8ddca4a796","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":42890},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}},{"id":"bac60387-cf60-43eb-8d7f-b8fba331dd12","type":"ABILITY_BLOCK","operation":{"id":"7f169f4f-e66d-4a25-b8bd-a1621f3bf306","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":42891},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}},{"id":"e9adccc8-159d-4beb-a6cc-792d79093666","type":"ABILITY_BLOCK","operation":{"id":"17090041-d56b-41c6-b8f9-73882619ec2e","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":42892},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}}]},"type":"select"}],"description":"Your deity blesses your service with a boon. This might come in the form of a spirit that visits you and inhabits your items or body, a mysterious divine tattoo upon your body, or the like. Choose one of the following blessings.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":31244,"cost":"","name":"Blessing of the Devoted","type":"class-feature","uuid":"5840604374345909","level":3,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3628],"actions":null,"special":"","trigger":"","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Classes.aspx?ID=58","book":"Player Core 2","page":"86"}},"created_at":"2024-08-01T06:26:50.21267+00:00","operations":[{"id":"e429f4d2-b36f-42fc-8c87-8fa2532928e1","data":{"title":"Select a Blessing","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"ABILITY_BLOCK","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"c0d2b001-1876-45b1-b0d4-204f6d6b3283","type":"ABILITY_BLOCK","operation":{"id":"53d128c3-1583-4490-b849-2d8ddca4a796","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":42890},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}},{"id":"bac60387-cf60-43eb-8d7f-b8fba331dd12","type":"ABILITY_BLOCK","operation":{"id":"7f169f4f-e66d-4a25-b8bd-a1621f3bf306","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":42891},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}},{"id":"e9adccc8-159d-4beb-a6cc-792d79093666","type":"ABILITY_BLOCK","operation":{"id":"17090041-d56b-41c6-b8f9-73882619ec2e","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":42892},"type":"giveAbilityBlock"}}]},"type":"select"}],"description":"Your deity blesses your service with a boon. This might come in the form of a spirit that visits you and inhabits your items or body, a mysterious divine tattoo upon your body, or the like. Choose one of the following blessings.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":[],"content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"ability_block","id":32007,"type":"feat","before":{"id":32007,"cost":"","name":"Disarming Block","type":"feat","uuid":"8136690009196142","level":4,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[3758],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","special":"","trigger":"You Shield Block a melee Strike made with a\nheld weapon.","version":null,"frequency":"","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=6263","book":"Player Core 2","page":"187"}},"created_at":"2024-08-07T23:03:01.58534+00:00","operations":[],"description":"With deft and practiced movement, you block at an angle to potentially dislodge the weapon. You attempt to [Disarm](link_action_19626) the creature whose attack you blocked of the weapon they attacked you with. You can do so even if you don’t have a hand free.","availability":null,"requirements":"","prerequisites":["Bastion Dedication","trained in Athletics"],"content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":32007,"cost":"","name":"Disarming Block","type":"feat","uuid":"8136690009196142","level":4,"access":"","rarity":"COMMON","trai