_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The benthic worm negates the triggering condition or effect by sloughing an outer layer of its skin. Effects from artifacts, deities, or a similarly powerful source can't be avoided in this way.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Benthic Worm Venom","type":"action","level":15,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1476],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:37\\]\n\n* * *\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 3d6 poison damage and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 2} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 4d6 poison damage and clumsy 2 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** 6d6 poison damage and clumsy 2 (1 round)","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Breach","type":"action","level":15,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The benthic worm Swims up to its swim Speed, then \\[\\[Leap\\]\\]{Leaps} vertically out of the water up to 30 feet, making a Strike against a creature at the apex of the jump (this lets it attack a creature within 45 feet of the water's surface). After the Strike, the worm splashes back down. It can use \\[\\[Improved Grab\\]\\] on this Strike and follow it up with Fast Swallow.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Fast Swallow","type":"action","level":15,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","trigger":"The worm [[Grabbed]]{Grabs} a creature.","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The worm uses Swallow Whole.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Swallow Whole","type":"action","level":15,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Huge, (3d8+10) bludgeoning, Rupture 27\n\n* * *\n\nSwallowWhole","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Thrash","type":"action","level":15,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The worm makes a Strike once against each creature in its reach. It can Strike up to once with its jaws, up to once with its stinger, and any number of times with its body. Each attack counts toward the worm's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after it makes all the attacks.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Improved Grab","type":"action","level":15,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"ImprovedGrab","content_source_id":8}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":8},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":9948,"type":"creature","before":{"id":9948,"name":"Boar","type":"creature","uuid":"7030109219462453","level":2,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Boar.webp","description":"Boars are omnivorous mammals, hunted heavily because their meat is considered a delicacy. Boars are most likely to attack humanoids either in self-defense or during their mating season in the winter months, when the males grow an extra inch of tissue to protect their organs as they fight off rivals. Of course, in some cultures, boars are trained to become much more aggressive so they can fill the roles of warbeast and guardian. When such boars escape back into the wild, they can become true terrors in the region.\n\n* * *\n\nWhile domesticated pigs are a staple of farm life, wild boars are much more dangerous. Foul-tempered warthogs are relatively common, while the lumbering, primeval beasts known as daeodons are less so. Voracious boars can ravage the countryside in which they live, making them a particular nuisance to farmers. Boars breed freely, and a pair of boars can rapidly grow to a large family."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"79cef4c0-1e9f-4cd7-8245-17110e1669ec","item":{"id":1286993736165149,"name":"Tusk","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":2,"damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":6},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=2854","book":"Monster Core","page":"43"}},"created_at":"2024-12-29T21:51:51.502604+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"51782988-0bbd-4441-a1e6-0e88dac49e4a","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"9f85a8e6-3a4d-44be-92e4-e47e7199a84d","data":{"value":{"value":1,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"9ffd7fc9-63f9-4d52-8818-9ad30de7e69c","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"a3888e16-d32a-49aa-8f25-4165a91cda23","data":{"value":{"value":-4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"eff71c38-9f10-4303-b59d-a6ebf7d85328","data":{"value":{"value":2,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"5f4cafb2-181d-4f5d-8c54-cbeee8317fe5","data":{"value":{"value":-3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"d60b330c-987e-4062-9f3b-b5a5441bdd39","data":{"value":40,"variable":"SPEED"},"ty