},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"roll_history":null,"abilities_base":[{"id":-1,"name":"Regeneration 15 (Deactivated by Fire)","type":"action","level":10,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Regeneration","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Stench","type":"action","level":10,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1492,2131],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"30 feet, @Check\\[fortitude|dc:27\\]\n\n* * *\n\nStench","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Amnesia Venom","type":"action","level":10,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1476],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:29\\]\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** \\[\\[Off-Guard\\]\\] (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** off-guard and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 1} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** \\[\\[Confused\\]\\], off-guard, and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 2} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 4** as Stage 3 and permanently forget the last hour (1 round)","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Constrict","type":"action","level":10,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"(2d6+2) bludgeoning, @Check\\[fortitude|dc:29|basic\\]\n\n* * *\n\nConstrict","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Root","type":"action","level":10,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Until the next time it acts, the dezullon appears to be a normal pitcher plant. It has an automatic result of 41 (44 in forests or swamps) on Deception checks and DCs to pass as a non-creature plant.","content_source_id":8}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":8},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":10013,"type":"creature","before":{"id":10013,"name":"Dire Wolf","type":"creature","uuid":"1879311801801483","level":3,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"description":"Much larger and more foul-tempered than their common cousins, dire wolves haunt primeval lands that accommodate their massive size and proportionately large hunting grounds and appetites. Orcs are fond of using dire wolves as mounts, finding their vicious tempers perfect for hunting and warfare. Dire wolves are far more likely to prey on humanoids than ordinary wolves, considering them nothing but another kind of smaller, nutritious animal.\n\n* * *\n\nWolves roam forests, hills, and other wild lands, where they hunt in packs to beleaguer and surround their prey before going in for the kill. Like most predatory animals, wolves prefer to attack the weakest or most vulnerable prey they can find."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"4b64fcb3-2807-466b-a200-32782e892485","item":{"id":495625396837420,"name":"Jaws","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":1,"extra":"Improved Grab, Improved Knockdown","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":7},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=3242","book":"Monster Core","page":"350"}},"created_at":"2024-12-29T21:52:27.201606+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"48bde104-fac5-4182-b250-de7ca833bc6b","da