t":"","description":"The gosreg senses a creature's mental essence as a precise sense with the listed range; it cannot sense mindless creatures with thoughtsense.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Unsettled Aura","type":"action","level":11,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1492,1448,1514],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"30 feet.\n\nGosregs project a field of discordant energy that unsettles the minds of thinking creatures. Any non-mindless creature within 30 feet of a gosreg takes a –1 status penalty to Will saves.\n\n\\[\\[Effect: Unsettled Aura\\]\\]","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Broadcast Stance","type":"action","level":11,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1514,1480],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The gosreg secures its limbs into the ground as its brain-like head crackles with psychic energy. The gosreg's unsettled aura extends to 60 feet, and it blocks all other creatures' telepathy in the aura. Its Mind Bolt can also affect any number of targets in 60 feet. These effects end when the gosreg uses its claw Strike, leaves its space, or is knocked \\[\\[Prone\\]\\].","requirements":"the gosreg is in its natural form","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Change Shape","type":"action","level":11,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1514,1453],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The gosreg takes on the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid. This doesn't change its Speed or attack and damage modifiers with its claw, but it might change the damage type it deals (typically to bludgeoning). It cannot use its jaws Strike while in humanoid form.\n\n* * *\n\nChangeShape","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Mind Bolt","type":"action","level":11,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1514],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"A gosreg concentrates its field of discordant mental energy and projects it into the mind of one creature within 60 feet. The target takes 6d6 mental damage (@Check\\[will|dc:30|basic\\] save). On a critical failure, the creature is also \\[\\[Confused\\]\\] for 1 minute or until it takes damage.","content_source_id":8}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":8},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":10111,"type":"creature","before":{"id":10111,"name":"Griffon","type":"creature","uuid":"2338463709281465","level":4,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Griffon.webp","description":"Griffons are regal beasts revered as symbols of freedom and strength in many cultures. They are physically striking, with the hindquarters of a lion and the head, wings, and forelimbs of a great bird of prey—typically an eagle, but some instead bear the features of a hawk, falcon, or even an osprey or vulture. In rare cases, the griffon's hindquarters may resemble those of a different great cat, such as a leopard or tiger. The variations seem to conform to the griffon's environment—for instance, especially rare griffons of northern Avistan have the hindquarters of a Grungir lynx and the upper body of a snowy owl.\n\nWild griffons rely on their powerful wings to hold them aloft and their keen eyesight to spy out prey. The speed with which they plunge toward the ground and snatch up victims is astonishing. They often tear apart a kill's flesh with razor-sharp beaks but not before alighting to secluded location where they can enjoy their meal without interruption. Griffons hunting to feed their chicks are more cautious, tearing apart prey rather than risking bringing a living creature back to their nests.\n\nSkilled animal trainers long ago learned how to raise griffons as mounts for military forces or powerful individuals. Such mounts are known for their strength, bravery, and unfailing loyalty. They are among the smartest of animals, and many griffon variants are considered intelligent beasts instead; it's thought that a griffon chooses its rider as much as a rider chooses the griffon. The process of training a griffon to accept and carry a rider in flight is a long and expensive ordeal. Griffon trainers charge rich sums for their services, and a ruler who can boast of owning a stable of griffons is the subject of great respect and envy."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"e8b33460-8919-4d62-a6e8-a29883ef9906","item":{"id":2434909571025298,"name":"Beak","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1706],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d8","dice":2,"damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":10},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"0359bccc-2236-4603-bcf0-7de5a7303d10","item":{"id":4163315455953490,"name":"Talon","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":2,"damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":10},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"a679c72a-231a-4064-828b-eb6e1242aa45","item":{"id":3867369073430197,"name":"Wing","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":2,"damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":10},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=3034","book":"Monster Core","page":"182"}},"created_at":"2024-12-29T21:53:25.712618+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"237382d8-13c8-4066-99db-9b89b0039abf","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"3ceac3bf-2f6a-404a-814d-85ca54a3699c","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"1bfdd23d-5b17-4f31-bf4d-fd803187e984","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"6cdae4c7-ce67-4596-97c7-96da1b93f730","data":{"value":{"value":-4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"0a3e5d77-3b58-46f4-8938-350742f873ec","data":{"value":{"value":1,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"cd830112-432a-4b27-bbef-372d9e239ad2","data":{"value":{"value":2,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"0c985ce8-6388-48de-8156-3d12abee8599","data":{"value":25,"variable":"SPEED"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"b2439b38-f597-4921-901d-d3b4f93b661e","data":{"value":60,"variable":"SPEED_FLY"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"7981fdd5-c05f-4c2b-a05e-3ba210e60c60","data":{"value":"darkvision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"bfdd59e2-734c-4450-a005-6b96ff7474f5","data":{"value":"scent, 60","variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"7507d2bc-3f56-40ff-ab69-39f3acd5cb70","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"526a3d11-a2cc-4976-9898-fcdee768a622","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"24c64474-ab44-4743-ac20-44de6ee5bba3","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_INTIMIDATION"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"8d42ecda-6a4d-42aa-a784-615ca07dc74e","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"a9ca9f16-9db4-45ed-a51d-279ff4137704","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_SURVIVAL"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"3ff12cee-e613-48f3-83bb-f10803a120eb","data":{"value":"LARGE","variable":"SIZE"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"6a7dcac3-0b39-49b0-a56d-c7f67e2355f9","data":{"traitId":2409},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"a36ef7ba-8739-4a1f-8955-9186e1ca4399","data":{"value":8,"variable":"AC_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"e218430a-0b2d-4f02-b52d-7d1765ca3e70","data":{"text":"","value":"+10","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"a11a15d7-c521-4219-bdaa-d9e3222f6786","data":{"text":"","value":"+10","variable":"SAVE_REFLEX"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"c7935b2e-eed5-47cd-af18-9cf4b07de670","data":{"text":"","value":"+6","variable":"SAVE_WILL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"f798faff-c12a-4121-9554-c89e464786c4","data":{"value":48,"variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"af16f030-00ca-4097-9c16-f2aed6d51983","data":{"text":"","value":"+12","variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"d9404051-cd15-4cd5-a2f5-5fd2439a719b","data":{"text":"","value":"+2","variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"34b54155-f2da-4974-bbec-4b856802a6fa","data":{"text":"","value":"+2","variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"956c1090-3d88-4c73-bbbe-384738d7fa35","data":{"text":"","value":"+2","variable":"SKILL_INTIMIDATION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"7df8e7cf-e4d2-480b-b854-ca4989881e55","data":{"text":"","value":"+2","variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"785b4780-e3cd-4e7f-99f3-090813727908","data":{"text":"","value":"+2","variable":"SKILL_SURVIVAL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"roll_history":null,"abilities_base":[{"id":-1,"name":"Flying Strafe","type":"action","level":4,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The griffon Flies up to its fly Speed and makes two talon Strikes at any point during that movement. Each Strike must target a different creature. The attacks take the normal multiple attack penalty.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Pounce","type":"action","level":4,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The griffon Strides and makes a talon Strike at the end of that movement. If the griffon began this action \\[\\[Hidden\\]\\], it remains hidden until after the attack.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Regal Shriek","type":"action","level":4,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1486,1487,1448],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The griffon unleashes a shriek that transitions into a terrifying roar. Each creature in a @Template\\[emanation|distance:60\\] must attempt a @Check\\[will|dc:20\\] save. Regardless of the result, creatures are temporarily immune to all griffons' Regal Shrieks for 10 minutes.\n\n* * *\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is \\[\\[Frightened\\]\\]{Frightened 1}.\n\n**Failure** The creature is \\[\\[Frightened\\]\\]{Frightened 2}. Animals are \\[\\[Slowed\\]\\]{Slowed 1} for as long as they're frightened.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is \\[\\[Frightened\\]\\]{Frightened 3}. Animals are \\[\\[Paralyzed\\]\\] as long as they're frightened.","content_source_id":8}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":8},"after":{"id":10111,"name":"Griffon","type":"creature","uuid":"2338463709281465","level":4,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Griffon.webp","description":"Griffons are regal beasts revered as symbols of freedom and strength in many cultures. They are physically striking, with the hindquarters of a lion and the head, wings, and forelimbs of a great bird of prey—typically an eagle, but some instead bear the features of a hawk, falcon, or even an osprey or vulture. In rare cases, the griffon's hindquarters may resemble those of a different great cat, such as a leopard or tiger. The variations seem to conform to the griffon's environment—for instance, especially rare griffons of northern Avistan have the hindquarters of a Grungir lynx and the upper body of a snowy owl.\n\nWild griffons rely on their powerful wings to hold them aloft and their keen eyesight to spy out prey. The speed with which they plunge toward the ground and snatch up victims is astonishing. They often tear apart a kill's flesh with razor-sharp beaks but not before alighting to secluded location where they can enjoy their meal without interruption. Griffons hunting to feed their chicks are more cautious, tearing apart prey rather than risking bringing a living creature back to their nests.\n\nSkilled animal trainers long ago learned how to raise griffons as mounts for military forces or powerful individuals. Such mounts are known for their strength, bravery, and unfailing loyalty. They are among the smartest of animals, and many griffon variants are considered intelligent beasts instead; it's thought that a griffon chooses its rider as much as a rider chooses the griffon. The process of training a griffon to accept and carry a rider in flight is a long and expensive ordeal. Griffon trainers charge rich sums for their services, and a ruler who can boast of owning a stable of griffons is the subject of great respect and envy."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"e8b33460-8919-4d62-a6e8-a29883ef9906","item":{"id":2434909571025298,"name":"Beak","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1706],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d8","dice":2,"damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":10},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"0359bccc-2236-4603-bcf0-7de5a7303d10","item":{"id":4163315455953490,"name":"Talon","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":2,"damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":10},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"a679c72a-231a-4064-828b-eb6e1242aa45","item":{"id":3867369073430197,"name":"Wing","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":2,"damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":10},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=3034","book":"Monster Core","page":"182"}},"created_at":"2024-12-29T21:53:25.712618+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"