ata":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The imp regains 1d6 healing Hit Points.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Fiendish Temptation","type":"action","level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1475,1460,1846],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","frequency":"once per day","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The imp offers a nonfiend within 15 feet a bargain, granting a boon of good luck if the creature accepts voluntarily. The boon lasts for 1 hour once accepted.\n\nOnce during the hour, the creature can roll an attack roll or saving throw twice and use the higher result. If the creature dies while the boon is in place, the imp decides where the creature's soul travels. This typically makes the soul bound for eternity in the imp's home plane, and the creature unable to be raised or resurrected except by the \\[\\[Wish\\]\\] ritual or similar magic.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Imp Venom","type":"action","level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1476],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:16\\]\n\n* * *\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d6 poison damage and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 1} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 1d6 poison damage, clumsy 1, and \\[\\[Slowed\\]\\]{Slowed 1} (1 round)","content_source_id":8}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":8},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":10154,"type":"creature","before":{"id":10154,"name":"Jah-Tohl","type":"creature","uuid":"6781812251685666","level":8,"notes":null,"rarity":"UNCOMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Jah-Tohl.webp","description":"The grotesque jah-tohl arrive in living starships to harvest the brains of intelligent creatures. These aberrations draw no nutrition from brains, instead storing them for analysis and as vessels for occult energies.\n\nA mind snatcher's form evokes that of a tailless scorpion, but the pulsing brain-filled blisters that glisten along its back make them impossible to mistake for oversized arachnids. Baleful eyes glare from the joints on their legs, and the unsettling, intrusive whisper-thoughts they telepathically broadcast into the minds of those they seek to feed on can be interpreted as threats or promises alike.\n\nMind snatchers have little empathy for the denizens of any world they visit, despite the fact that certain cults venerate them and the Dominion they hail from. To mind snatchers, terrestrial creatures are simply resources for their investigations. They have little interest in gods or being worshipped, instead practicing a philosophy that considers the primordial forces of deep space as worthy of faith and fear. Jah-tohlian philosophers contemplate these mysterious forces from many perspectives at once, burning through numerous brains in the search of insight.\n\n* * *\n\nThe Dominion of the Black is a conglomeration of deep-space conquerors with a strong presence on Aucturn, the most remote planet in Golarion's solar system. The Dominion has secret outposts all over Golarion; most of its members on the planet are scouts, using their skills to steal brains and identities, gathering information without any consideration for the inhabitants of the worlds they infiltrate."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"1c0c69d4-fe87-45ae-97f5-cd7d3258b393","item":{"id":2153644354748883,"name":"Jaws","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d12","dice":2,"extra":"Brain Collector Venom","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":14},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"92012b57-96de-40e6-892d-71cb6ebc1884","item":{"id":7919656221965106,"name":"Claw","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d8","dice":2,"damageType":"slashing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":14},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=2930","book":"Monster Core","page":"106"}},"created_at":"2024-12-29T21:53:51.633791+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"ec7bcbc6-78d2-44ed-8f12-4bc0eac96c09","data":{"value":{"value":6,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"e0a5dbdf-2bda-435b-803f-8dfac58a67ee","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"20cd09ad-02e6-4657-93ee-0f623cf21f0b","data":{"value":{"value":5,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"2d6c8844-2f2a-40f7-b94e-8c457e916c8d","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"869e382b-5693-47e7-b1b5-1d70a3388542","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"da036fb3-7aec-4dc9-a4a1-10b895eac575","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"ff7b65de-e961-44e9-a815-6a0f7881daef","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"c19af8c3-2497-46e5-af57-224