t breathe and is immune to effects that require breathing (such as inhaled poisons).","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Excruciating Enzyme","type":"action","level":6,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1514,1476],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"A rhu-chalik's tendrils secrete an enzyme that causes intense pain. A living creature hit by a tendril Strike must succeed at a @Check\\[fortitude|dc:24\\] save or become \\[\\[Sickened\\]\\]{Sickened 1} from the pain.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Label Memories","type":"action","level":6,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1448,1514],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The rhu-chalik invades the mind of a target within 100 feet, sorting the memories into alien structures for transmission. The target must attempt a @Check\\[will|dc:24\\] save.\n\n* * *\n\n**Critical Success** The target creature is unaffected and temporarily immune to Label Memories for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes \\[\\[Stupefied\\]\\]{Stupefied 2} for 1 minute as its mind is reorganized to fit the rhu-chalik's needs. If it's already stupefied by this effect, the target instead becomes \\[\\[Confused\\]\\] for 1 minute or until it recovers due to taking damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but if the target is already stupefied by Label Memories, they become \\[\\[Paralyzed\\]\\] for 1 minute instead of confused.","content_source_id":8},{"id":-1,"name":"Transmit Memories","type":"action","level":6,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1448,1514],"actions":"THREE-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The rhu-chalik copies the creature's consciousness and mentally sends this copied consciousness through the void of space to their waiting masters. The target creature is deeply disoriented by this procedure, becoming \\[\\[Stupefied\\]\\]{Stupefied 2} for 1 day afterward.","requirements":"The rhu-chalik is adjacent to a creature [[Paralyzed]] due to Label Memories","content_source_id":8}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":8},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":10277,"type":"creature","before":{"id":10277,"name":"Roc","type":"creature","uuid":"6526793119185784","level":9,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"image_url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Images/Monsters/Roc.webp","description":"These legendary, massive raptors, capable of carrying off elephants as prey, are typically about 30 feet long from beak to tail and have a wingspan of 80 feet or more. While their beaks are hooked to rip flesh from bone, their hunting strategy involves grabbing their prey in their powerful talons and then dropping it from great heights before feeding. This method creates a massive amount of carrion, which guarantees that rocs are followed by flocks of opportunistic scavengers, such as ravens and buzzards, who find it easy to steal bits of the larger birds' meals. Rocs, for the most part, don't mind these creatures, which sometimes get gobbled up along with the rest of the roc's food.\n\nRocs usually nest among mountaintops and cliffs inaccessible to all but the bravest of terrestrial dwellers. They are long-range predators that hunt both land and sea in search for massive prey to sustain them and their young. Rocs are antisocial and lone hunters who compete with each other in fierce aerial battles to protect territory. But about once a decade, a mating couple pairs up to raise their chicks. Once the chicks are old enough to hunt on their own, the parents separate to once again engage in lone hunting.\n\nParticularly skilled druids or rangers might capture and train a roc to serve as a flying mount or hunting companion, though examples of such an incredible feat of domestication are few and far between. The easiest way to rear a roc is to do so from the moment it hatches, since the chick imprints on the first creature it sees. Acquiring a roc egg is by no means an easy feat, though, and is often a death sentence for the would-be egg-snatcher."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"a4ced9df-f35b-41ba-b9dc-b0cfdfdf25bb","item":{"id":283642099262927,"name":"Beak","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[4174],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":2,"extra":"4","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":13},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"dab6c467-a3b9-41a6-b248-e44a224412fd","item":{"id":8379144203641926,"name":"Talon","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,4174],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d8","dice":2,"extra":"4 + Improved Grab","damageType":"slashing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":13},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"7c63811e-5720-4eb6-ab4c-a87bc7b67de6","item":{"id":1368412962668360,"name":"Wing","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,4179],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":2,"extra":"2 + Improved Push","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":13},"create