a":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Regeneration","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Attack of Opportunity (Tail Only)","type":"action","level":19,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Tail only.\n\n* * *\n\nAttackOfOpportunity","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Curse of Endless Storms","type":"action","level":19,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1855,1576,1454],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"When a creature slays a taiga linnorm, it must succeed at a @Check\\[will|dc:46\\] save or permanently gain weakness 20 to electricity.","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Spines","type":"action","level":19,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Any creature that makes a melee attack against a taiga linnorm is stabbed by the taiga linnorm's spines and takes 1d6 piercing damage per attack. A melee weapon with reach protects the user against these spines.","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Breath Weapon","type":"action","level":19,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1576,1454],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The taiga linnorm breathes a @Template\\[cone|distance:60\\] of electrified vapor, dealing 20d6 electricity damage to creatures in the area (@Check\\[reflex|dc:41|basic\\] save). The electrified mist persists for \\[\\[/br 1d4 #rounds\\]\\]{1d4 rounds}, dealing 6d6 electricity damage (@Check\\[reflex|dc:41|basic\\] save) to each creature that ends its turn in the mist.\n\nThe taiga linnorm can't use Breath Weapon again for \\[\\[/br 1d4 #Recharge Breath Weapon\\]\\]{1d4 rounds}.","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Taiga Linnorm Venom","type":"action","level":19,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1576,1476],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:42\\]\n\n**Maximum Duration** 10 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 7d6 electricity damage and \\[\\[Drained\\]\\]{Drained 1} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 10d6 electricity damage and \\[\\[Drained\\]\\]{Drained 2} (1 round)","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Improved Grab","type":"action","level":19,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"ImprovedGrab","content_source_id":240}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":240},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":11195,"type":"creature","before":{"id":11195,"name":"Violet Fungus","type":"creature","uuid":"8171277498647651","level":3,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"description":"At a glance, a violet fungus might seem to be little more than an unsightly and sickeningly purple mushroom of unusual size. Only once one draws closer-once whip-like tentacles dripping with flesh-rotting venom slither out from the fungus's cratered cap-does the terrifying truth of this carnivorous toadstool become apparent. Many amateur spelunkers have met untimely ends in the clutches of this monstrous fungus's tentacles, since violet fungi are practically synonymous with caverns on Golarion.\n\nAnyone who has ever braved the world's caves for an extended period of time know the dangers of the deadly violet fungus. Darklands dwellers such as drow and duergars often bear the long, whip-like scars of at least one brush with this vicious plant's cruel, poison-infused tentacles. Canny subterranean trappers and scouts sometimes make use of cultivated violent fungi to catch game in the enormous caverns below the surface world. Some Darklands peoples also cultivate violet fungi as a means to defend their territory. Xulgaths in particular place violet fungi around the perimeters of their settlements as a first line of defense."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"87dc1378-79c3-48cf-a788-59680cb5b190","item":{"id":2013488871661870,"name":"Tentacle","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":1,"extra":"Violet Rot","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":7},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=853","book":"Bestiary 2","page":"286"}},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:18:19.97085+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"dd84ee8f-c0ed-439a-a46f-c8eab45c38d3","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"586ac2f5-b8bd-4407-b94f-1efbb3f1ddbb","data":{"value":{"value":0,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"72a27ddf-4da0-4655-82c1-771bf70ab513","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"b2674dc0-c84e-49cd-8fb7-7a6814355371","data":{"value":{"value":-5,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"78b2c27e-b417-4172-82b8-eadf6e3a6f56","data":{"value":{"value":1,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"3cc7b8fb-5d5b-4e0f-8009-83497f1a830b","data":{"value":{"value":-2,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"72bd439e-e12f-43d3-b653-717f7cf0ebce","dat