dBonusToValue"},{"id":"f7878fa8-2ab7-4e48-8fd7-d94e76f63ec2","data":{"value":51,"variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"b0168afa-bb34-42bc-bcbf-477fc6a26a73","data":{"text":"","value":"+7","variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"155823bb-5de3-47c5-8ec8-b34d55776f1a","data":{"text":"","value":"+4","variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"roll_history":null,"abilities_base":[{"id":-1,"name":"Tremorsense 60 feet","type":"action","level":3,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"interaction"}},"created_at":"","description":"Tremorsense","content_source_id":240},{"id":-1,"name":"Violet Rot","type":"action","level":3,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1476],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:20\\]\n\n* * *\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d6 poison damage plus \\[\\[Enfeebled\\]\\]{Enfeebled 1} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 1d6 poison damage plus enfeebled 1 and \\[\\[Drained\\]\\]{Drained 1} (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** 2d6 poison damage plus enfeebled 1 and drained 1 (1 round)","content_source_id":240}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":240},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":11759,"type":"creature","before":{"id":11759,"name":"Ouroboros","type":"creature","uuid":"8794877349107104","level":21,"notes":null,"rarity":"RARE","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"description":"Ouroboros are the embodiment of eternity. Though they're prevalent as a symbol, often scrawled across the margins of alchemical tomes, few know that the beasts actually exist in the Astral Plane, where they fly through the silvery-gray void like a serpentine wheel. The ouroboros is usually depicted as a snake devouring its tail. This circular symbol is synonymous with infinity, self-sufficiency, and eternal unity.\n\nAn ouroboros' form exemplifies the unfathomable concepts of forever. Its undulating body is composed of smaller serpents, who are in turn composed of ever smaller serpents, continuing indefinitely. These smaller components are recycled as the ouroboros devours its tail, existing in a perpetual, cyclical process of creation and destruction. It is a massive creature, forming a loop roughly 50 feet in diameter and weighing hundreds of tons.\n\nAn ouroboros's most striking feature is its ability to almost instantly grow new flesh and heal from nearly any wound. This profound regenerative ability comes in part from an ouroboros's magical blood, which is rumored to have many miraculous properties.\n\nThrough their inscrutable behavior suggests that an ouroboros is mindless, the creatures boast crude intellects and can understand speech, though they have no way to speak. They possess an instinctive, almost obsessive will to survive and defend themselves ferociously if threatened in even the slightest way. Often these perceived threats take the form of another creature simply existing within the ouroboros's line of sight, leading other Astral creatures to give these powerful beings a wide berth. The only creature an ouroboros reliably ignores is another ouroboros, but they're so incredibly rare that these meetings occur only once an age.\n\nBeing entirely self-sustaining, an ouroboros rarely deigns to emerge from its consumption to engage with the Material Plane. Yet, the creature remains capable of inflicting tremendous devastation that far surpasses what it could wreak leveraging only its massive size alone. Left to its own devices, an ouroboros is likely to simply roam the Astral Plane in eon-spanning cycles, following some pattern too long and large for any mortal to even chart, much less fully comprehend. When conjured to the Material Plane, however, an ouroboros eagerly begins to initiate the cycle of renewal for which it is best known, beginning with that cycle's first step: destruction."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"b9fe9f31-fd59-491f-9389-abb224e5baa2","item":{"id":288810885140686,"name":"Maw","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1504,4179],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d12","dice":4,"extra":"8 + Improved Grab","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":29},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"0a4956c9-c950-4aef-aaf7-4b8803fa1175","item":{"id":2259958961148464,"name":"Body","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1504,4175],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":4,"extra":"8","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":29},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"67eb09ce-345d-4333-8835-08cdeb59e0c8","item":{"id":3395099360373034,"name":"Incalculable Fangs","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,1504,4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":3,"extra":"6","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":27},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"239a154e-bd41-4a8a-afa7-697d601935d7","item":{"id":541299974078674,"name":"Tail","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1504,4179],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d12","dice":4,"extra":"8","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":29},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=1256","book":"Bestiary 3","page":"195"}},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:35:26.441892+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"88c6c8d9-784f-4890-adda-011872cc99be","data":{"value":{"value":10,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"abf81011-b1bf-43ad-afbe-1729937b37d8","data":{"value":{"value":5,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"a83f71d4-dc9a-4f41-98b1-417aca02ee67","data":{"value":{"value":7,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"0a5dffdb-911c-467b-9f6d-87bb501376e9","data":{"value":{"value":-4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"abf9f004-a9e0-438c-9ee8-683747b77231","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"13e3279e-a210-4099-b59c-1bb583b6ca7b","data":{"value":{"value":8,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"33d7dd25-404d-4232-be33-e6006727eeef","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"ed87bb35-4b8e-439d-9c4e-529481fd8b40","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_REFLEX"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"0edc7216-5ef2-4bfe-893f-595cd7f7c2ce","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_WILL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"3d60347a-ee97-48c3-91c3-f1ab8b048d9a","data":{"text":"regeneration 50 (deactivated by fire)","variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"5494bb58-540d-45b8-8043-73bf69b10467","data":{"value":"acid, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"2233e96a-5145-46cc-830a-c2479e1510fe","data":{"value":"death-effects, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"526139e7-e974-478e-8070-5381c15406c1","data":{"value":"disease, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"3ffeb6bc-7402-42ff-9b9d-36314e70f282","data":{"value":"void, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"1f617579-043c-4d40-a5dd-fcf2ffa87dc2","data":{"value":"poison, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"24693e8d-e5ec-43e6-8a11-18e728b5fd95","data":{"value":"precision, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9a435363-c2c2-4a79-b8e8-39e47c3e13dc","data":{"value":"piercing, 15","variable":"WEAKNESSES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"2dd09769-3043-4334-ad65-9b32fb2b10a9","data":{"value":"slashing, 15","variable":"WEAKNESSES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"f6d3e7bc-ecac-45ec-9e9d-1982ed7c7f79","data":{"value":100,"variable":"SPEED"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"17509966-6911-4b09-b1f4-22bf736c90ca","data":{"value":100,"variable":"SPEED_FLY"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"4af0ac0d-ce38-4478-9b18-d0b7815bca5e","data":{"languageId":93},"type":"giveLanguage"},{"id":"7b13f1f9-737e-490e-b135-26349602d586","data":{"value":"darkvision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"2e8a8cc3-d5df-422a-86e9-d66fa650f6b1","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"19068f79-168f-40ae-b23a-b1f6dd1de481","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"274eb42d-6bf6-4289-90b7-62e7b3269b82","data":{"value":"GARGANTUAN","variable":"SIZE"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"2be5cebf-787f-4e70-aa75-fa691b7805a6","data":{"traitId":2466},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"b7797c9b-8a52-48b7-89d1-bced3efc2218","data":{"traitId":2422},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"807ca3c0-d115-467a-b76d-55946ff1e410","data":{"value":30,"variable":"AC_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"b1884579-967d-463d-b9ad-e67a5300cd50","data":{"text":"","value":"+31","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"2018541a-56b7-4a38-87fc-5c483c2d2bfd","data":{"text":"","value":"+29","variable":"SAVE_REFLEX"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"712bf071-691e-490d-88a0-4fde1aab270b","data":{"text":"","value":"+29","variable":"SAVE_WILL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"55666a66-bf5e-4a43-80a3-5ab25a6e9e99","data":{"value":353,"variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9dc65374-49bc-46d5-8949-acdad2a82766","data":{"text":"","value":"+29","variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"78de6950-308f-4197-b712-5fabd1ffa24d","data":{"text":"","value":"+8","variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"ebb27074-962c-4dfa-9c47-87b5efbe6644","data":{"text":"","value":"+8","variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"roll_history":null,"abilities_base":[{"id":-1,"name":"Regeneration 50 (Deactivated by Fire)","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Regeneration","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Attack of Opportunity (Special)","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Incalculable Fangs Only\n\nBecause the ouroboros contains an infinite number of snakes that act independently, its Attack of Opportunity is a free action (though it can still use only one per trigger).\n\n* * *\n\nAttackOfOpportunity","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Sanguine Spray","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"When the ouroboros takes slashing or piercing damage, or when Devour Tail ends, blood gushes from the wound in a @Template\\[cone|distance:15\\]. Each creature in the area takes 5d6 acid damage (@Check\\[reflex|dc:41|basic\\] save). A creature that takes any damage is exposed to the ouroboros's regenerative blood.\n\nWhere the blood falls upon ground, it coagulates into magical snakes that bite at anyone who passes. This is hazardous terrain deals @Damage\\[17\\[piercing\\],5\\[poison\\]\\]{17 piercing damage and 5 poison damage} to any non-ouroboros creature that moves through the square or ends its turn there. A creature that avoids all the piercing damage doesn't take the poison damage. After 1 hour, a blood patch permanently becomes a living snake, typically an \\[\\[Emperor Cobra\\]\\].","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Unfathomable Infinity","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1492,1481,1448,1479],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"100 feet. The ouroboros is the embodiment of perfect infinity, and this concept pulls at the threads of mortal minds, desperately straining the limits of their comprehension. When a creature ends its turn in the aura, it must attempt a @Check\\[will|dc:41\\] save.\n\nThe creature is then temporarily immune for 1 minute.\n\n* * *\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is \\[\\[Stupefied\\]\\]{Stupefied 1} for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The creature is stupefied 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Failure** The creature is stupefied 1 for 1 minute and \\[\\[Stunned\\]\\]{Stunned 3}.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is \\[\\[Stupefied\\]\\]{Stupefied 3} and \\[\\[Stunned\\]\\], both for 1 minute.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Devour Tail","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"An ouroboros spend most of its life eating its own tail, which perpetually regrows at the same rate it's consumed. The ouroboros places its maw around the end of its tail and begins devouring its own body.\n\nWhile the ouroboros is consuming itself, its regeneration can't be suppressed, and it is immune to \\[\\[Drained\\]\\], \\[\\[Enfeebled\\]\\], \\[\\[Fatigued\\]\\], \\[\\[Persistent Damage\\]\\], and \\[\\[Sickened\\]\\] conditions. If any of these conditions is in effect when the ouroboros takes this action, the condition immediately ends.\n\nWhile eating its tail, the ouroboros can't make maw or tail strikes, and its Speeds are 50 feet. It continues devouring its tail even while \\[\\[Dying\\]\\], \\[\\[Unconscious\\]\\], \\[\\[Stunned\\]\\], or otherwise unable to act.\n\nTo end this effect, the ouroboros must first be \\[\\[Immobilized\\]\\], then a creature must successfully \\[\\[Grapple\\]\\] it, which tears the maw free in addition to its normal effects. The ouroboros can also cease Devouring its Tail with a single action. Either of these tears the maw free of the tail, causing the stump to spill blood as described in sanguine spray.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Fast Swallow","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","trigger":"The ouroboros [[Grabbed]]{Grabs} a creature with their maw","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The ouroboros uses Swallow Whole.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Flying Wheel","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** As Trample, except the ouroboros can Fly up to double its Speed instead of Striding.\n\nHuge or smaller, body, @Check\\[reflex|dc:45|basic\\]\n\n* * *\n\nTrample","requirements":"The ouroboros is eating its own tail (see Devour Tail)","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Regenerative Blood","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1566,1855,1481,1476,1453,1454],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The regenerative and transmutative properties of ouroboros blood regenerate and mutate a creature's body into ouroboros-like snakes. A creature already affected by regenerative blood is immune to additional exposure.\n\n**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:42\\]\n\n* * *\n\n**Maximum Duration** 24 hours\n\n**Stage 1** regeneration 5 (deactivated by fire), \\[\\[Slowed\\]\\]{Slowed 1}, and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 2} (12 hours)\n\n**Stage 2** regeneration 5 (deactivated by fire), \\[\\[Slowed\\]\\]{Slowed 2} and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 4} (12 hours)\n\n**Stage 3** The creature's body transmutes into a mass of writhing snakes, with the effects an 8th-rank \\[\\[Animal Form\\]\\] spell but with an unlimited duration.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Swallow Whole","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Huge, (4d10+9) acid, Rupture 50\n\n* * *\n\nSwallowWhole","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Improved Grab","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"ImprovedGrab","content_source_id":241}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":241},"after":{"id":11759,"name":"Ouroboros","type":"creature","uuid":"8794877349107104","level":21,"notes":null,"rarity":"RARE","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"description":"Ouroboros are the embodiment of eternity. Though they're prevalent as a symbol, often scrawled across the margins of alchemical tomes, few know that the beasts actually exist in the Astral Plane, where they fly through the silvery-gray void like a serpentine wheel. The ouroboros is usually depicted as a snake devouring its tail. This circular symbol is synonymous with infinity, self-sufficiency, and eternal unity.\n\nAn ouroboros' form exemplifies the unfathomable concepts of forever. Its undulating body is composed of smaller serpents, who are in turn composed of ever smaller serpents, continuing indefinitely. These smaller components are recycled as the ouroboros devours its tail, existing in a perpetual, cyclical process of creation and destruction. It is a massive creature, forming a loop roughly 50 feet in diameter and weighing hundreds of tons.\n\nAn ouroboros's most striking feature is its ability to almost instantly grow new flesh and heal from nearly any wound. This profound regenerative ability comes in part from an ouroboros's magical blood, which is rumored to have many miraculous properties.\n\nThrough their inscrutable behavior suggests that an ouroboros is mindless, the creatures boast crude intellects and can understand speech, though they have no way to speak. They possess an instinctive, almost obsessive will to survive and defend themselves ferociously if threatened in even the slightest way. Often these perceived threats take the form of another creature simply existing within the ouroboros's line of sight, leading other Astral creatures to give these powerful beings a wide berth. The only creature an ouroboros reliably ignores is another ouroboros, but they're so incredibly rare that these meetings occur only once an age.\n\nBeing entirely self-sustaining, an ouroboros rarely deigns to emerge from its consumption to engage with the Material Plane. Yet, the creature remains capable of inflicting tremendous devastation that far surpasses what it could wreak leveraging only its massive size alone. Left to its own devices, an ouroboros is likely to simply roam the Astral Plane in eon-spanning cycles, following some pattern too long and large for any mortal to even chart, much less fully comprehend. When conjured to the Material Plane, however, an ouroboros eagerly begins to initiate the cycle of renewal for which it is best known, beginning with that cycle's first step: destruction."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"b9fe9f31-fd59-491f-9389-abb224e5baa2","item":{"id":288810885140686,"name":"Maw","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1504,4179],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d12","dice":4,"extra":"8 + Improved Grab","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":29},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"0a4956c9-c950-4aef-aaf7-4b8803fa1175","item":{"id":2259958961148464,"name":"Body","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1504,4175],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":4,"extra":"8","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":29},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"67eb09ce-345d-4333-8835-08cdeb59e0c8","item":{"id":3395099360373034,"name":"Incalculable Fangs","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,1504,4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d6","dice":3,"extra":"6","damageType":"piercing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":27},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"239a154e-bd41-4a8a-afa7-697d601935d7","item":{"id":541299974078674,"name":"Tail","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1504,4179],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d12","dice":4,"extra":"8","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":29},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=1256","book":"Bestiary 3","page":"195"}},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:35:26.441892+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"88c6c8d9-784f-4890-adda-011872cc99be","data":{"value":{"value":10,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"abf81011-b1bf-43ad-afbe-1729937b37d8","data":{"value":{"value":5,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"a83f71d4-dc9a-4f41-98b1-417aca02ee67","data":{"value":{"value":7,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"0a5dffdb-911c-467b-9f6d-87bb501376e9","data":{"value":{"value":-4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"abf9f004-a9e0-438c-9ee8-683747b77231","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"13e3279e-a210-4099-b59c-1bb583b6ca7b","data":{"value":{"value":8,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"33d7dd25-404d-4232-be33-e6006727eeef","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"ed87bb35-4b8e-439d-9c4e-529481fd8b40","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_REFLEX"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"0edc7216-5ef2-4bfe-893f-595cd7f7c2ce","data":{"text":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","variable":"SAVE_WILL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"3d60347a-ee97-48c3-91c3-f1ab8b048d9a","data":{"text":"regeneration 50 (deactivated by fire)","variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"5494bb58-540d-45b8-8043-73bf69b10467","data":{"value":"acid, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"2233e96a-5145-46cc-830a-c2479e1510fe","data":{"value":"death-effects, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"526139e7-e974-478e-8070-5381c15406c1","data":{"value":"disease, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"3ffeb6bc-7402-42ff-9b9d-36314e70f282","data":{"value":"void, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"1f617579-043c-4d40-a5dd-fcf2ffa87dc2","data":{"value":"poison, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"24693e8d-e5ec-43e6-8a11-18e728b5fd95","data":{"value":"precision, ","variable":"IMMUNITIES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9a435363-c2c2-4a79-b8e8-39e47c3e13dc","data":{"value":"piercing, 15","variable":"WEAKNESSES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"2dd09769-3043-4334-ad65-9b32fb2b10a9","data":{"value":"slashing, 15","variable":"WEAKNESSES"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"f6d3e7bc-ecac-45ec-9e9d-1982ed7c7f79","data":{"value":100,"variable":"SPEED"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"17509966-6911-4b09-b1f4-22bf736c90ca","data":{"value":100,"variable":"SPEED_FLY"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"4af0ac0d-ce38-4478-9b18-d0b7815bca5e","data":{"languageId":93},"type":"giveLanguage"},{"id":"7b13f1f9-737e-490e-b135-26349602d586","data":{"value":"darkvision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"2e8a8cc3-d5df-422a-86e9-d66fa650f6b1","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"19068f79-168f-40ae-b23a-b1f6dd1de481","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"274eb42d-6bf6-4289-90b7-62e7b3269b82","data":{"value":"GARGANTUAN","variable":"SIZE"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"2be5cebf-787f-4e70-aa75-fa691b7805a6","data":{"traitId":2466},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"b7797c9b-8a52-48b7-89d1-bced3efc2218","data":{"traitId":2422},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"807ca3c0-d115-467a-b76d-55946ff1e410","data":{"value":30,"variable":"AC_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"b1884579-967d-463d-b9ad-e67a5300cd50","data":{"text":"","value":"+31","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"2018541a-56b7-4a38-87fc-5c483c2d2bfd","data":{"text":"","value":"+29","variable":"SAVE_REFLEX"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"712bf071-691e-490d-88a0-4fde1aab270b","data":{"text":"","value":"+29","variable":"SAVE_WILL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"55666a66-bf5e-4a43-80a3-5ab25a6e9e99","data":{"value":353,"variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"9dc65374-49bc-46d5-8949-acdad2a82766","data":{"text":"","value":"+29","variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"78de6950-308f-4197-b712-5fabd1ffa24d","data":{"text":"","value":"+8","variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"ebb27074-962c-4dfa-9c47-87b5efbe6644","data":{"text":"","value":"+8","variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"roll_history":null,"abilities_base":[{"id":-1,"name":"Regeneration 50 (Deactivated by Fire)","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Regeneration","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Attack of Opportunity (Special)","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Incalculable Fangs Only\n\nBecause the ouroboros contains an infinite number of snakes that act independently, its Attack of Opportunity is a free action (though it can still use only one per trigger).\n\n* * *\n\nAttackOfOpportunity","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Sanguine Spray","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"When the ouroboros takes slashing or piercing damage, or when Devour Tail ends, blood gushes from the wound in a @Template\\[cone|distance:15\\]. Each creature in the area takes 5d6 acid damage (@Check\\[reflex|dc:41|basic\\] save). A creature that takes any damage is exposed to the ouroboros's regenerative blood.\n\nWhere the blood falls upon ground, it coagulates into magical snakes that bite at anyone who passes. This is hazardous terrain deals @Damage\\[17\\[piercing\\],5\\[poison\\]\\]{17 piercing damage and 5 poison damage} to any non-ouroboros creature that moves through the square or ends its turn there. A creature that avoids all the piercing damage doesn't take the poison damage. After 1 hour, a blood patch permanently becomes a living snake, typically an \\[\\[Emperor Cobra\\]\\].","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Unfathomable Infinity","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1492,1481,1448,1479],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"100 feet. The ouroboros is the embodiment of perfect infinity, and this concept pulls at the threads of mortal minds, desperately straining the limits of their comprehension. When a creature ends its turn in the aura, it must attempt a @Check\\[will|dc:41\\] save.\n\nThe creature is then temporarily immune for 1 minute.\n\n* * *\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is \\[\\[Stupefied\\]\\]{Stupefied 1} for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The creature is stupefied 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Failure** The creature is stupefied 1 for 1 minute and \\[\\[Stunned\\]\\]{Stunned 3}.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is \\[\\[Stupefied\\]\\]{Stupefied 3} and \\[\\[Stunned\\]\\], both for 1 minute.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Devour Tail","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"An ouroboros spend most of its life eating its own tail, which perpetually regrows at the same rate it's consumed. The ouroboros places its maw around the end of its tail and begins devouring its own body.\n\nWhile the ouroboros is consuming itself, its regeneration can't be suppressed, and it is immune to \\[\\[Drained\\]\\], \\[\\[Enfeebled\\]\\], \\[\\[Fatigued\\]\\], \\[\\[Persistent Damage\\]\\], and \\[\\[Sickened\\]\\] conditions. If any of these conditions is in effect when the ouroboros takes this action, the condition immediately ends.\n\nWhile eating its tail, the ouroboros can't make maw or tail strikes, and its Speeds are 50 feet. It continues devouring its tail even while \\[\\[Dying\\]\\], \\[\\[Unconscious\\]\\], \\[\\[Stunned\\]\\], or otherwise unable to act.\n\nTo end this effect, the ouroboros must first be \\[\\[Immobilized\\]\\], then a creature must successfully \\[\\[Grapple\\]\\] it, which tears the maw free in addition to its normal effects. The ouroboros can also cease Devouring its Tail with a single action. Either of these tears the maw free of the tail, causing the stump to spill blood as described in sanguine spray.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Fast Swallow","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","trigger":"The ouroboros [[Grabbed]]{Grabs} a creature with their maw","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The ouroboros uses Swallow Whole.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Flying Wheel","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"TWO-ACTIONS","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** As Trample, except the ouroboros can Fly up to double its Speed instead of Striding.\n\nHuge or smaller, body, @Check\\[reflex|dc:45|basic\\]\n\n* * *\n\nTrample","requirements":"The ouroboros is eating its own tail (see Devour Tail)","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Regenerative Blood","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1566,1855,1481,1476,1453,1454],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The regenerative and transmutative properties of ouroboros blood regenerate and mutate a creature's body into ouroboros-like snakes. A creature already affected by regenerative blood is immune to additional exposure.\n\n**Saving Throw** @Check\\[fortitude|dc:42\\]\n\n* * *\n\n**Maximum Duration** 24 hours\n\n**Stage 1** regeneration 5 (deactivated by fire), \\[\\[Slowed\\]\\]{Slowed 1}, and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 2} (12 hours)\n\n**Stage 2** regeneration 5 (deactivated by fire), \\[\\[Slowed\\]\\]{Slowed 2} and \\[\\[Clumsy\\]\\]{Clumsy 4} (12 hours)\n\n**Stage 3** The creature's body transmutes into a mass of writhing snakes, with the effects an 8th-rank \\[\\[Animal Form\\]\\] spell but with an unlimited duration.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Swallow Whole","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"Huge, (4d10+9) acid, Rupture 50\n\n* * *\n\nSwallowWhole","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Improved Grab","type":"action","level":21,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"FREE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"ImprovedGrab","content_source_id":241}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":241},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"creature","id":11808,"type":"creature","before":{"id":11808,"name":"Skull Peeler","type":"creature","uuid":"6643953480484688","level":6,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"description":"Skull peelers, despite their ferocious and well-deserved moniker, are considered by many to be downright adorable, especially when viewed from a safe distance. Their soft, dappled brown fur helps them hide in forest canopies, and they have shimmering insectile wings and big eyes that draw in the faintest beams of light. At first glance, a skull peeler looks like a cuddly pet or a wizard's familiar. Any illusions of domesticating such a beast are quickly dismissed upon seeing how a skull peeler eats, however.\n\nSkull peelers have evolved to hang motionlessly in treetop canopies as they wait until appropriate prey appears, usually long-necked dinosaurs but also brachiating primates and large birds. The skull peeler then lashes out with its long tongue, severing the creature's head from its body and pulling the detached cranium back into its hungry paws. It then uses its claws to crack open the cranial cavity-hence its name-before lapping up the tasty insides.\n\nDespite skull peelers' gruesome eating habits, some enterprises and individuals can't resist the urge to add these beasts to their menageries. Fey and other creatures with ties to the First World, such as gnomes, can occasionally coax a skull peeler into a form of domestication. While the adorable beasts can never be fully tamed due to their hyper-evolved hunting instincts, they can be bribed with food and, if kept satiated, displayed on a perch or indoor terrarium as an example of their master's cunning and deadliness. As often as not, these pseudo-domesticated skull peelers end up devouring a guest, pet, or their would-be owner, but this possibility doesn't stop up-and-coming crime lords from attempting to domesticate the little predators. Skull peelers kept in well-managed zoos fare somewhat better, but these clever creatures don't always stay in their cages, which has led to wild skull peelers in places travelers might not expect."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"9e670a49-65b2-4e2b-bd59-69fe1b4041bb","item":{"id":8216743901542927,"name":"Tongue","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,1670,4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d4","dice":2,"extra":"3","damageType":"slashing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":12},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"f6d22c8b-b3c4-4be2-9685-8572f91c68fc","item":{"id":3861899754629357,"name":"Claw","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":2,"extra":"3","damageType":"slashing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":12},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=1306","book":"Bestiary 3","page":"243"}},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:35:53.827273+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"3146617a-b116-4854-bde4-8a030b50bd53","data":{"value":{"value":5,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_STR"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"6760c573-0405-46a4-a6d0-ecce701c1f0e","data":{"value":{"value":4,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_DEX"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"b66d15f8-3a1d-4091-b220-2f991997dac2","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CON"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"b633fe59-1429-4e85-b0d1-dddc62ba7f3a","data":{"value":{"value":-3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_INT"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"4cc03fc7-018f-4d5f-bf74-2678e995bdc4","data":{"value":{"value":3,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_WIS"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"f2c85355-9c96-48f1-af3f-28e08c49e1de","data":{"value":{"value":1,"partial":false},"variable":"ATTRIBUTE_CHA"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"1251756a-5272-40f2-94a5-d1927d8f3cae","data":{"value":20,"variable":"SPEED"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"da1b98d3-fbdf-4766-8825-baab0ba6acad","data":{"value":15,"variable":"SPEED_CLIMB"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"115d10f2-2495-4229-a13f-f031851c68dd","data":{"value":10,"variable":"SPEED_FLY"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"71d9c3c3-a081-4d0e-82c1-5df71481fa9a","data":{"value":"low-light-vision","variable":"SENSES_PRECISE"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"dc915404-7900-49a5-9d1d-4f8c590936bf","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"a7df2bc6-50aa-4efc-9c01-2c1ef3f0f639","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"cf6d9eab-1e29-4706-94fa-974cac117e03","data":{"value":{"value":"T"},"variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"57b0fa49-036f-4292-8ce5-ad0c8f31665b","data":{"value":"SMALL","variable":"SIZE"},"type":"setValue"},{"id":"0df17b7c-5fb6-44c9-8d9e-96770e1d8b11","data":{"traitId":2422},"type":"giveTrait"},{"id":"a51d0842-e8ec-40f5-9a21-4154645e8096","data":{"value":10,"variable":"AC_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"baaa8b19-aa16-4779-b9b3-e55aac88464d","data":{"text":"","value":"+10","variable":"SAVE_FORT"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"b5be7f2a-c69d-470f-9409-99fe9517a8a1","data":{"text":"","value":"+12","variable":"SAVE_REFLEX"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"fe8b117d-a965-43a1-ae44-a756966ad743","data":{"text":"","value":"+8","variable":"SAVE_WILL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"58506dfa-9b0d-4bb3-bdc2-bfd797aa7d3d","data":{"value":57,"variable":"MAX_HEALTH_BONUS"},"type":"adjValue"},{"id":"882c3d9f-16ab-4475-b9ee-bc57a4cc9886","data":{"text":"","value":"+14","variable":"PERCEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"947bc064-c580-437a-85be-bc436e093bbc","data":{"text":"","value":"+0","variable":"SKILL_ACROBATICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"8df18ebf-54ce-4eb1-acb0-e529ec3038a0","data":{"text":"","value":"+2","variable":"SKILL_ATHLETICS"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"a064a02f-30bf-4354-b7bb-a0b7a204dd45","data":{"text":"","value":"+4","variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"roll_history":null,"abilities_base":[{"id":-1,"name":"Snatch Skull","type":"action","level":6,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":"REACTION","trigger":"The skull peeler is using Perfect Camouflage and a creature moves into a space within 15 feet of it","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"defensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** The skull peeler Leaps toward the triggering creature and Strikes with its tongue. If this Strike is successful, the skull peeler automatically \\[\\[Grab\\]\\]{Grabs} the target with its tongue.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Anticoagulant","type":"action","level":6,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"actions":null,"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"The skull peeler's razor-sharp tongue is coated in an anticoagulant substance that makes wounds it inflicts particularly hard to close.\n\nThe DC of the flat check to end the persistent bleed damage from a skull peeler's tongue is @Check\\[flat|dc:16\\], or @Check\\[flat|dc:11\\] with appropriate assistance.","content_source_id":241},{"id":-1,"name":"Perfect Camouflage","type":"action","level":6,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"actions":"ONE-ACTION","version":"1.0","meta_data":{"foundry":{"category":"offensive"}},"created_at":"","description":"* * *\n\n**Effect** Until the next time it acts, the skull peeler hangs perfectly still, blending into the treetop surroundings. It has an automatic result of 36 on Stealth checks and DCs to \\[\\[Hide\\]\\] from any creature more than 10 feet away from it.","requirements":"The skull peeler is in a treetop or standing on a tree limb","content_source_id":241}],"operation_data":null,"abilities_added":null,"resolve_current":null,"stamina_current":null,"content_source_id":241},"after":{"id":11808,"name":"Skull Peeler","type":"creature","uuid":"6643953480484688","level":6,"notes":null,"rarity":"COMMON","spells":{"list":[],"slots":[],"innate_casts":[],"focus_point_current":0},"details":{"description":"Skull peelers, despite their ferocious and well-deserved moniker, are considered by many to be downright adorable, especially when viewed from a safe distance. Their soft, dappled brown fur helps them hide in forest canopies, and they have shimmering insectile wings and big eyes that draw in the faintest beams of light. At first glance, a skull peeler looks like a cuddly pet or a wizard's familiar. Any illusions of domesticating such a beast are quickly dismissed upon seeing how a skull peeler eats, however.\n\nSkull peelers have evolved to hang motionlessly in treetop canopies as they wait until appropriate prey appears, usually long-necked dinosaurs but also brachiating primates and large birds. The skull peeler then lashes out with its long tongue, severing the creature's head from its body and pulling the detached cranium back into its hungry paws. It then uses its claws to crack open the cranial cavity-hence its name-before lapping up the tasty insides.\n\nDespite skull peelers' gruesome eating habits, some enterprises and individuals can't resist the urge to add these beasts to their menageries. Fey and other creatures with ties to the First World, such as gnomes, can occasionally coax a skull peeler into a form of domestication. While the adorable beasts can never be fully tamed due to their hyper-evolved hunting instincts, they can be bribed with food and, if kept satiated, displayed on a perch or indoor terrarium as an example of their master's cunning and deadliness. As often as not, these pseudo-domesticated skull peelers end up devouring a guest, pet, or their would-be owner, but this possibility doesn't stop up-and-coming crime lords from attempting to domesticate the little predators. Skull peelers kept in well-managed zoos fare somewhat better, but these clever creatures don't always stay in their cages, which has led to wild skull peelers in places travelers might not expect."},"hp_temp":null,"version":"1.0","inventory":{"coins":{"cp":0,"gp":0,"pp":0,"sp":0},"items":[{"id":"9e670a49-65b2-4e2b-bd59-69fe1b4041bb","item":{"id":8216743901542927,"name":"Tongue","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,1670,4173],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d4","dice":2,"extra":"3","damageType":"slashing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":12},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]},{"id":"f6d22c8b-b3c4-4be2-9685-8572f91c68fc","item":{"id":3861899754629357,"name":"Claw","size":"MEDIUM","group":"WEAPON","level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","damage":{"die":"d10","dice":2,"extra":"3","damageType":"slashing"},"reload":"null","foundry":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","quantity":1,"attack_bonus":12},"created_at":"","operations":[],"description":"","content_source_id":1},"is_formula":false,"is_equipped":true,"is_invested":false,"is_implanted":false,"container_contents":[]}]},"meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Monsters.aspx?ID=1306","book":"Bestiary 3","page":"243"}},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:35:53.827273+00:00","deprecated":null,"experience":null,"hp_current":null,"operations":[{"id":"3146617a-b116-4854-bde4-8a030b50bd53","data":{"value":{"value":5,"partial":false},"var