son](link_trait_1476) damage.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** The ribs from the armor spread into functional spider limbs. For 1 minute, you gain a climb Speed equal to half your land Speed and have your limbs free as you [Climb](link_action_19612). If you use all your free limbs to help you [Climb](link_action_19612), your climb Speed equals your land Speed.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"The initial raw materials must include four intact legs from an [giant tarantula](link_creature_10083)."},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11710,"type":"item","before":{"id":11710,"bulk":"1","name":"Arboreal Staff","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6098057913523335","group":"WEAPON","hands":null,"level":12,"price":{"gp":1750},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1613,1504,1454,1546,1831],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"club","range":null,"runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0},"damage":{"die":"d4","dice":1,"damageType":"bludgeoning"},"hp_max":0,"reload":"","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4921","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"193"},"foundry":{"bonus":0,"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","value":2,"selector":"skill-check","predicate":[{"or":["target:trait:plant","target:trait:fungus"]},{"or":["action:recall-knowledge","action:identify"]}]}],"bonus_damage":0,"container_id":null,"splash_damage":0},"category":"simple","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":"staff","broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:03.036959+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Perception** +25; precise vision ([low-light](link_sense_19330)) 60 feet, imprecise [hearing](link_sense_21081) 30 feet, imprecise [tremorsense](link_sense_21079) 30 feet (only when touching the ground)\n\n**Communication** speech ([Arboreal](link_language_663), [Common](link_language_81), [Fey](link_language_90); *[speak with plants](link_spell_4848)*)\n\n**Skills** Diplomacy +22, Forest Lore +25, Nature +25\n\n**Int** +4, **Wis** +6, **Cha** +4\n\n**Will** +27\n\nRather than passing on when they feel their death approaching, a rare few elderly arboreals undergo a ritual of preservation. This rite fuses the arboreal's consciousness into a branch, allowing their spirit to live on within the object. The branch functions as a [greater verdant staff](link_item_7915), though the arboreal spirit allows only partners willing to safeguard nature to use the staff's spells. An arboreal who decides to become an [arboreal staff](link_item_11710) is more connected to shorter-lived species than others of their kind. Most choose to endure to share their knowledge with future generations, but they take a long view in ways that can be frustrating to their wielders.\n\nIn addition to the activation and spells of a [greater verdant staff](link_item_7915), an [arboreal staff](link_item_11710) can cast the spells it holds as if it were the staff's wielder, though it usually does so only to benefit a partner. The staff also has *[earthbind](link_spell_4588)* available as a 3rd-rank spell.\n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611)\n\n**Effect** You expend a number of charges from the staff to [Cast a spell](link_action_19611) from its list.\n\n*   **Cantrip** *[tangle vine](link_spell_4888)*\n*   **1st** *[runic body](link_spell_4812)*, *[runic weapon](link_spell_4813)*\n*   **2nd** *[entangling flora](link_spell_4602)*, *[oaken resilience](link_spell_4744)*, *[one with plants](link_spell_4746)*, *[shape wood](link_spell_4827)*\n*   **3rd** *[wall of thorns](link_spell_4945)*, *[speak with plants](link_spell_4848)*, *[earthbind](link_spell_4588)*\n*   **4th** *[oaken resilience](link_spell_4744)*, *[speak with plants](link_spell_4848)*\n*   **5th** *[plant form](link_spell_4774)*, *[wall of thorns](link_spell_4945)*","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"Supply one casting of all listed levels of all listed spells."},"after":{"id":11710,"bulk":"1","name":"Arboreal Staff","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6098057913523335","group":"WEAPON","hands":null,"level":12,"price":{"gp":1750},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1613,1504,1454,1546,1831],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"club","range":null,"runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0},"damage":{"die":"d4","dice":1,"damageType":"bludgeoning"},"hp_max":0,"reload":"","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4921","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"193"},"foundry":{"bonus":0,"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"circumstance","value":2,"selector":"skill-check","predicate":[{"or":["target:trait:plant","target:trait:fungus"]},{"or":["action:recall-knowledge","action:identify"]}]}],"bonus_damage":0,"container_id":null,"splash_damage":0},"category":"simple","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":"staff","broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:03.036959+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Perception** +25; precise vision ([low-light](link_sense_19330)) 60 feet, imprecise [hearing](link_sense_21081) 30 feet, imprecise [tremorsense](link_sense_21079) 30 feet (only when touching the ground)\n\n**Communication** speech ([Arboreal](link_language_663), [Common](link_language_81), [Fey](link_language_90); *[speak with plants](link_spell_4848)*)\n\n**Skills** Diplomacy +22, Forest Lore +25, Nature +25\n\n**Int** +4, **Wis** +6, **Cha** +4\n\n**Will** +27\n\nRather than passing on when they feel their death approaching, a rare few elderly arboreals undergo a ritual of preservation. This rite fuses the arboreal's consciousness into a branch, allowing their spirit to live on within the object. The branch functions as a [greater verdant staff](link_item_7915), though the arboreal spirit allows only partners willing to safeguard nature to use the staff's spells. An arboreal who decides to become an [arboreal staff](link_item_11710) is more connected to shorter-lived species than others of their kind. Most choose to endure to share their knowledge with future generations, but they take a long view in ways that can be frustrating to their wielders.\n\nIn addition to the activation and spells of a [greater verdant staff](link_item_7915), an [arboreal staff](link_item_11710) can cast the spells it holds as if it were the staff's wielder, though it usually does so only to benefit a partner. The staff also has *[earthbind](link_spell_4588)* available as a 3rd-rank spell.\n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611)\n\n**Effect** You expend a number of charges from the staff to [Cast a spell](link_action_19611) from its list.\n\n*   **Cantrip** *[tangle vine](link_spell_4888)*\n*   **1st** *[runic body](link_spell_4812)*, *[runic weapon](link_spell_4813)*\n*   **2nd** *[entangling flora](link_spell_4602)*, *[oaken resilience](link_spell_4744)*, *[one with plants](link_spell_4746)*, *[shape wood](link_spell_4827)*\n*   **3rd** *[wall of thorns](link_spell_4945)*, *[speak with plants](link_spell_4848)*, *[earthbind](link_spell_4588)*\n*   **4th** *[oaken resilience](link_spell_4744)*, *[speak with plants](link_spell_4848)*\n*   **5th** *[plant form](link_spell_4774)*, *[wall of thorns](link_spell_4945)*","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"Supply one casting of all listed levels of all listed spells."},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11711,"type":"item","before":{"id":11711,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Architect's Pattern Book","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3846293505399428","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":6,"price":{"gp":240},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2855,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4705","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"110"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:03.61484+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Typically created by [wizards](link_class_26) who are hobbyists or professional architects, an [architect's pattern book](link_item_11711) allows the caster to customize certain spells that create [magical](link_trait_1504) [structures](link_trait_1600) or domiciles, adding recreational areas such as an indoor bathhouse, gaming room, swimming pool, or similar luxury.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">4</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [spellshape](link_trait_1465)); **Frequency** once per week; **Effect** If your next action is to cast a *[cozy cabin](link_spell_4541)*, *[planar palace](link_spell_4770)*, or *[resplendent mansion](link_spell_6762)* spell, you add a room to the structure that is up to 10 feet per side per rank of the spell. This room is outfitted with all the accoutrements for a particular type of recreation, determined by you when you cast the spell. Any character who spends at least 1 hour using this recreational facility and then sleeps a full 8 hours inside the location created by the spell is exceptionally well-rested. They regain double the amount of Hit Points they would normally receive for an 8-hour rest, and when they make the next day's preparations, they gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks and Will saves for the next 12 hours.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11711,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Architect's Pattern Book","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3846293505399428","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":6,"price":{"gp":240},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2855,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4705","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"110"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:03.61484+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Typically created by [wizards](link_class_26) who are hobbyists or professional architects, an [architect's pattern book](link_item_11711) allows the caster to customize certain spells that create [magical](link_trait_1504) [structures](link_trait_1600) or domiciles, adding recreational areas such as an indoor bathhouse, gaming room, swimming pool, or similar luxury.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">4</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [spellshape](link_trait_1465)); **Frequency** once per week; **Effect** If your next action is to cast a *[cozy cabin](link_spell_4541)*, *[planar palace](link_spell_4770)*, or *[resplendent mansion](link_spell_6762)* spell, you add a room to the structure that is up to 10 feet per side per rank of the spell. This room is outfitted with all the accoutrements for a particular type of recreation, determined by you when you cast the spell. Any character who spends at least 1 hour using this recreational facility and then sleeps a full 8 hours inside the location created by the spell is exceptionally well-rested. They regain double the amount of Hit Points they would normally receive for an 8-hour rest, and when they make the next day's preparations, they gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks and Will saves for the next 12 hours.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11712,"type":"item","before":{"id":11712,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Armbands of the Gorgon","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5234565442309159","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":17,"price":{"gp":15000},"usage":"worn armbands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1552,1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4666","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"102"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"AdjustDegreeOfSuccess","type":"save","selector":"saving-throw","predicate":["incapacitation"],"adjustment":{"success":"one-degree-better"}}],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:04.372379+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Each of these shining, bluish-gray metal armbands is adorned with the plated visage of a [gorgon's](link_creature_11012) head. When targeted by a spell or effect with the [incapacitation](link_trait_1481) effect, you treat the result of your save as if it were one degree of success better, and the result of any check made to inflict such an effect on you as one degree of success worse (as if you were more than twice the rank of the spell or effect targeting you). When you [invest](link_action_20775) the armbands, you either increase your Constitution modifier by 1 or increase it to +4, whichever would give you a higher value.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You clap the bracers together and remove a single condition of your choice currently afflicting you. If the condition is permanent, it's instead suppressed for 1 hour.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11712,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Armbands of the Gorgon","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5234565442309159","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":17,"price":{"gp":15000},"usage":"worn armbands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1552,1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4666","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"102"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"AdjustDegreeOfSuccess","type":"save","selector":"saving-throw","predicate":["incapacitation"],"adjustment":{"success":"one-degree-better"}}],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:04.372379+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Each of these shining, bluish-gray metal armbands is adorned with the plated visage of a [gorgon's](link_creature_11012) head. When targeted by a spell or effect with the [incapacitation](link_trait_1481) effect, you treat the result of your save as if it were one degree of success better, and the result of any check made to inflict such an effect on you as one degree of success worse (as if you were more than twice the rank of the spell or effect targeting you). When you [invest](link_action_20775) the armbands, you either increase your Constitution modifier by 1 or increase it to +4, whichever would give you a higher value.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You clap the bracers together and remove a single condition of your choice currently afflicting you. If the condition is permanent, it's instead suppressed for 1 hour.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11713,"type":"item","before":{"id":11713,"bulk":"0","name":"Armor Latches","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1443112656615971","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":4},"usage":"applied-to-armor","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2858],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4357","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"11"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:06.34513+00:00","operations":null,"description":"This armor is easily doffed. A set of armor with [armor latches](link_item_11713) gains the [noisy](link_trait_1582) trait; you can't add latches to armor that already possesses the [noisy](link_trait_1582) trait. You can remove a set of armor with [armor latches](link_item_11713) with a 3-action activity, which has the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait. This doesn't affect the time it takes to don the armor.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11713,"bulk":"0","name":"Armor Latches","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1443112656615971","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":4},"usage":"applied-to-armor","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2858],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4357","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"11"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:06.34513+00:00","operations":null,"description":"This armor is easily doffed. A set of armor with [armor latches](link_item_11713) gains the [noisy](link_trait_1582) trait; you can't add latches to armor that already possesses the [noisy](link_trait_1582) trait. You can remove a set of armor with [armor latches](link_item_11713) with a 3-action activity, which has the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait. This doesn't affect the time it takes to don the armor.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11714,"type":"item","before":{"id":11714,"bulk":"0","name":"Armory Bracelet (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6981190099351577","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":11,"price":{"gp":1350},"usage":"worn","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4872","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"153"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:06.915044+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Several small charms shaped like weapons hang from an _[armory bracelet](link_item_11714)_, which is often brass. The bracelet has one charm each for the groups bow, brawling, club, dart, flail, hammer, knife, pick, polearm, shield, sling, spear, and sword. Rare versions of the [armory bracelet](link_item_11714) include charms for firearms.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You pull one charm from the bracelet. The charm transforms into a weapon of your choice from the charm's weapon group. If the weapon requires ammunition, it appears with a quiver or pouch with 20 pieces of ammunition for the weapon. The weapon is a _[+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860)_ weapon of the type you chose. After 1 minute, the weapon transforms into a _[+2](link_item_7951) [striking](link_item_7862)_ weapon and remains until your next daily preparations. At that point, the weapon and any remaining ammunition crumble to dust and all the charms reappear on the bracelet. The weapon and ammunition created with the charm are noticeably different from others and can't be sold.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11714,"bulk":"0","name":"Armory Bracelet (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6981190099351577","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":11,"price":{"gp":1350},"usage":"worn","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4872","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"153"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:06.915044+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Several small charms shaped like weapons hang from an _[armory bracelet](link_item_11714)_, which is often brass. The bracelet has one charm each for the groups bow, brawling, club, dart, flail, hammer, knife, pick, polearm, shield, sling, spear, and sword. Rare versions of the [armory bracelet](link_item_11714) include charms for firearms.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You pull one charm from the bracelet. The charm transforms into a weapon of your choice from the charm's weapon group. If the weapon requires ammunition, it appears with a quiver or pouch with 20 pieces of ammunition for the weapon. The weapon is a _[+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860)_ weapon of the type you chose. After 1 minute, the weapon transforms into a _[+2](link_item_7951) [striking](link_item_7862)_ weapon and remains until your next daily preparations. At that point, the weapon and any remaining ammunition crumble to dust and all the charms reappear on the bracelet. The weapon and ammunition created with the charm are noticeably different from others and can't be sold.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11715,"type":"item","before":{"id":11715,"bulk":"0","name":"Armory Bracelet (Lesser)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7846580371922098","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":150},"usage":"worn","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4872","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"153"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:07.505067+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Several small charms shaped like weapons hang from an _[armory bracelet](link_item_11715)_, which is often brass. The bracelet has one charm each for the groups bow, brawling, club, dart, flail, hammer, knife, pick, polearm, shield, sling, spear, and sword. Rare versions of the [armory bracelet](link_item_11715) include charms for firearms.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433)) **Frequency** Once per day;\n\n**Effect** You pull one charm from the bracelet. The charm transforms into a weapon of your choice from the charm's weapon group. If the weapon requires ammunition, it appears with a quiver or pouch with 20 pieces of ammunition for the weapon. The weapon is a [_+1_](link_item_7950) [_striking_](link_item_7862) weapon of the type you chose. After 1 minute, the weapon transforms into a [_+1_](link_item_7950) weapon and remains until your next daily preparations. At that point, the weapon and any remaining ammunition crumble to dust and all the charms reappear on the bracelet. The weapon and ammunition created with the charm are noticeably different from others and can't b