re Vault (Remastered)","page":"120"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:34.379223+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A [fauna guardian](link_item_11798) is a [tattoo](link_trait_2857) of an [animal](link_trait_2409), which you can temporarily animate to protect you. The [animal](link_trait_2409) must be chosen when you get the [tattoo](link_trait_2857), and can be any [animal](link_trait_2409) of 4th level or lower. (Your GM might allow other options.)\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"THREE-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">3</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)) **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You animate your [tattoo](link_trait_2857) using the duration and other parameters of a 5th-rank *[summon animal](link_spell_4866)* spell. It appears in a space adjacent to you. If your [tattoo](link_trait_2857) [animal](link_trait_2409) drops to 0 HP, the activation ends, and the inanimate [tattoo](link_trait_2857) returns to your skin.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11798,"bulk":"0","name":"Fauna Guardian","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"2751643598725950","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":675},"usage":"tattooed on the body","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2205","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"120"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:34.379223+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A [fauna guardian](link_item_11798) is a [tattoo](link_trait_2857) of an [animal](link_trait_2409), which you can temporarily animate to protect you. The [animal](link_trait_2409) must be chosen when you get the [tattoo](link_trait_2857), and can be any [animal](link_trait_2409) of 4th level or lower. (Your GM might allow other options.)\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"THREE-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">3</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)) **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You animate your [tattoo](link_trait_2857) using the duration and other parameters of a 5th-rank *[summon animal](link_spell_4866)* spell. It appears in a space adjacent to you. If your [tattoo](link_trait_2857) [animal](link_trait_2409) drops to 0 HP, the activation ends, and the inanimate [tattoo](link_trait_2857) returns to your skin.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11799,"type":"item","before":{"id":11799,"bulk":"1","name":"Bow Staff","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7705002447218636","group":"WEAPON","hands":"2","level":0,"price":{"gp":8},"usage":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[3369,1570,3630,1572,1562],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":12,"bulk":{},"group":"club","range":"","runes":{"property":[]},"damage":{"die":"d6","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"hp_max":12,"reload":"","charges":{},"foundry":{"bonus":0,"items":[],"rules":[],"bonus_damage":0,"container_id":null,"splash_damage":0},"category":"martial","hardness":3,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"grade":null,"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":6,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Weapons.aspx?ID=344","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"31"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:35.330207+00:00","operations":[{"id":"0393fbe5-684f-43b2-bb75-c273827c552c","data":{"itemId":19871},"type":"giveItem"}],"description":"**Ammunition** [Arrows](link_item_6722)\n\n* * *\n\nThe [bow staff](link_item_11799) is a [whipstaff](link_item_12720) with a retracting spool of wire inside a metal cap on one end and a hooked protrusion on the other. A wielder trained in the weapon's use can quickly spool and attach or detach the wire to transition the weapon between bow and staff functionality.\n\n* * *\n\n_Combination Weapon:_ **_Melee_**_,_ [_Ranged_](link_item_19871)\n\n* * *\n\n### Ranged\n\n[Deadly d8](link_trait_1852), [Monk](link_trait_3630)  \n**Damage** 1d6 P  \n**Range** 80 ft.  \n**Reload** 0  \n**Group** Bow","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11799,"bulk":"1","name":"Bow Staff","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7705002447218636","group":"WEAPON","hands":"2","level":0,"price":{"gp":8},"usage":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[3369,1570,3630,1572,1562],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":12,"bulk":{},"group":"club","range":"","runes":{"property":[]},"damage":{"die":"d6","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":"bludgeoning"},"hp_max":12,"reload":"","charges":{},"foundry":{"bonus":0,"items":[],"rules":[],"bonus_damage":0,"container_id":null,"splash_damage":0},"category":"martial","hardness":3,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"grade":null,"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":6,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Weapons.aspx?ID=344","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"31"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:35.330207+00:00","operations":[{"id":"0393fbe5-684f-43b2-bb75-c273827c552c","data":{"itemId":19871},"type":"giveItem"}],"description":"**Ammunition** [Arrows](link_item_6722)\n\n* * *\n\nThe [bow staff](link_item_11799) is a [whipstaff](link_item_12720) with a retracting spool of wire inside a metal cap on one end and a hooked protrusion on the other. A wielder trained in the weapon's use can quickly spool and attach or detach the wire to transition the weapon between bow and staff functionality.\n\n* * *\n\n_Combination Weapon:_ **_Melee_**_,_ [_Ranged_](link_item_19871)\n\n* * *\n\n### Ranged\n\n[Deadly d8](link_trait_1852), [Monk](link_trait_3630)  \n**Damage** 1d6 P  \n**Range** 80 ft.  \n**Reload** 0  \n**Group** Bow","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11800,"type":"item","before":{"id":11800,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Bower Fruit","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3635572786249603","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":13,"price":{},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1531,1558,1454],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4904","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"190"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:35.961767+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n_[Bower fruit](link_item_11800)_ got its name from its association with the Green Mother, a [fey](link_trait_2021) Eldest with a fondness for plants and manipulation, whose domain is known as the Hanging Bower. She uses these cursed fruits to keep mortals in her thrall, but it's unknown whether she created them or simply popularized their use.\n\nA _[bower fruit](link_item_11800)_ condemns a non-[fey](link_trait_2021) who tastes it to never again be satisfied with the fare found in the mundane Universe. Any fruit can be cursed in this manner, but stone fruits such as peaches, plums, mangoes, and lychees are most common. Upon activating a [bower fruit](link_item_11800) by eating it, you’re afflicted with the [curse](link_trait_1855) of decadence. You can’t recover from stage 1 of the [curse](link_trait_1855) naturally, even if you succeed at the save to do so.\n\n**Curse of Decadence** ([curse](link_trait_1855)) **Saving Throw** DC 30 Fortitude\n\n**Stage 1** You’re afflicted by hunger as if you hadn’t eaten food in days. You become fatigued and take 1d4 damage each day that can’t be healed until you sate your hunger. No amount of eating food can sate your hunger during the spell’s duration, with one exception—food from the First World sates your hunger and suppresses the effects, but permanently increases the save DC by 1 (to a maximum of DC 35). After the week ends, if your hunger is still not sated, you take damage from starvation. (1 week)\n\n**Stage 2** As stage 1, plus you’re sickened 1.\n\n**Stage 3** As stage 1, plus you’re drained 1 and sickened 1.\n\n**Stage 4** As stage 1, plus you’re drained 2, sickened 2, and stupefied 2.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11800,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Bower Fruit","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3635572786249603","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":13,"price":{},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1531,1558,1454],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4904","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"190"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:35.961767+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n_[Bower fruit](link_item_11800)_ got its name from its association with the Green Mother, a [fey](link_trait_2021) Eldest with a fondness for plants and manipulation, whose domain is known as the Hanging Bower. She uses these cursed fruits to keep mortals in her thrall, but it's unknown whether she created them or simply popularized their use.\n\nA _[bower fruit](link_item_11800)_ condemns a non-[fey](link_trait_2021) who tastes it to never again be satisfied with the fare found in the mundane Universe. Any fruit can be cursed in this manner, but stone fruits such as peaches, plums, mangoes, and lychees are most common. Upon activating a [bower fruit](link_item_11800) by eating it, you’re afflicted with the [curse](link_trait_1855) of decadence. You can’t recover from stage 1 of the [curse](link_trait_1855) naturally, even if you succeed at the save to do so.\n\n**Curse of Decadence** ([curse](link_trait_1855)) **Saving Throw** DC 30 Fortitude\n\n**Stage 1** You’re afflicted by hunger as if you hadn’t eaten food in days. You become fatigued and take 1d4 damage each day that can’t be healed until you sate your hunger. No amount of eating food can sate your hunger during the spell’s duration, with one exception—food from the First World sates your hunger and suppresses the effects, but permanently increases the save DC by 1 (to a maximum of DC 35). After the week ends, if your hunger is still not sated, you take damage from starvation. (1 week)\n\n**Stage 2** As stage 1, plus you’re sickened 1.\n\n**Stage 3** As stage 1, plus you’re drained 1 and sickened 1.\n\n**Stage 4** As stage 1, plus you’re drained 2, sickened 2, and stupefied 2.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11801,"type":"item","before":{"id":11801,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Bracers of Devotion","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5489904511965243","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":11,"price":{"cp":"","gp":1400,"pp":"","sp":""},"usage":"worn bracers","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1475,1526,1527],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4852","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"148"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","cleaning":{"updatedAt":"2026-04-12T06:24:30.724Z"},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:36.490155+00:00","operations":null,"description":"[Champions](link_class_109) adorn these bracers with the symbol of their deity or the text of the tenets they follow. While they're clasped around your forearms, reassuring focus and devotion flow into you through them. Each time you spend a [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) to cast a [devotion spell](link_class-feature_31209), your [blessing of the devoted](link_class-feature_31244) gains a benefit until the start of your next turn, depending on its type.\n\n*   **Blessed Armament** The bracers hold your weapon in place. You gain a +2 item bonus against attempts to [Disarm](link_action_19626) you of your blessed armament.\n*   **Blessed Shield** While raised, the shield grants you resistance 10 to [unholy](link_trait_1846) if you're [holy](link_trait_1630), resistance 10 to [holy](link_trait_1630) if you're [unholy](link_trait_1846), or resistance 5 to [holy](link_trait_1630) and [unholy](link_trait_1846) if you're neither.\n*   **Blessed Swiftness** The bonus to Speed is +10 feet.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">F</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You gain 1 [Focus Point](link_trait_1856), which you can use only to cast a [champion devotion spell](link_class-feature_31209). If not used by the end of your turn, this [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) is lost.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"You are a [champion](link_class_109)."},"after":{"id":11801,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Bracers of Devotion","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5489904511965243","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":11,"price":{"cp":"","gp":1400,"pp":"","sp":""},"usage":"worn bracers","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1475,1526,1527],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4852","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"148"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","cleaning":{"updatedAt":"2026-04-12T06:24:30.724Z"},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:36.490155+00:00","operations":null,"description":"[Champions](link_class_109) adorn these bracers with the symbol of their deity or the text of the tenets they follow. While they're clasped around your forearms, reassuring focus and devotion flow into you through them. Each time you spend a [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) to cast a [devotion spell](link_class-feature_31209), your [blessing of the devoted](link_class-feature_31244) gains a benefit until the start of your next turn, depending on its type.\n\n*   **Blessed Armament** The bracers hold your weapon in place. You gain a +2 item bonus against attempts to [Disarm](link_action_19626) you of your blessed armament.\n*   **Blessed Shield** While raised, the shield grants you resistance 10 to [unholy](link_trait_1846) if you're [holy](link_trait_1630), resistance 10 to [holy](link_trait_1630) if you're [unholy](link_trait_1846), or resistance 5 to [holy](link_trait_1630) and [unholy](link_trait_1846) if you're neither.\n*   **Blessed Swiftness** The bonus to Speed is +10 feet.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">F</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You gain 1 [Focus Point](link_trait_1856), which you can use only to cast a [champion devotion spell](link_class-feature_31209). If not used by the end of your turn, this [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) is lost.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"You are a [champion](link_class_109)."},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11802,"type":"item","before":{"id":11802,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Deadlock Mint (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1935242820815068","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":110},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2856,1531,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{},"hp_max":0,"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2021","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"74"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:37.265163+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) (add 1 action)\n\n* * *\n\n_[Deadlock mint](link_item_11802)_ is a species of mint with small, green flowers, said to grow on battlefields where the opposing sides were equally matched. Sprigs of the flowers blow gently in a breeze of their own creation. If you cast *[mystic armor](link_spell_4734)* using _[deadlock mint](link_item_11802)_, you release a small blast of concussive air in an emanation of a size that depends on the catalyst’s type. Unattended objects of 1 Bulk or less are pushed 10 feet away from you, and objects of up to 2 Bulk are pushed 5 feet. Large or smaller creatures must succeed at a Fortitude save equal to your spell save DC or be pushed 10 feet away from you, and Huge creatures must succeed at the save or be pushed 5 feet.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11802,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Deadlock Mint (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1935242820815068","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":110},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","