uuid":"5739811183521687","group":"ARMOR","hands":null,"level":0,"price":{"gp":5},"usage":null,"rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2879],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"skeletal","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"resilient":0},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Armor.aspx?ID=60","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"10"},"dex_cap":2,"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"ac_bonus":3,"category":"medium","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"strength":2,"base_item":"coral-armor","check_penalty":-2,"speed_penalty":-5,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:53.568901+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A good option for undersea explorers and aquatic peoples alike, [coral armor](link_item_11887) consists of panels of carved coral. If worn underwater, some of this coral can even be alive.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11888,"type":"item","before":{"id":11888,"bulk":"0","name":"Corpseward Pendant","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3051944143879684","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":150},"usage":"worn","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4873","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"153"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:54.199151+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A _[corpseward pendant](link_item_11888)_ is usually shaped like the skull of a [humanoid](link_trait_2399) or small [animal](link_trait_2409).\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Effect** You become undetectable to [undead](link_trait_2425) creatures for 10 minutes. [Undead](link_trait_2425) can't see, hear, or smell you, nor detect you with sensory capabilities such as tremorsense. A creature can attempt a single DC 18 Will saving throw to ignore this effect. If an [undead](link_trait_2425) has reason to believe that undetected opponents are present, it can still attempt to [Seek](link_action_19845) or [Strike](link_action_19856) you. If you attempt to use a [vitality](link_trait_1478) spell to damage [undead](link_trait_2425), touch or damage an [undead](link_trait_2425) creature, or attack any creature while warded in this manner, the pendant's effects immediately end. An [undead](link_trait_2425) creature who observes you in this manner or one who succeeds at the Will save is immune to the _[corpseward pendant](link_item_11888)_ for 24 hours.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11888,"bulk":"0","name":"Corpseward Pendant","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3051944143879684","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":150},"usage":"worn","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4873","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"153"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:54.199151+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A _[corpseward pendant](link_item_11888)_ is usually shaped like the skull of a [humanoid](link_trait_2399) or small [animal](link_trait_2409).\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Effect** You become undetectable to [undead](link_trait_2425) creatures for 10 minutes. [Undead](link_trait_2425) can't see, hear, or smell you, nor detect you with sensory capabilities such as tremorsense. A creature can attempt a single DC 18 Will saving throw to ignore this effect. If an [undead](link_trait_2425) has reason to believe that undetected opponents are present, it can still attempt to [Seek](link_action_19845) or [Strike](link_action_19856) you. If you attempt to use a [vitality](link_trait_1478) spell to damage [undead](link_trait_2425), touch or damage an [undead](link_trait_2425) creature, or attack any creature while warded in this manner, the pendant's effects immediately end. An [undead](link_trait_2425) creature who observes you in this manner or one who succeeds at the Will save is immune to the _[corpseward pendant](link_item_11888)_ for 24 hours.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11889,"type":"item","before":{"id":11889,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Corrosive Engravings","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"784469931024561","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":140},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1528,2855,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4709","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"111"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:55.12426+00:00","operations":null,"description":"These tin sheets are bound in brass and show significant signs of erosion. The [grimoire](link_trait_2855)'s title is acid-etched, and flipping between the sheets leaves your fingers covered in flecks of rust and powdery metal.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">F</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** If your next action is to cast an [acid](link_trait_1528) or [poison](link_trait_1476) spell that deals persistent damage, any creature who takes persistent damage from the spell is also sickened 2 until the persistent damage ends. Using an action to retch can reduce the sickened value as normal, but it can't reduce the sickened value below 1 until the persistent damage ends.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11889,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Corrosive Engravings","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"784469931024561","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":140},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1528,2855,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4709","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"111"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:55.12426+00:00","operations":null,"description":"These tin sheets are bound in brass and show significant signs of erosion. The [grimoire](link_trait_2855)'s title is acid-etched, and flipping between the sheets leaves your fingers covered in flecks of rust and powdery metal.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">F</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** If your next action is to cast an [acid](link_trait_1528) or [poison](link_trait_1476) spell that deals persistent damage, any creature who takes persistent damage from the spell is also sickened 2 until the persistent damage ends. Using an action to retch can reduce the sickened value as normal, but it can't reduce the sickened value below 1 until the persistent damage ends.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11890,"type":"item","before":{"id":11890,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Corruption Cassock","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1028379649251823","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":11,"price":{"gp":1150},"usage":"worn garment","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1558,1475,1526,1613,1527,1846],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4905","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"190"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","cleaning":{"updatedAt":"2026-04-12T10:21:10.701Z"},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:55.737366+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Perception** +20; precise vision 30 feet, imprecise [hearing](link_sense_21081) 30 feet\n\n**Communication** telepathy ([Common](link_language_81), [Empyreal](link_language_307), four other languages)\n\n**Skills** Deception +21, Diplomacy +19, Religion +19\n\n**Int** +2, **Wis** +5, **Cha** +4\n\n**Will** +20\n\nDevotees of benevolent faiths fear and loathe _[corruption cassocks](link_item_11890)_, each of which is dedicated to an [unholy](link_trait_1846) deity. When the garment chooses a target, such as when it senses a worshipper of a deity who isn't [unholy](link_trait_1846), it alters its form to match another deity's iconography, appearing to be a [_devoted vestments_](link_item_6872) for that deity. Once donned, the cassock tries to subtly sway its wearer to the worship of its deity. If the wearer begins to succumb, the _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ gradually reverts to its true appearance, replacing its false iconography as its wearer converts.\n\nA _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ functions as a [_devoted vestments_](link_item_6872) for any wearer it chooses. Once you [invest](link_action_20775) the cassock, it fuses to you. While you remain loyal to another deity, you believe the cassock grants you a +2 item bonus to Religion checks and a +1 item bonus to the divine skill of the deity to whom you believe the cassock is dedicated. It does neither. The GM secretly adjusts your checks with those skills, causing you to fail at religious tasks more often. If you have multiple equal or lower item bonuses to the affected skills, the cassock takes precedence, negating those bonuses. If you convert to following the cassock's true [unholy](link_trait_1846) deity, however, these bonuses function normally for you.\n\nIf you attempt to [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) that has the [holy](link_trait_1630) trait, the cassock can force you to attempt a DC 28 Will save. On a failure, you're stupefied 1 for one minute (stupefied 2 on a critical failure). A _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ uses this ability to convince you that your deity has forsaken you.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You gain 1 [Focus Point](link_trait_1856), which you can spend only to cast a [cleric](link_class_22) domain spell for a domain belonging to the deity you believe the cassock is dedicated to. If you don't spend this [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) by the end of this turn, it's lost. However, when you use this activation, the _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ can instead cast a domain spell of the same rank from its deity. It does so only to confuse and dismay you, harming your faith.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":11890,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Corruption Cassock","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1028379649251823","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":11,"price":{"gp":1150},"usage":"worn garment","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1558,1475,1526,1613,1527,1846],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4905","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"190"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","cleaning":{"updatedAt":"2026-04-12T10:21:10.701Z"},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:55.737366+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Perception** +20; precise vision 30 feet, imprecise [hearing](link_sense_21081) 30 feet\n\n**Communication** telepathy ([Common](link_language_81), [Empyreal](link_language_307), four other languages)\n\n**Skills** Deception +21, Diplomacy +19, Religion +19\n\n**Int** +2, **Wis** +5, **Cha** +4\n\n**Will** +20\n\nDevotees of benevolent faiths fear and loathe _[corruption cassocks](link_item_11890)_, each of which is dedicated to an [unholy](link_trait_1846) deity. When the garment chooses a target, such as when it senses a worshipper of a deity who isn't [unholy](link_trait_1846), it alters its form to match another deity's iconography, appearing to be a [_devoted vestments_](link_item_6872) for that deity. Once donned, the cassock tries to subtly sway its wearer to the worship of its deity. If the wearer begins to succumb, the _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ gradually reverts to its true appearance, replacing its false iconography as its wearer converts.\n\nA _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ functions as a [_devoted vestments_](link_item_6872) for any wearer it chooses. Once you [invest](link_action_20775) the cassock, it fuses to you. While you remain loyal to another deity, you believe the cassock grants you a +2 item bonus to Religion checks and a +1 item bonus to the divine skill of the deity to whom you believe the cassock is dedicated. It does neither. The GM secretly adjusts your checks with those skills, causing you to fail at religious tasks more often. If you have multiple equal or lower item bonuses to the affected skills, the cassock takes precedence, negating those bonuses. If you convert to following the cassock's true [unholy](link_trait_1846) deity, however, these bonuses function normally for you.\n\nIf you attempt to [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) that has the [holy](link_trait_1630) trait, the cassock can force you to attempt a DC 28 Will save. On a failure, you're stupefied 1 for one minute (stupefied 2 on a critical failure). A _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ uses this ability to convince you that your deity has forsaken you.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You gain 1 [Focus Point](link_trait_1856), which you can spend only to cast a [cleric](link_class_22) domain spell for a domain belonging to the deity you believe the cassock is dedicated to. If you don't spend this [Focus Point](link_trait_1856) by the end of this turn, it's lost. However, when you use this activation, the _[corruption cassock](link_item_11890)_ can instead cast a domain spell of the same rank from its deity. It does so only to confuse and dismay you, harming your faith.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":11891,"type":"item","before":{"id":11891,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Corset Knife","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1180377240072615","group":"WEAPON","hands":"1","level":0,"price":{"sp":3},"usage":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1569,1841,1570,1626],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":20,"bulk":{},"group":"knife","range":null,"runes":{"property":[]},"damage":{"die":"d4","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":"piercing"},"hp_max":20,"reload":"","source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Weapons.aspx?ID=606","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"27"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"bonus":0,"items":[],"rules":[],"bonus_damage":0,"container_id":null,"splash_damage":0},"category":"simple","hardness":5,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starf