mon among fatalists and adventurers with access to resurrection magic, [mortal chronicles](link_item_12223) look like tombstones, funeral plaques, or simple scrolls bearing the wearer's name or nickname. If you die, the date and cause of your death appear on the tattoo. The cause is literal and inexact, failing to identify specifics; it could read \"beheaded\" or \"immolated\" but not \"beheaded by Amiri\" or \"murdered with fire.\" If you're raised from the dead, a mark on the tattoo indicates the date you reversed your death. The tattoo then expands enough to list your next death when it comes.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12223,"bulk":"0","name":"Mortal Chronicle","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"696150095481255","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":10},"usage":"tattooed-on-the-body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4745","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"121"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:18.670348+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Common among fatalists and adventurers with access to resurrection magic, [mortal chronicles](link_item_12223) look like tombstones, funeral plaques, or simple scrolls bearing the wearer's name or nickname. If you die, the date and cause of your death appear on the tattoo. The cause is literal and inexact, failing to identify specifics; it could read \"beheaded\" or \"immolated\" but not \"beheaded by Amiri\" or \"murdered with fire.\" If you're raised from the dead, a mark on the tattoo indicates the date you reversed your death. The tattoo then expands enough to list your next death when it comes.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12224,"type":"item","before":{"id":12224,"bulk":"0","name":"Mortalis Coin","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8932287246143805","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":4,"price":{"gp":20},"usage":"affixed-to-armor","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504,1544],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4643","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"94"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:19.199836+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">4</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Trigger** You are reduced to 0 Hit Points by damage but not immediately killed; **Requirements** You are an expert in Fortitude saves\n\nThis small golden coin is usually stamped with the image of a boar or other resilient creature. If the triggering damage would cause you to become dying 2 (typically due to a critical hit or your critical failure), you become dying 1 instead. In addition, for 10 minutes, you die from the dying condition at dying 5, rather than dying 4.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12224,"bulk":"0","name":"Mortalis Coin","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8932287246143805","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":4,"price":{"gp":20},"usage":"affixed-to-armor","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504,1544],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4643","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"94"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:19.199836+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">4</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Trigger** You are reduced to 0 Hit Points by damage but not immediately killed; **Requirements** You are an expert in Fortitude saves\n\nThis small golden coin is usually stamped with the image of a boar or other resilient creature. If the triggering damage would cause you to become dying 2 (typically due to a critical hit or your critical failure), you become dying 1 instead. In addition, for 10 minutes, you die from the dying condition at dying 5, rather than dying 4.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12225,"type":"item","before":{"id":12225,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Mother Maw","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4025362911235579","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":15,"price":{"gp":6000},"usage":"placed on a surface","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1558,1559,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{"ignored":1000000,"capacity":1000000,"held_or_stowed":0.1},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4913","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"192"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:19.818553+00:00","operations":null,"description":"This item appears to be and functions as a _[portable hole](link_item_12290)_, but it's actually the maw of an alien [extradimensional](link_trait_1559) creature akin to and older than a _bag of devouring_. Any animal or vegetable matter put in the hole has a chance of triggering the creature's interest. Whenever you reach into the hole to retrieve an item or place an animal or plant product within the bag, roll a DC 11 flat check. On a success, the hole ignores the intrusion. On a failure, the _[mother maw](link_item_12225)_ devours the triggering material, removing it from existence. The maw can't eat [artifacts](link_trait_1568). If the triggering material isn't entirely inside the maw, such as when someone reaches inside, the _[mother maw](link_item_12225)_ attempts to pull it completely inside using a [Grapple](link_action_19725) action with a +28 Athletics bonus. On a success, it devours the victim or object.\n\nWhenever the maw critically fails the Athletics check, it regurgitates one creature or object it previously devoured. The condition of the vomited creature or object depends on its resilience and the time it has spent inside the maw. Typically, the maw spews forth items it finds difficult to digest, such as those made of [adamantine](link_item_15064) or protected by magic. It can and does regurgitate remains, though.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12225,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Mother Maw","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4025362911235579","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":15,"price":{"gp":6000},"usage":"placed on a surface","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1558,1559,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{"ignored":1000000,"capacity":1000000,"held_or_stowed":0.1},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4913","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"192"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:19.818553+00:00","operations":null,"description":"This item appears to be and functions as a _[portable hole](link_item_12290)_, but it's actually the maw of an alien [extradimensional](link_trait_1559) creature akin to and older than a _bag of devouring_. Any animal or vegetable matter put in the hole has a chance of triggering the creature's interest. Whenever you reach into the hole to retrieve an item or place an animal or plant product within the bag, roll a DC 11 flat check. On a success, the hole ignores the intrusion. On a failure, the _[mother maw](link_item_12225)_ devours the triggering material, removing it from existence. The maw can't eat [artifacts](link_trait_1568). If the triggering material isn't entirely inside the maw, such as when someone reaches inside, the _[mother maw](link_item_12225)_ attempts to pull it completely inside using a [Grapple](link_action_19725) action with a +28 Athletics bonus. On a success, it devours the victim or object.\n\nWhenever the maw critically fails the Athletics check, it regurgitates one creature or object it previously devoured. The condition of the vomited creature or object depends on its resilience and the time it has spent inside the maw. Typically, the maw spews forth items it finds difficult to digest, such as those made of [adamantine](link_item_15064) or protected by magic. It can and does regurgitate remains, though.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12226,"type":"item","before":{"id":12226,"bulk":"0","name":"Mourner's Dawnlight Fulu","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7534503860033423","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":120},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1531,2854,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4572","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"78"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:20.440855+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"THREE-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">3</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA _[mourner's dawnlight](link_item_12226) fulu_ is a stack of pages that resembles joss paper, used to locate the remains of the lost. When you Activate the fulu, you envision a specific object or deceased creature you're familiar with and want to find. You then rip the fulu into pieces and let them drift in the wind. If the item or creature you seek is within 500 feet, the pieces flutter through the air and land on the target, or on the surface closest to a buried or otherwise obscured target. If the torn fulu lands or fails to locate the desired target, its magic ends.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12226,"bulk":"0","name":"Mourner's Dawnlight Fulu","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7534503860033423","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":120},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1531,2854,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4572","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"78"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:20.440855+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"THREE-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">3</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA _[mourner's dawnlight](link_item_12226) fulu_ is a stack of pages that resembles joss paper, used to locate the remains of the lost. When you Activate the fulu, you envision a specific object or deceased creature you're familiar with and want to find. You then rip the fulu into pieces and let them drift in the wind. If the item or creature you seek is within 500 feet, the pieces flutter through the air and land on the target, or on the surface closest to a buried or otherwise obscured target. If the torn fulu lands or fails to locate the desired target, its magic ends.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12227,"type":"item","before":{"id":12227,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Mukradi Jar","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3825763843320258","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":15,"price":{"gp":1300},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1668],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4484","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"56"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:21.047136+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA miniature [mukradi](link_creature_10208), its chitin shrunken and pale, is coiled within this jar. Its hollow form grows to a Gargantuan shell when you open the jar. It emits one of three breath weapons, chosen by you. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 34 basic Reflex save.\n\n*   **Acid Maw** ([acid](link_trait_1528)) 10-foot-wide, 60-foot line of [acid](link_trait_1528) dealing 12d6 [acid](link_trait_1528) damage.\n*   **Flame Maw** ([fire](link_trait_1542)) 60-foot cone of [fire](link_trait_1542) dealing 12d6 [fire](link_trait_1542) damage.\n*   **Shock Maw** ([electricity](link_trait_1576)) 120-foot line of [electricity](link_trait_1576) dealing 12d6 [electricity](link_trait_1576) damage.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"Supply a [mukradi](link_creature_10208) corpse."},"after":{"id":12227,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Mukradi Jar","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3825763843320258","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":15,"price":{"gp":1300},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1668],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4484","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"56"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:21.047136+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA miniature [mukradi](link_creature_10208), its chitin shrunken and pale, is coiled within this jar. Its hollow form grows to a Gargantuan shell when you open the jar. It emits one of three breath weapons, chosen by you. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 34 basic Reflex save.\n\n*   **Acid Maw** ([acid](link_trait_1528)) 10-foot-wide, 60-foot line of [acid](link_trait_1528) dealing 12d6 [acid](link_trait_1528) damage.\n*   **Flame Maw** ([fire](link_trait_1542)) 60-foot cone of [fire](link_trait_1542) dealing 12d6 [fire](link_trait_1542) damage.\n*   **Shock Maw** ([electricity](link_trait_1576)) 120-foot line of [electricity](link_trait_1576) dealing 12d6 [electricity](link_trait_1576) damage.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"Supply a [mukradi](link_creature_10208) corpse."},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12228,"type":"item","before":{"id":12228,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Mustard Powder","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4645507244279286","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":25},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1578,1476],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4541","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"70"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:22.038609+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nConcocted from the formulas provided by otherworldly refugees to Irrisen, [mustard powder](link_item_12228) is rumored to be devastating to entire armies with proper dispersal. Recipes have quickly spread across Golarion. [Mustard powder](link_item_12228)'s sickened condition ends when the [poison](link_trait_1476)'s other effects do.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 22 Fortitude\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d6 [poison](link_trait_1476) damage and dazzled (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 2d4 [poison](link_trait_1476) damage, dazzled, sickened 1, and unable to smell (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** 2d6 [poison](link_trait_1476) damage, dazzled, sickened 2, and unable to smell (1 round)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12228,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Mustard Powder","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4645507244279286","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":25},"usage":"held-in-one-hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1578,1476],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4541","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"70"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:22.038609+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nConcocted from the formulas provided by otherworldly refugees to Irrisen, [mustard powder](link_item_12228) is rumored to be devastating to entire armies with proper dispersal. Recipes have quickly spread across Golarion. [Mustard powder](link_item_12228)'s sickened condition ends when the [poison](link_trait_1476)'s other effects do.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 22 Fortitude\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d6 [poison](link_trait_1476) damage and dazzled (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 2d4 [poison](link_trait_1476) damage, dazzled, sickened 1, and unable to smell (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** 2d6 [poison](link_trait_1476) damage, dazzled, sickened 2, and unable to smell (1 round)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12229,"type":"item","before":{"id":12229,"bulk":"0","name":"Navigator's Star","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8765695594569220","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":18},"usage":"tattooed on the body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4746","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"121"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:22.692935+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A star inked on the back of the hand, usually between the thumb and forefinger, keeps you on the right path.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433)); **Effect** As you hold up your hand and align the star in view, you learn which direction you're facing.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12229,"bulk":"0","name":"Navigator's Star","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8765695594569220","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":18},"usage":"tattooed on the body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4746","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"121"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:22.692935+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A star inked on the back of the hand, usually between the thumb and forefinger, keeps you on the right path.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433)); **Effect** As you hold up your hand and align the star in view, you learn which direction you're facing.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12230,"type":"item","before":{"id":12230,"bulk":"0","name":"Nemesis Name","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8976196378839346","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":650},"usage":"tattooed-on-the-body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4747","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"121"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:23.236954+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You want revenge badly enough that you tattoo your nemesis's name in a place you can easily see to remember your vow to settle the score. Anyone who sees the tattoo senses your hatred of the named being. Receiving a new [nemesis name](link_item_12230) makes any you already have non-[magical](link_trait_1504).\n\nYou gain a +2 status bonus to damage rolls against the creature named on your tattoo, but this nemesis gains a +1 status bonus to damage rolls against you.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [mental](link_trait_1448))\n\n**Frequency** once per round; **Requirements** You can see your nemesis, and they're within 30 feet of you\n\n**Effect** You focus your hatred into a mental scream. Your nemesis takes 3d6 [mental](link_trait_1448) damage, which they can resist with a basic DC 26 Will save. You take half as much damage as your nemesis does, and you can't reduce this damage in any way.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12230,"bulk":"0","name":"Nemesis Name","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8976196378839346","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":650},"usage":"tattooed-on-the-body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4747","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"121"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:23.236954+00:00","operations":null,"description":"You want revenge badly enough that you tattoo your nemesis's name in a place you can easily see to remember your vow to settle the score. Anyone who sees the tattoo senses your hatred of the named being. Receiving a new [nemesis name](link_item_12230) makes any you already have non-[magical](link_trait_1504).\n\nYou gain a +2 status bonus to damage rolls against the creature named on your tattoo, but this nemesis gains a +1 status bonus to damage rolls against you.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [mental](link_trait_1448))\n\n**Frequency** once per round; **Requirements** You can see your nemesis, and they're within 30 feet of you\n\n**Effect** You focus your hatred into a mental scream. Your nemesis takes 3d6 [mental](link_trait_1448) damage, which they can resist with a basic DC 26 Will save. You take half as much damage as your nemesis does, and you can't reduce this damage in any way.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12231,"type":"item","before":{"id":12231,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Neophyte's Fipple","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8226821327686819","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":3,"price":{"gp":8},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4655","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"97"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:23.931493+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Requirements** You are untrained in Performance\n\nMade of polished wood, a [neophyte's fipple](link_item_12231) is a block flute enchanted to guarantee melodic sound. When you [Perform](link_action_19746) a song on the fipple to Activate it, your ability modifier, proficiency bonus, and item bonus for the Performance check total +7, regardless of what they would normally be. Add other bonuses and penalties to the check normally. Once the magic is used, the fipple remains as a mundane instrument.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12231,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Neophyte's Fipple","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8226821327686819","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":3,"price":{"gp":8},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4655","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"97"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:23.931493+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Requirements** You are untrained in Performance\n\nMade of polished wood, a [neophyte's fipple](link_item_12231) is a block flute enchanted to guarantee melodic sound. When you [Perform](link_action_19746) a song on the fipple to Activate it, your ability modifier, proficiency bonus, and item bonus for the Performance check total +7, regardless of what they would normally be. Add other bonuses and penalties to the check normally. Once the magic is used, the fipple remains as a mundane instrument.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12232,"type":"item","before":{"id":12232,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Nevercold (Compressed)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4814637282505999","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":14,"price":{"gp":720},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2856,1531,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4559","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"75"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:24.543921+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) (add 1 action)\n\n* * *\n\n_[Nevercold](link_item_12232)_, sometimes mistakenly referred to as nevercoal, is the charcoal left after wildfires in the First World. True to it