lk":"0","name":"Phantasmal Doorknob","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"2493675447216665","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":6,"price":{"gp":215},"usage":"affixed to armor or a weapon","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1486,1504,1448,2570],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4769","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"127"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0,"spellheart_casting":{"dc":20}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:48.295376+00:00","operations":[{"id":"24c73128-71df-4b97-abfe-7704c29d580a","data":{"title":"What is the spellheart affixed to?","modeType":"PREDEFINED","optionType":"CUSTOM","optionsPredefined":[{"id":"6022b6bd-eae7-453e-af79-d53f4bc304bf","type":"CUSTOM","title":"Armor","operations":[{"id":"ab6b840e-6b68-4d40-8979-8f75cfe7d702","data":{"text":"to Pick a Lock.","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_THIEVERY"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"You gain a +1 item bonus to Thievery checks to [Pick a Lock](link_action_19747)."},{"id":"1a6b53ad-4c2a-4cda-912b-e2055a2aed17","type":"CUSTOM","title":"Weapon","operations":[],"description":"If you critically succeed at a [Strike](link_action_19856) with the weapon, the target is dazzled until the end of its next turn."}]},"type":"select"}],"description":"This ornate doorknob can open doors both material and metaphysical, revealing dreams and nightmares. The spell DC of any spell cast by activating this item is 20.\n\n*   **Armor** You gain a +1 item bonus to Thievery checks to [Pick a Lock](link_action_19747).\n    \n*   **Weapon** If you critically succeed at a [Strike](link_action_19856) with the weapon, the target is dazzled until the end of its next turn.\n    \n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611); **Effect** You cast *[figment](link_spell_4620)*.\n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You cast *[phantasmal treasure](link_spell_6757)*.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12271,"type":"item","before":{"id":12271,"bulk":"16","name":"Phantom Piano","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5111698620210928","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":12,"price":{"gp":100},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1526,1613,1514],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4929","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"196"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","label":"Virtuoso Instrument (playing it)","value":1,"selector":"performance","predicate":["playing"]}],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:50.334576+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Perception** +22; [precise vision](link_sense_20776) 30 feet, [imprecise hearing](link_sense_21081) 30 feet\n\n**Communication** [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884) (any languages the possessing spirit knew in life)\n\n**Skills** Diplomacy +23, Music Lore +23, Performance +25, Society +21\n\n**Int** +3, **Wis** +4, **Cha** +5\n\n**Will** +22\n\nWhen a skilled musician dies before reaching their full potential or accomplishing an important goal, their soul might refuse to move on to the Boneyard. Rather than becoming [undead](link_trait_2425), the spirit possesses an instrument they played in life, turning it into an intelligent item and a [virtuoso instrument](link_item_7605). (Other phantom instruments exist, but most are heavy.) A [phantom piano](link_item_12271) offers a bargain to any bard or other skilled musician who finds it: receive musical aid as you dedicate yourself to reaching the success the spirit felt they were denied in life. The piano refuses to play for those who reject this deal. If you accept, the piano asks only that you practice with it and perform for increasingly refined and august audiences, requiring a successful Performance check appropriate to your proficiency level. The piano sets no strict timeline, but at the GM's discretion, if you go too long without making progress, the piano can cease cooperating with you until it's satisfied with your dedication once again.\n\nWhile you keep up your end of the bargain, the piano grants you a +2 item bonus to Performance checks made with it. The piano also provides access to [composition](link_trait_1895) spells based on your Performance proficiency rank, as if you had the corresponding feat. The spells you can use comprise a cumulative list, but you can cast them only when using the piano. You must spend the actions and Focus Points required to cast these spells.\n\n**Trained:** *[uplifting overture](link_spell_4923)*, *[courageous anthem](link_spell_4540)*\n\n**Expert:** *[hymn of healing](link_spell_4670)*, *[rallying anthem](link_spell_4792)*\n\n**Master:** *[symphony of the unfettered heart](link_spell_4883)*\n\n**Legendary:** *[soothing ballad](link_spell_4843)*\n\nA [phantom piano](link_item_12271) has the following activations.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Effect** The piano shrinks down to a figurine of light Bulk compact enough to store in a pouch, or from figurine form back to instrument form. In figurine form, the piano doesn't function as an instrument or provide magic other than this activation.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">4</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You gain 1 Focus Point, which you can spend only to [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) the piano provides you.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12271,"bulk":"16","name":"Phantom Piano","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5111698620210928","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":12,"price":{"gp":100},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1526,1613,1514],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4929","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"196"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","label":"Virtuoso Instrument (playing it)","value":1,"selector":"performance","predicate":["playing"]}],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:50.334576+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Perception** +22; [precise vision](link_sense_20776) 30 feet, [imprecise hearing](link_sense_21081) 30 feet\n\n**Communication** [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884) (any languages the possessing spirit knew in life)\n\n**Skills** Diplomacy +23, Music Lore +23, Performance +25, Society +21\n\n**Int** +3, **Wis** +4, **Cha** +5\n\n**Will** +22\n\nWhen a skilled musician dies before reaching their full potential or accomplishing an important goal, their soul might refuse to move on to the Boneyard. Rather than becoming [undead](link_trait_2425), the spirit possesses an instrument they played in life, turning it into an intelligent item and a [virtuoso instrument](link_item_7605). (Other phantom instruments exist, but most are heavy.) A [phantom piano](link_item_12271) offers a bargain to any bard or other skilled musician who finds it: receive musical aid as you dedicate yourself to reaching the success the spirit felt they were denied in life. The piano refuses to play for those who reject this deal. If you accept, the piano asks only that you practice with it and perform for increasingly refined and august audiences, requiring a successful Performance check appropriate to your proficiency level. The piano sets no strict timeline, but at the GM's discretion, if you go too long without making progress, the piano can cease cooperating with you until it's satisfied with your dedication once again.\n\nWhile you keep up your end of the bargain, the piano grants you a +2 item bonus to Performance checks made with it. The piano also provides access to [composition](link_trait_1895) spells based on your Performance proficiency rank, as if you had the corresponding feat. The spells you can use comprise a cumulative list, but you can cast them only when using the piano. You must spend the actions and Focus Points required to cast these spells.\n\n**Trained:** *[uplifting overture](link_spell_4923)*, *[courageous anthem](link_spell_4540)*\n\n**Expert:** *[hymn of healing](link_spell_4670)*, *[rallying anthem](link_spell_4792)*\n\n**Master:** *[symphony of the unfettered heart](link_spell_4883)*\n\n**Legendary:** *[soothing ballad](link_spell_4843)*\n\nA [phantom piano](link_item_12271) has the following activations.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Effect** The piano shrinks down to a figurine of light Bulk compact enough to store in a pouch, or from figurine form back to instrument form. In figurine form, the piano doesn't function as an instrument or provide magic other than this activation.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">4</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You gain 1 Focus Point, which you can spend only to [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611) the piano provides you.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12272,"type":"item","before":{"id":12272,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Phantom Roll","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8014067586036129","group":"GENERAL","hands":"1","level":4,"price":{"gp":13},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4458","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"50"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:50.947054+00:00","operations":[{"id":"c92c5c5b-4dfa-4848-9be1-74699dc6e750","data":{"text":"to Stealth checks you attempt during the Avoid Notice exploration activity","type":"item","value":1,"variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"**Activate** 10 minutes ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA [phantom roll](link_item_12272) contains vegetables, greens, and fine, clear noodles, all wrapped in transparent, edible starch paper and alchemically treated and laced with a tangy sauce. Upon eating the roll, you gain a +1 item bonus to Stealth checks you attempt during the [Avoid Notice](link_action_21146) exploration activity. You can also [Avoid Notice](link_action_21146) at full Speed or combine it with [Investigate](link_action_21202) or [Scout](link_action_21196) while moving at half Speed. These effects expire 24 hours after you eat the roll or when you make your next daily preparations, whichever comes first.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12272,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Phantom Roll","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8014067586036129","group":"GENERAL","hands":"1","level":4,"price":{"gp":13},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4458","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"50"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:50.947054+00:00","operations":[{"id":"c92c5c5b-4dfa-4848-9be1-74699dc6e750","data":{"text":"to Stealth checks you attempt during the Avoid Notice exploration activity","type":"item","value":1,"variable":"SKILL_STEALTH"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"**Activate** 10 minutes ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA [phantom roll](link_item_12272) contains vegetables, greens, and fine, clear noodles, all wrapped in transparent, edible starch paper and alchemically treated and laced with a tangy sauce. Upon eating the roll, you gain a +1 item bonus to Stealth checks you attempt during the [Avoid Notice](link_action_21146) exploration activity. You can also [Avoid Notice](link_action_21146) at full Speed or combine it with [Investigate](link_action_21202) or [Scout](link_action_21196) while moving at half Speed. These effects expire 24 hours after you eat the roll or when you make your next daily preparations, whichever comes first.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12273,"type":"item","before":{"id":12273,"bulk":"0","name":"Phoenix Cinder","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"991070947169618","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":16,"price":{},"usage":"touched","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1531,1542,1454],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4901","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"188"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:51.488345+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nAn incandescent, multipronged crystal the color of dying [fire](link_trait_1542), a [phoenix cinder](link_item_12273) gives off pleasant warmth and a sense of peace. A low, soft chirruping around the crystal invokes the idea of using fire to cleanse and protect. The crystal offers this power to anyone who touches it. A partaker must be willing to gain the boon's effects.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 1 (1 Week)** The first time you enter this stage from a particular [phoenix cinder](link_item_12273), you are affected as if by *[regenerate](link_spell_4798)*.\n\nFor 3 days after taking in the cinder, you are immune to [fire](link_trait_1542). While in this stage or higher, you have fast healing equal to half your level, as well as resistance to [fire](link_trait_1542) damage equal to half your level. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws (or any other defense) against [fire](link_trait_1542). Treat the outcome of any saving throw you roll against [fire](link_trait_1542) effects as one step better. You can cast *[ignition](link_spell_4674)* as an innate spell, and you have access to the following Activation.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [fire](link_trait_1542)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You wreathe yourself in flame for 1 minute. Adjacent creatures that hit you with a melee attack, as well as creatures that touch you or hit you with an [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack, take 2d6 [fire](link_trait_1542) damage. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the Activation.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 2 (1 Month)** You can use the Activation once per hour. Always feverish and flushed, you feel as if temperatures lower than sweltering are cold. Reduce your current and maximum Hit Points by 2 × your level, and you have a weakness to [cold](link_trait_1519) damage equal to half your level. You have urges to burn and use fire when you can. When confronted with the opportunity to do so, you must succeed at a Will save to avoid it. Doing so once after each time you roll initiative is enough.\n\nIf you die at this stage or higher, your body burns from the inside out over 1d4 rounds, reducing you to fine ash. Anything flammable on you is destroyed. A [phoenix](link_creature_10243) emerges from your remains, but does not have the [holy](link_trait_1630) trait and is interested more in selfish pursuits and spreading fire than kindness. You also attempt a DC 8 flat check; on a failure, the [phoenix](link_creature_10243) gains the [unholy](link_trait_1846) trait and also thirsts for vengeance against the little beings like the one who dared to use its power for a time.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 3 (1 Month)** You now have fast healing equal to your level but reduce your current and maximum Hit Points by 4 × your level, rounded up, instead of 2 × your level. Also, you have a weakness to [cold](link_trait_1519) damage equal to your level and a weakness to [unholy](link_trait_1846) equal to half your level. You can use the Activation you previously gained once per minute, but you can no longer [Dismiss](link_action_19627) it. Whenever you drop to 0 Hit Points, a *[divine immolation](link_spell_4576)* erupts from a randomly chosen point on the edge of your space.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 4** You die.\n\n* * *\n\n**Purging** You must collect the remains of a [phoenix](link_creature_10243) of your level or higher who has been unable to self-resurrect, compressing the remains with powdered diamonds, opals, and rubies worth 75 gp × your level into an egg. You can then use _[divine immolation](link_spell_4576)_ as if you dropped to 0 Hit Points during this boon's stage 3. If you do so, the [phoenix](link_creature_10243) whose remains you collected is reborn as if it used its Self-Resurrection, and the [phoenix cinder](link_item_12273)'s effects end on you.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12273,"bulk":"0","name":"Phoenix Cinder","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"991070947169618","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":16,"price":{},"usage":"touched","rarity":"RARE","traits":[1531,1542,1454],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4901","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"188"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:51.488345+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nAn incandescent, multipronged crystal the color of dying [fire](link_trait_1542), a [phoenix cinder](link_item_12273) gives off pleasant warmth and a sense of peace. A low, soft chirruping around the crystal invokes the idea of using fire to cleanse and protect. The crystal offers this power to anyone who touches it. A partaker must be willing to gain the boon's effects.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 1 (1 Week)** The first time you enter this stage from a particular [phoenix cinder](link_item_12273), you are affected as if by *[regenerate](link_spell_4798)*.\n\nFor 3 days after taking in the cinder, you are immune to [fire](link_trait_1542). While in this stage or higher, you have fast healing equal to half your level, as well as resistance to [fire](link_trait_1542) damage equal to half your level. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws (or any other defense) against [fire](link_trait_1542). Treat the outcome of any saving throw you roll against [fire](link_trait_1542) effects as one step better. You can cast *[ignition](link_spell_4674)* as an innate spell, and you have access to the following Activation.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [fire](link_trait_1542)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You wreathe yourself in flame for 1 minute. Adjacent creatures that hit you with a melee attack, as well as creatures that touch you or hit you with an [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attack, take 2d6 [fire](link_trait_1542) damage. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the Activation.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 2 (1 Month)** You can use the Activation once per hour. Always feverish and flushed, you feel as if temperatures lower than sweltering are cold. Reduce your current and maximum Hit Points by 2 × your level, and you have a weakness to [cold](link_trait_1519) damage equal to half your level. You have urges to burn and use fire when you can. When confronted with the opportunity to do so, you must succeed at a Will save to avoid it. Doing so once after each time you roll initiative is enough.\n\nIf you die at this stage or higher, your body burns from the inside out over 1d4 rounds, reducing you to fine ash. Anything flammable on you is destroyed. A [phoenix](link_creature_10243) emerges from your remains, but does not have the [holy](link_trait_1630) trait and is interested more in selfish pursuits and spreading fire than kindness. You also attempt a DC 8 flat check; on a failure, the [phoenix](link_creature_10243) gains the [unholy](link_trait_1846) trait and also thirsts for vengeance against the little beings like the one who dared to use its power for a time.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 3 (1 Month)** You now have fast healing equal to your level but reduce your current and maximum Hit Points by 4 × your level, rounded up, instead of 2 × your level. Also, you have a weakness to [cold](link_trait_1519) damage equal to your level and a weakness to [unholy](link_trait_1846) equal to half your level. You can use the Activation you previously gained once per minute, but you can no longer [Dismiss](link_action_19627) it. Whenever you drop to 0 Hit Points, a *[divine immolation](link_spell_4576)* erupts from a randomly chosen point on the edge of your space.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 4** You die.\n\n* * *\n\n**Purging** You must collect the remains of a [phoenix](link_creature_10243) of your level or higher who has been unable to self-resurrect, compressing the remains with powdered diamonds, opals, and rubies worth 75 gp × your level into an egg. You can then use _[divine immolation](link_spell_4576)_ as if you dropped to 0 Hit Points during this boon's stage 3. If you do so, the [phoenix](link_creature_10243) whose remains you collected is reborn as if it used its Self-Resurrection, and the [phoenix cinder](link_item_12273)'s effects end on you.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12274,"type":"item","before":{"id":12274,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Pilferer's Gloves","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7293519172294660","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":17,"price":{"gp":15000},"usage":"worn gloves","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1552,1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4674","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"104"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:52.072394+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Made of soft and subtle black leather, these gloves fit tightly but aren't uncomfortable and don't impede your sense of touch. As long as you're trained in Thievery while wearing these gloves, you're always considered one skill rank higher than your actual rank. If you possess a Legendary skill rank in Thievery, you gain a +2 item bonus to Thievery checks instead. When you [invest](link_action_20775) the gloves, you either increase your Dexterity modifier by 1 or increase it to +4, whichever would give you a higher value.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"REACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">5</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day; **Trigger** You fail or critically fail a Thievery skill check\n\n**Effect** If you failed the Thievery skill check, you succeed at that check instead. If you critically failed, you fail instead.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12274,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Pilferer's Gloves","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7293519172294660","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":17,"price":{"gp":15000},"usage":"worn gloves","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1552,1527,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4674","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"104"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:52.072394+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Made of soft and subtle black leather, these gloves fit tightly but aren't uncomfortable and don't impede your sense of touch. As long as you're trained in Thievery while wearing these gloves, you're always considered one skill rank higher than your actual rank. If you possess a Legendary skill rank in Thievery, you gain a +2 item bonus to Thievery checks instead. When you [invest](link_action_20775) the gloves, you either increase your Dexterity modifier by 1 or increase it to +4, whichever would give you a higher value.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"REACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">5</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day; **Trigger** You fail or critically fail a Thievery skill check\n\n**Effect** If you failed the Thievery skill check, you succeed at that check instead. If you critically failed, you fail instead.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12275,"type":"item","before":{"id":12275,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Pipes of Compulsion (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6079148181090300","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":8,"price":{"gp":460},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2861,1514,1546],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4803","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"137"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","value":1,"selector":["performance","diplomacy"]}],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:20:52.714773+00:00","operations":[{"id":"7a94a081-febf-4435-9eae-caa9aac24cf3","data":{"text":"while playing the pipes","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_PERFORMANCE"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"db07ab1d-72ee-4618-bc7f-0253238b1c4f","data":{"text":"while playing the pipes","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_DIPLOMACY"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"These panpipes are made of what seems to be beat-up tin bound by frayed leather and look like they shouldn't function at all, but in skilled hands they emit a beautiful sound that beguiles the senses. While playing the pipes, you gain a +1 item bonus to Diplomacy and Performance checks.\n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611)\n\n**Effect** You expend a number of charges from this instrument to [Cast a spell](link_action_19611) from its list.\n\n*   **Cantrip** *[daze](link_spell_4