dy","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4754","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"122"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","value":2,"selector":"crafting"},{"key":"AdjustDegreeOfSuccess","selector":"crafting","predicate":["action:earn-income"],"adjustment":{"criticalFailure":"one-degree-better"}}],"container_id":null},"category":"","cleaning":{"updatedAt":"2026-04-12T13:32:44.218Z"},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:22.100322+00:00","operations":[{"id":"2579b8fc-3a67-417c-9a1b-ba0d5b8dea5a","data":{"text":"","type":"item","value":2,"variable":"SKILL_CRAFTING"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"94c4d066-0d40-4e3a-a325-42f23831c774","data":{"id":19631,"text":"**Tradecraft Tattoo** When you roll a critical failure on a Crafting check to [Earn Income](link_action_19631), treat it as a failure instead.","type":"action"},"type":"injectText"}],"description":"Crafters choose tattoos that represent their dedication and skill in their chosen field. Such tattoos might adorn the arm, fingers, or eyes, and they take the form of artistic patterns or depict tools of the trade, such as anvils, paintbrushes, or trowels. You gain a +2 item bonus to Crafting checks. Furthermore, when you roll a critical failure on a Crafting check to [Earn Income](link_action_19631), treat it as a failure instead.\n\n**Activate** 1 minute ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433)); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** The tattoo casts *[creation](link_spell_4545)*. You choose the item and its appearance, and whether the spell is 4th or 5th rank.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[{"path":["operations","1","data","text"],"before":"**Tradecraft Tattoo** When you roll a critical failure on a Crafting check to Earn Income, treat it as a failure instead.","after":"**Tradecraft Tattoo** When you roll a critical failure on a Crafting check to [Earn Income](link_action_19631), treat it as a failure instead."}]},{"table":"item","id":12556,"type":"item","before":{"id":12556,"bulk":"1","name":"Traveling Companion's Chair","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7644797502759074","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":4},"usage":"other","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1627,1538],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4681","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"106"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:22.720066+00:00","operations":null,"description":"This more robust assembly is well suited for longer travel and all manner of adventuring. As with the [traveler's chair](link_item_7904), small mechanisms built into the wheels and support struts allow the user to traverse up and down stairs without any additional difficulty (though moving up stairs is still difficult terrain, just like for other adventurers) and move without additional difficulty through ladders, uneven ground, and other common adventuring terrain.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12556,"bulk":"1","name":"Traveling Companion's Chair","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7644797502759074","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":4},"usage":"other","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1627,1538],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4681","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"106"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:22.720066+00:00","operations":null,"description":"This more robust assembly is well suited for longer travel and all manner of adventuring. As with the [traveler's chair](link_item_7904), small mechanisms built into the wheels and support struts allow the user to traverse up and down stairs without any additional difficulty (though moving up stairs is still difficult terrain, just like for other adventurers) and move without additional difficulty through ladders, uneven ground, and other common adventuring terrain.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12557,"type":"item","before":{"id":12557,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Tremorsensors","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8745683576635467","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":4,"price":{"gp":100},"usage":"affixed-to-armor","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2858,1539],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4702","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"109"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:23.240988+00:00","operations":null,"description":"These small, metallic devices resemble squashed spheres. They each contain a tiny gyroscope that's incredibly sensitive to vibrations in the earth. While typically worn on one's footwear, the device can be affixed to any part of your armor.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">F</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You stomp a foot, clap your hands, or create some other source of sound, gaining tremorsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 20 feet for the next 10 minutes.\n\n","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12557,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Tremorsensors","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8745683576635467","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":4,"price":{"gp":100},"usage":"affixed-to-armor","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2858,1539],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4702","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"109"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:23.240988+00:00","operations":null,"description":"These small, metallic devices resemble squashed spheres. They each contain a tiny gyroscope that's incredibly sensitive to vibrations in the earth. While typically worn on one's footwear, the device can be affixed to any part of your armor.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"FREE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">F</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Effect** You stomp a foot, clap your hands, or create some other source of sound, gaining tremorsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 20 feet for the next 10 minutes.\n\n","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12558,"type":"item","before":{"id":12558,"bulk":"0","name":"Triangular Teeth","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3694379258315238","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":2,"price":{"gp":33},"usage":"tattooed on the body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4755","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"122"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","value":1,"selector":"survival","predicate":["water"]},{"key":"RollOption","domain":"survival","option":"navwater"}],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:23.86474+00:00","operations":[{"id":"0e3cc0c8-7296-4f74-8897-ce41dd24bebe","data":{"text":"to navigate bodies of water.","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_SURVIVAL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"Rows of triangles symbolizing shark teeth protect you from danger and enable you to take fierce retaliation against those who try to harm you. Seafarers, especially those on the seas of Minata, wear these tattoos in patterns, with multiple rows of regular triangles. You gain a +1 item bonus to Survival checks to navigate bodies of water.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"REACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">5</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Trigger** You would be hit by an attack against your AC; **Effect** You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against the attack, or a +2 circumstance bonus if the attacker is in water or has the [amphibious](link_trait_2416), [aquatic](link_trait_2429), or [water](link_trait_1584) trait. Whether the attack hits or misses, you gain a +2 status bonus to damage with the next [Strike](link_action_19856) you make against the attacker before the end of your next turn.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12558,"bulk":"0","name":"Triangular Teeth","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"3694379258315238","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":2,"price":{"gp":33},"usage":"tattooed on the body","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527,1504,2857],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":"","extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4755","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"122"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","value":1,"selector":"survival","predicate":["water"]},{"key":"RollOption","domain":"survival","option":"navwater"}],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{"slots":[]},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:23.86474+00:00","operations":[{"id":"0e3cc0c8-7296-4f74-8897-ce41dd24bebe","data":{"text":"to navigate bodies of water.","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_SURVIVAL"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"Rows of triangles symbolizing shark teeth protect you from danger and enable you to take fierce retaliation against those who try to harm you. Seafarers, especially those on the seas of Minata, wear these tattoos in patterns, with multiple rows of regular triangles. You gain a +1 item bonus to Survival checks to navigate bodies of water.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"REACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">5</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)); **Frequency** once per day; **Trigger** You would be hit by an attack against your AC; **Effect** You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against the attack, or a +2 circumstance bonus if the attacker is in water or has the [amphibious](link_trait_2416), [aquatic](link_trait_2429), or [water](link_trait_1584) trait. Whether the attack hits or misses, you gain a +2 status bonus to damage with the next [Strike](link_action_19856) you make against the attacker before the end of your next turn.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12559,"type":"item","before":{"id":12559,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Trickster's Mandolin (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5004326318681088","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":8,"price":{"gp":460},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[2861,1514,1546],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4805","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"137"},"charges":{},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"item","value":1,"selector":["deception","performance"]}],"container_id":null},"category":"","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:24.491209+00:00","operations":[{"id":"42759d64-fa15-4c74-bfb4-0b28f96ae928","data":{"text":"while playing the mandolin","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_PERFORMANCE"},"type":"addBonusToValue"},{"id":"bb0b51c3-f69c-4598-be54-10578bde555a","data":{"text":"while playing the mandolin","type":"item","value":"1","variable":"SKILL_DECEPTION"},"type":"addBonusToValue"}],"description":"Sought after by many unscrupulous bards, this instrument is surprisingly light and easy to carry, but also empowered with a number of spells carefully selected to help with fooling others or making a hasty retreat. While playing the mandolin, you gain a +1 item bonus to Deception and Performance checks.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)) **Effect** You change the instrument's color and shape to one you prefer, and you can turn it into a different handheld string instrument that takes two hands to play.\n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611); **Effect** You expend a number of charges from this instrument to [Cast a spell](link_action_19611) from its list.\n\n*   **Cantrip** *[prestidigitation](link_spell_4778)*\n    \n*   **1st** *[illusory disguise](link_spell_4677)*, *[item facade](link_spell_4691)*, *[ventriloquism](link_spell_4931)*\n    \n*   **2nd** *[blur](link_spel