 [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884)'s range, which increases to 60 feet. However, you have a tough time filtering the mental noise. If any creatures can be detected by your thoughtsense, you take a –1 penalty to Perception checks. When you arrive in a space after using the activation to teleport, you create a 10-foot emanation that works like *[strange geometry](link_spell_6775)* for 1 round. This emanation can affect you.\n\nIf you die at this stage or higher, your body implodes. Your soul reincarnates as an [aberration](link_trait_2427) of a level close to yours, which extrudes from the location of your implosion. Common forms include [jah-tohl](link_creature_10154), [gosreg](link_creature_10101), [quelaunt](link_creature_10260), [rhu-chalik](link_creature_10272), [shoggoth](link_creature_10542), and [xoarian](link_creature_10388). This creature isn't you, but fleeting memories of your former existence remain with it. You can't be raised from the dead while this monster endures. The [void fragment](link_item_12594) reappears somewhere on the same planet.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 3 (32 Days)** Your [telepathy](link_physical-feature_28884) range increases to 100 feet, and the wisp grants you resistance to [mental](link_trait_1448) damage equal to your level. The mental noise increases the penalty to Perception to –2. Whenever you roll initiative, you become confused for up to 1d4 rounds.\n\n* * *\n\n**Stage 4** You die.\n\n* * *\n\n**Purging** You must find and slay a powerful [aberration](link_trait_2427) or a servant of such creatures the GM deems appropriate. The creature must be of your level or higher. Then, someone must cast a *[rest eternal](link_spell_6688)* ritual on you and the dead being; you must be anointed with the same oils the ritual normally requires. If the ritual results in a success, it casts the slain creature into the void along with the _[void fragment](link_item_12594)_ inside you, ending its effects on you.","availability":null,"content_sou