st a Spell](link_action_19611); **Effect** You [cast](link_action_19611) *[shield](link_spell_4831)*.\n\n**Activate** [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611); **Frequency** once per day; **Effect** You [cast](link_action_19611) *[spiritual armament](link_spell_4855)*.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12709,"type":"item","before":{"id":12709,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Warpwobble Poison","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1246852420845927","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":8,"price":{"gp":90},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1476,1564,1448],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2020","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"71"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:57.393969+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n[Warpwobble poison](link_item_12709) causes hallucinations of space bending and stretching, leading to vertigo and an inability to discern a stable place to move.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 26 Will\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** treat all squares as difficult terrain (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** treat all squares as greater difficult terrain (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** treat all squares as uneven ground (DC 26), treating a critical success to [Balance](link_action_19608) as a success, and a success as a success but moving on greater difficult terrain (1 round)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12709,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Warpwobble Poison","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"1246852420845927","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":8,"price":{"gp":90},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1476,1564,1448],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2020","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"71"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:57.393969+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n[Warpwobble poison](link_item_12709) causes hallucinations of space bending and stretching, leading to vertigo and an inability to discern a stable place to move.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 26 Will\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** treat all squares as difficult terrain (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** treat all squares as greater difficult terrain (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** treat all squares as uneven ground (DC 26), treating a critical success to [Balance](link_action_19608) as a success, and a success as a success but moving on greater difficult terrain (1 round)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12710,"type":"item","before":{"id":12710,"bulk":"1","name":"Wasp Guard","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4497824975924283","group":"ARMOR","hands":null,"level":8,"price":{"gp":487},"usage":"worn armor","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"leather","runes":{"potency":1,"property":[],"resilient":0},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4388","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"19"},"dex_cap":3,"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"status","value":1,"selector":"reflex","predicate":[{"or":["action:swarming-bites","action:swarming-stings"]}]}],"container_id":null},"ac_bonus":2,"category":"light","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"strength":1,"base_item":"studded-leather-armor","check_penalty":-1,"speed_penalty":0,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:57.954712+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Druids and Calistria's faithful alike value this vindictive armor for its ability to turn away pests and exact revenge on foes in a manner that can easily turn coordinated enemies into a chaotic mass. _[Wasp guard](link_item_12710)_ is _[+1](link_item_6719) [studded leather](link_item_7863)_ studded with the carapaces of wasps, subtly diverting swarms away and granting a +1 status bonus to Reflex saving throws against Swarming Bites, Swarming Stings, and similar abilities from swarms.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"REACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">R</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An enemy within 30 feet [Strikes](link_action_19856) you with an attack\n\n**Effect** You animate the exoskeletons of the _[wasp guard](link_item_12710)_ armor into a spectral swarm of wasps that seeks revenge for the slight. The swarm flies to the triggering enemy's space and swarms about them, dealing 1d8 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476) damage. If the affected enemy has any allies within 30 feet, the enemy can spend a single action, which has the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait, to shoo the swarm away. This ends the persistent damage on that enemy automatically, but the swarm instead moves to affect the enemy's ally.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"The initial raw materials must include 1 Bulk of wasp exoskeletons."},"after":{"id":12710,"bulk":"1","name":"Wasp Guard","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4497824975924283","group":"ARMOR","hands":null,"level":8,"price":{"gp":487},"usage":"worn armor","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1527],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"group":"leather","runes":{"potency":1,"property":[],"resilient":0},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4388","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"19"},"dex_cap":3,"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","type":"status","value":1,"selector":"reflex","predicate":[{"or":["action:swarming-bites","action:swarming-stings"]}]}],"container_id":null},"ac_bonus":2,"category":"light","hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"strength":1,"base_item":"studded-leather-armor","check_penalty":-1,"speed_penalty":0,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:57.954712+00:00","operations":null,"description":"Druids and Calistria's faithful alike value this vindictive armor for its ability to turn away pests and exact revenge on foes in a manner that can easily turn coordinated enemies into a chaotic mass. _[Wasp guard](link_item_12710)_ is _[+1](link_item_6719) [studded leather](link_item_7863)_ studded with the carapaces of wasps, subtly diverting swarms away and granting a +1 status bonus to Reflex saving throws against Swarming Bites, Swarming Stings, and similar abilities from swarms.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"REACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">R</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An enemy within 30 feet [Strikes](link_action_19856) you with an attack\n\n**Effect** You animate the exoskeletons of the _[wasp guard](link_item_12710)_ armor into a spectral swarm of wasps that seeks revenge for the slight. The swarm flies to the triggering enemy's space and swarms about them, dealing 1d8 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476) damage. If the affected enemy has any allies within 30 feet, the enemy can spend a single action, which has the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait, to shoo the swarm away. This ends the persistent damage on that enemy automatically, but the swarm instead moves to affect the enemy's ally.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":"The initial raw materials must include 1 Bulk of wasp exoskeletons."},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12711,"type":"item","before":{"id":12711,"bulk":"1","name":"Watchful Portrait","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8956715484045066","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":125},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504,1590],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4662","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"98"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:58.547955+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA [watchful portrait](link_item_12711) appears to be an innocuous depiction of a bored noble, unassuming relative, or unknown local celebrity. You Activate the portrait by hanging it. While it's activated, you can use a single action with the [concentrate](link_trait_1432) trait to see through the eyes of the portrait instead of your own. You can do so while you're within 500 feet of the portrait, even if it's outside your line of sight or line of effect. You visually observe the area around the portrait from its perspective, using your own visual senses. While you're scrying through it, the portrait's eyes follow others more than usual. A creature that succeeds at a Perception 30 check notices this phenomenon.\n\nThe scrying ends after 10 minutes or when you decide to stop watching through the portrait. The painting loses its magic when the scrying ends, if 4 hours pass after you Activate it without you looking through it, or if you Activate a different [watchful portrait](link_item_12711). The portrait then remains a normal, non-[magical](link_trait_1504) work of art, but due to its rather bland subject matter, it is worth no more than 5 gp.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12711,"bulk":"1","name":"Watchful Portrait","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"8956715484045066","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":9,"price":{"gp":125},"usage":"held-in-two-hands","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504,1590],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4662","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"98"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:58.547955+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\nA [watchful portrait](link_item_12711) appears to be an innocuous depiction of a bored noble, unassuming relative, or unknown local celebrity. You Activate the portrait by hanging it. While it's activated, you can use a single action with the [concentrate](link_trait_1432) trait to see through the eyes of the portrait instead of your own. You can do so while you're within 500 feet of the portrait, even if it's outside your line of sight or line of effect. You visually observe the area around the portrait from its perspective, using your own visual senses. While you're scrying through it, the portrait's eyes follow others more than usual. A creature that succeeds at a Perception 30 check notices this phenomenon.\n\nThe scrying ends after 10 minutes or when you decide to stop watching through the portrait. The painting loses its magic when the scrying ends, if 4 hours pass after you Activate it without you looking through it, or if you Activate a different [watchful portrait](link_item_12711). The portrait then remains a normal, non-[magical](link_trait_1504) work of art, but due to its rather bland subject matter, it is worth no more than 5 gp.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12712,"type":"item","before":{"id":12712,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Weapon Harness","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7390826418504289","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":6},"usage":"applied-to-armor","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2858],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4359","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"11"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:59.174972+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A suit of armor with this adjustment incorporates short, flexible harnesses meant to connect weapons to each of its vambraces. These harnesses can each be connected to a melee weapon of light Bulk or less. Attaching or removing a weapon takes an [Interact](link_action_19733) action. Someone else can attach or remove a weapon if you're willing to let them or you're unable to act. You must remove a weapon from its mount before you can completely [Release](link_action_19755) or otherwise stow it.\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC against attempts to [Disarm](link_action_19626) you of a weapon connected to the armor. If the weapon would be knocked from your grasp or you would drop it, the weapon dangles from the bracer by its harness rather than falling to the ground. You can regain control of the weapon in the normal time it takes you to draw it. Attaching a weapon to a [weapon harness](link_item_12712) prevents you from throwing it or using other abilities that would require it to leave your person.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12712,"bulk":"0.1","name":"Weapon Harness","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7390826418504289","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"gp":6},"usage":"applied-to-armor","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[2858],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4359","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"11"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:59.174972+00:00","operations":null,"description":"A suit of armor with this adjustment incorporates short, flexible harnesses meant to connect weapons to each of its vambraces. These harnesses can each be connected to a melee weapon of light Bulk or less. Attaching or removing a weapon takes an [Interact](link_action_19733) action. Someone else can attach or remove a weapon if you're willing to let them or you're unable to act. You must remove a weapon from its mount before you can completely [Release](link_action_19755) or otherwise stow it.\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC against attempts to [Disarm](link_action_19626) you of a weapon connected to the armor. If the weapon would be knocked from your grasp or you would drop it, the weapon dangles from the bracer by its harness rather than falling to the ground. You can regain control of the weapon in the normal time it takes you to draw it. Attaching a weapon to a [weapon harness](link_item_12712) prevents you from throwing it or using other abilities that would require it to leave your person.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12713,"type":"item","before":{"id":12713,"bulk":"0","name":"Weapon Shot (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4023936678029538","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":12,"price":{"gp":400},"usage":"other","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4592","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"83"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:59.693022+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Ammunition** any\n\nThe body of a [weapon shot](link_item_12713) is translucent and filled with quicksilver. It imparts its magic to the weapon used to fire it or it summons a translucent weapon, made of [force](link_trait_1560), to fire it. It's a favorite of killers and sharpshooters who need just one shot in a situation where carrying ammunition is easier than carrying a weapon.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Effect** For the [Strike](link_action_19856) with which you consume the ammunition, the weapon is a [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860) weapon, instead of those of the weapon firing it.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Effect** A ghostly weapon made of [force](link_trait_1560) appears, wielded by you and loaded with the [weapon shot](link_item_12713) you activated. The conjured weapon sublimates into motes of briefly luminous dust if the [weapon shot](link_item_12713) deactivates without you using it or just after you use the activated shot. For the [Strike](link_action_19856) with which it functions, the weapon is a [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860) weapon.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"after":{"id":12713,"bulk":"0","name":"Weapon Shot (Greater)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"4023936678029538","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":12,"price":{"gp":400},"usage":"other","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"hp":0,"bulk":{},"runes":{},"damage":null,"hp_max":0,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=4592","book":"Treasure Vault","page":"83"},"foundry":{"items":[],"rules":[],"container_id":null},"hardness":0,"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"quantity":1,"base_item":null,"broken_threshold":0},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:25:59.693022+00:00","operations":null,"description":"**Ammunition** any\n\nThe body of a [weapon shot](link_item_12713) is translucent and filled with quicksilver. It imparts its magic to the weapon used to fire it or it summons a translucent weapon, made of [force](link_trait_1560), to fire it. It's a favorite of killers and sharpshooters who need just one shot in a situation where carrying ammunition is easier than carrying a weapon.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432))\n\n**Effect** For the [Strike](link_action_19856) with which you consume the ammunition, the weapon is a [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860) weapon, instead of those of the weapon firing it.\n\n**Activate** <abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432), [manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n**Effect** A ghostly weapon made of [force](link_trait_1560) appears, wielded by you and loaded with the [weapon shot](link_item_12713) you activated. The conjured weapon sublimates into motes of briefly luminous dust if the [weapon shot](link_item_12713) deactivates without you using it or just after you use the activated shot. For the [Strike](link_action_19856) with which it functions, the weapon is a [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860) weapon.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","id":12714,"type":"item","before":{"id":12714,"bulk":"0","name":"Weapon Shot (Lesser)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"2924427944680780","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":5,"price":{"gp":20},"usage":"other","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1531,1504],"version":"1.0","me