by 8.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"You channel vital energy to heal the living or damage the undead. If the target is a willing living creature, you restore 1d8 Hit Points. If the target is [undead](link_trait_2425), you deal that amount of vitality damage to it, and it gets a basic Fortitude save. The number of actions you spend when Casting this Spell determines its targets, range, area, and other parameters.\n\n<abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> The spell has a range of touch.\n\n<abbr cost=\"TWO-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">2</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)) The spell has a range of 30 feet. If you're healing a living creature, increase the Hit Points restored by 8.\n\n<abbr cost=\"THREE-ACTIONS\" class=\"action-symbol\">3</abbr> ([concentrate](link_trait_1432)) You disperse vital energy in a 30-foot emanation. This targets all living and undead creatures in the burst.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4658,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4658,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Heroism","rank":3,"uuid":"7197228569596568","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1555","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:41:55.859571+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The status bonus increases to +2.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The status bonus increases to +3.","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You unlock the target’s inner heroism, granting it a +1 status bonus to attack rolls, Perception checks, saving throws, and skill checks.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4658,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Heroism","rank":3,"uuid":"7197228569596568","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1555","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:41:55.859571+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The status bonus increases to +2.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The status bonus increases to +3.","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You unlock the target’s inner heroism, granting it a +1 status bonus to attack rolls, Perception checks, saving throws, and skill checks.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4660,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4660,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Holy Light","rank":3,"uuid":"5838189803258842","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1432,1542,1630,1517,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1557","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"DamageDice","dieSize":"d6","selector":"{item|_id}-damage","predicate":["target:trait:unholy"],"damageType":"spirit","diceNumber":"(@spell.level*2)-1"}],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:42:16.889905+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The fire damage increases by 2d6, and the spirit damage against unholy creatures increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"You shine a blazing ray of light tinged with holy energy. Make a ranged spell attack. The ray deals 5d6 fire damage. If the target has the unholy trait, you deal an extra 5d6 spirit damage.\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes double damage.\n\n**Success** The target takes full damage.\n\nIf the light passes through an area of magical darkness or targets a creature affected by magical darkness, holy light attempts to counteract the darkness. If you need to determine whether the light passes through an area of darkness, draw a line between yourself and the spell's target.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4660,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Holy Light","rank":3,"uuid":"5838189803258842","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1432,1542,1630,1517,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1557","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[{"key":"DamageDice","dieSize":"d6","selector":"{item|_id}-damage","predicate":["target:trait:unholy"],"damageType":"spirit","diceNumber":"(@spell.level*2)-1"}],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:42:16.889905+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The fire damage increases by 2d6, and the spirit damage against unholy creatures increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"You shine a blazing ray of light tinged with holy energy. Make a ranged spell attack. The ray deals 5d6 fire damage. If the target has the unholy trait, you deal an extra 5d6 spirit damage.\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes double damage.\n\n**Success** The target takes full damage.\n\nIf the light passes through an area of magical darkness or targets a creature affected by magical darkness, holy light attempts to counteract the darkness. If you need to determine whether the light passes through an area of darkness, draw a line between yourself and the spell's target.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4661,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4661,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Honeyed Words","rank":4,"uuid":"2986156443295368","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1558","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:42:23.305633+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"Falsehoods pass your lips as smoothly as silk. You gain a +4 status bonus to Deception checks to Lie and against Perception checks to discern if you are telling the truth, and you add your level even if untrained. If the implausibility of your lies prompts a circumstance penalty or a DC increase, reduce that penalty by half or increase it by half.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4661,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Honeyed Words","rank":4,"uuid":"2986156443295368","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1558","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:42:23.305633+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"Falsehoods pass your lips as smoothly as silk. You gain a +4 status bonus to Deception checks to Lie and against Perception checks to discern if you are telling the truth, and you add your level even if untrained. If the implausibility of your lies prompts a circumstance penalty or a DC increase, reduce that penalty by half or increase it by half.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4663,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4663,"area":"Varies","cast":"TWO-TO-THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Howling Blizzard","rank":5,"uuid":"6782831603390241","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1524,1519,1432,1433],"defense":"basic Reflex","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1559","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:42:44.5971+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"2YlEXgT93lbWXENb":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"Freezing winds extend from your hands, pushing away from you with great force. If you [Cast this Spell](link_action_19611) with 2 actions, it has an area of a 60-foot cone; if you Cast this Spell with 3 actions, it has a range of 500 feet and an area of a 30-foot burst. Each creature in the area takes 10d6 cold damage with a basic Reflex save. Snowdrifts and icy gales fill the area until the start of your next turn, making the area difficult terrain.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4663,"area":"Varies","cast":"TWO-TO-THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Howling Blizzard","rank":5,"uuid":"6782831603390241","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1524,1519,1432,1433],"defense":"basic Reflex","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1559","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:42:44.5971+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"2YlEXgT93lbWXENb":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"Freezing winds extend from your hands, pushing away from you with great force. If you [Cast this Spell](link_action_19611) with 2 actions, it has an area of a 60-foot cone; if you Cast this Spell with 3 actions, it has a range of 500 feet and an area of a 30-foot burst. Each creature in the area takes 10d6 cold damage with a basic Reflex save. Snowdrifts and icy gales fill the area until the start of your next turn, making the area difficult terrain.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4664,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4664,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Humanoid Form","rank":2,"uuid":"1836540857014733","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1560","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:02.99899+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You gain darkvision or low-light vision if the form you assume has that ability.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can take on the appearance of a Large humanoid. If this increases your size, you gain the effects of the [enlarge](link_spell_4601) spell.","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You transform your appearance to that of a Small or Medium humanoid, such as a dwarf, elf, goblin, halfling, human, or orc. You gain the [humanoid](link_trait_2399) trait in addition to your other traits while in this form, as well as any trait related to the creature's kind (such as [goblin](link_trait_1468) or [human](link_trait_1436)). If this transformation reduces your size, it reduces your reach accordingly (typically to 5 feet). This transformation doesn't change your statistics in any way, and you don't gain any special abilities of the humanoid form you assume. You can still wear and use your gear, which changes size (if necessary) to match your new form. If items leave your person, they return to their usual size.\n\nHumanoid form grants you a +4 status bonus to Deception checks to pass as a generic member of the chosen ancestry, and you add your level even if you're untrained, but you can't make yourself look like a specific person. If you want to [Impersonate](link_action_19731) an individual, you still need to create a disguise, though the GM won't factor in the difference in ancestry when determining the DC of your Deception check. You can Dismiss this spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4664,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Humanoid Form","rank":2,"uuid":"1836540857014733","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1560","book":"Player Core","page":"335"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:02.99899+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You gain darkvision or low-light vision if the form you assume has that ability.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can take on the appearance of a Large humanoid. If this increases your size, you gain the effects of the [enlarge](link_spell_4601) spell.","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You transform your appearance to that of a Small or Medium humanoid, such as a dwarf, elf, goblin, halfling, human, or orc. You gain the [humanoid](link_trait_2399) trait in addition to your other traits while in this form, as well as any trait related to the creature's kind (such as [goblin](link_trait_1468) or [human](link_trait_1436)). If this transformation reduces your size, it reduces your reach accordingly (typically to 5 feet). This transformation doesn't change your statistics in any way, and you don't gain any special abilities of the humanoid form you assume. You can still wear and use your gear, which changes size (if necessary) to match your new form. If items leave your person, they return to their usual size.\n\nHumanoid form grants you a +4 status bonus to Deception checks to pass as a generic member of the chosen ancestry, and you add your level even if you're untrained, but you can't make yourself look like a specific person. If you want to [Impersonate](link_action_19731) an individual, you still need to create a disguise, though the GM won't factor in the difference in ancestry when determining the DC of your Deception check. You can Dismiss this spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4668,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4668,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hydraulic Push","rank":1,"uuid":"7933251160172783","range":"60 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1432,1433,1584],"defense":"AC","targets":"1 creature or unattended object","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1561","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:27.375833+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The bludgeoning damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You call forth a powerful blast of pressurized water that bludgeons the target and knocks it back. Make a ranged spell attack roll.\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage and is knocked back 10 feet.\n\n**Success** The target takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage and is knocked back 5 feet.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4668,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hydraulic Push","rank":1,"uuid":"7933251160172783","range":"60 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1432,1433,1584],"defense":"AC","targets":"1 creature or unattended object","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1561","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:27.375833+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The bludgeoning damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You call forth a powerful blast of pressurized water that bludgeons the target and knocks it back. Make a ranged spell attack roll.\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage and is knocked back 10 feet.\n\n**Success** The target takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage and is knocked back 5 feet.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4669,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4669,"area":"60-foot line","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hydraulic Torrent","rank":4,"uuid":"483303192342829","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1584],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1562","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:31.523702+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"A swirling torrent of water manifests along a straight line, battering creatures and unattended objects in its path and possibly pushing them away from you. The torrent deals 8d6 bludgeoning damage. Each creature in the area must attempt a basic Fortitude save; unattended objects automatically fail. Creatures and objects that fail are also knocked back 5 feet (10 feet on a critical failure).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4669,"area":"60-foot line","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hydraulic Torrent","rank":4,"uuid":"483303192342829","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1584],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1562","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:31.523702+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"A swirling torrent of water manifests along a straight line, battering creatures and unattended objects in its path and possibly pushing them away from you. The torrent deals 8d6 bludgeoning damage. Each creature in the area must attempt a basic Fortitude save; unattended objects automatically fail. Creatures and objects that fail are also knocked back 5 feet (10 feet on a critical failure).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4670,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4670,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hymn of Healing","rank":1,"uuid":"8727617155097585","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1341,1895,1432,1856,1442,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"you or 1 ally","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained up to 4 rounds","meta_data":{"focus":true,"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1768","book":"Player Core","page":"370"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":true}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:38.092117+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"damage":{}},"text":[{"text":"The fast healing and temporary Hit Points each increase by 2.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":[],"description":"Your glorious singing mends wounds and provides a temporary respite from harm. The target gains fast healing 2. When you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) and the first time each round you [Sustain the Spell](link_action_19858), the target gains 2 temporary Hit Points, which last for 1 round.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4670,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hymn of Healing","rank":1,"uuid":"8727617155097585","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1341,1895,1432,1856,1442,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"you or 1 ally","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained up to 4 rounds","meta_data":{"focus":true,"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1768","book":"Player Core","page":"370"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":true}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:38.092117+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"damage":{}},"text":[{"text":"The fast healing and temporary Hit Points each increase by 2.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":[],"description":"Your glorious singing mends wounds and provides a temporary respite from harm. The target gains fast healing 2. When you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) and the first time each round you [Sustain the Spell](link_action_19858), the target gains 2 temporary Hit Points, which last for 1 round.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4671,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4671,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Hypercognition","rank":3,"uuid":"706993312092064","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1563","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:42.673163+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"You rapidly catalog and collate information relevant to your current situation. You can instantly use up to 6 [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753) actions as part of [Casting this Spell](link_action_19611). For these actions, you can't use any special abilities, reactions, or free actions that trigger when you [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4671,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Hypercognition","rank":3,"uuid":"706993312092064","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1563","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:42.673163+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"You rapidly catalog and collate information relevant to your current situation. You can instantly use up to 6 [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753) actions as part of [Casting this Spell](link_action_19611). For these actions, you can't use any special abilities, reactions, or free actions that trigger when you [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4672,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4672,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hypnotize","rank":3,"uuid":"1700774664024665","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1447,1433,1899,1479],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1564","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:54.931349+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You create a cloud of mesmerizing patterns and colors that hovers in the air. Creatures are dazzled while inside the cloud. In addition, a creature must attempt a Will saving throw if it is inside the cloud when you cast it, when it enters the cloud, when it ends its turn within the cloud, or if it uses a [Seek](link_action_19845) or [Interact](link_action_19733) action on the cloud. A creature currently fascinated by hypnotize doesn't attempt new saves.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target is fascinated by the cloud.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is fascinated by the cloud. While it remains fascinated, it can't use reactions.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4672,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Hypnotize","rank":3,"uuid":"1700774664024665","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1447,1433,1899,1479],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1564","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:43:54.931349+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You create a cloud of mesmerizing patterns and colors that hovers in the air. Creatures are dazzled while inside the cloud. In addition, a creature must attempt a Will saving throw if it is inside the cloud when you cast it, when it enters the cloud, when it ends its turn within the cloud, or if it uses a [Seek](link_action_19845) or [Interact](link_action_19733) action on the cloud. A creature currently fascinated by hypnotize doesn't attempt new saves.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target is fascinated by the cloud.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is fascinated by the cloud. While it remains fascinated, it can't use reactions.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4674,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4674,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Ignition","rank":0,"uuid":"3795465821336162","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1858,1432,1542,1433],"defense":"AC","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1565","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:13.038333+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"cQDyW0QpjJ38MlSi":"1d4"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The initial damage increases by 1d4 and the persistent fire damage on a critical hit increases by 1d4.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You snap your fingers and point at a target, which begins to smolder. Make a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 2d4 (⬆️{{ceil(level/2)+1}}d4) fire damage on a hit. If the target is within your melee reach, you can choose to make a melee spell attack with the flame instead of a ranged spell attack, which increases all the spell's damage dice to d6s.\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes double damage and 1d4 (⬆️{{ceil(level/2)}}d4) persistent fire damage.\n\n**Success** The target takes full damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4674,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Ignition","rank":0,"uuid":"3795465821336162","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1858,1432,1542,1433],"defense":"AC","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1565","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:13.038333+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"cQDyW0QpjJ38MlSi":"1d4"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The initial damage increases by 1d4 and the persistent fire damage on a critical hit increases by 1d4.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You snap your fingers and point at a target, which begins to smolder. Make a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 2d4 (⬆️{{ceil(level/2)+1}}d4) fire damage on a hit. If the target is within your melee reach, you can choose to make a melee spell attack with the flame instead of a ranged spell attack, which increases all the spell's damage dice to d6s.\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes double damage and 1d4 (⬆️{{ceil(level/2)}}d4) persistent fire damage.\n\n**Success** The target takes full damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4675,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4675,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Ill Omen","rank":1,"uuid":"5824007121754357","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1433,1677],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 round","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1566","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:23.406235+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"The target is struck with [misfortune](link_trait_1677), which throws it off balance. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The first time during the duration that the target attempts an attack roll or skill check, it must roll twice and use the worse result.\n\n**Critical Failure** Every time during the duration that the target attempts an attack roll or skill check, it must roll twice and use the worse result.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4675,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Ill Omen","rank":1,"uuid":"5824007121754357","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1433,1677],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 round","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1566","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:23.406235+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"The target is struck with [misfortune](link_trait_1677), which throws it off balance. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The first time during the duration that the target attempts an attack roll or skill check, it must roll twice and use the worse result.\n\n**Critical Failure** Every time during the duration that the target attempts an attack roll or skill check, it must roll twice and use the worse result.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4676,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4676,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Illusory Creature","rank":2,"uuid":"1833735849829376","range":"500 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1447,1433,2131,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1567","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:45.53647+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The damage of the image's Strikes increases by 1d4, and the maximum size of creature you can create increases by one (to a maximum of Gargantuan).","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You create an illusory image of a Large or smaller creature. It generates the appropriate sounds, smells, and feels believable to the touch. If you and the image are ever farther than 500 feet apart, the spell ends.\n\nThe image can't speak, but you can use your actions to speak through the creature, with the spell disguising your voice as appropriate. You might need to attempt a Deception or Performance check to mimic the creature, as determined by the GM. This is especially likely if you're trying to imitate a specific person and engage with someone that person knows.\n\nIn combat, the illusion can use 2 actions per turn, which it uses when you [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948). It uses your spell attack modifier for attack rolls and your spell DC for its AC. Its saving throw modifiers are equal to your spell DC – 10. It is substantial enough that it can flank other creatures. If the image is hit by an attack or fails a save, the spell ends.\n\nThe illusion can cause damage by making the target believe the illusion's attacks are real, but it cannot otherwise directly affect the physical world. If the illusory creature hits with a Strike, the target takes 3d4 mental damage. The illusion's [Strikes](link_action_20926) are [nonlethal](link_trait_1571). If the damage doesn't correspond to the image of the monster—for example, if an illusory Large dragon deals only 5 damage—the GM might allow the target to attempt an immediate Perception check to disbelieve the spell. Any relevant resistances and weaknesses apply if the target thinks they do, as judged by the GM. For example, if the illusion wields a warhammer and attacks a creature resistant to bludgeoning damage, the creature would take less mental damage. However, illusory damage does not deactivate regeneration or trigger other effects that require a certain damage type. The GM should track illusory damage dealt by the illusion.\n\nAny creature that touches the image or uses the [Seek](link_action_19845) action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion. When a creature disbelieves the illusion, it recovers from half the damage it had taken from it (if any) and doesn't take any further damage from it.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4676,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Illusory Creature","rank":2,"uuid":"1833735849829376","range":"500 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1447,1433,2131,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1567","book":"Player Core","page":"336"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:45.53647+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The damage of the image's Strikes increases by 1d4, and the maximum size of creature you can create increases by one (to a maximum of Gargantuan).","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You create an illusory image of a Large or smaller creature. It generates the appropriate sounds, smells, and feels believable to the touch. If you and the image are ever farther than 500 feet apart, the spell ends.\n\nThe image can't speak, but you can use your actions to speak through the creature, with the spell disguising your voice as appropriate. You might need to attempt a Deception or Performance check to mimic the creature, as determined by the GM. This is especially likely if you're trying to imitate a specific person and engage with someone that person knows.\n\nIn combat, the illusion can use 2 actions per turn, which it uses when you [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948). It uses your spell attack modifier for attack rolls and your spell DC for its AC. Its saving throw modifiers are equal to your spell DC – 10. It is substantial enough that it can flank other creatures. If the image is hit by an attack or fails a save, the spell ends.\n\nThe illusion can cause damage by making the target believe the illusion's attacks are real, but it cannot otherwise directly affect the physical world. If the illusory creature hits with a Strike, the target takes 3d4 mental damage. The illusion's [Strikes](link_action_20926) are [nonlethal](link_trait_1571). If the damage doesn't correspond to the image of the monster—for example, if an illusory Large dragon deals only 5 damage—the GM might allow the target to attempt an immediate Perception check to disbelieve the spell. Any relevant resistances and weaknesses apply if the target thinks they do, as judged by the GM. For example, if the illusion wields a warhammer and attacks a creature resistant to bludgeoning damage, the creature would take less mental damage. However, illusory damage does not deactivate regeneration or trigger other effects that require a certain damage type. The GM should track illusory damage dealt by the illusion.\n\nAny creature that touches the image or uses the [Seek](link_action_19845) action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion. When a creature disbelieves the illusion, it recovers from half the damage it had taken from it (if any) and doesn't take any further damage from it.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4677,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4677,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Illusory Disguise","rank":1,"uuid":"2506771266650650","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1568","book":"Player Core","page":"337"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:56.386986+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The target can appear as any creature of the same size, even a specific individual. You must have seen an individual to replicate its appearance, and must have heard its voice to replicate its voice.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can target up to 10 willing creatures. If you target multiple creatures, you can choose a different disguise for each target, but none can impersonate a specific individual. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) each disguise individually or all collectively.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"As 4th, but you can choose disguises that impersonate specific individuals. You must have seen an individual to replicate its appearance, and must have heard its voice to replicate its voice.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You create an illusion that causes the target to appear as another creature of the same body shape, and with roughly similar height (within 6 inches) and weight (within 50 pounds). The disguise is typically good enough to hide their identity, but not to impersonate a specific individual. The spell changes their appearance and voice, but not mannerisms. You can change the appearance of its clothing and worn items, such as making its armor look like a dress. Held items are unaffected, and any worn item removed from the creature returns to its true appearance.\n\nCasting _illusory disguise_ counts as setting up a disguise for the [Impersonate](link_action_19731) use of Deception; it ignores any circumstance penalties the target might take for disguising itself as a dissimilar creature, gives a +4 status bonus to Deception checks to prevent others from seeing through the disguise, and lets the target add its level to such Deception checks even if untrained. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) this spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4677,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Illusory Disguise","rank":1,"uuid":"2506771266650650","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1568","book":"Player Core","page":"337"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:44:56.386986+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The target can appear as any creature of the same size, even a specific individual. You must have seen an individual to replicate its appearance, and must have heard its voice to replicate its voice.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can target up to 10 willing creatures. If you target multiple creatures, you can choose a different disguise for each target, but none can impersonate a specific individual. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) each disguise individually or all collectively.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"As 4th, but you can choose disguises that impersonate specific individuals. You must have seen an individual to replicate its appearance, and must have heard its voice to replicate its voice.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You create an illusion that causes the target to appear as another creature of the same body shape, and with roughly similar height (within 6 inches) and weight (within 50 pounds). The disguise is typically good enough to hide their identity, but not to impersonate a specific individual. The spell changes their appearance and voice, but not mannerisms. You can change the appearance of its clothing and worn items, such as making its armor look like a dress. Held items are unaffected, and any worn item removed from the creature returns to its true appearance.\n\nCasting _illusory disguise_ counts as setting up a disguise for the [Impersonate](link_action_19731) use of Deception; it ignores any circumstance penalties the target might take for disguising itself as a dissimilar creature, gives a +4 status bonus to Deception checks to prevent others from seeing through the disguise, and lets the target add its level to such Deception checks even if untrained. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) this spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4679,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4679,"area":"30-foot burst","cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Illusory Scene","rank":5,"uuid":"6119491827813298","range":"500 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1447,1433,2131,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1570","book":"Player Core","page":"337"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:45:19.789719+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Creatures or objects in your scene can speak. You must speak the specific lines for each actor when creating your program. The spell disguises your voice for each actor.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"As the 6th-rank version, and the duration is unlimited.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You craft an imaginary scene that includes up to 10 discrete creatures or objects of various sizes, all of which must be within the spell's area. These elements generate appropriate sounds and smells, and they feel right to the touch. Elements of an illusory scene are incapable of speech. Unlike with the [illusory creature](link_spell_4676) spell, creatures in your scene lack combat abilities and statistics. Your scene doesn't include changes to the environment around it, though you can place your scene within the illusory environment of a [mirage](link_spell_4726) spell.\n\nWhen you create the scene, you can choose to have it be static or follow a program. Though a static scene is stationary, it includes basic natural movement. For example, wind blowing on an illusory piece of paper would rustle it. A program can be up to 1 minute long and repeats when finished. For instance, you could create a scene of two orcs fighting each other, and the fight would go the same way for each repetition. If you create a loop, the two fighters end up in the same place at the start of the scene and at the end of it, but you can smooth the program so it's hard to tell when the loop ends and begins. Anyone observing the scene for more than a few minutes almost always notices it looping. You're unable to alter the program after you create the illusion.\n\nAny creature that touches any part of the image or uses the [Seek](link_action_19845) action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion. If they interact with a portion of the illusion, they disbelieve only that portion. They disbelieve the entire scene only on a critical success.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4679,"area":"30-foot burst","cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Illusory Scene","rank":5,"uuid":"6119491827813298","range":"500 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1432,1447,1433,2131,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1570","book":"Player Core","page":"337"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:45:19.789719+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Creatures or objects in your scene can speak. You must speak the specific lines for each actor when creating your program. The spell disguises your voice for each actor.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"As the 6th-rank version, and the duration is unlimited.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You craft an imaginary scene that includes up to 10 discrete creatures or objects of various sizes, all of which must be within the spell's area. These elements generate appropriate sounds and smells, and they feel right to the touch. Elements of an illusory scene are incapable of speech. Unlike with the [illusory creature](link_spell_4676) spell, creatures in your scene lack combat abilities and statistics. Your scene doesn't include changes to the environment around it, though you can place your scene within the illusory environment of a [mirage](link_spell_4726) spell.\n\nWhen you create the scene, you can choose to have it be static or follow a program. Though a static scene is stationary, it includes basic natural movement. For example, wind blowing on an illusory piece of paper would rustle it. A program can be up to 1 minute long and repeats when finished. For instance, you could create a scene of two orcs fighting each other, and the fight would go the same way for each repetition. If you create a loop, the two fighters end up in the same place at the start of the scene and at the end of it, but you can smooth the program so it's hard to tell when the loop ends and begins. Anyone observing the scene for more than a few minutes almost always notices it looping. You're unable to alter the program after you create the illusion.\n\nAny creature that touches any part of the image or uses the [Seek](link_action_19845) action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion. If they interact with a portion of the illusion, they disbelieve only that portion. They disbelieve the entire scene only on a critical success.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4683,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4683,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Indestructibility","rank":10,"uuid":"5975336473953083","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the start of your next turn","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1573","book":"Player Core","page":"338"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:46:05.97091+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You sever yourself from cause and effect. For the duration of the spell, you are immune to any effect or damage that would harm you, excluding effects caused by artifacts, deific power, and similarly powerful sources. You can selectively allow yourself to be affected by anything you're willing to have affect you.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4683,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Indestructibility","rank":10,"uuid":"5975336473953083","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the start of your next turn","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1573","book":"Player Core","page":"338"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:46:05.97091+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You sever yourself from cause and effect. For the duration of the spell, you are immune to any effect or damage that would harm you, excluding effects caused by artifacts, deific power, and similarly powerful sources. You can selectively allow yourself to be affected by anything you're willing to have affect you.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4685,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4685,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Insect Form","rank":3,"uuid":"1464551210591452","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1575","book":"Player Core","page":"338"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:47:14.532055+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Your battle form is Large, and your attacks have 10-foot [reach](link_trait_1573). You instead gain 15 temporary HP, attack modifier +16, damage bonus +6, and Athletics +16.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"Your battle form is Huge, and your attacks have 15-foot reach. You instead gain 20 temporary HP, attack modifier +18, damage bonus +2 and double damage dice (including persistent damage), and Athletics +20.","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You envision a simple bug and transform into a Medium animal battle form. When you [Cast this Spell](link_action_19611), choose a listed battle form. You can decide the specific type of animal (such as such as a ladybug or scarab for beetle), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the [animal](link_trait_2409) trait. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) this spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose:\n\n*   AC = 18 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n    \n*   10 temporary Hit Points.\n    \n*   [Low-light vision](link_sense_19330).\n    \n*   One or more attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can [Strike](link_action_19856) with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +13, and your damage bonus is +2. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the enfeebled condition). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.\n    \n*   Athletics modifier of +13, unless your own is higher.\n    \n\nYou also gain specific abilities based on the form you choose:\n\n*   **Ant** Speed 30 feet, climb 30 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> mandibles, **Damage** 2d6 bludgeoning.\n    \n*   **Beetle** Speed 25 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> mandibles, **Damage** 2d10 bludgeoning.\n    \n*   **Centipede** Speed 25 feet, climb 25 feet; darkvision; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> mandibles, **Damage** 1d8 piercing plus 1d4 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476).\n    \n*   **Mantis** Speed 40 feet; imprecise scent 30 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> foreleg, **Damage** 2d8 piercing.\n    \n*   **Scorpion** Speed 40 feet; [darkvision](link_sense_20769), imprecise [tremorsense](link_sense_21079) 60 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> stinger, **Damage** 1d8 piercing plus 1d4 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476); **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> pincer (agile), **Damage** 1d6 bludgeoning.\n    \n*   **Spider** Speed 25 feet, climb 25 feet; [darkvision](link_sense_20769); **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> fangs, **Damage** 1d6 piercing plus 1d4 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476); **Ranged** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> web (range increment 20 feet), **Damage** immobilizes the target for 1 round or until it [Escapes](link_action_19632).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4685,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Insect Form","rank":3,"uuid":"1464551210591452","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1575","book":"Player Core","page":"338"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:47:14.532055+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Your battle form is Large, and your attacks have 10-foot [reach](link_trait_1573). You instead gain 15 temporary HP, attack modifier +16, damage bonus +6, and Athletics +16.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"Your battle form is Huge, and your attacks have 15-foot reach. You instead gain 20 temporary HP, attack modifier +18, damage bonus +2 and double damage dice (including persistent damage), and Athletics +20.","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You envision a simple bug and transform into a Medium animal battle form. When you [Cast this Spell](link_action_19611), choose a listed battle form. You can decide the specific type of animal (such as such as a ladybug or scarab for beetle), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the [animal](link_trait_2409) trait. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) this spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose:\n\n*   AC = 18 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n    \n*   10 temporary Hit Points.\n    \n*   [Low-light vision](link_sense_19330).\n    \n*   One or more attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can [Strike](link_action_19856) with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +13, and your damage bonus is +2. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the enfeebled condition). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.\n    \n*   Athletics modifier of +13, unless your own is higher.\n    \n\nYou also gain specific abilities based on the form you choose:\n\n*   **Ant** Speed 30 feet, climb 30 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> mandibles, **Damage** 2d6 bludgeoning.\n    \n*   **Beetle** Speed 25 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> mandibles, **Damage** 2d10 bludgeoning.\n    \n*   **Centipede** Speed 25 feet, climb 25 feet; darkvision; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> mandibles, **Damage** 1d8 piercing plus 1d4 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476).\n    \n*   **Mantis** Speed 40 feet; imprecise scent 30 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> foreleg, **Damage** 2d8 piercing.\n    \n*   **Scorpion** Speed 40 feet; [darkvision](link_sense_20769), imprecise [tremorsense](link_sense_21079) 60 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> stinger, **Damage** 1d8 piercing plus 1d4 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476); **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> pincer (agile), **Damage** 1d6 bludgeoning.\n    \n*   **Spider** Speed 25 feet, climb 25 feet; [darkvision](link_sense_20769); **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> fangs, **Damage** 1d6 piercing plus 1d4 persistent [poison](link_trait_1476); **Ranged** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> web (range increment 20 feet), **Damage** immobilizes the target for 1 round or until it [Escapes](link_action_19632).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4687,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4687,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Interplanar Teleport","rank":7,"uuid":"7609947194314161","range":"5 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1470],"defense":null,"targets":"up to 8 willing creatures","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1576","book":"Player Core","page":"339"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:47:38.419121+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You and your allies traverse the barriers between planes of existence. The targets move to another plane, such as the Plane of Fire, the Netherworld, or the Outer Rifts. You must know the destination plane exists and use a magic planar key created from material from that plane as a locus for the spell. While the planar keys for most prominent planes are uncommon, just like the spell _interplanar teleport_, more obscure planes and demiplanes often have rare or possibly even unique planar keys.\n\nThe spell is highly imprecise, and you appear 1d20×25 miles from the last place one of the targets (of your choice) was located the last time that target traveled to the plane. If it's the first time traveling to a particular plane for all targets, you appear at a random location on the plane. _Interplanar teleport_ doesn't provide a means of return travel, though casting _interplanar teleport_ again allows you to return to your previous plane unless there are extenuating circumstances.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a planar key for the destination plane, used as a locus","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4687,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Interplanar Teleport","rank":7,"uuid":"7609947194314161","range":"5 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1470],"defense":null,"targets":"up to 8 willing creatures","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1576","book":"Player Core","page":"339"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:47:38.419121+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You and your allies traverse the barriers between planes of existence. The targets move to another plane, such as the Plane of Fire, the Netherworld, or the Outer Rifts. You must know the destination plane exists and use a magic planar key created from material from that plane as a locus for the spell. While the planar keys for most prominent planes are uncommon, just like the spell _interplanar teleport_, more obscure planes and demiplanes often have rare or possibly even unique planar keys.\n\nThe spell is highly imprecise, and you appear 1d20×25 miles from the last place one of the targets (of your choice) was located the last time that target traveled to the plane. If it's the first time traveling to a particular plane for all targets, you appear at a random location on the plane. _Interplanar teleport_ doesn't provide a means of return travel, though casting _interplanar teleport_ again allows you to return to your previous plane unless there are extenuating circumstances.","availability":null,"requirements":"You have a planar key for the destination plane, used as a locus","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4689,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4689,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Invisibility","rank":2,"uuid":"8105806537970817","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1447,1433,1899],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1577","book":"Player Core","page":"339"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:47:51.959949+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The spell lasts 1 minute, but it doesn't end if the target uses a hostile action.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"Illusions bend light around the target, rendering it invisible. This makes it undetected to all creatures, though the creatures can attempt to find the target, making it hidden to them instead. If the target uses a hostile action, the spell ends after that hostile action is completed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4689,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Invisibility","rank":2,"uuid":"8105806537970817","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1447,1433,1899],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1577","book":"Player Core","page":"339"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:47:51.959949+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The spell lasts 1 minute, but it doesn't end if the target uses a hostile action.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"Illusions bend light around the target, rendering it invisible. This makes it undetected to all creatures, though the creatures can attempt to find the target, making it hidden to them instead. If the target uses a hostile action, the spell ends after that hostile action is completed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4690,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4690,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Invoke Spirits","rank":5,"uuid":"4078371931720666","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1487,1433,1448,1485],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1578","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:02.947705+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d4","1":"1d4"},"interval":2},"text":[{"text":"The mental damage and void damage each increase by 1d4.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"Ragged apparitions of the dead rise to stalk the living. They deal 2d4 mental damage and 2d4 void damage to each living creature in the area, with a basic Will save. Additionally, creatures that critically fail the save are frightened 2 and are fleeing for 1 round.\n\nOn subsequent rounds, the first time you [Sustain the Spell](link_action_20948) each round, you can move the area up to 30 feet within the range of the spell. Living creatures in the new area must attempt saves with the same effects as above, except that critically failing doesn't make them flee.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4690,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Invoke Spirits","rank":5,"uuid":"4078371931720666","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1487,1433,1448,1485],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1578","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:02.947705+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d4","1":"1d4"},"interval":2},"text":[{"text":"The mental damage and void damage each increase by 1d4.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"Ragged apparitions of the dead rise to stalk the living. They deal 2d4 mental damage and 2d4 void damage to each living creature in the area, with a basic Will save. Additionally, creatures that critically fail the save are frightened 2 and are fleeing for 1 round.\n\nOn subsequent rounds, the first time you [Sustain the Spell](link_action_20948) each round, you can move the area up to 30 feet within the range of the spell. Living creatures in the new area must attempt saves with the same effects as above, except that critically failing doesn't make them flee.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4691,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4691,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Item Facade","rank":1,"uuid":"247290672016665","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"1 object no more than 10 feet by 10 feet by 10 feet","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1579","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:12.030723+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The duration is 24 hours.","amount":"(2nd)"},{"text":"The duration is unlimited.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You make the target object look and feel as though it were in much better or worse physical condition. When you Cast this Spell, decide whether you want to make the object look decrepit or perfect. An item made to look decrepit appears broken and shoddy. An intact item made to look better appears as though it's brand new and highly polished or well maintained. A broken item appears to be intact and functional. Destroyed items can't be affected by this spell. A creature that [Interacts](link_action_19733) with the item can attempt to disbelieve the illusion.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4691,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Item Facade","rank":1,"uuid":"247290672016665","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"1 object no more than 10 feet by 10 feet by 10 feet","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1579","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:12.030723+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The duration is 24 hours.","amount":"(2nd)"},{"text":"The duration is unlimited.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You make the target object look and feel as though it were in much better or worse physical condition. When you Cast this Spell, decide whether you want to make the object look decrepit or perfect. An item made to look decrepit appears broken and shoddy. An intact item made to look better appears as though it's brand new and highly polished or well maintained. A broken item appears to be intact and functional. Destroyed items can't be affected by this spell. A creature that [Interacts](link_action_19733) with the item can attempt to disbelieve the illusion.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4692,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4692,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Jump","rank":1,"uuid":"3325365287661769","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1505],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1580","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:17.921221+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"3":{"range":{"value":"touch"},"target":{"value":"1 creature"}}}},"text":[{"text":"The range becomes touch, the target changes to one touched creature, and the duration becomes 1 minute, allowing the target to jump as described whenever it takes the [Leap](link_action_19735) action.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"Your legs surge with strength, ready to leap high and far. You jump 30 feet in any direction without touching the ground. You must land on a space of solid ground within 30 feet of you, or else you fall after using your next action.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4692,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Jump","rank":1,"uuid":"3325365287661769","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1433,1505],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1580","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:17.921221+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"3":{"range":{"value":"touch"},"target":{"value":"1 creature"}}}},"text":[{"text":"The range becomes touch, the target changes to one touched creature, and the duration becomes 1 minute, allowing the target to jump as described whenever it takes the [Leap](link_action_19735) action.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"Your legs surge with strength, ready to leap high and far. You jump 30 feet in any direction without touching the ground. You must land on a space of solid ground within 30 feet of you, or else you fall after using your next action.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4693,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4693,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Knock","rank":2,"uuid":"4915241677831616","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 door, lock, or container","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1581","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:30.514691+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You make the target easier to open.\n\nKnock grants a +4 status bonus to any creature that tries to open the target door, lock, or container with an Athletics or a Thievery check. You can attempt a Thievery check to open the target as part of casting knock, and you add your level even if you're untrained.\n\nKnock counteracts [lock](link_spell_4705).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4693,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Knock","rank":2,"uuid":"4915241677831616","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 door, lock, or container","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1581","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:30.514691+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You make the target easier to open.\n\nKnock grants a +4 status bonus to any creature that tries to open the target door, lock, or container with an Athletics or a Thievery check. You can attempt a Thievery check to open the target as part of casting knock, and you add your level even if you're untrained.\n\nKnock counteracts [lock](link_spell_4705).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4695,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4695,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Know the Way","rank":0,"uuid":"6662429283182919","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1508,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1582","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:39.301612+00:00","heightened":{"text":[{"text":"You can choose a location you were at within the last week.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can choose a location you were at regardless of how long ago you were there.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult","primal"],"description":"In your mind's eye, you magically reorient yourself. You immediately know which direction is north (if it exists at your current location), and you can choose a location you were at within the last 24 hours and learn what direction it lies.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4695,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Know the Way","rank":0,"uuid":"6662429283182919","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1508,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1582","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:39.301612+00:00","heightened":{"text":[{"text":"You can choose a location you were at within the last week.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can choose a location you were at regardless of how long ago you were there.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult","primal"],"description":"In your mind's eye, you magically reorient yourself. You immediately know which direction is north (if it exists at your current location), and you can choose a location you were at within the last 24 hours and learn what direction it lies.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4696,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4696,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Laughing Fit","rank":2,"uuid":"338027563002012","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 living creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1583","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:44.93271+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"The target is overtaken with uncontrollable laughter. It must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is plagued with uncontrollable laughter. It can't use reactions.\n\n**Failure** The target is slowed 1 and can't use reactions.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target falls prone and can't use actions or reactions for 1 round. It then takes the effects of a failure.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4696,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Laughing Fit","rank":2,"uuid":"338027563002012","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 living creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1583","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:48:44.93271+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"The target is overtaken with uncontrollable laughter. It must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is plagued with uncontrollable laughter. It can't use reactions.\n\n**Failure** The target is slowed 1 and can't use reactions.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target falls prone and can't use actions or reactions for 1 round. It then takes the effects of a failure.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4699,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4699,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Light","rank":0,"uuid":"2956398977648258","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1517,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until your next daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1585","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:49:12.96187+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The orb sheds light in a 60-foot radius (and dim light for the next 60 feet).","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You create an orb of light that sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius (and dim light for the next 20 feet) in a color you choose. If you create the light in the same space as a willing creature, you can attach the light to the creature, causing it to float near that creature as it moves. You can [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell to move the light up to 60 feet; you can attach or detach it from a creature as part of this movement.\n\nYou can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell. If you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) while you already have four light spells active, you must choose one of the existing spells to end.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4699,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Light","rank":0,"uuid":"2956398977648258","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1517,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until your next daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1585","book":"Player Core","page":"340"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:49:12.96187+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The orb sheds light in a 60-foot radius (and dim light for the next 60 feet).","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You create an orb of light that sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius (and dim light for the next 20 feet) in a color you choose. If you create the light in the same space as a willing creature, you can attach the light to the creature, causing it to float near that creature as it moves. You can [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell to move the light up to 60 feet; you can attach or detach it from a creature as part of this movement.\n\nYou can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell. If you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) while you already have four light spells active, you must choose one of the existing spells to end.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4700,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4700,"area":"120-foot line","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Lightning Bolt","rank":3,"uuid":"2087284738656077","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1576,1433],"defense":"basic Reflex","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1586","book":"Player Core","page":"341"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:49:17.424125+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d12"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d12.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"A bolt of lightning strikes outward from your hand, dealing 4d12 electricity damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4700,"area":"120-foot line","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Lightning Bolt","rank":3,"uuid":"2087284738656077","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1576,1433],"defense":"basic Reflex","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1586","book":"Player Core","page":"341"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:49:17.424125+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d12"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d12.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"A bolt of lightning strikes outward from your hand, dealing 4d12 electricity damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4715,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4715,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mariner's Curse","rank":5,"uuid":"1591404526152490","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1433],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1593","book":"Player Core","page":"342"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:51:44.08822+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You afflict the target with the curse of the roiling, unforgiving sea. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target becomes sickened 1. Reducing its sickened condition to 0 ends the curse.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes sickened 1 and can't reduce its sickened condition below 1 while the curse remains. The curse can be lifted by 4th-rank [cleanse affliction](link_spell_4522) or similar magic. Whenever the target is sickened and on the water at least a mile from shore, it is also slowed 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target becomes sickened 2.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4715,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mariner's Curse","rank":5,"uuid":"1591404526152490","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1433],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1593","book":"Player Core","page":"342"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:51:44.08822+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You afflict the target with the curse of the roiling, unforgiving sea. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target becomes sickened 1. Reducing its sickened condition to 0 ends the curse.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes sickened 1 and can't reduce its sickened condition below 1 while the curse remains. The curse can be lifted by 4th-rank [cleanse affliction](link_spell_4522) or similar magic. Whenever the target is sickened and on the water at least a mile from shore, it is also slowed 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target becomes sickened 2.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4717,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4717,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mask of Terror","rank":7,"uuid":"4027258221148968","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1487,1447,1433,1448,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1595","book":"Player Core","page":"342"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:02.429371+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 5 creatures. If a creature uses a hostile action or reaction that affects multiple targets simultaneously, it needs to attempt only one save against <em>mask of terror</em>.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"The target appears to be a gruesome and terrifying creature. The effect is unique to each observer, so a human viewing the target might see a [demon](link_trait_2428) with bloody fangs, but a demon observing the target might see a glowing [angelic](link_trait_2421) visage.\n\nWhen any creature attempts a hostile action against the target, the creature must attempt a Will save. It is then temporarily immune until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature becomes frightened 2 before using its action.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature becomes frightened 2, and its action fails and is wasted.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4717,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mask of Terror","rank":7,"uuid":"4027258221148968","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1487,1447,1433,1448,1479],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1595","book":"Player Core","page":"342"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:02.429371+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 5 creatures. If a creature uses a hostile action or reaction that affects multiple targets simultaneously, it needs to attempt only one save against <em>mask of terror</em>.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"The target appears to be a gruesome and terrifying creature. The effect is unique to each observer, so a human viewing the target might see a [demon](link_trait_2428) with bloody fangs, but a demon observing the target might see a glowing [angelic](link_trait_2421) visage.\n\nWhen any creature attempts a hostile action against the target, the creature must attempt a Will save. It is then temporarily immune until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature becomes frightened 2 before using its action.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature becomes frightened 2, and its action fails and is wasted.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4719,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4719,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Mending","rank":1,"uuid":"4590434376769051","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"non-magical object of light Bulk or less","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1597","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:17.850021+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"2":{"target":{"value":"non-magical object of 1 Bulk or less"}},"3":{"target":{"value":"non-magical object of 2 Bulk or less, or a magical object of 1 Bulk or less"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target a non-magical object of 1 Bulk or less.","amount":"(2nd)"},{"text":"You can target a non-magical object of 2 Bulk or less, or a magical object of 1 Bulk or less.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You repair the target item. You restore 5 Hit Points per spell rank to the target, potentially removing the broken condition if this repairs it past the item's Broken Threshold. You can't replace lost pieces or repair an object that's been completely destroyed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4719,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Mending","rank":1,"uuid":"4590434376769051","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"non-magical object of light Bulk or less","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1597","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:17.850021+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"2":{"target":{"value":"non-magical object of 1 Bulk or less"}},"3":{"target":{"value":"non-magical object of 2 Bulk or less, or a magical object of 1 Bulk or less"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target a non-magical object of 1 Bulk or less.","amount":"(2nd)"},{"text":"You can target a non-magical object of 2 Bulk or less, or a magical object of 1 Bulk or less.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You repair the target item. You restore 5 Hit Points per spell rank to the target, potentially removing the broken condition if this repairs it past the item's Broken Threshold. You can't replace lost pieces or repair an object that's been completely destroyed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4720,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4720,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Message","rank":0,"uuid":"7549769104150674","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1858,1432,1447,1458,1448,1899],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"see below","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1598","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:24.730951+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"3":{"range":{"value":"500 feet"}}}},"text":[{"text":"The spell's range increases to 500 feet.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You mouth words quietly, but instead of coming out of your mouth, they're transferred directly to the ears of the target. While others can't hear your words any better than if you normally mouthed them, the target can hear your words as if they were standing next to you. The target can give a brief response as a reaction, or as a free action on their next turn if they wish, but they must be able to see you and be within range to do so. If they respond, their response is delivered directly to your ear, just like the original message.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4720,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Message","rank":0,"uuid":"7549769104150674","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1469,1858,1432,1447,1458,1448,1899],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"see below","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1598","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:24.730951+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"3":{"range":{"value":"500 feet"}}}},"text":[{"text":"The spell's range increases to 500 feet.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You mouth words quietly, but instead of coming out of your mouth, they're transferred directly to the ears of the target. While others can't hear your words any better than if you normally mouthed them, the target can hear your words as if they were standing next to you. The target can give a brief response as a reaction, or as a free action on their next turn if they wish, but they must be able to see you and be within range to do so. If they respond, their response is delivered directly to your ear, just like the original message.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4723,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4723,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Mind Probe","rank":5,"uuid":"663877456927456","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1458,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1601","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:50.393537+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You cast your thoughts through a creature's mind, sifting for information. You access the target's memories and knowledge unless it fends you off with a Will save.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** Each round of the spell's duration, you can Sustain the spell to ask a different question and attempt to uncover the answer. For each question, the target can attempt a Deception check against your spell DC; if the target succeeds, you don't learn the answer, and on a critical success, the target gives you a false answer that you believe is truthful Once you've asked the target a given question, asking it again, even with a separate casting of mind probe, produces the same result.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and the target takes a –4 circumstance penalty to Deception checks against your questions.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4723,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Mind Probe","rank":5,"uuid":"663877456927456","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1458,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1601","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:52:50.393537+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You cast your thoughts through a creature's mind, sifting for information. You access the target's memories and knowledge unless it fends you off with a Will save.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** Each round of the spell's duration, you can Sustain the spell to ask a different question and attempt to uncover the answer. For each question, the target can attempt a Deception check against your spell DC; if the target succeeds, you don't learn the answer, and on a critical success, the target gives you a false answer that you believe is truthful Once you've asked the target a given question, asking it again, even with a separate casting of mind probe, produces the same result.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and the target takes a –4 circumstance penalty to Deception checks against your questions.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4724,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4724,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mind Reading","rank":3,"uuid":"4786919478073506","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1508,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 round or sustained up to 1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1602","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:01.601395+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"With a cursory mental touch, you attempt to read the target's mind. It must attempt a Will save. The target then becomes temporarily immune to your mind reading for 1 hour.\n\n**Critical Success** The target perceives vague surface thoughts from you when you Cast the Spell.\n\n**Success** You find out whether the target's Intelligence modifier is higher than, equal to, or lower than yours.\n\n**Failure** You perceive vague surface thoughts from the target when you Cast the Spell, and you find out whether its Intelligence is higher than, equal to, or lower than yours.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and for the duration of the spell, you can [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948) to detect the target's surface thoughts again. The target doesn't receive any additional saves.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4724,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mind Reading","rank":3,"uuid":"4786919478073506","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1508,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 round or sustained up to 1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1602","book":"Player Core","page":"343"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:01.601395+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"With a cursory mental touch, you attempt to read the target's mind. It must attempt a Will save. The target then becomes temporarily immune to your mind reading for 1 hour.\n\n**Critical Success** The target perceives vague surface thoughts from you when you Cast the Spell.\n\n**Success** You find out whether the target's Intelligence modifier is higher than, equal to, or lower than yours.\n\n**Failure** You perceive vague surface thoughts from the target when you Cast the Spell, and you find out whether its Intelligence is higher than, equal to, or lower than yours.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and for the duration of the spell, you can [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948) to detect the target's surface thoughts again. The target doesn't receive any additional saves.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4726,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4726,"area":"50-foot burst","cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Mirage","rank":4,"uuid":"4327900904107565","range":"500 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until your next daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1604","book":"Player Core","page":"344"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:15.0573+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Your image can also disguise structures or create illusory structures (but still doesn't disguise creatures).","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You create an illusion that causes natural terrain to look, sound, feel, and smell like a different kind of terrain. This doesn't disguise any structures or creatures in the area.\n\nAny creature that touches the illusion or uses the [Seek](link_action_19845) action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4726,"area":"50-foot burst","cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Mirage","rank":4,"uuid":"4327900904107565","range":"500 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until your next daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1604","book":"Player Core","page":"344"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:15.0573+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Your image can also disguise structures or create illusory structures (but still doesn't disguise creatures).","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You create an illusion that causes natural terrain to look, sound, feel, and smell like a different kind of terrain. This doesn't disguise any structures or creatures in the area.\n\nAny creature that touches the illusion or uses the [Seek](link_action_19845) action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4727,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4727,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mislead","rank":6,"uuid":"3115247485126020","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1605","book":"Player Core","page":"344"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:24.823562+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You turn yourself invisible and create an illusory duplicate of yourself. When you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell, you can mentally dictate a course of action for your duplicate to follow that round. Your duplicate acts as though it had your full number of actions, though it can't actually affect anything in the environment. Both the duplicate and your invisibility persist for the spell's duration. Performing a hostile action doesn't end _mislead_'s invisibility, just like a 4th-rank [_invisibility_](link_spell_4689) spell. A creature that determines the duplicate is an illusion doesn't necessarily know you're invisible, and one that can see your invisible form doesn't necessarily know your duplicate is an illusion.\n\nIf you [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611), attack, or otherwise interact with another creature, as a part of that action you can attempt a Deception check against observers' Perception DCs to convince them your duplicate used that action. This doesn't fool anyone who's aware your duplicate is an illusion, nor does it work if the attack obviously couldn't have come from the duplicate. For instance, if you fired a ray, you could make it look like it came from the duplicate as long as the duplicate was positioned appropriately, but if you attacked with a sword and your duplicate was across the room from the target, your Deception check would automatically fail.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4727,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mislead","rank":6,"uuid":"3115247485126020","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1605","book":"Player Core","page":"344"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:24.823562+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You turn yourself invisible and create an illusory duplicate of yourself. When you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell, you can mentally dictate a course of action for your duplicate to follow that round. Your duplicate acts as though it had your full number of actions, though it can't actually affect anything in the environment. Both the duplicate and your invisibility persist for the spell's duration. Performing a hostile action doesn't end _mislead_'s invisibility, just like a 4th-rank [_invisibility_](link_spell_4689) spell. A creature that determines the duplicate is an illusion doesn't necessarily know you're invisible, and one that can see your invisible form doesn't necessarily know your duplicate is an illusion.\n\nIf you [Cast a Spell](link_action_19611), attack, or otherwise interact with another creature, as a part of that action you can attempt a Deception check against observers' Perception DCs to convince them your duplicate used that action. This doesn't fool anyone who's aware your duplicate is an illusion, nor does it work if the attack obviously couldn't have come from the duplicate. For instance, if you fired a ray, you could make it look like it came from the duplicate as long as the duplicate was positioned appropriately, but if you attacked with a sword and your duplicate was across the room from the target, your Deception check would automatically fail.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4728,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4728,"area":"20-foot burst","cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mist","rank":2,"uuid":"1267987522088116","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1584],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1606","book":"Player Core","page":"344"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:29.631569+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You call forth a cloud of mist. All creatures within the mist become concealed, and all creatures outside the mist become concealed to creatures within it. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the cloud.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4728,"area":"20-foot burst","cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mist","rank":2,"uuid":"1267987522088116","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1584],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1606","book":"Player Core","page":"344"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:53:29.631569+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You call forth a cloud of mist. All creatures within the mist become concealed, and all creatures outside the mist become concealed to creatures within it. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the cloud.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4731,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4731,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Moon Frenzy","rank":5,"uuid":"1618977606287186","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1456],"defense":null,"targets":"up to 5 willing creatures","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1609","book":"Player Core","page":"345"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:54:30.23591+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The temporary Hit Points increase to 10, the silver weakness to 10, and the damage dealt by the attacks to three dice.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The temporary Hit Points increase to 20, the silver weakness to 20, and the damage dealt by the attacks to four dice.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"A feral aspect overcomes the targets, filling them with strength and ferocity. Targets gain 5 temporary Hit Points, a +10-foot status bonus to their Speeds, and weakness 5 to silver. They also grow vicious fangs and claws, which are unarmed attacks. The fangs deal 2d8 piercing damage; the claws deal 2d6 slashing damage and have the agile and finesse traits. The targets use their highest weapon or unarmed attack proficiency with these attacks, and if they have weapon specialization or greater weapon specialization, they add this damage as well. On a critical hit with one of these unarmed attacks, the creature struck takes 1d4 persistent bleed damage.\n\nThe targets can't use concentrate actions unless those actions also have the [rage](link_trait_1455) trait, with the exception of [Seek](link_action_19845). A creature can attempt to end the spell's effect on itself by using a single action, which has the rage trait, to attempt a Will save against your spell DC; on a success, it ends the spell's effect on itself.\n\nIf a target is in the light of a full moon, it also grows by one size if it were Medium or smaller. This increases the reach of a Medium or Tiny creature by 5 feet.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4731,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Moon Frenzy","rank":5,"uuid":"1618977606287186","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1456],"defense":null,"targets":"up to 5 willing creatures","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1609","book":"Player Core","page":"345"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:54:30.23591+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The temporary Hit Points increase to 10, the silver weakness to 10, and the damage dealt by the attacks to three dice.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The temporary Hit Points increase to 20, the silver weakness to 20, and the damage dealt by the attacks to four dice.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"A feral aspect overcomes the targets, filling them with strength and ferocity. Targets gain 5 temporary Hit Points, a +10-foot status bonus to their Speeds, and weakness 5 to silver. They also grow vicious fangs and claws, which are unarmed attacks. The fangs deal 2d8 piercing damage; the claws deal 2d6 slashing damage and have the agile and finesse traits. The targets use their highest weapon or unarmed attack proficiency with these attacks, and if they have weapon specialization or greater weapon specialization, they add this damage as well. On a critical hit with one of these unarmed attacks, the creature struck takes 1d4 persistent bleed damage.\n\nThe targets can't use concentrate actions unless those actions also have the [rage](link_trait_1455) trait, with the exception of [Seek](link_action_19845). A creature can attempt to end the spell's effect on itself by using a single action, which has the rage trait, to attempt a Will save against your spell DC; on a success, it ends the spell's effect on itself.\n\nIf a target is in the light of a full moon, it also grows by one size if it were Medium or smaller. This increases the reach of a Medium or Tiny creature by 5 feet.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4733,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4733,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mountain Resilience","rank":4,"uuid":"7082574177986015","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1523,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"20 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1610","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:54:50.279599+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The resistance increases to 10.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The resistance increases to 15.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"The resistance increases to 20.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"The target's skin hardens like the stone of a mountain face. It gains resistance 5 to physical damage, except [adamantine](link_item_15064). Each time the target is hit by a bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing attack, _mountain resilience_'s duration decreases by 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4733,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mountain Resilience","rank":4,"uuid":"7082574177986015","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1523,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"20 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1610","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:54:50.279599+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The resistance increases to 10.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The resistance increases to 15.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"The resistance increases to 20.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"The target's skin hardens like the stone of a mountain face. It gains resistance 5 to physical damage, except [adamantine](link_item_15064). Each time the target is hit by a bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing attack, _mountain resilience_'s duration decreases by 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4734,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4734,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mystic Armor","rank":1,"uuid":"8568450016327694","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until your next daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1611","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:54:58.989699+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You gain a +1 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"The item bonus to AC increases to +2, and you gain a +1 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The item bonus to AC increases to +2, and you gain a +2 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"The item bonus to AC increases to +3, and you gain a +3 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You ward yourself with shimmering magical energy, gaining a +1 item bonus to AC and a maximum Dexterity modifier of +5. While wearing _mystic armor_, you use your unarmored proficiency to calculate your AC.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4734,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Mystic Armor","rank":1,"uuid":"8568450016327694","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until your next daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1611","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:54:58.989699+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You gain a +1 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"The item bonus to AC increases to +2, and you gain a +1 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The item bonus to AC increases to +2, and you gain a +2 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"The item bonus to AC increases to +3, and you gain a +3 item bonus to saving throws.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You ward yourself with shimmering magical energy, gaining a +1 item bonus to AC and a maximum Dexterity modifier of +5. While wearing _mystic armor_, you use your unarmored proficiency to calculate your AC.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4738,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4738,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Nature's Pathway","rank":5,"uuid":"6684343970853996","range":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448,2938,1470],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1613","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:55:45.508528+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The tree you exit can be up to 50 miles away.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The tree you exit can be up to 500 miles away.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"The tree you exit can be anywhere on the same planet.","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"You step into a living tree with a trunk big enough for you to fit inside it and instantly teleport to any tree within 5 miles that also has a sufficiently large trunk. Once you enter the first tree, you instantly know the rough locations of other sufficiently large trees within range and can exit from the original tree, if you prefer. You can't carry [extradimensional](link_trait_1559) spaces with you; if you attempt to do so, the spell fails.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4738,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Nature's Pathway","rank":5,"uuid":"6684343970853996","range":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448,2938,1470],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1613","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:55:45.508528+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The tree you exit can be up to 50 miles away.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The tree you exit can be up to 500 miles away.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"The tree you exit can be anywhere on the same planet.","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"You step into a living tree with a trunk big enough for you to fit inside it and instantly teleport to any tree within 5 miles that also has a sufficiently large trunk. Once you enter the first tree, you instantly know the rough locations of other sufficiently large trees within range and can exit from the original tree, if you prefer. You can't carry [extradimensional](link_trait_1559) spaces with you; if you attempt to do so, the spell fails.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4740,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4740,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Never Mind","rank":6,"uuid":"3906332091842579","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1481,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1614","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:05.492319+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You drastically reduce the target's mental faculties. The target must attempt a Will save. The effects of this curse can be removed only through effects that target curses.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is stupefied 2 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is stupefied 4 with an unlimited duration.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target's intellect is permanently reduced below that of an animal, and it treats its Charisma, Intelligence, and Wisdom modifiers as –5. It loses all class abilities that require mental faculties, including all spellcasting. If the target is a PC, they become an NPC under the GM's control.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4740,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Never Mind","rank":6,"uuid":"3906332091842579","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1481,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1614","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:05.492319+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You drastically reduce the target's mental faculties. The target must attempt a Will save. The effects of this curse can be removed only through effects that target curses.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is stupefied 2 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is stupefied 4 with an unlimited duration.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target's intellect is permanently reduced below that of an animal, and it treats its Charisma, Intelligence, and Wisdom modifiers as –5. It loses all class abilities that require mental faculties, including all spellcasting. If the target is a PC, they become an NPC under the GM's control.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4741,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4741,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Nightmare","rank":4,"uuid":"8512899926376894","range":"planetary","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature you know by name","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 day","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1615","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:19.084394+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You send disturbing nightmares to your target. The next time the target falls asleep, it must attempt a Will save. If you know the target only by name and have never met them, the target gets a +4 circumstance bonus to the Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target suffers no adverse effects and is temporarily immune for 1 week.\n\n**Success** The target experiences the nightmares but suffers no adverse effects other than unpleasant memories.\n\n**Failure** The target experiences the nightmares and awakens fatigued.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target experiences the nightmares, awakens fatigued, and is drained 2 until it is no longer fatigued.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4741,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Nightmare","rank":4,"uuid":"8512899926376894","range":"planetary","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature you know by name","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 day","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1615","book":"Player Core","page":"346"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:19.084394+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You send disturbing nightmares to your target. The next time the target falls asleep, it must attempt a Will save. If you know the target only by name and have never met them, the target gets a +4 circumstance bonus to the Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target suffers no adverse effects and is temporarily immune for 1 week.\n\n**Success** The target experiences the nightmares but suffers no adverse effects other than unpleasant memories.\n\n**Failure** The target experiences the nightmares and awakens fatigued.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target experiences the nightmares, awakens fatigued, and is drained 2 until it is no longer fatigued.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4742,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4742,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Noise Blast","rank":2,"uuid":"5288734719423937","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1484],"defense":"Fortitude","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1616","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:27.67406+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d10"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d10.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"A cacophonous noise blasts out, dealing 2d10 sonic damage. Each creature must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is deafened for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, is deafened for 1 minute, and is stunned 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4742,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Noise Blast","rank":2,"uuid":"5288734719423937","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1484],"defense":"Fortitude","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1616","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:27.67406+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d10"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d10.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"A cacophonous noise blasts out, dealing 2d10 sonic damage. Each creature must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is deafened for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, is deafened for 1 minute, and is stunned 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4744,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4744,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Oaken Resilience","rank":2,"uuid":"5139250072298153","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1617","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:49.686154+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The resistances increase by 2, and the weakness increases by 3.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"The target's skin becomes tough, with a consistency like bark or wood. The target gains resistance 2 to bludgeoning and piercing damage and weakness 3 to fire. After the target takes fire damage, it can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell as a free action triggered by taking the damage; doing so doesn't reduce the fire damage the target was dealt.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4744,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Oaken Resilience","rank":2,"uuid":"5139250072298153","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1617","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:56:49.686154+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The resistances increase by 2, and the weakness increases by 3.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"The target's skin becomes tough, with a consistency like bark or wood. The target gains resistance 2 to bludgeoning and piercing damage and weakness 3 to fire. After the target takes fire damage, it can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell as a free action triggered by taking the damage; doing so doesn't reduce the fire damage the target was dealt.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4746,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4746,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"One with Plants","rank":2,"uuid":"2272578972804192","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1453,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes or 8 hours","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1618","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:57:17.579291+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"You can either transform into a plant or merge with plant matter. While transformed, you can't move or affect anything outside the plant, but you can cast spells as long as they don't require line of effect beyond the plant. You can Dismiss this spell.\n\n*   **Merge with Plants** The spell's duration is 10 minutes. While casting the spell, you must touch a plant with enough volume to fit you and your possessions or the spell is disrupted. While merged, you can hear, but not see, what's going on outside the plant. If the plant takes damage while you're inside it, you're expelled from the plant and take 10d6 damage. _Magic passage_ expels you without dealing damage. The spell ends if you're ever outside the plant.\n*   **Turn into a Plant** The spell's duration is 8 hours. You become a Large plant—typically a tree. Perception checks don't reveal your true nature, but a successful Nature or Survival check against your spell DC reveals that you appear to be a plant that is strangely new to the area. While in this form, you can observe everything around you, using your normal senses. As a plant, your AC is 20, and only status bonuses, status penalties, circumstance bonuses, and circumstance penalties affect you. Any successes and critical successes you roll on Reflex saves are failures","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4746,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"One with Plants","rank":2,"uuid":"2272578972804192","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1453,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes or 8 hours","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1618","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:57:17.579291+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"You can either transform into a plant or merge with plant matter. While transformed, you can't move or affect anything outside the plant, but you can cast spells as long as they don't require line of effect beyond the plant. You can Dismiss this spell.\n\n*   **Merge with Plants** The spell's duration is 10 minutes. While casting the spell, you must touch a plant with enough volume to fit you and your possessions or the spell is disrupted. While merged, you can hear, but not see, what's going on outside the plant. If the plant takes damage while you're inside it, you're expelled from the plant and take 10d6 damage. _Magic passage_ expels you without dealing damage. The spell ends if you're ever outside the plant.\n*   **Turn into a Plant** The spell's duration is 8 hours. You become a Large plant—typically a tree. Perception checks don't reveal your true nature, but a successful Nature or Survival check against your spell DC reveals that you appear to be a plant that is strangely new to the area. While in this form, you can observe everything around you, using your normal senses. As a plant, your AC is 20, and only status bonuses, status penalties, circumstance bonuses, and circumstance penalties affect you. Any successes and critical successes you roll on Reflex saves are failures","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4748,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4748,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Outcast's Curse","rank":4,"uuid":"1544781473546902","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1433,1448,1677],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1620","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:57:52.435541+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You afflict the target with a curse that makes its presence abrasive and off-putting. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** For 10 minutes, the target must roll twice and use the worse result whenever attempting a Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, or Performance check, and creatures they encounter have an initial attitude toward them of one step worse (for instance, unfriendly instead of indifferent).\n\n**Failure** As success, but the effect is permanent.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and creatures that the target encounters have an initial attitude toward them of two steps worse.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4748,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Outcast's Curse","rank":4,"uuid":"1544781473546902","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1855,1433,1448,1677],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1620","book":"Player Core","page":"347"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:57:52.435541+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You afflict the target with a curse that makes its presence abrasive and off-putting. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** For 10 minutes, the target must roll twice and use the worse result whenever attempting a Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, or Performance check, and creatures they encounter have an initial attitude toward them of one step worse (for instance, unfriendly instead of indifferent).\n\n**Failure** As success, but the effect is permanent.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and creatures that the target encounters have an initial attitude toward them of two steps worse.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4751,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4751,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Paralyze","rank":3,"uuid":"6945932396725328","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1481,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1622","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:58:37.513042+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"7":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 creatures.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You block the target's motor impulses before they can leave its mind, threatening to freeze the target in place. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is stunned 1.\n\n**Failure** The target is paralyzed for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is paralyzed for 4 rounds. At the end of each of its turns, it can attempt a new Will save to reduce the remaining duration by 1 round, or end it entirely on a critical success.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4751,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Paralyze","rank":3,"uuid":"6945932396725328","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1481,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1622","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:58:37.513042+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"7":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 creatures.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You block the target's motor impulses before they can leave its mind, threatening to freeze the target in place. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is stunned 1.\n\n**Failure** The target is paralyzed for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is paralyzed for 4 rounds. At the end of each of its turns, it can attempt a new Will save to reduce the remaining duration by 1 round, or end it entirely on a critical success.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4754,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4754,"area":"100-foot burst","cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Peaceful Bubble","rank":4,"uuid":"7491378481814701","range":"touch","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"24 hours","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1624","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:59:09.973818+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"An opaque shell of drifting, iridescent runes covers the area, creating a bubble. You can choose to make the burst smaller, in 10-foot increments. The runes don't block travel, but those inside the bubble can't perceive those outside it and vice versa. [Detection](link_trait_1508) and [scrying](link_trait_1590) effects are likewise blocked.\n\nCreatures sleeping within the bubble are immune to dreams sent by spells. Those sleeping 8 hours reduce their doomed condition by 2 instead of 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4754,"area":"100-foot burst","cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Peaceful Bubble","rank":4,"uuid":"7491378481814701","range":"touch","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"24 hours","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1624","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:59:09.973818+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"An opaque shell of drifting, iridescent runes covers the area, creating a bubble. You can choose to make the burst smaller, in 10-foot increments. The runes don't block travel, but those inside the bubble can't perceive those outside it and vice versa. [Detection](link_trait_1508) and [scrying](link_trait_1590) effects are likewise blocked.\n\nCreatures sleeping within the bubble are immune to dreams sent by spells. Those sleeping 8 hours reduce their doomed condition by 2 instead of 1.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4755,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4755,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Peaceful Rest","rank":2,"uuid":"6461669493111039","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 corpse","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the next time you make your daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1625","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:59:19.405286+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"5":{"time":{"value":"3"},"traits":{"value":["concentrate","manipulate"]}}}},"text":[{"text":"The spell's duration is unlimited, but the spell takes one more action to cast and requires a cost (embalming fluid worth 6 gp).","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"The targeted corpse doesn't decay, nor can it be transformed into an [undead](link_trait_2425). If the corpse is subject to a spell that requires the corpse to have died within a certain amount of time (for example, [raise dead](link_spell_4791)), do not count the duration of _peaceful rest_ against that time. This spell also prevents ordinary bugs and pests (such as maggots) from consuming the body.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4755,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Peaceful Rest","rank":2,"uuid":"6461669493111039","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 corpse","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the next time you make your daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1625","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T20:59:19.405286+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"5":{"time":{"value":"3"},"traits":{"value":["concentrate","manipulate"]}}}},"text":[{"text":"The spell's duration is unlimited, but the spell takes one more action to cast and requires a cost (embalming fluid worth 6 gp).","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"The targeted corpse doesn't decay, nor can it be transformed into an [undead](link_trait_2425). If the corpse is subject to a spell that requires the corpse to have died within a certain amount of time (for example, [raise dead](link_spell_4791)), do not count the duration of _peaceful rest_ against that time. This spell also prevents ordinary bugs and pests (such as maggots) from consuming the body.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4759,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4759,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Pest Form","rank":1,"uuid":"7666863353548012","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1626","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:02:17.547139+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You can turn into a flying creature, such as a bird, which grants you a fly Speed of 20 feet.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You transform into the battle form of a Tiny animal, such as a cat, insect, lizard, or rat. You can decide the specific type of animal (such as a rat or praying mantis), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the [animal](link_trait_2409) trait and you can't make [Strikes](link_action_20926). You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities:\n\n*   AC = 15 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n    \n*   Speed 20 feet.\n    \n*   Weakness 5 to physical damage. (If you take physical damage in this form, you take 5 additional damage.)\n    \n*   [Low-light vision](link_sense_19330) and [imprecise scent (30 feet).](link_sense_20773)\n    \n*   Acrobatics and Stealth modifiers of +10, unless your own modifier is higher; Athletics modifier -4.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4759,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Pest Form","rank":1,"uuid":"7666863353548012","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1626","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:02:17.547139+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You can turn into a flying creature, such as a bird, which grants you a fly Speed of 20 feet.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You transform into the battle form of a Tiny animal, such as a cat, insect, lizard, or rat. You can decide the specific type of animal (such as a rat or praying mantis), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the [animal](link_trait_2409) trait and you can't make [Strikes](link_action_20926). You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities:\n\n*   AC = 15 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n    \n*   Speed 20 feet.\n    \n*   Weakness 5 to physical damage. (If you take physical damage in this form, you take 5 additional damage.)\n    \n*   [Low-light vision](link_sense_19330) and [imprecise scent (30 feet).](link_sense_20773)\n    \n*   Acrobatics and Stealth modifiers of +10, unless your own modifier is higher; Athletics modifier -4.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4760,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4760,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Pet Cache","rank":1,"uuid":"8797117525350440","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1559,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature that is your companion","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"8 hours","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1627","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:02:30.8439+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You open your cloak or create a gap with your hands, drawing the target into a pocket dimension just large enough for its basic comfort. No other creature can enter this extradimensional space, and the target can bring along objects only if they were designed to be worn by a creature of its kind. The space has enough air, food, and water to sustain the target for the duration.\n\nYou can Dismiss the spell. The spell also ends if you die or enter an extradimensional space. When the spell ends, the target reappears in the nearest unoccupied space (outside of any extradimensional space you may have entered).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4760,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Pet Cache","rank":1,"uuid":"8797117525350440","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1559,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature that is your companion","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"8 hours","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1627","book":"Player Core","page":"348"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:02:30.8439+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You open your cloak or create a gap with your hands, drawing the target into a pocket dimension just large enough for its basic comfort. No other creature can enter this extradimensional space, and the target can bring along objects only if they were designed to be worn by a creature of its kind. The space has enough air, food, and water to sustain the target for the duration.\n\nYou can Dismiss the spell. The spell also ends if you die or enter an extradimensional space. When the spell ends, the target reappears in the nearest unoccupied space (outside of any extradimensional space you may have entered).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4763,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4763,"area":"30-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Phantasmal Calamity","rank":6,"uuid":"4703186213255330","range":"500 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1630","book":"Player Core","page":"349"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:03:12.271839+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"A vision of apocalyptic destruction fills the mind of each creature in the area. The vision deals 11d6 mental damage (basic Will save). On a critical failure, the creature must also succeed at a Reflex save or believe it's trapped (stuck in a fissure, adrift at sea, or some other fate in keeping with its vision). If it fails the second save, it's also stunned for 1 minute. It can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns, and on a success, it disbelieves the illusion and recovers from the stunned condition.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4763,"area":"30-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Phantasmal Calamity","rank":6,"uuid":"4703186213255330","range":"500 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1447,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1630","book":"Player Core","page":"349"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:03:12.271839+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 2d6.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"A vision of apocalyptic destruction fills the mind of each creature in the area. The vision deals 11d6 mental damage (basic Will save). On a critical failure, the creature must also succeed at a Reflex save or believe it's trapped (stuck in a fissure, adrift at sea, or some other fate in keeping with its vision). If it fails the second save, it's also stunned for 1 minute. It can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns, and on a success, it disbelieves the illusion and recovers from the stunned condition.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4770,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4770,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Planar Palace","rank":7,"uuid":"1338985079291010","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1559,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the next time you make your daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1634","book":"Player Core","page":"350"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:04:40.099855+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You grow an extradimensional demiplane consisting of a spacious dwelling with a single entrance. The entrance connects to the plane where you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611), appearing anywhere within the spell's range as a faint, shimmering, vertical rectangle 5 feet wide and 10 feet high. You designate who can enter when you Cast the Spell. Once inside, you can shut the entrance, making it invisible. You and the creatures you designated can reopen the door at will.\n\nInside, the demiplane appears to be a mansion featuring a magnificent foyer and numerous opulent chambers. The mansion can have any floor plan you imagine as you Cast the Spell, provided it fits within a space 40 feet wide, 40 feet deep, and 30 feet tall. While the entrance to the mansion is closed, effects from outside the mansion fail to penetrate it, and vice versa, except for [_interplanar teleport_](link_spell_4687), which can be used to enter the mansion. You can use scrying magic and similar effects to observe the outside only if they're capable of crossing planes.\n\nA staff of up to 24 servants attends to anyone within the mansion. These are like the servant created by the [_phantasmal minion_](link_spell_4764) spell, though they're visible, with an appearance you determine during casting. The mansion is stocked with enough food to serve a nine-course banquet to 150 people.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4770,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Planar Palace","rank":7,"uuid":"1338985079291010","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1559,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the next time you make your daily preparations","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1634","book":"Player Core","page":"350"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:04:40.099855+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You grow an extradimensional demiplane consisting of a spacious dwelling with a single entrance. The entrance connects to the plane where you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611), appearing anywhere within the spell's range as a faint, shimmering, vertical rectangle 5 feet wide and 10 feet high. You designate who can enter when you Cast the Spell. Once inside, you can shut the entrance, making it invisible. You and the creatures you designated can reopen the door at will.\n\nInside, the demiplane appears to be a mansion featuring a magnificent foyer and numerous opulent chambers. The mansion can have any floor plan you imagine as you Cast the Spell, provided it fits within a space 40 feet wide, 40 feet deep, and 30 feet tall. While the entrance to the mansion is closed, effects from outside the mansion fail to penetrate it, and vice versa, except for [_interplanar teleport_](link_spell_4687), which can be used to enter the mansion. You can use scrying magic and similar effects to observe the outside only if they're capable of crossing planes.\n\nA staff of up to 24 servants attends to anyone within the mansion. These are like the servant created by the [_phantasmal minion_](link_spell_4764) spell, though they're visible, with an appearance you determine during casting. The mansion is stocked with enough food to serve a nine-course banquet to 150 people.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4774,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4774,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Plant Form","rank":5,"uuid":"1106830282830497","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453,1680,2938],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1637","book":"Player Core","page":"350"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:05:37.10263+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Your battle form is Huge, and the reach of your attacks increases by 5 feet. You instead gain AC = 22 + your level, 24 temporary HP, attack modifier +21, damage bonus +16, and Athletics +22.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"Taking inspiration from verdant creatures, you transform into a Large plant battle form. When you [Cast](link_action_19611) this Spell, choose a listed battle form. You can substitute a similar specific plant to turn into (such as a pitcher plant instead of a flytrap), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the [plant](link_trait_1654) trait. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose:\n\n*   AC = 19 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n    \n*   12 temporary Hit Points.\n    \n*   Resistance 10 to [poison](link_trait_1476).\n    \n*   [Low-light vision](link_sense_19330).\n    \n*   One or more unarmed melee attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can [Strike](link_action_19856) with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +17, and your damage bonus is +11. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.\n    \n*   Athletics modifier of +19, unless your own modifier is higher.\n    \n\nYou also gain specific abilities based on the type of plant you choose:\n\n*   **Arboreal** Speed 30 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> branch ([reach 15 feet](link_trait_4174)), **Damage** 2d10 bludgeoning; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> foot, **Damage** 2d8 bludgeoning; you can speak in this form\n    \n*   **Flytrap** Speed 15 feet; resistance 10 to [acid](link_trait_1528); **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> leaf ([reach 10 feet](link_trait_4173)), **Damage** 2d8 piercing, and you can spend an action after a hit to Grab the target.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4774,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Plant Form","rank":5,"uuid":"1106830282830497","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1453,1680,2938],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1637","book":"Player Core","page":"350"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:05:37.10263+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Your battle form is Huge, and the reach of your attacks increases by 5 feet. You instead gain AC = 22 + your level, 24 temporary HP, attack modifier +21, damage bonus +16, and Athletics +22.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"Taking inspiration from verdant creatures, you transform into a Large plant battle form. When you [Cast](link_action_19611) this Spell, choose a listed battle form. You can substitute a similar specific plant to turn into (such as a pitcher plant instead of a flytrap), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the [plant](link_trait_1654) trait. You can [Dismiss](link_action_19627) the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose:\n\n*   AC = 19 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n    \n*   12 temporary Hit Points.\n    \n*   Resistance 10 to [poison](link_trait_1476).\n    \n*   [Low-light vision](link_sense_19330).\n    \n*   One or more unarmed melee attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can [Strike](link_action_19856) with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +17, and your damage bonus is +11. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.\n    \n*   Athletics modifier of +19, unless your own modifier is higher.\n    \n\nYou also gain specific abilities based on the type of plant you choose:\n\n*   **Arboreal** Speed 30 feet; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> branch ([reach 15 feet](link_trait_4174)), **Damage** 2d10 bludgeoning; **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> foot, **Damage** 2d8 bludgeoning; you can speak in this form\n    \n*   **Flytrap** Speed 15 feet; resistance 10 to [acid](link_trait_1528); **Melee** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> leaf ([reach 10 feet](link_trait_4173)), **Damage** 2d8 piercing, and you can spend an action after a hit to Grab the target.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4778,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4778,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Prestidigitation","rank":0,"uuid":"6753710862634370","range":"10 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 object (cook, lift, or tidy only)","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1639","book":"Player Core","page":"351"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:06:56.439429+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"The simplest magic does your bidding. You can perform simple magical effects for as long as you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell. Each time you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell, you can choose one of four options.\n\n*   **Cook** Cool, warm, or flavor 1 pound of nonliving material.\n    \n*   **Lift** Slowly lift an unattended object of light Bulk or less 1 foot off the ground.\n    \n*   **Make** Create a temporary object of negligible Bulk, made of congealed magical substance. The object looks crude and artificial and is extremely fragile-it can't be used as a tool, weapon, or locus or cost for a spell.\n    \n*   **Tidy** Color, clean, or soil an object of light Bulk or less. You can affect an object of 1 Bulk with 10 rounds of concentration, and a larger object a 1 minute per Bulk.\n    \n\n_Prestidigitation_ can't deal damage or cause adverse conditions. Any actual change to an object (beyond what is noted above) persists only as long as you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4778,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Prestidigitation","rank":0,"uuid":"6753710862634370","range":"10 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 object (cook, lift, or tidy only)","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1639","book":"Player Core","page":"351"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:06:56.439429+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"The simplest magic does your bidding. You can perform simple magical effects for as long as you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell. Each time you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell, you can choose one of four options.\n\n*   **Cook** Cool, warm, or flavor 1 pound of nonliving material.\n    \n*   **Lift** Slowly lift an unattended object of light Bulk or less 1 foot off the ground.\n    \n*   **Make** Create a temporary object of negligible Bulk, made of congealed magical substance. The object looks crude and artificial and is extremely fragile-it can't be used as a tool, weapon, or locus or cost for a spell.\n    \n*   **Tidy** Color, clean, or soil an object of light Bulk or less. You can affect an object of 1 Bulk with 10 rounds of concentration, and a larger object a 1 minute per Bulk.\n    \n\n_Prestidigitation_ can't deal damage or cause adverse conditions. Any actual change to an object (beyond what is noted above) persists only as long as you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4782,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4782,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Protection","rank":1,"uuid":"4764342492787178","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1641","book":"Player Core","page":"351"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:08:47.870657+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You can choose to have the benefits also affect all your allies in a 10-foot emanation around the target.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You ward a creature against harm. The target gains a +1 status bonus to Armor Class and saving throws.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4782,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Protection","rank":1,"uuid":"4764342492787178","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1641","book":"Player Core","page":"351"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:08:47.870657+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"You can choose to have the benefits also affect all your allies in a 10-foot emanation around the target.","amount":"(3rd)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You ward a creature against harm. The target gains a +1 status bonus to Armor Class and saving throws.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4787,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4787,"area":"15-foot cone","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Pummeling Rubble","rank":1,"uuid":"8808332626892125","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1523,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1642","book":"Player Core","page":"351"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:09:29.0867+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d4"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"Increase the damage by 2d4.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"A spray of heavy rocks flies through the air in front of you. The rubble deals 2d4 bludgeoning damage to each creature in the area. Each creature must attempt a Reflex save.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is pushed 5 feet away from you.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is pushed 10 feet away from you.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4787,"area":"15-foot cone","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Pummeling Rubble","rank":1,"uuid":"8808332626892125","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1523,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1642","book":"Player Core","page":"351"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:09:29.0867+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"2d4"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"Increase the damage by 2d4.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"A spray of heavy rocks flies through the air in front of you. The rubble deals 2d4 bludgeoning damage to each creature in the area. Each creature must attempt a Reflex save.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is pushed 5 feet away from you.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is pushed 10 feet away from you.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4792,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4792,"area":"60-foot emanation","cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Rallying Anthem","rank":0,"uuid":"4598746374929320","range":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1341,1858,1895,1432,1486,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 round","meta_data":{"focus":true,"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1773","book":"Player Core","page":"371"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":true}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:10:27.444874+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":[],"description":"Your song moves allies to protect themselves more effectively. You and all allies in the area gain a +1 status bonus to AC and saving throws, as well as resistance equal to half the spell's rank to physical damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4792,"area":"60-foot emanation","cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Rallying Anthem","rank":0,"uuid":"4598746374929320","range":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1341,1858,1895,1432,1486,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 round","meta_data":{"focus":true,"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1773","book":"Player Core","page":"371"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":true}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:10:27.444874+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":[],"description":"Your song moves allies to protect themselves more effectively. You and all allies in the area gain a +1 status bonus to AC and saving throws, as well as resistance equal to half the spell's rank to physical damage.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4794,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4794,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Read Aura","rank":0,"uuid":"6759173537294350","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1508,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 object","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1646","book":"Player Core","page":"352"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:10:40.352353+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"3":{"target":{"value":"10 objects"}},"6":{"target":{"value":"any number of objects"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 objects.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can target any number of objects.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You focus on the target object, opening your mind to perceive magical auras. When the casting is complete, you know whether that item is [magical](link_trait_1504). You or anyone you advise about the aura gains a +2 circumstance bonus to [Identify Magic](link_action_19730) on the item. If the object is illusory, you detect this only if the effect's rank is lower than the rank of your _read aura_ spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4794,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Read Aura","rank":0,"uuid":"6759173537294350","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1508,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 object","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1646","book":"Player Core","page":"352"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:10:40.352353+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"3":{"target":{"value":"10 objects"}},"6":{"target":{"value":"any number of objects"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 objects.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"You can target any number of objects.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You focus on the target object, opening your mind to perceive magical auras. When the casting is complete, you know whether that item is [magical](link_trait_1504). You or anyone you advise about the aura gains a +2 circumstance bonus to [Identify Magic](link_action_19730) on the item. If the object is illusory, you detect this only if the effect's rank is lower than the rank of your _read aura_ spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4796,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4796,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Read Omens","rank":4,"uuid":"1383830079857474","range":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1896],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1647","book":"Player Core","page":"352"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:10:52.052738+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You peek into the future. Choose a particular goal or activity you plan to engage in within 1 week, or an event you expect might happen within 1 week. You learn a cryptic clue or piece of advice that could help with the chosen event, often in the form of a rhyme or omen.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4796,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Read Omens","rank":4,"uuid":"1383830079857474","range":"","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1896],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1647","book":"Player Core","page":"352"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:10:52.052738+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You peek into the future. Choose a particular goal or activity you plan to engage in within 1 week, or an event you expect might happen within 1 week. You learn a cryptic clue or piece of advice that could help with the chosen event, often in the form of a rhyme or omen.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4798,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4798,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Regenerate","rank":7,"uuid":"673232179961484","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1442,1433,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing living creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1648","book":"Player Core","page":"352"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:11:15.918354+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The regeneration increases to 20.","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"An infusion of vital energy grants a creature continuous healing. The target temporarily gains regeneration 15, which restores 15 Hit Points to it at the start of each of its turns. While it has regeneration, the target can't die from taking Hit Point damage and its dying condition can't increase to a value that would kill it (this stops most creatures' dying condition at dying 3), though if its wounded value becomes 4 or higher, it stays unconscious until its wounds are treated. If the target takes acid or fire damage, its regeneration deactivates until after the end of its next turn.\n\nEach time the creature regains Hit Points from regeneration, it also regrows one damaged or ruined organ (if any). During the spell's duration, the creature can also reattach severed body parts by spending an [Interact](link_action_19733) action to hold the body part to the area it was severed from.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4798,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Regenerate","rank":7,"uuid":"673232179961484","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1442,1433,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing living creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1648","book":"Player Core","page":"352"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:11:15.918354+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The regeneration increases to 20.","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"An infusion of vital energy grants a creature continuous healing. The target temporarily gains regeneration 15, which restores 15 Hit Points to it at the start of each of its turns. While it has regeneration, the target can't die from taking Hit Point damage and its dying condition can't increase to a value that would kill it (this stops most creatures' dying condition at dying 3), though if its wounded value becomes 4 or higher, it stays unconscious until its wounds are treated. If the target takes acid or fire damage, its regeneration deactivates until after the end of its next turn.\n\nEach time the creature regains Hit Points from regeneration, it also regrows one damaged or ruined organ (if any). During the spell's duration, the creature can also reattach severed body parts by spending an [Interact](link_action_19733) action to hold the body part to the area it was severed from.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4800,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4800,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Repulsion","rank":6,"uuid":"2863514270301352","range":"emanation up to 40-feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1492,1432,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1650","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:11:33.53682+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You manifest an aura that prevents creatures from approaching you. When casting the spell, you can make the area any radius you choose, up to 40 feet. A creature must attempt a Will save if it's within the area when you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) or as soon as it enters the area while the spell is in effect. Once a creature has attempted the save, it uses the same result for that casting of _repulsion_. Any restrictions on a creature's movement apply only if it voluntarily moves toward you. For example, if you move closer to a creature, it doesn't then need to move away.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature's movement is not restricted.\n\n**Success** The creature treats each square in the area as difficult terrain when moving closer to you.\n\n**Failure** The creature can't move closer to you within the area.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4800,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Repulsion","rank":6,"uuid":"2863514270301352","range":"emanation up to 40-feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1492,1432,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1650","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:11:33.53682+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You manifest an aura that prevents creatures from approaching you. When casting the spell, you can make the area any radius you choose, up to 40 feet. A creature must attempt a Will save if it's within the area when you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) or as soon as it enters the area while the spell is in effect. Once a creature has attempted the save, it uses the same result for that casting of _repulsion_. Any restrictions on a creature's movement apply only if it voluntarily moves toward you. For example, if you move closer to a creature, it doesn't then need to move away.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature's movement is not restricted.\n\n**Success** The creature treats each square in the area as difficult terrain when moving closer to you.\n\n**Failure** The creature can't move closer to you within the area.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4801,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4801,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Resist Energy","rank":2,"uuid":"692182445077421","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1651","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:11:41.208414+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"4":{"target":{"value":"2 creatures"}},"7":{"target":{"value":"5 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"The resistance increases to 10, and you can target up to two creatures.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"The resistance increases to 15, and you can target up to five creatures.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"A shield of elemental energy protects a creature against one type of energy damage. Choose acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage. The target and its gear gain resistance 5 against the damage type you chose.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4801,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Resist Energy","rank":2,"uuid":"692182445077421","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1651","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:11:41.208414+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"4":{"target":{"value":"2 creatures"}},"7":{"target":{"value":"5 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"The resistance increases to 10, and you can target up to two creatures.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"The resistance increases to 15, and you can target up to five creatures.","amount":"(7th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"A shield of elemental energy protects a creature against one type of energy damage. Choose acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage. The target and its gear gain resistance 5 against the damage type you chose.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4806,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4806,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Revealing Light","rank":2,"uuid":"3008574121131990","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1517,1433],"defense":"Reflex","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1653","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:12:42.446615+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"A wave of magical light washes over the area. You choose the appearance of the light, such as colorful, heatless flames or sparkling motes. A creature affected by _revealing light_ is dazzled. If the creature was invisible, it becomes concealed instead. If the creature was already concealed for any other reason, it is no longer concealed.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The light affects the creature for 2 rounds.\n\n**Failure** The light affects the creature for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The light affects the creature for 10 minutes.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4806,"area":"10-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Revealing Light","rank":2,"uuid":"3008574121131990","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1517,1433],"defense":"Reflex","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1653","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:12:42.446615+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"A wave of magical light washes over the area. You choose the appearance of the light, such as colorful, heatless flames or sparkling motes. A creature affected by _revealing light_ is dazzled. If the creature was invisible, it becomes concealed instead. If the creature was already concealed for any other reason, it is no longer concealed.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The light affects the creature for 2 rounds.\n\n**Failure** The light affects the creature for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The light affects the creature for 10 minutes.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4808,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4808,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Rewrite Memory","rank":4,"uuid":"8226349911201226","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"unlimited","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1655","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:13:08.29037+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"6":{}}},"text":[{"text":"You can Cast the Spell on a willing target to suppress all memory of a particular topic, detailed in 50 words or fewer. The effect is permanent, and it patches these omissions with an indistinct haze.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"You alter the target's memories by erasing a memory, enhancing a memory's clarity, altering a memory, or adding a false memory. The target can attempt a Will save to resist the spell.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected and realizes you tried to alter its memory.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected but thinks your spell was something harmless instead of _rewrite memory_, unless it identifies the spell.\n\n**Failure** During the first 5 minutes of the spell's duration, you can [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948) to modify a memory once each round. When you do, you imagine up to 6 seconds of memory to modify, to a maximum of 5 continuous minutes of memory.\n\nAny memories you've altered remain changed as long as the spell is active. If the target moves out of range before the 5 minutes is up, you can't alter any further memories.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4808,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Rewrite Memory","rank":4,"uuid":"8226349911201226","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"unlimited","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1655","book":"Player Core","page":"353"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:13:08.29037+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"6":{}}},"text":[{"text":"You can Cast the Spell on a willing target to suppress all memory of a particular topic, detailed in 50 words or fewer. The effect is permanent, and it patches these omissions with an indistinct haze.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"You alter the target's memories by erasing a memory, enhancing a memory's clarity, altering a memory, or adding a false memory. The target can attempt a Will save to resist the spell.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected and realizes you tried to alter its memory.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected but thinks your spell was something harmless instead of _rewrite memory_, unless it identifies the spell.\n\n**Failure** During the first 5 minutes of the spell's duration, you can [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948) to modify a memory once each round. When you do, you imagine up to 6 seconds of memory to modify, to a maximum of 5 continuous minutes of memory.\n\nAny memories you've altered remain changed as long as the spell is active. If the target moves out of range before the 5 minutes is up, you can't alter any further memories.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4809,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4809,"area":"20-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Ring of Truth","rank":3,"uuid":"7503141930567488","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1508,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1656","book":"Player Core","page":"354"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:13:20.033391+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You designate an area in which lies are revealed. Creatures in the area also take a –2 status penalty to Deception checks. Each time a creature in the area speaks a true statement, the soft ring of a bell sounds in the area. Creatures are aware of the magic; therefore, they can avoid answering questions to which they would normally respond with a lie, or they can be evasive as long as they remain within the boundaries of the truth. If a creature is in the area when the spell is cast or later enters the area, that creature attempts a Will save. It uses the results of this initial save if it leaves and reenters the area.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is so convincing that the bell rings even if they lie.\n\n**Success** If the target lies and succeeds at their Deception check against all targets, the bell still rings.\n\n**Failure** The bell accurately sees through their deception and will never ring if they lie","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4809,"area":"20-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Ring of Truth","rank":3,"uuid":"7503141930567488","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1508,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1656","book":"Player Core","page":"354"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:13:20.033391+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You designate an area in which lies are revealed. Creatures in the area also take a –2 status penalty to Deception checks. Each time a creature in the area speaks a true statement, the soft ring of a bell sounds in the area. Creatures are aware of the magic; therefore, they can avoid answering questions to which they would normally respond with a lie, or they can be evasive as long as they remain within the boundaries of the truth. If a creature is in the area when the spell is cast or later enters the area, that creature attempts a Will save. It uses the results of this initial save if it leaves and reenters the area.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is so convincing that the bell rings even if they lie.\n\n**Success** If the target lies and succeeds at their Deception check against all targets, the bell still rings.\n\n**Failure** The bell accurately sees through their deception and will never ring if they lie","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4812,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4812,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Runic Body","rank":1,"uuid":"385478542821882","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1657","book":"Player Core","page":"354"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:05.247025+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks are [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860).","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks are [+3](link_item_7952) [major striking](link_item_7861).","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"Glowing runes appear on the target's body. All its [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks become [+1](link_item_7950) [striking](link_item_7862) [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks, gaining a +1 item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of damage dice to two.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4812,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Runic Body","rank":1,"uuid":"385478542821882","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1657","book":"Player Core","page":"354"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:05.247025+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks are [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860).","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks are [+3](link_item_7952) [major striking](link_item_7861).","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"Glowing runes appear on the target's body. All its [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks become [+1](link_item_7950) [striking](link_item_7862) [unarmed](link_trait_2398) attacks, gaining a +1 item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of damage dice to two.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4813,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4813,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Runic Weapon","rank":1,"uuid":"264731091157005","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 weapon that is unattended or wielded by a willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1658","book":"Player Core","page":"354"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:09.838311+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The weapon is [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860).","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The weapon is [+3](link_item_7952) [major striking.](link_item_7861)","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"The weapon glimmers with magic as temporary runes carve down its length. The target becomes a [+1](link_item_7950) [striking](link_item_7862) weapon, gaining a +1 item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of weapon damage dice to two.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4813,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Runic Weapon","rank":1,"uuid":"264731091157005","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 weapon that is unattended or wielded by a willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1658","book":"Player Core","page":"354"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:09.838311+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The weapon is [+2](link_item_7951) [greater striking](link_item_7860).","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"The weapon is [+3](link_item_7952) [major striking.](link_item_7861)","amount":"(9th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"description":"The weapon glimmers with magic as temporary runes carve down its length. The target becomes a [+1](link_item_7950) [striking](link_item_7862) weapon, gaining a +1 item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of weapon damage dice to two.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4814,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4814,"area":"10-foot-wide, 10-foot-tall, 60-foot-long section of terrain","cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Safe Passage","rank":3,"uuid":"6425681134899699","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained up to 1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1659","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:19.548242+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The granted resistance increases to 10, and the area can be 120 feet long.","amount":"(5th)"},{"text":"The granted resistance increases to 15, and the area can be 500 feet long.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","primal"],"description":"You make passage through the area safe for a brief amount of time. Anyone passing through the area gains the following benefits against harmful effects of the terrain and environment, including environmental damage, hazardous terrain, and hazards in the area. The spell grants a +2 status bonus to AC and saves against such effects, and resistance 5 to all damage from such effects. Furthermore, the spell prevents anything in the area that's prone to collapse, such as a rickety bridge or an unstable ceiling, from collapsing, except under extreme strain that would collapse a normal structure of its type.\n\n_Safe passage_ protects only against harm, not inconvenience, and it doesn't reduce difficult terrain, remove the concealed condition caused by precipitation, or the like, nor does it protect against creatures within the spell's area.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4814,"area":"10-foot-wide, 10-foot-tall, 60-foot-long section of terrain","cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Safe Passage","rank":3,"uuid":"6425681134899699","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained up to 1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1659","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:19.548242+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The granted resistance increases to 10, and the area can be 120 feet long.","amount":"(5th)"},{"text":"The granted resistance increases to 15, and the area can be 500 feet long.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","primal"],"description":"You make passage through the area safe for a brief amount of time. Anyone passing through the area gains the following benefits against harmful effects of the terrain and environment, including environmental damage, hazardous terrain, and hazards in the area. The spell grants a +2 status bonus to AC and saves against such effects, and resistance 5 to all damage from such effects. Furthermore, the spell prevents anything in the area that's prone to collapse, such as a rickety bridge or an unstable ceiling, from collapsing, except under extreme strain that would collapse a normal structure of its type.\n\n_Safe passage_ protects only against harm, not inconvenience, and it doesn't reduce difficult terrain, remove the concealed condition caused by precipitation, or the like, nor does it protect against creatures within the spell's area.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4816,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4816,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sanctuary","rank":1,"uuid":"4354886920738812","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1660","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:37.67952+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You ward a creature with protective energy that deters attacks. Creatures attempting to attack the target must attempt a Will save each time. If the target uses a hostile action, the spell ends.\n\n**Critical Success** _Sanctuary_ ends.\n\n**Success** The creature can attempt its attack and any other attacks against the target this turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature can't attack the target and wastes the action. It can't attempt further attacks against the target this turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature wastes the action and can't attempt to attack the target for the rest of _sanctuary_'s duration.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4816,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sanctuary","rank":1,"uuid":"4354886920738812","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1660","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:37.67952+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You ward a creature with protective energy that deters attacks. Creatures attempting to attack the target must attempt a Will save each time. If the target uses a hostile action, the spell ends.\n\n**Critical Success** _Sanctuary_ ends.\n\n**Success** The creature can attempt its attack and any other attacks against the target this turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature can't attack the target and wastes the action. It can't attempt further attacks against the target this turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature wastes the action and can't attempt to attack the target for the rest of _sanctuary_'s duration.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4819,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4819,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Scouting Eye","rank":5,"uuid":"2000008397123013","range":"see text","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1590],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1661","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:58.963712+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You create an invisible, floating eye, 1 inch in diameter, at a location you can see within 500 feet. It sees in all directions with your normal visual senses and continuously transmits what it sees to you.\n\nThe first time you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell each round, you can either move the eye up to 30 feet, seeing only things in front of the eye, or move it up to 10 feet, seeing everything in all directions around it. There is no limit to how far from you the eye can move, but the spell ends immediately if you and the eye ever cease to be on the same plane of existence. You can attempt [Seek](link_action_19845) actions through the eye if you want to attempt Perception checks with it. Any damage dealt to the eye destroys it and ends the spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4819,"area":null,"cast":"1 minute","cost":"","name":"Scouting Eye","rank":5,"uuid":"2000008397123013","range":"see text","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1590],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1661","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:14:58.963712+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You create an invisible, floating eye, 1 inch in diameter, at a location you can see within 500 feet. It sees in all directions with your normal visual senses and continuously transmits what it sees to you.\n\nThe first time you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the spell each round, you can either move the eye up to 30 feet, seeing only things in front of the eye, or move it up to 10 feet, seeing everything in all directions around it. There is no limit to how far from you the eye can move, but the spell ends immediately if you and the eye ever cease to be on the same plane of existence. You can attempt [Seek](link_action_19845) actions through the eye if you want to attempt Perception checks with it. Any damage dealt to the eye destroys it and ends the spell.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4821,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4821,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Scrying","rank":6,"uuid":"6923951885682808","range":"planetary","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1590],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1662","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:25.26857+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You magically spy on a creature of your choice. _Scrying_ works like [_clairvoyance_](link_spell_4521), except that the image you receive is less precise, insufficient for [_teleport_](link_spell_4895) and similar spells. Instead of creating an eye in a set location within 500 feet, you instead create an eye that manifests just above the target. You can choose a target either by name or by touching one of its possessions or a piece of its body. If you haven't met the target in person, _scrying_'s DC is 2 lower, and if you are unaware of the target's identity (perhaps because you found an unknown creature's fang at a crime scene), the DC is instead 10 lower.\n\nThe effect of _scrying_ depends on the target's Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The spell fails and the target is temporarily immune for 1 week. The target also gains a glimpse of you and learns its rough distance and direction from you.\n\n**Success** The spell fails and the target is temporarily immune for 1 day.\n\n**Failure** The spell succeeds.\n\n**Critical Failure** The spell succeeds, and the eye follows the target if it moves, traveling up to 60 feet per round.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4821,"area":null,"cast":"10 minutes","cost":"","name":"Scrying","rank":6,"uuid":"6923951885682808","range":"planetary","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1590],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1662","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:25.26857+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You magically spy on a creature of your choice. _Scrying_ works like [_clairvoyance_](link_spell_4521), except that the image you receive is less precise, insufficient for [_teleport_](link_spell_4895) and similar spells. Instead of creating an eye in a set location within 500 feet, you instead create an eye that manifests just above the target. You can choose a target either by name or by touching one of its possessions or a piece of its body. If you haven't met the target in person, _scrying_'s DC is 2 lower, and if you are unaware of the target's identity (perhaps because you found an unknown creature's fang at a crime scene), the DC is instead 10 lower.\n\nThe effect of _scrying_ depends on the target's Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The spell fails and the target is temporarily immune for 1 week. The target also gains a glimpse of you and learns its rough distance and direction from you.\n\n**Success** The spell fails and the target is temporarily immune for 1 day.\n\n**Failure** The spell succeeds.\n\n**Critical Failure** The spell succeeds, and the eye follows the target if it moves, traveling up to 60 feet per round.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4822,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4822,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"See the Unseen","rank":2,"uuid":"7478443012920624","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1907],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1663","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:37.514279+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"This spell has a duration of 8 hours.","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"Your gaze pierces through illusions and finds invisible creatures and spirits. You can see invisible creatures as though they weren't invisible, although their features are blurred, making them concealed and difficult to identify. You can also see [incorporeal](link_trait_2424) creatures, like ghosts, phased through an object from within 10 feet of an object's surface as blurry shapes seen through those objects. Subtler clues also grant you a +2 status bonus to checks you make to disbelieve [illusions](link_trait_1447).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4822,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"See the Unseen","rank":2,"uuid":"7478443012920624","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1907],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1663","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:37.514279+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"This spell has a duration of 8 hours.","amount":"(5th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"Your gaze pierces through illusions and finds invisible creatures and spirits. You can see invisible creatures as though they weren't invisible, although their features are blurred, making them concealed and difficult to identify. You can also see [incorporeal](link_trait_2424) creatures, like ghosts, phased through an object from within 10 feet of an object's surface as blurry shapes seen through those objects. Subtler clues also grant you a +2 status bonus to checks you make to disbelieve [illusions](link_trait_1447).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4823,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4823,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"item worth at least the target's level x 100 gp","name":"Seize Soul","rank":9,"uuid":"1846620362288438","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1846],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature that died within the last minute","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"unlimited","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1664","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:52.810154+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You trap the target's soul in the item before the soul can pass on to the afterlife. The item used to contain the soul can be anything as long as it's of the appropriate value. The item has AC 16 and its normal Hardness and HP. Destroying (not just breaking) an item or counteracting _seize soul_ releases the soul to the afterlife.\n\nWhile the soul is in the item, the target can't be returned to life through any means, even powerful magic such as a [Wish](link_spell_4955) ritual. If the item is destroyed or _seize soul_ is counteracted on the item, the soul is freed. An item can't hold more than one soul, and any attempt wastes the spell.\n\nYou can also target an item that has had a soul trapped it in with a second casting of _seize soul_, which destroys the item and either releases the soul or relocates it to a different item, whichever you choose. This fails if the target is an artifact or the trapped soul is a creature of 19th level or higher.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4823,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"item worth at least the target's level x 100 gp","name":"Seize Soul","rank":9,"uuid":"1846620362288438","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1846],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature that died within the last minute","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"unlimited","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1664","book":"Player Core","page":"355"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:52.810154+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You trap the target's soul in the item before the soul can pass on to the afterlife. The item used to contain the soul can be anything as long as it's of the appropriate value. The item has AC 16 and its normal Hardness and HP. Destroying (not just breaking) an item or counteracting _seize soul_ releases the soul to the afterlife.\n\nWhile the soul is in the item, the target can't be returned to life through any means, even powerful magic such as a [Wish](link_spell_4955) ritual. If the item is destroyed or _seize soul_ is counteracted on the item, the soul is freed. An item can't hold more than one soul, and any attempt wastes the spell.\n\nYou can also target an item that has had a soul trapped it in with a second casting of _seize soul_, which destroys the item and either releases the soul or relocates it to a different item, whichever you choose. This fails if the target is an artifact or the trapped soul is a creature of 19th level or higher.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4824,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4824,"area":null,"cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sending","rank":5,"uuid":"3904319677412295","range":"planetary","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature with whom you are familiar","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1665","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:55.935265+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You send the creature a mental message of 25 words or fewer, and it can respond immediately with its own message of 25 words or fewer.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4824,"area":null,"cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sending","rank":5,"uuid":"3904319677412295","range":"planetary","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature with whom you are familiar","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1665","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:15:55.935265+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You send the creature a mental message of 25 words or fewer, and it can respond immediately with its own message of 25 words or fewer.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4826,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4826,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Shape Stone","rank":4,"uuid":"2327032269903286","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1523,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"cube of stone 10 feet across or smaller","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1667","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:20.899226+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You shape the stone into a rough shape of your choice. The shaping process is too crude to produce intricate parts, fine details, moving pieces, or the like. Any creatures standing atop the stone when you reshape it must each attempt a Reflex save or Acrobatics check.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature falls prone atop the stone.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature falls off the stone (if applicable) and lands prone.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4826,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Shape Stone","rank":4,"uuid":"2327032269903286","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1523,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"cube of stone 10 feet across or smaller","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1667","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:20.899226+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You shape the stone into a rough shape of your choice. The shaping process is too crude to produce intricate parts, fine details, moving pieces, or the like. Any creatures standing atop the stone when you reshape it must each attempt a Reflex save or Acrobatics check.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature falls prone atop the stone.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature falls off the stone (if applicable) and lands prone.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4827,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4827,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Shape Wood","rank":2,"uuid":"3285224033806253","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"an unworked piece of wood up to 20 cubic feet in volume","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1668","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:24.837875+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You shape the wood into a rough shape of your choice. The shaping power is too crude to produce with intricate parts, fine details, moving pieces, or the like. You cannot use this spell to enhance the value of the wooden object you are shaping.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4827,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Shape Wood","rank":2,"uuid":"3285224033806253","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"an unworked piece of wood up to 20 cubic feet in volume","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1668","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:24.837875+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You shape the wood into a rough shape of your choice. The shaping power is too crude to produce with intricate parts, fine details, moving pieces, or the like. You cannot use this spell to enhance the value of the wooden object you are shaping.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4828,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4828,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Share Life","rank":2,"uuid":"5190280870034237","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1669","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:33.385722+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine"],"description":"You forge a temporary link between the target's life essence and your own. The target takes half damage from all effects that deal Hit Point damage, and you take the remainder of the damage. When you take damage through this link, you don't apply any resistances, weaknesses, or other abilities you have to that damage; you simply take that amount of damage. The spell ends if the target is ever more than 30 feet away from you. If either you or the target is reduced to 0 Hit Points, any damage from this spell is resolved and then the spell ends.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4828,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Share Life","rank":2,"uuid":"5190280870034237","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1669","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:33.385722+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["divine"],"description":"You forge a temporary link between the target's life essence and your own. The target takes half damage from all effects that deal Hit Point damage, and you take the remainder of the damage. When you take damage through this link, you don't apply any resistances, weaknesses, or other abilities you have to that damage; you simply take that amount of damage. The spell ends if the target is ever more than 30 feet away from you. If either you or the target is reduced to 0 Hit Points, any damage from this spell is resolved and then the spell ends.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4830,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4830,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Shatter","rank":2,"uuid":"63403261982511","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1484],"defense":null,"targets":"1 unattended object","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1670","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:47.668097+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d10"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d10, and the Hardness the spell ignores increases by 2.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["occult","primal"],"description":"A high-frequency sonic attack shatters a nearby object. You deal 2d10 sonic damage to the object, ignoring the object's Hardness if it is 4 or lower.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4830,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Shatter","rank":2,"uuid":"63403261982511","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1484],"defense":null,"targets":"1 unattended object","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1670","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:47.668097+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d10"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d10, and the Hardness the spell ignores increases by 2.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["occult","primal"],"description":"A high-frequency sonic attack shatters a nearby object. You deal 2d10 sonic damage to the object, ignoring the object's Hardness if it is 4 or lower.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4831,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4831,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Shield","rank":0,"uuid":"4728691256418017","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1560],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the start of your next turn","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1671","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:59.384966+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The shield's Hardness increases by 5.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You raise a magical shield of force. This counts as using the [Raise a Shield](link_action_19750) action, giving you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn, but it doesn't require a hand to use.\n\nWhile the spell is in effect, you can use the [Shield Block](link_feat_20534) reaction with your magic shield. The shield has Hardness 5 (⬆️{{ceil(level/4)\\*5}}). You can use the spell's reaction to reduce damage from any spell or [magical](link_trait_1504) effect, even if it doesn't deal physical damage. After you use [Shield Block](link_feat_20534), the spell ends and you can't cast it again for 10 minutes.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4831,"area":null,"cast":"ONE-ACTION","cost":"","name":"Shield","rank":0,"uuid":"4728691256418017","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1560],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"until the start of your next turn","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1671","book":"Player Core","page":"356"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:16:59.384966+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The shield's Hardness increases by 5.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","divine","occult"],"description":"You raise a magical shield of force. This counts as using the [Raise a Shield](link_action_19750) action, giving you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn, but it doesn't require a hand to use.\n\nWhile the spell is in effect, you can use the [Shield Block](link_feat_20534) reaction with your magic shield. The shield has Hardness 5 (⬆️{{ceil(level/4)\\*5}}). You can use the spell's reaction to reduce damage from any spell or [magical](link_trait_1504) effect, even if it doesn't deal physical damage. After you use [Shield Block](link_feat_20534), the spell ends and you can't cast it again for 10 minutes.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4837,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4837,"area":"5-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sleep","rank":1,"uuid":"8957165275518678","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1481,1433,1448,1650],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1675","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:17:56.378303+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The creatures fall unconscious for 1 round on a failure or 1 minute on a critical failure. They fall prone and release what they're holding, and they can't attempt Perception checks to wake up. When the duration ends, the creature is sleeping normally instead of automatically waking up.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"Each creature in the area becomes drowsy and might fall asleep. A creature that falls unconscious from this spell doesn't fall prone or release what it's holding. This spell doesn't prevent creatures from waking up due to a successful Perception check, limiting its utility in combat.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature falls unconscious. If it's still unconscious after 1 minute, it wakes up automatically.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature falls unconscious. If it's still unconscious after 1 hour, it wakes up automatically.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4837,"area":"5-foot burst","cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sleep","rank":1,"uuid":"8957165275518678","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1481,1433,1448,1650],"defense":"Will","targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1675","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:17:56.378303+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"The creatures fall unconscious for 1 round on a failure or 1 minute on a critical failure. They fall prone and release what they're holding, and they can't attempt Perception checks to wake up. When the duration ends, the creature is sleeping normally instead of automatically waking up.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"Each creature in the area becomes drowsy and might fall asleep. A creature that falls unconscious from this spell doesn't fall prone or release what it's holding. This spell doesn't prevent creatures from waking up due to a successful Perception check, limiting its utility in combat.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature falls unconscious. If it's still unconscious after 1 minute, it wakes up automatically.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature falls unconscious. If it's still unconscious after 1 hour, it wakes up automatically.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4839,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4839,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Slow","rank":3,"uuid":"638861616431530","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":"Fortitude","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1677","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:18:20.856872+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"6":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 creatures.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You dilate the flow of time around the target, slowing its actions.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is slowed 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is slowed 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is slowed 2 for 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4839,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Slow","rank":3,"uuid":"638861616431530","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":"Fortitude","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1677","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:18:20.856872+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"6":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 creatures.","amount":"(6th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"],"description":"You dilate the flow of time around the target, slowing its actions.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is slowed 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is slowed 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is slowed 2 for 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4842,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4842,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Soothe","rank":1,"uuid":"8232643471498446","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1442,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1678","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:18:45.289892+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d10+4"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The amount of healing increases by 1d10+4.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"You grace the target's mind, boosting its mental defenses and healing its wounds. The target regains 1d10+4 Hit Points when you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) and gains a +2 status bonus to saves against [mental](link_trait_1448) effects for the duration.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4842,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Soothe","rank":1,"uuid":"8232643471498446","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1486,1442,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1678","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:18:45.289892+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d10+4"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The amount of healing increases by 1d10+4.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["occult"],"description":"You grace the target's mind, boosting its mental defenses and healing its wounds. The target regains 1d10+4 Hit Points when you [Cast the Spell](link_action_19611) and gains a +2 status bonus to saves against [mental](link_trait_1448) effects for the duration.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4843,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4843,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Soothing Ballad","rank":7,"uuid":"1614228655797566","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1341,1895,1432,1486,1856,1442,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"you and up to 9 allies","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"focus":true,"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1776","book":"Player Core","page":"371"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":true}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:18:54.331361+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d8"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"When used to heal, soothing ballad restores 1d8 more Hit Points.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":[],"description":"You draw upon your muse to soothe your allies. Choose one of the following three effects:\n\n*   The spell attempts to counteract fear effects on the targets.\n*   The spell attempts to counteract effects imposing paralysis on the targets.\n*   The spell restores 7d8 Hit Points to the targets.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4843,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Soothing Ballad","rank":7,"uuid":"1614228655797566","range":"30 feet","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1341,1895,1432,1486,1856,1442,1433,1448],"defense":null,"targets":"you and up to 9 allies","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"focus":true,"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1776","book":"Player Core","page":"371"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":true}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:18:54.331361+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d8"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"When used to heal, soothing ballad restores 1d8 more Hit Points.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":[],"description":"You draw upon your muse to soothe your allies. Choose one of the following three effects:\n\n*   The spell attempts to counteract fear effects on the targets.\n*   The spell attempts to counteract effects imposing paralysis on the targets.\n*   The spell restores 7d8 Hit Points to the targets.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4846,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4846,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sound Body","rank":2,"uuid":"6067498680484567","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1442,1433,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1679","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:19:29.208226+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Add drained and slowed to the list of conditions.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"As 4th rank, plus add petrified.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"As 4th rank, plus add petrified and stunned.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You send a surge of healing energy to restore the target's body. Attempt to [counteract](link_action_27519) an effect of your choice imposing one of these conditions on the target: blinded, dazzled, deafened, enfeebled, or sickened. If you didn't [counteract](link_action_27519) the effect, but you would have if its [counteract](link_action_27519) rank were 2 lower, instead suppress the effect until the beginning of your next turn. The effect's duration doesn't elapse while it's suppressed.\n\nThis spell can't [counteract](link_action_27519) or suppress [curses](link_trait_1855), [diseases](link_trait_1857), or conditions that are part of the target's normal state.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4846,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Sound Body","rank":2,"uuid":"6067498680484567","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1442,1433,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1679","book":"Player Core","page":"357"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:19:29.208226+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Add drained and slowed to the list of conditions.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"As 4th rank, plus add petrified.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"As 4th rank, plus add petrified and stunned.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You send a surge of healing energy to restore the target's body. Attempt to [counteract](link_action_27519) an effect of your choice imposing one of these conditions on the target: blinded, dazzled, deafened, enfeebled, or sickened. If you didn't [counteract](link_action_27519) the effect, but you would have if its [counteract](link_action_27519) rank were 2 lower, instead suppress the effect until the beginning of your next turn. The effect's duration doesn't elapse while it's suppressed.\n\nThis spell can't [counteract](link_action_27519) or suppress [curses](link_trait_1855), [diseases](link_trait_1857), or conditions that are part of the target's normal state.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4847,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4847,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Speak with Animals","rank":2,"uuid":"1234193248414972","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1680","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:19:34.437041+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals. The spell doesn't make them more friendly than normal. Cunning animals are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4847,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Speak with Animals","rank":2,"uuid":"1234193248414972","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1680","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:19:34.437041+00:00","heightened":{},"traditions":["primal"],"description":"You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals. The spell doesn't make them more friendly than normal. Cunning animals are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4848,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4848,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Speak with Plants","rank":3,"uuid":"1827163946259419","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1681","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:19:42.107856+00:00","heightened":{"text":[{"text":"The duration is 8 hours.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You can ask questions of and receive answers from plants and fungi, but the spell doesn't make them more friendly or intelligent than normal. Most normal plants and fungi have a distinctive view of the world around them, so they don't recognize details about creatures or know anything about the world beyond their immediate vicinity. Cunning plant or fungus monsters are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4848,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Speak with Plants","rank":3,"uuid":"1827163946259419","range":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1654,1680],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 hour","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1681","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:19:42.107856+00:00","heightened":{"text":[{"text":"The duration is 8 hours.","amount":"(4th)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult","primal"],"description":"You can ask questions of and receive answers from plants and fungi, but the spell doesn't make them more friendly or intelligent than normal. Most normal plants and fungi have a distinctive view of the world around them, so they don't recognize details about creatures or know anything about the world beyond their immediate vicinity. Cunning plant or fungus monsters are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4851,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4851,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spider Sting","rank":1,"uuid":"2306974155258094","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1476],"defense":"Fortitude","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1684","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:20:15.883828+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You magically duplicate a spider's venomous sting. You deal 1d4 piercing damage to the touched creature and afflict it with spider venom. The target must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes 1d4 poison damage.\n\n**Failure** The target is afflicted with spider venom at stage 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is afflicted with spider venom at stage 2.\n\n* * *\n\n**Spider Venom** ([poison](link_trait_1476))\n\n**Level** 1\\. **Maximum Duration** 4 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d4 poison damage and enfeebled 1 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 1d4 poison damage and enfeebled 2 (1 round).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4851,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spider Sting","rank":1,"uuid":"2306974155258094","range":"touch","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1476],"defense":"Fortitude","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1684","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:20:15.883828+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You magically duplicate a spider's venomous sting. You deal 1d4 piercing damage to the touched creature and afflict it with spider venom. The target must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes 1d4 poison damage.\n\n**Failure** The target is afflicted with spider venom at stage 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is afflicted with spider venom at stage 2.\n\n* * *\n\n**Spider Venom** ([poison](link_trait_1476))\n\n**Level** 1\\. **Maximum Duration** 4 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d4 poison damage and enfeebled 1 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 1d4 poison damage and enfeebled 2 (1 round).","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4854,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4854,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spirit Link","rank":1,"uuid":"8789368260063135","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1442,1433,1556],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1686","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:20:43.056124+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"9k8ayqgvgultdghx":"2"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The number of Hit Points transferred each time increases by 2.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You form a spiritual link with another creature, taking in its pain. When you Cast this Spell and at the start of each of your turns, if the target is below maximum Hit Points, it regains 2 Hit Points (or the difference between its current and maximum Hit Points, if that's lower). You lose as many Hit Points as the target regained.\n\nThis is a spiritual transfer, so no effects apply that would increase the Hit Points the target regains or decrease the Hit Points you lose. This transfer also ignores any temporary Hit Points you or the target have. Since this effect doesn't involve vitality or void energy, _spirit link_ works even if you or the target is undead. While the duration persists, you gain no benefit from regeneration or fast healing. You can Dismiss this spell, and if you're ever at 0 Hit Points, _spirit link_ ends automatically.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4854,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spirit Link","rank":1,"uuid":"8789368260063135","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1442,1433,1556],"defense":null,"targets":"1 willing creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"10 minutes","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1686","book":"Player Core","page":"358"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:20:43.056124+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"9k8ayqgvgultdghx":"2"},"interval":1},"text":[{"text":"The number of Hit Points transferred each time increases by 2.","amount":"(+1)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You form a spiritual link with another creature, taking in its pain. When you Cast this Spell and at the start of each of your turns, if the target is below maximum Hit Points, it regains 2 Hit Points (or the difference between its current and maximum Hit Points, if that's lower). You lose as many Hit Points as the target regained.\n\nThis is a spiritual transfer, so no effects apply that would increase the Hit Points the target regains or decrease the Hit Points you lose. This transfer also ignores any temporary Hit Points you or the target have. Since this effect doesn't involve vitality or void energy, _spirit link_ works even if you or the target is undead. While the duration persists, you gain no benefit from regeneration or fast healing. You can Dismiss this spell, and if you're ever at 0 Hit Points, _spirit link_ ends automatically.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4855,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4855,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spiritual Armament","rank":2,"uuid":"4624534352223640","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1432,1433,1897,1556],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1687","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:20:57.466829+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0Uok2pip94aNbBFd":"1d8"},"interval":2},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d8","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You create a ghostly, magical echo of one weapon you're wielding or wearing and fling it. Attempt a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 2d8 damage on a hit (or double damage on a critical hit). The damage type is the same as the chosen weapon (or any of its types for a versatile weapon). The attack deals spirit damage instead if that would be more detrimental to the creature (as determined by the GM). This attack uses and contributes to your multiple attack penalty. After the attack, the weapon returns to your side. If you sanctify the spell, the attacks are sanctified as well. Each time you [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948), you can repeat the attack against any creature within 120 feet.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4855,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spiritual Armament","rank":2,"uuid":"4624534352223640","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1520,1432,1433,1897,1556],"defense":null,"targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1687","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:20:57.466829+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0Uok2pip94aNbBFd":"1d8"},"interval":2},"text":[{"text":"The damage increases by 1d8","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["divine","occult"],"description":"You create a ghostly, magical echo of one weapon you're wielding or wearing and fling it. Attempt a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 2d8 damage on a hit (or double damage on a critical hit). The damage type is the same as the chosen weapon (or any of its types for a versatile weapon). The attack deals spirit damage instead if that would be more detrimental to the creature (as determined by the GM). This attack uses and contributes to your multiple attack penalty. After the attack, the weapon returns to your side. If you sanctify the spell, the attacks are sanctified as well. Each time you [Sustain the spell](link_action_20948), you can repeat the attack against any creature within 120 feet.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4856,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4856,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spiritual Guardian","rank":5,"uuid":"3851023312306970","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1897,1556],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1688","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:21:12.198019+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d8"},"interval":2},"text":[{"text":"The guardian's damage increases by 1d8, and its Hit Points increase by 20.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["divine"],"description":"A Medium guardian made of magical force appears in an unoccupied space in range. The spiritual guardian is translucent and wields a ghostly echo of one weapon you're wielding or wearing. If you have a deity, the guardian takes the form of one of your deity's attendants or servitors. If you sanctify the spell, the guardian's attacks are sanctified as well.\n\nCreatures can move through the guardian's space but can't end their movement in it. You and your allies can flank with the guardian. The guardian doesn't have any other attributes a creature would normally have, aside from 50 Hit Points that it can't recover by any means and that it can lose only when protecting a creature (see below).\n\nWhen you Cast the Spell and each time you [Sustain](link_action_20948) it, you can have the guardian move to any unoccupied space within 120 feet of you and either attack or protect.\n\n*   **Attack** The guardian makes a melee spell attack against an adjacent creature, dealing 3d8 damage on a hit (or double damage on a critical hit). The damage type is the same as the chosen weapon (or any of its types for a versatile weapon). The attack deals spirit damage instead if that would be more detrimental to the creature (as determined by the GM). This attack uses and contributes to your multiple attack penalty.\n*   **Protect** The guardian protects a creature of your choice. Each time the chosen creature would take damage and the guardian is adjacent to it, the guardian takes the first 10 damage instead of the ally. This protection lasts until you command the guardian to attack or to protect a different creature, or the guardian is destroyed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"after":{"id":4856,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Spiritual Guardian","rank":5,"uuid":"3851023312306970","range":"120 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1897,1556],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1688","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:21:12.198019+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"interval","damage":{"0":"1d8"},"interval":2},"text":[{"text":"The guardian's damage increases by 1d8, and its Hit Points increase by 20.","amount":"(+2)"}]},"traditions":["divine"],"description":"A Medium guardian made of magical force appears in an unoccupied space in range. The spiritual guardian is translucent and wields a ghostly echo of one weapon you're wielding or wearing. If you have a deity, the guardian takes the form of one of your deity's attendants or servitors. If you sanctify the spell, the guardian's attacks are sanctified as well.\n\nCreatures can move through the guardian's space but can't end their movement in it. You and your allies can flank with the guardian. The guardian doesn't have any other attributes a creature would normally have, aside from 50 Hit Points that it can't recover by any means and that it can lose only when protecting a creature (see below).\n\nWhen you Cast the Spell and each time you [Sustain](link_action_20948) it, you can have the guardian move to any unoccupied space within 120 feet of you and either attack or protect.\n\n*   **Attack** The guardian makes a melee spell attack against an adjacent creature, dealing 3d8 damage on a hit (or double damage on a critical hit). The damage type is the same as the chosen weapon (or any of its types for a versatile weapon). The attack deals spirit damage instead if that would be more detrimental to the creature (as determined by the GM). This attack uses and contributes to your multiple attack penalty.\n*   **Protect** The guardian protects a creature of your choice. Each time the chosen creature would take damage and the guardian is adjacent to it, the guardian takes the first 10 damage instead of the ally. This protection lasts until you command the guardian to attack or to protect a different creature, or the guardian is destroyed.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":1},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4857,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4857,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Stabilize","rank":0,"uuid":"7283546226554287","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1442,1433,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"1 dying creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1689","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:21:21.193484+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"Life energy shuts death's door. The target loses the dying condition, though it remains unconscious at 0 Hit Points.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4857,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Stabilize","rank":0,"uuid":"7283546226554287","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1858,1432,1442,1433,1478],"defense":null,"targets":"1 dying creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1689","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:21:21.193484+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["divine","primal"],"description":"Life energy shuts death's door. The target loses the dying condition, though it remains unconscious at 0 Hit Points.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4862,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4862,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Stupefy","rank":2,"uuid":"533602166925795","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1691","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:22:00.066354+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You dull the target's mind, depending on its Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is stupefied 1 until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** The target is stupefied 2 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is stupefied 3 for 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4862,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Stupefy","rank":2,"uuid":"533602166925795","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,1448],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1691","book":"Player Core","page":"359"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:22:00.066354+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"You dull the target's mind, depending on its Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is stupefied 1 until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** The target is stupefied 2 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is stupefied 3 for 1 minute.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4865,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4865,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Suggestion","rank":4,"uuid":"8196158280494249","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1481,1458,1433,1448,1899],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1693","book":"Player Core","page":"360"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:22:29.398933+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"8":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 creatures.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"Your honeyed words are difficult for creatures to resist. You suggest a course of action to the target, which must be phrased in such a way as to seem like a logical course of action to the target and can't be self-destructive or obviously against the target's self-interest. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected and knows you tried to control it.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target immediately follows your suggestion. The spell has a duration of 1 minute, or until the target has completed a finite suggestion or the suggestion becomes self-destructive or has other obvious negative effects.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the base duration is 1 hour.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4865,"area":null,"cast":"TWO-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Suggestion","rank":4,"uuid":"8196158280494249","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1481,1458,1433,1448,1899],"defense":"Will","targets":"1 creature","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"varies","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1693","book":"Player Core","page":"360"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:22:29.398933+00:00","heightened":{"data":{"type":"fixed","levels":{"8":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}}},"text":[{"text":"You can target up to 10 creatures.","amount":"(8th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","occult"],"description":"Your honeyed words are difficult for creatures to resist. You suggest a course of action to the target, which must be phrased in such a way as to seem like a logical course of action to the target and can't be self-destructive or obviously against the target's self-interest. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected and knows you tried to control it.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target immediately follows your suggestion. The spell has a duration of 1 minute, or until the target has completed a finite suggestion or the suggestion becomes self-destructive or has other obvious negative effects.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the base duration is 1 hour.","availability":null,"requirements":null,"content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"spell","id":4866,"type":"spell","before":{"id":4866,"area":null,"cast":"THREE-ACTIONS","cost":"","name":"Summon Animal","rank":1,"uuid":"6158864017119068","range":"30 feet","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1432,1433,3070],"defense":null,"targets":"","trigger":null,"version":"1.0","duration":"sustained up to 1 minute","meta_data":{"damage":[],"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Spells.aspx?ID=1694","book":"Player Core","page":"360"},"foundry":{"rules":[],"is_focus":false}},"created_at":"2024-03-23T21:22:34.830467+00:00","heightened":{"data":{},"text":[{"text":"Level 1.","amount":"(2nd)"},{"text":"Level 2.","amount":"(3rd)"},{"text":"Level 3.","amount":"(4th)"},{"text":"Level 5.","amount":"(5th)"},{"text":"Level 7.","amount":"(6th)"},{"text":"Level 9.","amount":"(7th)"},{"text":"Level 11.","amount":"(8th)"},{"text":"Level 13.","amount":"(9th)"},{"text":"Level 15.","amount":"(10th)"}]},"traditions":["arcane","primal"],"description":"You summon a cre