e called ghosts.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2447,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2447,"name":"Ghoul","uuid":"3474545820700219","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=754","book":"Monster Core","page":"362"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:13:25.082385+00:00","description":"Ghouls are vile [undead](link_trait_2425) creatures that feast on flesh.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2447,"name":"Ghoul","uuid":"3474545820700219","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=754","book":"Monster Core","page":"362"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:13:25.082385+00:00","description":"Ghouls are vile [undead](link_trait_2425) creatures that feast on flesh.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2448,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2448,"name":"Ooze","uuid":"6113040896942946","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=665","book":"Player Core","page":"459"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:13:47.632925+00:00","description":"Oozes are creatures with simple anatomies. They tend to have low mental attribute modifiers and immunity to [mental](link_trait_1448) effects and precision damage.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2448,"name":"Ooze","uuid":"6113040896942946","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=665","book":"Player Core","page":"459"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:13:47.632925+00:00","description":"Oozes are creatures with simple anatomies. They tend to have low mental attribute modifiers and immunity to [mental](link_trait_1448) effects and precision damage.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2452,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2452,"name":"Gremlin","uuid":"1008684125215138","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=756","book":"Monster Core","page":"362"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:14:54.825006+00:00","description":"Cruel and mischievous [fey](link_trait_2021), gremlins have acclimated to life in the Universe.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2452,"name":"Gremlin","uuid":"1008684125215138","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=756","book":"Monster Core","page":"362"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:14:54.825006+00:00","description":"Cruel and mischievous [fey](link_trait_2021), gremlins have acclimated to life in the Universe.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2457,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2457,"name":"Psychopomp","uuid":"365999569092024","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=679","book":"GM Core","page":"333"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:16:10.440364+00:00","description":"A family of [monitors](link_trait_2408) spawned within the Boneyard to convey souls to the Outer Planes, most psychopomps are true neutral. They typically have [darkvision](link_sense_20769), [lifesense](link_sense_28490), and [spirit touch](link_item_6992), and they’re immune to [death](link_trait_1904) effects.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2457,"name":"Psychopomp","uuid":"365999569092024","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=679","book":"GM Core","page":"333"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:16:10.440364+00:00","description":"A family of [monitors](link_trait_2408) spawned within the Boneyard to convey souls to the Outer Planes, most psychopomps are true neutral. They typically have [darkvision](link_sense_20769), [lifesense](link_sense_28490), and [spirit touch](link_item_6992), and they’re immune to [death](link_trait_1904) effects.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2470,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2470,"name":"Vampire","uuid":"2019630437699860","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=778","book":"Monster Core","page":"364"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:19:01.553266+00:00","description":"[Undead](link_trait_2425) creatures who thirst for blood, vampires are notoriously versatile and hard to destroy.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2470,"name":"Vampire","uuid":"2019630437699860","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=778","book":"Monster Core","page":"364"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:19:01.553266+00:00","description":"[Undead](link_trait_2425) creatures who thirst for blood, vampires are notoriously versatile and hard to destroy.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2471,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2471,"name":"Werecreature","uuid":"432043577123150","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=733","book":"GM Core","page":"335"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:19:21.717125+00:00","description":"These shapechanging creatures either are naturally able to shift between [animal](link_trait_2409), humanoid, and hybrid forms or are afflicted with a [curse](link_trait_1855) that forces them to shift involuntarily.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2471,"name":"Werecreature","uuid":"432043577123150","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=733","book":"GM Core","page":"335"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-03-30T08:19:21.717125+00:00","description":"These shapechanging creatures either are naturally able to shift between [animal](link_trait_2409), humanoid, and hybrid forms or are afflicted with a [curse](link_trait_1855) that forces them to shift involuntarily.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2524,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2524,"name":"Grapple","uuid":"4456575701498702","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=619","book":"Player Core","page":"282"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-07T01:28:24.255121+00:00","description":"You can use this weapon to [Grapple](link_action_19725) with the Athletics skill even if you don’t have a free hand. This uses the weapon’s reach (if different from your own) and adds the weapon’s item bonus to attack rolls as an item bonus to the Athletics check. If you critically fail a check to [Grapple](link_action_19725) using the weapon, you can drop the weapon to take the effects of a failure instead of a critical failure.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2524,"name":"Grapple","uuid":"4456575701498702","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=619","book":"Player Core","page":"282"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-07T01:28:24.255121+00:00","description":"You can use this weapon to [Grapple](link_action_19725) with the Athletics skill even if you don’t have a free hand. This uses the weapon’s reach (if different from your own) and adds the weapon’s item bonus to attack rolls as an item bonus to the Athletics check. If you critically fail a check to [Grapple](link_action_19725) using the weapon, you can drop the weapon to take the effects of a failure instead of a critical failure.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2527,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2527,"name":"Minion","uuid":"8019553394437036","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=653","book":"Player Core","page":"301"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-17T18:32:34.376962+00:00","description":"Minions are creatures that directly serve another creature. Your minion acts on your turn in combat, once per turn, when you spend an action to issue it commands. For an animal companion, you [Command an Animal](link_action_19614); for a minion that's a spell or [magic](link_trait_1504) item effect, like a summoned minion, you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the effect; if not otherwise specified, you issue a verbal command as a single action with the [auditory](link_trait_1469) and [concentrate](link_trait_1432) traits. If given no commands, minions use no actions except to defend themselves or to escape obvious harm. If left unattended for long enough, typically 1 minute, [mindless](link_trait_2411) minions usually don't act, animals follow their instincts, and sapient minions act how they please. You can have a maximum of four minions under your control.\n\nA minion has only 2 actions and 0 reactions per turn, though certain conditions (such as slowed or quickened) or abilities might give them additional actions or a reaction. Alterations to a minion's actions occur when they gain their actions for the round. A minion can't control other creatures.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2527,"name":"Minion","uuid":"8019553394437036","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=653","book":"Player Core","page":"301"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-17T18:32:34.376962+00:00","description":"Minions are creatures that directly serve another creature. Your minion acts on your turn in combat, once per turn, when you spend an action to issue it commands. For an animal companion, you [Command an Animal](link_action_19614); for a minion that's a spell or [magic](link_trait_1504) item effect, like a summoned minion, you [Sustain](link_action_19858) the effect; if not otherwise specified, you issue a verbal command as a single action with the [auditory](link_trait_1469) and [concentrate](link_trait_1432) traits. If given no commands, minions use no actions except to defend themselves or to escape obvious harm. If left unattended for long enough, typically 1 minute, [mindless](link_trait_2411) minions usually don't act, animals follow their instincts, and sapient minions act how they please. You can have a maximum of four minions under your control.\n\nA minion has only 2 actions and 0 reactions per turn, though certain conditions (such as slowed or quickened) or abilities might give them additional actions or a reaction. Alterations to a minion's actions occur when they gain their actions for the round. A minion can't control other creatures.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2529,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2529,"name":"Deadly d12","uuid":"4147788006932001","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-17T20:43:30.905127+00:00","description":"On a critical hit, the weapon adds a weapon damage die of the listed size. Roll this after doubling the weapon’s damage. This increases to two dice if the weapon has a [_greater striking_](link_item_7860) rune and three dice if the weapon has a [_major striking_](link_item_7861) rune. For instance, a [rapier](link_item_7685) with a greater striking rune deals 2d8 extra piercing damage on a critical hit. An ability that changes the size of the weapon’s normal damage dice doesn’t change the size of its deadly die.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2529,"name":"Deadly d12","uuid":"4147788006932001","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-17T20:43:30.905127+00:00","description":"On a critical hit, the weapon adds a weapon damage die of the listed size. Roll this after doubling the weapon’s damage. This increases to two dice if the weapon has a [_greater striking_](link_item_7860) rune and three dice if the weapon has a [_major striking_](link_item_7861) rune. For instance, a [rapier](link_item_7685) with a greater striking rune deals 2d8 extra piercing damage on a critical hit. An ability that changes the size of the weapon’s normal damage dice doesn’t change the size of its deadly die.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2565,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2565,"name":"Kickback","uuid":"179187521381498","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T01:56:24.525263+00:00","description":"A kickback weapon is extra powerful and difficult to use due to its high recoil. A kickback weapon deals 1 additional damage with all attacks. Firing a kickback weapon gives a –2 circumstance penalty to the attack roll, but characters with +2 or more Strength ignore the penalty. Attaching a kickback weapon to a deployed [tripod](link_item_13501) or other stabilizer can lower or negate this penalty.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2565,"name":"Kickback","uuid":"179187521381498","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T01:56:24.525263+00:00","description":"A kickback weapon is extra powerful and difficult to use due to its high recoil. A kickback weapon deals 1 additional damage with all attacks. Firing a kickback weapon gives a –2 circumstance penalty to the attack roll, but characters with +2 or more Strength ignore the penalty. Attaching a kickback weapon to a deployed [tripod](link_item_13501) or other stabilizer can lower or negate this penalty.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2570,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2570,"name":"Spellheart","uuid":"909194880622593","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T01:56:53.063516+00:00","description":"Spellhearts are permanent items that work similarly to [talismans](link_trait_1544). You affix a spellheart using the Affix a Spellheart activity, which is otherwise identical to [Affix a Talisman](link_action_24828). The limit of one talisman per item remains—an item can have one spellheart or one talisman, not both. When casting a [cantrip](link_trait_1858) from a spellheart, you can use your own spell attack roll or spell DC if it's higher. Crafting a spellheart requires the spells the spellheart can cast. For example, a [major five-feather wreath](link_item_12926) requires [air walk](link_spell_6141), [gale blast](link_spell_6742), and [wall of wind](link_spell_4946).","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2570,"name":"Spellheart","uuid":"909194880622593","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T01:56:53.063516+00:00","description":"Spellhearts are permanent items that work similarly to [talismans](link_trait_1544). You affix a spellheart using the Affix a Spellheart activity, which is otherwise identical to [Affix a Talisman](link_action_24828). The limit of one talisman per item remains—an item can have one spellheart or one talisman, not both. When casting a [cantrip](link_trait_1858) from a spellheart, you can use your own spell attack roll or spell DC if it's higher. Crafting a spellheart requires the spells the spellheart can cast. For example, a [major five-feather wreath](link_item_12926) requires [air walk](link_spell_6141), [gale blast](link_spell_6742), and [wall of wind](link_spell_4946).","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2583,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2583,"name":"Contingency","uuid":"294749856183681","meta_data":null,"created_at":"2024-04-19T02:00:32.091525+00:00","description":"","content_source_id":15},"after":{"id":2583,"name":"Contingency","uuid":"294749856183681","meta_data":null,"created_at":"2024-04-19T02:00:32.091525+00:00","description":"","content_source_id":15},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2748,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2748,"name":"Jousting","uuid":"438922509591800","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=638","book":"Player Core","page":"282"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T03:19:59.28273+00:00","description":"The weapon is suited for mounted combat with a harness or similar means. When mounted, if you moved at least 10 feet on the action before your attack, add a circumstance bonus to damage for that attack equal to the number of damage dice for the weapon. In addition, while mounted, you can wield the weapon in one hand, changing the damage die to the listed value. As a part of your action to [Mount](link_action_19742) a creature, you can switch your grip on a jousting weapon to one-handed. After that, changing your grip takes an [Interact](link_action_19733) action as normal. If you dismount while wielding a jousting weapon onehanded, you can switch to using two hands as part of that action if you have a hand free at that point. If not, you’ll still be holding the weapon in one hand, but not wielding it.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2748,"name":"Jousting","uuid":"438922509591800","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=638","book":"Player Core","page":"282"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T03:19:59.28273+00:00","description":"The weapon is suited for mounted combat with a harness or similar means. When mounted, if you moved at least 10 feet on the action before your attack, add a circumstance bonus to damage for that attack equal to the number of damage dice for the weapon. In addition, while mounted, you can wield the weapon in one hand, changing the damage die to the listed value. As a part of your action to [Mount](link_action_19742) a creature, you can switch your grip on a jousting weapon to one-handed. After that, changing your grip takes an [Interact](link_action_19733) action as normal. If you dismount while wielding a jousting weapon onehanded, you can switch to using two hands as part of that action if you have a hand free at that point. If not, you’ll still be holding the weapon in one hand, but not wielding it.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2762,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2762,"name":"Volley 20 ft.","uuid":"3544624043347068","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T03:41:11.584033+00:00","description":"This ranged weapon is less effective at close distances. Your attacks against targets that are at a distance within the range listed take a –2 penalty.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2762,"name":"Volley 20 ft.","uuid":"3544624043347068","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T03:41:11.584033+00:00","description":"This ranged weapon is less effective at close distances. Your attacks against targets that are at a distance within the range listed take a –2 penalty.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2763,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2763,"name":"Additive 0","uuid":"6061496890794803","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T03:43:50.856272+00:00","description":"Feats with the additive trait allow you to spend actions to add special substances to bombs or elixirs. You can add only one additive to a single alchemical item, and attempting to add another spoils the item. You can typically use actions with the additive trait only when you’re creating an infused alchemical item, and some can be used only with the Quick Alchemy action. Additive 1 adds one to the level of the alchemical item you’re modifying; the result is the new level of the mixture. The mixture’s item level must be no higher than your Advanced Alchemy level.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2763,"name":"Additive 0","uuid":"6061496890794803","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T03:43:50.856272+00:00","description":"Feats with the additive trait allow you to spend actions to add special substances to bombs or elixirs. You can add only one additive to a single alchemical item, and attempting to add another spoils the item. You can typically use actions with the additive trait only when you’re creating an infused alchemical item, and some can be used only with the Quick Alchemy action. Additive 1 adds one to the level of the alchemical item you’re modifying; the result is the new level of the mixture. The mixture’s item level must be no higher than your Advanced Alchemy level.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2854,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2854,"name":"Fulu","uuid":"1867448432733917","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:10:38.40211+00:00","description":"Fulus are small paper charms that can be affixed to a suit of armor, a shield, a weapon, a creature, or even a structure. Some fulus are composed of multiple such charms, taking effect only once all have been affixed. Normal fulus have effects immediately once affixed, while fulu talismans have an effect only once activated. Once a fulu has been activated, it lasts for the given duration and then burns out. Unless otherwise noted, fulus expire one year after being created, reverting to mundane paper.\n\nAll fulus have the fulu and [consumable](link_trait_1531) traits. Fulus also have a tradition trait determined by the [magical](link_trait_1504) tradition of its creator. For example, a fulu created by a priest would have the [divine](link_trait_1475) trait, whereas a witch who dabbles in fate might create a fulu with the [occult](link_trait_1514) trait. Some fulus also have the [talisman](link_trait_1544) trait, if they work similarly to talismans (such as being affixed to a suit of armor, a shield, or a weapon).\n\nEach fulu’s stat block indicates the type of item or creature it can be affixed to. Affixing or removing a fulu requires using the [Affix a Fulu](link_action_58707) activity, or the [Affix a Talisman](link_action_24828) action instead if the fulu is also a [talisman](link_trait_1544).","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2854,"name":"Fulu","uuid":"1867448432733917","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:10:38.40211+00:00","description":"Fulus are small paper charms that can be affixed to a suit of armor, a shield, a weapon, a creature, or even a structure. Some fulus are composed of multiple such charms, taking effect only once all have been affixed. Normal fulus have effects immediately once affixed, while fulu talismans have an effect only once activated. Once a fulu has been activated, it lasts for the given duration and then burns out. Unless otherwise noted, fulus expire one year after being created, reverting to mundane paper.\n\nAll fulus have the fulu and [consumable](link_trait_1531) traits. Fulus also have a tradition trait determined by the [magical](link_trait_1504) tradition of its creator. For example, a fulu created by a priest would have the [divine](link_trait_1475) trait, whereas a witch who dabbles in fate might create a fulu with the [occult](link_trait_1514) trait. Some fulus also have the [talisman](link_trait_1544) trait, if they work similarly to talismans (such as being affixed to a suit of armor, a shield, or a weapon).\n\nEach fulu’s stat block indicates the type of item or creature it can be affixed to. Affixing or removing a fulu requires using the [Affix a Fulu](link_action_58707) activity, or the [Affix a Talisman](link_action_24828) action instead if the fulu is also a [talisman](link_trait_1544).","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2855,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2855,"name":"Grimoire","uuid":"7077107757295082","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:10:47.376981+00:00","description":"Spellbooks are useful tools for any magic user to write down incantations and runes of power, but where most spellbooks are nothing more than ink on parchment, grimoires have absorbed the magic of the spells within—magic that knowledgeable spellcasters can use to augment their spells.\n\nMost grimoires can hold up to 100 spells, like any [spellbook](link_item_7799), but allow spellcasters to erase spells written by a book's previous owner in favor of spells that employ their own magical formulas. If a spellcaster wants to transfer their spells from one of their spellbooks to a grimoire, they can conduct a simple, 1-minute ritual with the two books to cause the spells to vanish from their spellbook and appear in the grimoire.\n\nIf you prepare spells (whether from your class features, like a [cleric](link_class_22) or [wizard](link_class_26), or from a special feat or ability, like the [Esoteric Polymath](link_feat_20118) bard feat), you can study a grimoire during your daily preparations to enhance one or more of the spells within. Until your next daily preparations, you gain the ability to Activate the grimoire. As you've already absorbed the power from the grimoire during your daily preparations, you can Activate it even if you later lose possession of the book itself. Grimoires' benefits apply only to spells cast via spell slots—not cantrips, focus spells, or innate spells. No one can use more than one grimoire per day, nor can a grimoire be used by more than one person per day.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2855,"name":"Grimoire","uuid":"7077107757295082","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:10:47.376981+00:00","description":"Spellbooks are useful tools for any magic user to write down incantations and runes of power, but where most spellbooks are nothing more than ink on parchment, grimoires have absorbed the magic of the spells within—magic that knowledgeable spellcasters can use to augment their spells.\n\nMost grimoires can hold up to 100 spells, like any [spellbook](link_item_7799), but allow spellcasters to erase spells written by a book's previous owner in favor of spells that employ their own magical formulas. If a spellcaster wants to transfer their spells from one of their spellbooks to a grimoire, they can conduct a simple, 1-minute ritual with the two books to cause the spells to vanish from their spellbook and appear in the grimoire.\n\nIf you prepare spells (whether from your class features, like a [cleric](link_class_22) or [wizard](link_class_26), or from a special feat or ability, like the [Esoteric Polymath](link_feat_20118) bard feat), you can study a grimoire during your daily preparations to enhance one or more of the spells within. Until your next daily preparations, you gain the ability to Activate the grimoire. As you've already absorbed the power from the grimoire during your daily preparations, you can Activate it even if you later lose possession of the book itself. Grimoires' benefits apply only to spells cast via spell slots—not cantrips, focus spells, or innate spells. No one can use more than one grimoire per day, nor can a grimoire be used by more than one person per day.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2856,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2856,"name":"Catalyst","uuid":"2371583432058458","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:10:58.031047+00:00","description":"Items with the catalyst trait are [consumables](link_trait_1531) that alter or magnify specific spells. Using a catalyst adds the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait to the spell.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2856,"name":"Catalyst","uuid":"2371583432058458","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:10:58.031047+00:00","description":"Items with the catalyst trait are [consumables](link_trait_1531) that alter or magnify specific spells. Using a catalyst adds the [manipulate](link_trait_1433) trait to the spell.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2857,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2857,"name":"Tattoo","uuid":"3941412709609205","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:12:51.547616+00:00","description":"A [magical](link_trait_1504) tattoo has the tattoo trait. It's permanently a part of the subject's body, and reduces the number of items that creature can invest per day by 1. Each tattoo has the [invested](link_trait_1527) trait to indicate this limitation—a magical tattoo is like an invested item that the tattooed creature has no choice but to invest. If the tattoo loses its magic or is destroyed, it no longer reduces your investiture.\n\nJust like a physical magic item, a magical tattoo can be [counteracted](link_action_27519) by spells like [_dispel magic_](link_spell_4572) or [_detonate magic_](link_spell_4565). If destroyed, the tattoo fades from the skin.\n\nIf a creature gets a new magical tattoo when their limit on invested items has already been reduced to zero, the new tattoo's magic fails to take hold, and it becomes a non-magical tattoo instead. However, a tattooist can alter an existing tattoo when they [Craft](link_action_19617) a tattoo, modifying the old one into a different magical tattoo and removing the old effect. Magical tattoos can usually be upgraded into their greater versions by having a tattooist add to or modify the existing tattoo.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2857,"name":"Tattoo","uuid":"3941412709609205","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:12:51.547616+00:00","description":"A [magical](link_trait_1504) tattoo has the tattoo trait. It's permanently a part of the subject's body, and reduces the number of items that creature can invest per day by 1. Each tattoo has the [invested](link_trait_1527) trait to indicate this limitation—a magical tattoo is like an invested item that the tattooed creature has no choice but to invest. If the tattoo loses its magic or is destroyed, it no longer reduces your investiture.\n\nJust like a physical magic item, a magical tattoo can be [counteracted](link_action_27519) by spells like [_dispel magic_](link_spell_4572) or [_detonate magic_](link_spell_4565). If destroyed, the tattoo fades from the skin.\n\nIf a creature gets a new magical tattoo when their limit on invested items has already been reduced to zero, the new tattoo's magic fails to take hold, and it becomes a non-magical tattoo instead. However, a tattooist can alter an existing tattoo when they [Craft](link_action_19617) a tattoo, modifying the old one into a different magical tattoo and removing the old effect. Magical tattoos can usually be upgraded into their greater versions by having a tattooist add to or modify the existing tattoo.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2858,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2858,"name":"Adjustment","uuid":"461477225387697","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:05.474932+00:00","description":"Items with this trait are intended to alter existing pieces of equipment, typically armors, shields, and weapons. The given item will note which type of equipment it modifies. An adjustment that modifies armor can't modify [explorer's clothing](link_item_6939). A piece of equipment can only be affected by a single adjustment at a time. Unless otherwise noted, adding or removing an adjustment requires using a 10-minute activity and a [repair kit](link_item_7700).","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2858,"name":"Adjustment","uuid":"461477225387697","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:05.474932+00:00","description":"Items with this trait are intended to alter existing pieces of equipment, typically armors, shields, and weapons. The given item will note which type of equipment it modifies. An adjustment that modifies armor can't modify [explorer's clothing](link_item_6939). A piece of equipment can only be affected by a single adjustment at a time. Unless otherwise noted, adding or removing an adjustment requires using a 10-minute activity and a [repair kit](link_item_7700).","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2859,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2859,"name":"Processed","uuid":"8511464071271616","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=487","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:13.935196+00:00","description":"An [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) with the processed trait can be created with [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) but is too complex to create in a single action. Using [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) to create a processed item takes 1 minute. If the item would take more than 3 actions to Activate, the time the item remains potent after you create it is equal to its activation time. For instance, a processed item that takes 10 minutes to Activate would remain potent for 10 minutes when created with [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) instead of remaining potent only until the start of your next turn. This trait doesn't change other specifics of [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176). You could, for example, use [double brew](link_class-feature_31174) to create two of the same processed item over the course of 1 minute.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2859,"name":"Processed","uuid":"8511464071271616","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=487","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:13.935196+00:00","description":"An [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [consumable](link_trait_1531) with the processed trait can be created with [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) but is too complex to create in a single action. Using [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) to create a processed item takes 1 minute. If the item would take more than 3 actions to Activate, the time the item remains potent after you create it is equal to its activation time. For instance, a processed item that takes 10 minutes to Activate would remain potent for 10 minutes when created with [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176) instead of remaining potent only until the start of your next turn. This trait doesn't change other specifics of [Quick Alchemy](link_feat_31176). You could, for example, use [double brew](link_class-feature_31174) to create two of the same processed item over the course of 1 minute.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2860,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2860,"name":"Laminar","uuid":"8565369619548087","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:16.655194+00:00","description":"The armor is made up of layered sections, so when it breaks, it isn’t as much of a problem. The status penalty to AC if this armor is broken is –1 for broken medium armor, –2 for broken heavy armor, or no penalty for broken light armor.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2860,"name":"Laminar","uuid":"8565369619548087","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:16.655194+00:00","description":"The armor is made up of layered sections, so when it breaks, it isn’t as much of a problem. The status penalty to AC if this armor is broken is –1 for broken medium armor, –2 for broken heavy armor, or no penalty for broken light armor.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2861,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2861,"name":"Coda","uuid":"4102458763152910","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:19.547704+00:00","description":"Instruments with the coda trait work mostly like staves and have the [staff](link_trait_1546) trait. There are two differences: Coda instruments are in the form of musical instruments, and they can be prepared only by bards. Because they're not physically staves, you can't attack with a coda instrument, nor can you etch it with weapon runes.\n\nThe process of preparing a coda instrument involves playing significant portions of songs related to the spells within the instrument—either old standards or ones of your own creation. This leaves magical reverberations within the instrument that allow you to complete the songs by playing their coda later in the day.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2861,"name":"Coda","uuid":"4102458763152910","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:19.547704+00:00","description":"Instruments with the coda trait work mostly like staves and have the [staff](link_trait_1546) trait. There are two differences: Coda instruments are in the form of musical instruments, and they can be prepared only by bards. Because they're not physically staves, you can't attack with a coda instrument, nor can you etch it with weapon runes.\n\nThe process of preparing a coda instrument involves playing significant portions of songs related to the spells within the instrument—either old standards or ones of your own creation. This leaves magical reverberations within the instrument that allow you to complete the songs by playing their coda later in the day.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2862,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2862,"name":"Razing","uuid":"3487636607906101","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=784","book":"Player Core 2","page":"274"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:26.233427+00:00","description":"Razing weapons are particularly good at damaging objects, structures, and vehicles. Whenever you deal damage to an object (including shields and animated objects), structure, or vehicle with a razing weapon, the object takes an amount of additional damage equal to double the number of weapon damage dice.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2862,"name":"Razing","uuid":"3487636607906101","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=784","book":"Player Core 2","page":"274"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:26.233427+00:00","description":"Razing weapons are particularly good at damaging objects, structures, and vehicles. Whenever you deal damage to an object (including shields and animated objects), structure, or vehicle with a razing weapon, the object takes an amount of additional damage equal to double the number of weapon damage dice.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2863,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2863,"name":"Repeating","uuid":"1849673838729221","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:27.382311+00:00","description":"A repeating weapon is a type of ranged weapon with a shorter reload time. These weapons can't be loaded with individual bolts or bullets like other crossbows and firearms; instead, they require a magazine of specialized ammunition to be loaded into a special slot. Once that magazine is in place, the ammunition is automatically loaded each time the weapon is cocked to fire, reducing its reload to the value in its reload entry (typically 0). When the ammunition runs out, a new magazine must be loaded, which requires a free hand and 3 [Interact](link_action_19733) actions (to remove the old magazine, retrieve the new magazine, and slot the new magazine in place). These actions don't need to be consecutive and are the same as [Interacting](link_action_19733) to reload.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2863,"name":"Repeating","uuid":"1849673838729221","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:27.382311+00:00","description":"A repeating weapon is a type of ranged weapon with a shorter reload time. These weapons can't be loaded with individual bolts or bullets like other crossbows and firearms; instead, they require a magazine of specialized ammunition to be loaded into a special slot. Once that magazine is in place, the ammunition is automatically loaded each time the weapon is cocked to fire, reducing its reload to the value in its reload entry (typically 0). When the ammunition runs out, a new magazine must be loaded, which requires a free hand and 3 [Interact](link_action_19733) actions (to remove the old magazine, retrieve the new magazine, and slot the new magazine in place). These actions don't need to be consecutive and are the same as [Interacting](link_action_19733) to reload.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2864,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2864,"name":"Entrench Melee","uuid":"8827243510452337","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:33.161376+00:00","description":"You can position yourself in the armor or reposition its articulated pieces to better protect against some attacks. If you're trained in this armor, while wearing it you can spend a single action to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against a certain type of attack until the start of your next turn. The entrench trait lists the type of attack this bonus applies against, typically entrench melee or entrench ranged.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2864,"name":"Entrench Melee","uuid":"8827243510452337","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:33.161376+00:00","description":"You can position yourself in the armor or reposition its articulated pieces to better protect against some attacks. If you're trained in this armor, while wearing it you can spend a single action to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against a certain type of attack until the start of your next turn. The entrench trait lists the type of attack this bonus applies against, typically entrench melee or entrench ranged.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2865,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2865,"name":"Hindering","uuid":"8366535152045097","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:34.341116+00:00","description":"This armor is so heavy and bulky it slows you down no matter what. You take a –5 penalty to all your Speeds (to a minimum of a 5-foot Speed). This is separate from and in addition to the armor's Speed penalty, and affects you even if your Strength or an ability lets you reduce or ignore the armor's Speed penalty.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2865,"name":"Hindering","uuid":"8366535152045097","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:34.341116+00:00","description":"This armor is so heavy and bulky it slows you down no matter what. You take a –5 penalty to all your Speeds (to a minimum of a 5-foot Speed). This is separate from and in addition to the armor's Speed penalty, and affects you even if your Strength or an ability lets you reduce or ignore the armor's Speed penalty.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2867,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2867,"name":"Vehicular","uuid":"6746096175302936","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:39.52222+00:00","description":"A vehicular weapon is attached to a vehicle or worn by a mount and can typically only be wielded by the driver of the vehicle or the mount's primary rider. The driver or rider can control a vehicular weapon with the same hands they use to steer the vehicle or guide the mount. A vehicular weapon can be [Disarmed](link_action_19626) by knocking the controls (typically reins for a mount or a steering device for a vehicle) out of the wielder's hands.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2867,"name":"Vehicular","uuid":"6746096175302936","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:39.52222+00:00","description":"A vehicular weapon is attached to a vehicle or worn by a mount and can typically only be wielded by the driver of the vehicle or the mount's primary rider. The driver or rider can control a vehicular weapon with the same hands they use to steer the vehicle or guide the mount. A vehicular weapon can be [Disarmed](link_action_19626) by knocking the controls (typically reins for a mount or a steering device for a vehicle) out of the wielder's hands.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2868,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2868,"name":"Spellgun","uuid":"1640530375111539","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:50.7533+00:00","description":"The spellgun trait appears on items that can generate a [magical](link_trait_1504) effect that flies out like a bullet. You can make either a spell attack roll with a spellgun or a ranged attack roll using your proficiency with simple firearms. Spellguns have a range increment, which applies regardless of which type of attack roll you make. Though you can use your modifier for simple firearms, a spellgun isn't actually a firearm. You don't get the damage of a firearm [Strike](link_action_19856), nor other benefits like critical specialization. Similarly, you can't load or reload a spellgun, make a spellgun Strike as part of an action that lets you make a firearm Strike, affix [talismans](link_trait_1544) to one, attach scopes, affix [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons like bayonets or reinforced stocks, and so on.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2868,"name":"Spellgun","uuid":"1640530375111539","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:50.7533+00:00","description":"The spellgun trait appears on items that can generate a [magical](link_trait_1504) effect that flies out like a bullet. You can make either a spell attack roll with a spellgun or a ranged attack roll using your proficiency with simple firearms. Spellguns have a range increment, which applies regardless of which type of attack roll you make. Though you can use your modifier for simple firearms, a spellgun isn't actually a firearm. You don't get the damage of a firearm [Strike](link_action_19856), nor other benefits like critical specialization. Similarly, you can't load or reload a spellgun, make a spellgun Strike as part of an action that lets you make a firearm Strike, affix [talismans](link_trait_1544) to one, attach scopes, affix [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons like bayonets or reinforced stocks, and so on.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2869,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2869,"name":"Entrench Ranged","uuid":"8869747565614601","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:58.083031+00:00","description":"You can position yourself in the armor or reposition its articulated pieces to better protect against some attacks. If you're trained in this armor, while wearing it you can spend a single action to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against a certain type of attack until the start of your next turn. The entrench trait lists the type of attack this bonus applies against, typically entrench melee or entrench ranged.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2869,"name":"Entrench Ranged","uuid":"8869747565614601","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:58.083031+00:00","description":"You can position yourself in the armor or reposition its articulated pieces to better protect against some attacks. If you're trained in this armor, while wearing it you can spend a single action to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against a certain type of attack until the start of your next turn. The entrench trait lists the type of attack this bonus applies against, typically entrench melee or entrench ranged.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2870,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2870,"name":"Ponderous","uuid":"5812484639447685","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=486","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:59.033178+00:00","description":"The armor has moving parts or other complications that lengthen the wearer's initial reaction time. While wearing the armor, you take a -1 penalty to initiative checks. If you don't meet the armor's required Strength modifier, this penalty increases to be equal to the armor's check penalty if it's worse.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2870,"name":"Ponderous","uuid":"5812484639447685","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=486","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:13:59.033178+00:00","description":"The armor has moving parts or other complications that lengthen the wearer's initial reaction time. While wearing the armor, you take a -1 penalty to initiative checks. If you don't meet the armor's required Strength modifier, this penalty increases to be equal to the armor's check penalty if it's worse.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2872,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2872,"name":"Recovery","uuid":"4834525036120940","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=489","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:26.139029+00:00","description":"Recovery weapons are [thrown](link_trait_1575) weapons designed to return to the thrower when they miss the target. When you make an unsuccessful [thrown](link_trait_1575) [Strike](link_action_19856) with this weapon, it flies back to your hand after the [Strike](link_action_19856) is complete, allowing you to try again. If your hands are full when the weapon returns, it falls to the ground in your space.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2872,"name":"Recovery","uuid":"4834525036120940","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=489","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:26.139029+00:00","description":"Recovery weapons are [thrown](link_trait_1575) weapons designed to return to the thrower when they miss the target. When you make an unsuccessful [thrown](link_trait_1575) [Strike](link_action_19856) with this weapon, it flies back to your hand after the [Strike](link_action_19856) is complete, allowing you to try again. If your hands are full when the weapon returns, it falls to the ground in your space.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2873,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2873,"name":"Adjusted","uuid":"5764728699839630","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=468","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"216"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:48.738706+00:00","description":"The equipment comes with an adjustment described in its entry. This adjustment is built into the equipment permanently, meaning the equipment can't have another adjustment added, nor can it be swapped out for a different adjustment. If the adjustment alters the item's base statistics, such as adding the [noisy](link_trait_1582) trait, that's reflected in the equipment's table entry.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2873,"name":"Adjusted","uuid":"5764728699839630","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=468","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"216"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:48.738706+00:00","description":"The equipment comes with an adjustment described in its entry. This adjustment is built into the equipment permanently, meaning the equipment can't have another adjustment added, nor can it be swapped out for a different adjustment. If the adjustment alters the item's base statistics, such as adding the [noisy](link_trait_1582) trait, that's reflected in the equipment's table entry.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2874,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2874,"name":"Missive","uuid":"334918030833783","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=485","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:53.497528+00:00","description":"A missive is a piece of [magical](link_trait_1504) stationery that must be crafted and [Composed](link_action_43788) before it can be activated. All missives have the missive and [consumable](link_trait_1531) traits. Missives are often constructed of paper, parchment, or vellum, but any other thin, portable material that can hold writing or embossing upon it can be crafted into missives. After being crafted, the missive is a blank sheet until a message is [composed](link_action_43788) upon it, completing its magic.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2874,"name":"Missive","uuid":"334918030833783","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=485","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:53.497528+00:00","description":"A missive is a piece of [magical](link_trait_1504) stationery that must be crafted and [Composed](link_action_43788) before it can be activated. All missives have the missive and [consumable](link_trait_1531) traits. Missives are often constructed of paper, parchment, or vellum, but any other thin, portable material that can hold writing or embossing upon it can be crafted into missives. After being crafted, the missive is a blank sheet until a message is [composed](link_action_43788) upon it, completing its magic.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2875,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2875,"name":"Inscribed","uuid":"8114503160854873","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=480","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:56.77543+00:00","description":"The equipment, typically an armor or shield, has been treated so it can be inscribed with [magical](link_trait_1504) symbols using the same methods as [Crafting](link_action_19617) a [scroll](link_item_7729). Inscribed attire can hold one [scroll](link_item_7729) inscribed on it. You need a free hand to Activate the [scroll](link_item_7729), but you don't need to [Interact](link_action_19733) to draw it. You can also Activate the magic to erase the [scroll](link_item_7729) the equipment currently contains. You can't inscribe a new [scroll](link_item_7729) onto the equipment if a [scroll](link_item_7729) is currently inscribed on it or if the equipment is broken.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2875,"name":"Inscribed","uuid":"8114503160854873","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=480","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:14:56.77543+00:00","description":"The equipment, typically an armor or shield, has been treated so it can be inscribed with [magical](link_trait_1504) symbols using the same methods as [Crafting](link_action_19617) a [scroll](link_item_7729). Inscribed attire can hold one [scroll](link_item_7729) inscribed on it. You need a free hand to Activate the [scroll](link_item_7729), but you don't need to [Interact](link_action_19733) to draw it. You can also Activate the magic to erase the [scroll](link_item_7729) the equipment currently contains. You can't inscribe a new [scroll](link_item_7729) onto the equipment if a [scroll](link_item_7729) is currently inscribed on it or if the equipment is broken.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2876,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2876,"name":"Lozenge","uuid":"309773015660484","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=484","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:20.90333+00:00","description":"You Activate an [alchemical](link_trait_1529) lozenge by putting it in your mouth. It stays there, slowly dissolving and releasing its ingredients over time. You can bite a lozenge for a secondary effect. The action this takes is noted in the item. As soon as this secondary effect is over, the lozenge is used up and its benefits for you end. You can drink [elixirs](link_trait_1553), [potions](link_trait_1565), and beverages with a lozenge in your mouth, but you can't benefit from more than one lozenge at a time. If you have two lozenges in your mouth at the same time, both become inert. You can also spit out a lozenge as a single action to end its effect and make it inert. A lozenge dissolves due to its [alchemical](link_trait_1529) ingredients, so it typically still works even if you don't have saliva.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2876,"name":"Lozenge","uuid":"309773015660484","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=484","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:20.90333+00:00","description":"You Activate an [alchemical](link_trait_1529) lozenge by putting it in your mouth. It stays there, slowly dissolving and releasing its ingredients over time. You can bite a lozenge for a secondary effect. The action this takes is noted in the item. As soon as this secondary effect is over, the lozenge is used up and its benefits for you end. You can drink [elixirs](link_trait_1553), [potions](link_trait_1565), and beverages with a lozenge in your mouth, but you can't benefit from more than one lozenge at a time. If you have two lozenges in your mouth at the same time, both become inert. You can also spit out a lozenge as a single action to end its effect and make it inert. A lozenge dissolves due to its [alchemical](link_trait_1529) ingredients, so it typically still works even if you don't have saliva.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2877,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2877,"name":"Clockwork","uuid":"8808857827781470","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:24.909613+00:00","description":"Clockworks are intricate, complex [constructs](link_trait_2410) that can be programmed to perform specific functions. A clockwork creature must be wound regularly to function.\n\nClockwork items use clockwork to function, though they don’t necessarily require daily winding.\n\n**Wind-Up**: To remain operational, a clockwork vehicle or creature must be wound with a unique key by a creature. This takes an amount of time listed in the clockwork's wind-up entry, which also lists how long the clockwork remains operational once wound; after this duration, the clockwork becomes inactive and immobile until it's wound again. Some clockworks' abilities require them to spend some of their remaining operational time. They can't spend more than they have and shut down immediately once they have 0 time remaining. If it's unclear when a clockwork was last wound, most are re-wound approximately halfway through their operating time.\n\nA clockwork vehicle can be placed into standby mode by its pilot as a 3-action activity; a clockwork creature must perform this activity itself. A clockwork's operational time doesn't decrease in standby.\n\nA creature can attempt to [Disable a Device](link_action_19625) to wind a clockwork down (with a DC listed in the wind-up entry). For each success, a clockwork vehicle loses 10 minutes of operational time, while a clockwork creature loses 1 hour. This can be done even if the clockwork is in standby mode.\n\nBroken clockwork vehicles have difficulty holding energy. The first time each round that a broken clockwork vehicle moves, it must attempt a DC 5 flat check. On a failure, it loses 10 minutes of operational time.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2877,"name":"Clockwork","uuid":"8808857827781470","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:24.909613+00:00","description":"Clockworks are intricate, complex [constructs](link_trait_2410) that can be programmed to perform specific functions. A clockwork creature must be wound regularly to function.\n\nClockwork items use clockwork to function, though they don’t necessarily require daily winding.\n\n**Wind-Up**: To remain operational, a clockwork vehicle or creature must be wound with a unique key by a creature. This takes an amount of time listed in the clockwork's wind-up entry, which also lists how long the clockwork remains operational once wound; after this duration, the clockwork becomes inactive and immobile until it's wound again. Some clockworks' abilities require them to spend some of their remaining operational time. They can't spend more than they have and shut down immediately once they have 0 time remaining. If it's unclear when a clockwork was last wound, most are re-wound approximately halfway through their operating time.\n\nA clockwork vehicle can be placed into standby mode by its pilot as a 3-action activity; a clockwork creature must perform this activity itself. A clockwork's operational time doesn't decrease in standby.\n\nA creature can attempt to [Disable a Device](link_action_19625) to wind a clockwork down (with a DC listed in the wind-up entry). For each success, a clockwork vehicle loses 10 minutes of operational time, while a clockwork creature loses 1 hour. This can be done even if the clockwork is in standby mode.\n\nBroken clockwork vehicles have difficulty holding energy. The first time each round that a broken clockwork vehicle moves, it must attempt a DC 5 flat check. On a failure, it loses 10 minutes of operational time.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2878,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2878,"name":"Training","uuid":"1567405146783298","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:41.89758+00:00","description":"A training weapon is designed to be used when training an [animal](link_trait_2409) to participate in combat by identifying the target for the animal to attack. [Striking](link_action_19856) a creature with a training weapon gives your [animal companion](link_trait_3842) or your bonded animal a +1 circumstance bonus to its next attack roll against that target.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2878,"name":"Training","uuid":"1567405146783298","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:41.89758+00:00","description":"A training weapon is designed to be used when training an [animal](link_trait_2409) to participate in combat by identifying the target for the animal to attack. [Striking](link_action_19856) a creature with a training weapon gives your [animal companion](link_trait_3842) or your bonded animal a +1 circumstance bonus to its next attack roll against that target.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2879,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2879,"name":"Aquadynamic","uuid":"1997026650984948","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:52.668479+00:00","description":"This armor is designed for use underwater, with streamlined design and buoyant materials used in strategic places. You don’t apply the armor’s check penalty to Acrobatics or Athletics checks in water or similar liquids.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2879,"name":"Aquadynamic","uuid":"1997026650984948","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:15:52.668479+00:00","description":"This armor is designed for use underwater, with streamlined design and buoyant materials used in strategic places. You don’t apply the armor’s check penalty to Acrobatics or Athletics checks in water or similar liquids.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2881,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2881,"name":"Launching Dart","uuid":"8881833178962717","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=483","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:16:11.764549+00:00","description":"A mechanism within this shield can shoot projectiles, causing the shield to also function as a ranged weapon. The trait lists the type of weapon, such as “launching dart.” [Striking](link_action_19856) with the launcher requires the same number of hands as normal, except that the hand holding the shield counts toward this total, so a one-handed ranged weapon would require only one hand. Reloading takes the normal number of [Interact](link_action_19733) actions, to a minimum of 1 action, and you can't use the hand holding your shield to reload.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2881,"name":"Launching Dart","uuid":"8881833178962717","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=483","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"220"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:16:11.764549+00:00","description":"A mechanism within this shield can shoot projectiles, causing the shield to also function as a ranged weapon. The trait lists the type of weapon, such as “launching dart.” [Striking](link_action_19856) with the launcher requires the same number of hands as normal, except that the hand holding the shield counts toward this total, so a one-handed ranged weapon would require only one hand. Reloading takes the normal number of [Interact](link_action_19733) actions, to a minimum of 1 action, and you can't use the hand holding your shield to reload.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2883,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2883,"name":"Hefty 2","uuid":"3776296879363154","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=478","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:17:38.704561+00:00","description":"A hefty shield is so heavy that raising it takes more effort. [Raising a Shield](link_action_19750) with the hefty trait is a two-action activity unless your Strength modifier equals or exceeds the number with the trait.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2883,"name":"Hefty 2","uuid":"3776296879363154","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=478","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:17:38.704561+00:00","description":"A hefty shield is so heavy that raising it takes more effort. [Raising a Shield](link_action_19750) with the hefty trait is a two-action activity unless your Strength modifier equals or exceeds the number with the trait.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2885,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2885,"name":"Foldaway","uuid":"7632445537534669","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:17:52.277716+00:00","description":"This shield can collapse into a smaller form attached to a [gauntlet](link_item_6987) for stability and easy travel. You can use an [Interact](link_action_19733) action to deploy or stow the shield. While it's deployed, you can [Raise the Shield](link_action_19750) as long as you have that hand free or are holding an object of light Bulk that's not a weapon in that hand. The shield impedes the use of your hand while it's deployed. Though you can still hold items in that hand, you can't wield weapons in that hand, operate anything that takes two hands, or attack with the gauntlet.\n\nA foldaway shield must be attached to a gauntlet for stability. It can be affixed to an item with 10 minutes of work and a successful DC 10 Crafting check; this includes the time needed to remove the shield from a previous gauntlet, if necessary. If the gauntlet is destroyed, the foldaway shield can usually be salvaged. The collapsible nature of the shield makes it impossible to affix an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon to it.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2885,"name":"Foldaway","uuid":"7632445537534669","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:17:52.277716+00:00","description":"This shield can collapse into a smaller form attached to a [gauntlet](link_item_6987) for stability and easy travel. You can use an [Interact](link_action_19733) action to deploy or stow the shield. While it's deployed, you can [Raise the Shield](link_action_19750) as long as you have that hand free or are holding an object of light Bulk that's not a weapon in that hand. The shield impedes the use of your hand while it's deployed. Though you can still hold items in that hand, you can't wield weapons in that hand, operate anything that takes two hands, or attack with the gauntlet.\n\nA foldaway shield must be attached to a gauntlet for stability. It can be affixed to an item with 10 minutes of work and a successful DC 10 Crafting check; this includes the time needed to remove the shield from a previous gauntlet, if necessary. If the gauntlet is destroyed, the foldaway shield can usually be salvaged. The collapsible nature of the shield makes it impossible to affix an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon to it.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2886,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2886,"name":"Harnessed","uuid":"6134123836252393","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=477","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:18:23.426384+00:00","description":"This shield features a special brace or opening designed to hold [lances](link_item_7065) or other [jousting](link_trait_2748) weapons. Jousters often use these shields as a backup in narrow passages and other places where they're unable to ride a mount. You can [Interact](link_action_19733) to lock a weapon with the [jousting](link_trait_2748) trait in place in the shield, enabling you to use two hands to wield the shield and weapon simultaneously. If you're not wielding the combined unit with both hands, you can use neither the weapon nor the shield.\n\nWhile you have the shield [raised](link_action_19750), you can gain the [jousting](link_trait_2748) benefit of a weapon as if you were mounted. Because a significant portion of the weapon needs to be braced behind the shield, the weapon's reach is reduced by 5 feet if it is greater than 5 feet.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2886,"name":"Harnessed","uuid":"6134123836252393","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=477","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:18:23.426384+00:00","description":"This shield features a special brace or opening designed to hold [lances](link_item_7065) or other [jousting](link_trait_2748) weapons. Jousters often use these shields as a backup in narrow passages and other places where they're unable to ride a mount. You can [Interact](link_action_19733) to lock a weapon with the [jousting](link_trait_2748) trait in place in the shield, enabling you to use two hands to wield the shield and weapon simultaneously. If you're not wielding the combined unit with both hands, you can use neither the weapon nor the shield.\n\nWhile you have the shield [raised](link_action_19750), you can gain the [jousting](link_trait_2748) benefit of a weapon as if you were mounted. Because a significant portion of the weapon needs to be braced behind the shield, the weapon's reach is reduced by 5 feet if it is greater than 5 feet.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2887,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2887,"name":"Shield Throw 30","uuid":"2071518794795293","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=490","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:18:38.722082+00:00","description":"A shield with this trait is designed to be thrown as a ranged attack. When thrown, the shield is a martial [thrown](link_trait_1575) ranged weapon. Its damage dice and type are the same as its [shield bash](link_item_17475) attack, but if the shield includes an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon or integrated weapon, you can choose to attack with it instead when you throw the shield. You add your Strength modifier to damage, as typical of a [thrown](link_trait_1575) weapon. The trait also includes the range increment.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2887,"name":"Shield Throw 30","uuid":"2071518794795293","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=490","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:18:38.722082+00:00","description":"A shield with this trait is designed to be thrown as a ranged attack. When thrown, the shield is a martial [thrown](link_trait_1575) ranged weapon. Its damage dice and type are the same as its [shield bash](link_item_17475) attack, but if the shield includes an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon or integrated weapon, you can choose to attack with it instead when you throw the shield. You add your Strength modifier to damage, as typical of a [thrown](link_trait_1575) weapon. The trait also includes the range increment.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2890,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2890,"name":"Deflecting Bludgeoning","uuid":"6524555752659264","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=473","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"218"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:18:44.775083+00:00","description":"This shield is designed to block or divert certain types of attacks or weapons. Increase the shield's Hardness against the listed type of attack by 2.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2890,"name":"Deflecting Bludgeoning","uuid":"6524555752659264","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=473","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"218"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:18:44.775083+00:00","description":"This shield is designed to block or divert certain types of attacks or weapons. Increase the shield's Hardness against the listed type of attack by 2.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2892,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2892,"name":"Integrated 1 D 6 S Versatile P","uuid":"2839132031931483","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=481","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:19:16.71419+00:00","description":"This shield has been created to include a weapon in its construction, which works like an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon but can't be removed from the shield. This also prevents other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons from being added to the shield. The integrated weapon's damage is listed alongside the trait, such as “integrated d6 S,” with any traits in parentheses. Unless otherwise noted in the shield's description, an integrated weapon is a martial weapon in the shield weapon group and requires one hand to attack with.\n\nThe [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon can have runes etched onto it like other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons. You can continue fighting normally with the integrated weapon if the shield is broken, but if the shield is destroyed, so is the weapon.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2892,"name":"Integrated 1 D 6 S Versatile P","uuid":"2839132031931483","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=481","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:19:16.71419+00:00","description":"This shield has been created to include a weapon in its construction, which works like an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon but can't be removed from the shield. This also prevents other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons from being added to the shield. The integrated weapon's damage is listed alongside the trait, such as “integrated d6 S,” with any traits in parentheses. Unless otherwise noted in the shield's description, an integrated weapon is a martial weapon in the shield weapon group and requires one hand to attack with.\n\nThe [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon can have runes etched onto it like other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons. You can continue fighting normally with the integrated weapon if the shield is broken, but if the shield is destroyed, so is the weapon.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2893,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2893,"name":"Brace","uuid":"6857688639643685","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=471","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"24"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:19:41.322501+00:00","description":"A brace weapon is effective at damaging moving opponents. When you [Ready](link_action_19752) to [Strike](link_action_19856) an opponent that moves within your reach, until the start of your next turn [Strikes](link_action_19856) with the brace weapon deal an additional 2 precision damage for each weapon damage die it has.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2893,"name":"Brace","uuid":"6857688639643685","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=471","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"24"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:19:41.322501+00:00","description":"A brace weapon is effective at damaging moving opponents. When you [Ready](link_action_19752) to [Strike](link_action_19856) an opponent that moves within your reach, until the start of your next turn [Strikes](link_action_19856) with the brace weapon deal an additional 2 precision damage for each weapon damage die it has.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2895,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2895,"name":"Integrated 1 D 6 S","uuid":"415867526743598","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=481","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:21:19.404363+00:00","description":"This shield has been created to include a weapon in its construction, which works like an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon but can't be removed from the shield. This also prevents other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons from being added to the shield. The integrated weapon's damage is listed alongside the trait, such as “integrated d6 S,” with any traits in parentheses. Unless otherwise noted in the shield's description, an integrated weapon is a martial weapon in the shield weapon group and requires one hand to attack with.\n\nThe [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon can have runes etched onto it like other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons. You can continue fighting normally with the integrated weapon if the shield is broken, but if the shield is destroyed, so is the weapon.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2895,"name":"Integrated 1 D 6 S","uuid":"415867526743598","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=481","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"219"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:21:19.404363+00:00","description":"This shield has been created to include a weapon in its construction, which works like an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon but can't be removed from the shield. This also prevents other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons from being added to the shield. The integrated weapon's damage is listed alongside the trait, such as “integrated d6 S,” with any traits in parentheses. Unless otherwise noted in the shield's description, an integrated weapon is a martial weapon in the shield weapon group and requires one hand to attack with.\n\nThe [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon can have runes etched onto it like other [attached](link_trait_3653) weapons. You can continue fighting normally with the integrated weapon if the shield is broken, but if the shield is destroyed, so is the weapon.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2896,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2896,"name":"Shield Throw 20","uuid":"4636467218140761","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=490","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:21:20.72238+00:00","description":"A shield with this trait is designed to be thrown as a ranged attack. When thrown, the shield is a martial [thrown](link_trait_1575) ranged weapon. Its damage dice and type are the same as its [shield bash](link_item_17475) attack, but if the shield includes an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon or integrated weapon, you can choose to attack with it instead when you throw the shield. You add your Strength modifier to damage, as typical of a [thrown](link_trait_1575) weapon. The trait also includes the range increment.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2896,"name":"Shield Throw 20","uuid":"4636467218140761","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=490","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"221"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:21:20.72238+00:00","description":"A shield with this trait is designed to be thrown as a ranged attack. When thrown, the shield is a martial [thrown](link_trait_1575) ranged weapon. Its damage dice and type are the same as its [shield bash](link_item_17475) attack, but if the shield includes an [attached](link_trait_3653) weapon or integrated weapon, you can choose to attack with it instead when you throw the shield. You add your Strength modifier to damage, as typical of a [thrown](link_trait_1575) weapon. The trait also includes the range increment.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2898,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2898,"name":"Deflecting Physical Ranged","uuid":"6912649900147573","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=473","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"218"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:21:51.565687+00:00","description":"This shield is designed to block or divert certain types of attacks or weapons. Increase the shield's Hardness against the listed type of attack by 2.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2898,"name":"Deflecting Physical Ranged","uuid":"6912649900147573","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=473","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"218"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:21:51.565687+00:00","description":"This shield is designed to block or divert certain types of attacks or weapons. Increase the shield's Hardness against the listed type of attack by 2.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2904,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2904,"name":"Deflecting Slashing","uuid":"8398829696303312","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=473","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"218"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:23:44.89733+00:00","description":"This shield is designed to block or divert certain types of attacks or weapons. Increase the shield's Hardness against the listed type of attack by 2.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":2904,"name":"Deflecting Slashing","uuid":"8398829696303312","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=473","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"218"}},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:23:44.89733+00:00","description":"This shield is designed to block or divert certain types of attacks or weapons. Increase the shield's Hardness against the listed type of attack by 2.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2905,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2905,"name":"Scatter 10 ft.","uuid":"4139468490928652","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:06.719407+00:00","description":"This weapon fires a cluster of pellets in a wide spray. Scatter always has an area listed with it, indicating the radius of the spray. On a hit, the primary target of attacks with a scatter weapon take the listed damage, and the target and all other creatures within the listed radius around it take 1 point of [splash](link_trait_1532) damage per weapon damage die.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2905,"name":"Scatter 10 ft.","uuid":"4139468490928652","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-19T04:24:06.719407+00:00","description":"This weapon fires a cluster of pellets in a wide spray. Scatter always has an area listed with it, indicating the radius of the spray. On a hit, the primary target of attacks with a scatter weapon take the listed damage, and the target and all other creatures within the listed radius around it take 1 point of [splash](link_trait_1532) damage per weapon damage die.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2927,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2927,"name":"Cursebound","uuid":"1475291851852924","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=800","book":"Player Core 2","page":"133"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-20T05:15:23.237061+00:00","description":"Abilities with this trait tighten your oracular curse’s grasp on your soul in exchange for divine insights, giving you the cursebound condition. When you use a cursebound ability, you become cursebound 1, or if you were already cursebound, you increase the value of your cursebound condition by 1. As cursebound abilities are directly linked to your oracular curse, you can’t use a cursebound ability if you don’t have an oracular curse or if you are already at your maximum cursebound value. You can’t mitigate or bypass the drawbacks of any cursebound ability with spells or other effects (see [Oracular Curse](link_class-feature_31429)), and the effects of any cursebound ability end when you [Refocus](link_action_19754) and remove the cursebound condition. A cursebound ability that allows a defense uses your spell attack modifier or spell DC unless noted otherwise.","content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":2927,"name":"Cursebound","uuid":"1475291851852924","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=800","book":"Player Core 2","page":"133"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-20T05:15:23.237061+00:00","description":"Abilities with this trait tighten your oracular curse’s grasp on your soul in exchange for divine insights, giving you the cursebound condition. When you use a cursebound ability, you become cursebound 1, or if you were already cursebound, you increase the value of your cursebound condition by 1. As cursebound abilities are directly linked to your oracular curse, you can’t use a cursebound ability if you don’t have an oracular curse or if you are already at your maximum cursebound value. You can’t mitigate or bypass the drawbacks of any cursebound ability with spells or other effects (see [Oracular Curse](link_class-feature_31429)), and the effects of any cursebound ability end when you [Refocus](link_action_19754) and remove the cursebound condition. A cursebound ability that allows a defense uses your spell attack modifier or spell DC unless noted otherwise.","content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2938,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2938,"name":"Plant","uuid":"339889839350251","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=668","book":"Player Core","page":"459"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-20T06:47:45.400828+00:00","description":"[Magical](link_trait_1504) effects with this trait manipulate or conjure plants or plant matter in some way. Effects that manipulate plants have no effect in an area with no plants.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":2938,"name":"Plant","uuid":"339889839350251","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=668","book":"Player Core","page":"459"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-20T06:47:45.400828+00:00","description":"[Magical](link_trait_1504) effects with this trait manipulate or conjure plants or plant matter in some way. Effects that manipulate plants have no effect in an area with no plants.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2955,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2955,"name":"Amp","uuid":"4758220699918244","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=425","book":"Dark Archive","page":"218"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-20T07:12:25.394996+00:00","description":"An amp is a special thoughtform that modifies the properties of your psi cantrips. Psi cantrips each have their own amp, and feats with the amp trait provide different amps you can apply to psi cantrips in place of their normal amps.","content_source_id":12},"after":{"id":2955,"name":"Amp","uuid":"4758220699918244","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=425","book":"Dark Archive","page":"218"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-20T07:12:25.394996+00:00","description":"An amp is a special thoughtform that modifies the properties of your psi cantrips. Psi cantrips each have their own amp, and feats with the amp trait provide different amps you can apply to psi cantrips in place of their normal amps.","content_source_id":12},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2973,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2973,"name":"Kobold (legacy)","uuid":"2287973053270005","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=224","book":"Advanced Player's Guide","page":"268"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-23T16:06:11.707038+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the kobold (legacy) ancestry.","content_source_id":14},"after":{"id":2973,"name":"Kobold (legacy)","uuid":"2287973053270005","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=224","book":"Advanced Player's Guide","page":"268"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-23T16:06:11.707038+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the kobold (legacy) ancestry.","content_source_id":14},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":2977,"type":"trait","before":{"id":2977,"name":"Tengu (legacy)","uuid":"4515163208377767","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=240","book":"Advanced Player's Guide","page":"270"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-23T16:09:35.361155+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the tengu (legacy) ancestry.","content_source_id":14},"after":{"id":2977,"name":"Tengu (legacy)","uuid":"4515163208377767","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=240","book":"Advanced Player's Guide","page":"270"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-23T16:09:35.361155+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the tengu (legacy) ancestry.","content_source_id":14},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3070,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3070,"name":"Summon","uuid":"1097291325651328","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=520","book":"Player Core","page":"360"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-27T07:57:22.479635+00:00","description":"Spells with the summon trait can conjure creatures, typically ones with a particular trait. Such creatures can be found in _Monster Core_ and similar books. Unless noted otherwise, the creature must be common, it gains the [summoned](link_trait_2134) trait, and it must appear in an unoccupied space in range large enough to contain it. The highest level of creature the spell can summon depends on the rank of the spell, as listed below. The spell can still summon a creature of a lower level if you so choose. These rules apply only to spells that have the summon trait; other spells that call or conjure items or beings but that don't have the trait, like [_summon instrument_](link_spell_4875), work as explained in the spell.\n\n* * *\n\n| Spell Rank | Maximum Creature Level |\n\n|:--------------:|:---------------------------------:|\n\n| 1st | -1 |\n\n| 2nd | 1 |\n\n| 3rd | 2 |\n\n| 4th | 3 |\n\n| 5th | 5 |\n\n| 6th | 7 |\n\n| 7th | 9 |\n\n| 8th | 11 |\n\n| 9th | 13 |\n\n| 10th | 15 |","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":3070,"name":"Summon","uuid":"1097291325651328","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=520","book":"Player Core","page":"360"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-27T07:57:22.479635+00:00","description":"Spells with the summon trait can conjure creatures, typically ones with a particular trait. Such creatures can be found in _Monster Core_ and similar books. Unless noted otherwise, the creature must be common, it gains the [summoned](link_trait_2134) trait, and it must appear in an unoccupied space in range large enough to contain it. The highest level of creature the spell can summon depends on the rank of the spell, as listed below. The spell can still summon a creature of a lower level if you so choose. These rules apply only to spells that have the summon trait; other spells that call or conjure items or beings but that don't have the trait, like [_summon instrument_](link_spell_4875), work as explained in the spell.\n\n* * *\n\n| Spell Rank | Maximum Creature Level |\n\n|:--------------:|:---------------------------------:|\n\n| 1st | -1 |\n\n| 2nd | 1 |\n\n| 3rd | 2 |\n\n| 4th | 3 |\n\n| 5th | 5 |\n\n| 6th | 7 |\n\n| 7th | 9 |\n\n| 8th | 11 |\n\n| 9th | 13 |\n\n| 10th | 15 |","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3071,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3071,"name":"Unstable","uuid":"6607689905575663","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=907","book":"Guns & Gears","page":"18"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-27T10:57:58.287071+00:00","description":"Unstable actions are experimental applications of your innovation that even you can’t fully predict. When you take an unstable action, attempt a DC 15 flat check immediately after applying its effects. This DC is 13 if you’re legendary in Crafting. On a failure, the innovation malfunctions in a spectacular (though harmless) fashion, such as a belch of smoke or shower of sparks, and it becomes incapable of being used for further unstable actions. On a critical failure, you also take an amount of fire damage equal to half your level. You can spend 10 minutes retuning your innovation and making adjustments to return it to functionality, at which point you can use unstable actions with that innovation again.\n\nTo take an unstable action, you must be using your innovation (for example, wearing an armor innovation or wielding a weapon innovation). If you have a minion innovation, some unstable actions are taken by the minion instead of you. In these cases, only the minion can take that action, and the minion needs to have been Commanded that turn to take the action. If you critically fail the flat check, the minion takes the damage instead of you.\n\nSome actions have an Unstable Function entry, which you can use to add the unstable trait for a bigger benefit. If you’re unable to use unstable actions, you can still use the action normally, but you can’t use the unstable function.","content_source_id":17},"after":{"id":3071,"name":"Unstable","uuid":"6607689905575663","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=907","book":"Guns & Gears","page":"18"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-27T10:57:58.287071+00:00","description":"Unstable actions are experimental applications of your innovation that even you can’t fully predict. When you take an unstable action, attempt a DC 15 flat check immediately after applying its effects. This DC is 13 if you’re legendary in Crafting. On a failure, the innovation malfunctions in a spectacular (though harmless) fashion, such as a belch of smoke or shower of sparks, and it becomes incapable of being used for further unstable actions. On a critical failure, you also take an amount of fire damage equal to half your level. You can spend 10 minutes retuning your innovation and making adjustments to return it to functionality, at which point you can use unstable actions with that innovation again.\n\nTo take an unstable action, you must be using your innovation (for example, wearing an armor innovation or wielding a weapon innovation). If you have a minion innovation, some unstable actions are taken by the minion instead of you. In these cases, only the minion can take that action, and the minion needs to have been Commanded that turn to take the action. If you critically fail the flat check, the minion takes the damage instead of you.\n\nSome actions have an Unstable Function entry, which you can use to add the unstable trait for a bigger benefit. If you’re unable to use unstable actions, you can still use the action normally, but you can’t use the unstable function.","content_source_id":17},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3073,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3073,"name":"Concussive","uuid":"8087287454612738","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-27T10:59:18.681178+00:00","description":"These weapons smash as much as puncture. When determining a creature's resistance or immunity to damage from this weapon, use the weaker of the target's resistance or immunity to piercing or to bludgeoning. For instance, if the creature were immune to piercing and had no resistance or immunity to bludgeoning damage, it would take full damage from a concussive weapon. Resistance or immunity to all physical damage, or all damage, applies as normal.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":3073,"name":"Concussive","uuid":"8087287454612738","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-27T10:59:18.681178+00:00","description":"These weapons smash as much as puncture. When determining a creature's resistance or immunity to damage from this weapon, use the weaker of the target's resistance or immunity to piercing or to bludgeoning. For instance, if the creature were immune to piercing and had no resistance or immunity to bludgeoning damage, it would take full damage from a concussive weapon. Resistance or immunity to all physical damage, or all damage, applies as normal.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3074,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3074,"name":"Monk (legacy)","uuid":"4675025523768735","meta_data":{"class_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-27T11:01:53.969473+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the monk (legacy) class.","content_source_id":11},"after":{"id":3074,"name":"Monk (legacy)","uuid":"4675025523768735","meta_data":{"class_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-27T11:01:53.969473+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the monk (legacy) class.","content_source_id":11},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3122,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3122,"name":"Conrasu","uuid":"3941709999688801","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Ancestries.aspx?ID=43","book":"The Mwangi Expanse","page":"106"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-29T03:01:09.150022+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the conrasu ancestry.","content_source_id":28},"after":{"id":3122,"name":"Conrasu","uuid":"3941709999688801","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Ancestries.aspx?ID=43","book":"The Mwangi Expanse","page":"106"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-29T03:01:09.150022+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the conrasu ancestry.","content_source_id":28},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3139,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3139,"name":"Modular (B, P, S)","uuid":"3949317784318246","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=271","book":"Gods & Magic","page":"120"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-29T16:23:40.137616+00:00","description":"The weapon has multiple configurations that you can switch between using an [Interact](link_action_19733) action. Typically, switching between configurations of a modular weapon allows it to deal different types of damage, though it’s possible for a modular weapon’s description to list more complicated configurations.","content_source_id":22},"after":{"id":3139,"name":"Modular (B, P, S)","uuid":"3949317784318246","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=271","book":"Gods & Magic","page":"120"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-29T16:23:40.137616+00:00","description":"The weapon has multiple configurations that you can switch between using an [Interact](link_action_19733) action. Typically, switching between configurations of a modular weapon allows it to deal different types of damage, though it’s possible for a modular weapon’s description to list more complicated configurations.","content_source_id":22},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3143,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3143,"name":"Scatter 5 ft.","uuid":"4155312308784127","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-29T16:33:02.010359+00:00","description":"This weapon fires a cluster of pellets in a wide spray. Scatter always has an area listed with it, indicating the radius of the spray. On a hit, the primary target of attacks with a scatter weapon take the listed damage, and the target and all other creatures within the listed radius around it take 1 point of [splash](link_trait_1532) damage per weapon damage die.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":3143,"name":"Scatter 5 ft.","uuid":"4155312308784127","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-04-29T16:33:02.010359+00:00","description":"This weapon fires a cluster of pellets in a wide spray. Scatter always has an area listed with it, indicating the radius of the spray. On a hit, the primary target of attacks with a scatter weapon take the listed damage, and the target and all other creatures within the listed radius around it take 1 point of [splash](link_trait_1532) damage per weapon damage die.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3157,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3157,"name":"Skeleton","uuid":"3838372374465836","meta_data":{"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-30T08:56:50.051375+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the skeleton ancestry.","content_source_id":51},"after":{"id":3157,"name":"Skeleton","uuid":"3838372374465836","meta_data":{"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-04-30T08:56:50.051375+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the skeleton ancestry.","content_source_id":51},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3195,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3195,"name":"Capacity 4","uuid":"7384046082409164","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-01T15:08:54.298495+00:00","description":"Weapons that have the capacity trait typically have multiple barrels or chambers capable of containing a bolt or round of ammunition. Capacity is always accompanied by a number indicating the number of barrels or chambers. After a capacity weapon is fired, you can select the next loaded barrel or chamber as an [Interact](link_action_19733) action that doesn't require a free hand. You can use abilities that let or require you to [Interact](link_action_19733) to reload to switch barrels or chambers of a capacity weapon instead. Each barrel or chamber can be individually reloaded after it's fired as a separate [Interact](link_action_19733) action.","content_source_id":17},"after":{"id":3195,"name":"Capacity 4","uuid":"7384046082409164","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-01T15:08:54.298495+00:00","description":"Weapons that have the capacity trait typically have multiple barrels or chambers capable of containing a bolt or round of ammunition. Capacity is always accompanied by a number indicating the number of barrels or chambers. After a capacity weapon is fired, you can select the next loaded barrel or chamber as an [Interact](link_action_19733) action that doesn't require a free hand. You can use abilities that let or require you to [Interact](link_action_19733) to reload to switch barrels or chambers of a capacity weapon instead. Each barrel or chamber can be individually reloaded after it's fired as a separate [Interact](link_action_19733) action.","content_source_id":17},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3196,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3196,"name":"Capacity 3","uuid":"5380704076850793","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-01T15:08:59.192064+00:00","description":"Weapons that have the capacity trait typically have multiple barrels or chambers capable of containing a bolt or round of ammunition. Capacity is always accompanied by a number indicating the number of barrels or chambers. After a capacity weapon is fired, you can select the next loaded barrel or chamber as an [Interact](link_action_19733) action that doesn't require a free hand. You can use abilities that let or require you to [Interact](link_action_19733) to reload to switch barrels or chambers of a capacity weapon instead. Each barrel or chamber can be individually reloaded after it's fired as a separate [Interact](link_action_19733) action.","content_source_id":17},"after":{"id":3196,"name":"Capacity 3","uuid":"5380704076850793","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-01T15:08:59.192064+00:00","description":"Weapons that have the capacity trait typically have multiple barrels or chambers capable of containing a bolt or round of ammunition. Capacity is always accompanied by a number indicating the number of barrels or chambers. After a capacity weapon is fired, you can select the next loaded barrel or chamber as an [Interact](link_action_19733) action that doesn't require a free hand. You can use abilities that let or require you to [Interact](link_action_19733) to reload to switch barrels or chambers of a capacity weapon instead. Each barrel or chamber can be individually reloaded after it's fired as a separate [Interact](link_action_19733) action.","content_source_id":17},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3280,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3280,"name":"Hobgoblin (legacy)","uuid":"6875858145996890","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=268","book":"Character Guide","page":"133"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-05-09T01:20:37.467834+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the hobgoblin (legacy) ancestry.","content_source_id":19},"after":{"id":3280,"name":"Hobgoblin (legacy)","uuid":"6875858145996890","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=268","book":"Character Guide","page":"133"},"ancestry_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-05-09T01:20:37.467834+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the hobgoblin (legacy) ancestry.","content_source_id":19},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3295,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3295,"name":"Gelid Shard Archetype","uuid":"1200181923993124","meta_data":{"archetype_trait":true,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Archetypes.aspx?ID=201","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"184"}},"created_at":"2024-05-10T15:58:26.399528+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the [gelid shard](link_archetype_110) archetype.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":3295,"name":"Gelid Shard Archetype","uuid":"1200181923993124","meta_data":{"archetype_trait":true,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Archetypes.aspx?ID=201","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"184"}},"created_at":"2024-05-10T15:58:26.399528+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the [gelid shard](link_archetype_110) archetype.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3351,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3351,"name":"Ursine Avenger Hood Archetype","uuid":"4490771783681398","meta_data":{"archetype_trait":true,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Archetypes.aspx?ID=200","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"183"}},"created_at":"2024-05-10T17:31:44.157152+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the [ursine avenger hood](link_archetype_166) archetype.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":3351,"name":"Ursine Avenger Hood Archetype","uuid":"4490771783681398","meta_data":{"archetype_trait":true,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Archetypes.aspx?ID=200","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"183"}},"created_at":"2024-05-10T17:31:44.157152+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the [ursine avenger hood](link_archetype_166) archetype.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3369,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3369,"name":"Combination","uuid":"5029202016770230","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-13T18:11:31.650592+00:00","description":"Combination weapons combine the functionality of melee weapons and ranged weapons in unique or unusual ways. A combination weapon has a ranged form or usage and a melee weapon form or usage. The combination weapons table lists the ranged weapon statistics first and the melee weapon statistics indented beneath, just above the ammunition. Switching between the melee weapon usage and the ranged weapon usage requires an [Interact](link_action_19733) action. However, if your last action was a successful melee [Strike](link_action_19856) against a foe using a combination weapon, you can make a ranged [Strike](link_action_19856) with the combination weapon against that foe without fully switching to the ranged weapon usage, firing the ranged weapon just as you hit with the melee attack. In this case, the combination weapon returns to its melee usage after the ranged weapon [Strike](link_action_19856).\n\nSince a combination weapon is one weapon with two usages, both usages share any fundamental runes. You can put a property rune on a combination weapon as long as it's appropriate for either of the two usages, but if only one of the usages meets the property rune's requirements, the effects of the property rune only apply for that usage. For instance, a [vorpal](link_item_7921) axe musket only applies the [vorpal](link_item_7921) property rune when you're using it as an axe. Due to their complexity, combination weapons can't have another weapon, such as a [bayonet](link_item_13706) or [reinforced stock](link_item_13707), attached to them.","content_source_id":17},"after":{"id":3369,"name":"Combination","uuid":"5029202016770230","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-13T18:11:31.650592+00:00","description":"Combination weapons combine the functionality of melee weapons and ranged weapons in unique or unusual ways. A combination weapon has a ranged form or usage and a melee weapon form or usage. The combination weapons table lists the ranged weapon statistics first and the melee weapon statistics indented beneath, just above the ammunition. Switching between the melee weapon usage and the ranged weapon usage requires an [Interact](link_action_19733) action. However, if your last action was a successful melee [Strike](link_action_19856) against a foe using a combination weapon, you can make a ranged [Strike](link_action_19856) with the combination weapon against that foe without fully switching to the ranged weapon usage, firing the ranged weapon just as you hit with the melee attack. In this case, the combination weapon returns to its melee usage after the ranged weapon [Strike](link_action_19856).\n\nSince a combination weapon is one weapon with two usages, both usages share any fundamental runes. You can put a property rune on a combination weapon as long as it's appropriate for either of the two usages, but if only one of the usages meets the property rune's requirements, the effects of the property rune only apply for that usage. For instance, a [vorpal](link_item_7921) axe musket only applies the [vorpal](link_item_7921) property rune when you're using it as an axe. Due to their complexity, combination weapons can't have another weapon, such as a [bayonet](link_item_13706) or [reinforced stock](link_item_13707), attached to them.","content_source_id":17},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3370,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3370,"name":"Critical Fusion","uuid":"8992761186968496","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=910","book":"Guns & Gears","page":"217"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-14T03:10:44.401258+00:00","description":"Critical fusion is a trait for [combination](link_trait_3369) weapons that grants you two additional options for the critical specialization effect when using the [combination](link_trait_3369) weapon's melee version to make a melee attack while the ranged weapon is loaded. If you choose to use one of them, it replaces the melee usage's normal critical specialization effect.\n\nFirst, if the ranged weapon is a firearm, you can discharge it to create a loud bang and concussion, using the critical specialization effect for firearms instead of the melee weapon group's critical specialization effect. Second, you can choose to discharge the ranged weapon to increase the critical hit's momentum or shoot the foe as you attack in melee, dealing 2 additional damage per weapon damage die. Both of these options discharge the ranged weapon, which typically means you have to reload it before firing it again.","content_source_id":17},"after":{"id":3370,"name":"Critical Fusion","uuid":"8992761186968496","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=910","book":"Guns & Gears","page":"217"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-14T03:10:44.401258+00:00","description":"Critical fusion is a trait for [combination](link_trait_3369) weapons that grants you two additional options for the critical specialization effect when using the [combination](link_trait_3369) weapon's melee version to make a melee attack while the ranged weapon is loaded. If you choose to use one of them, it replaces the melee usage's normal critical specialization effect.\n\nFirst, if the ranged weapon is a firearm, you can discharge it to create a loud bang and concussion, using the critical specialization effect for firearms instead of the melee weapon group's critical specialization effect. Second, you can choose to discharge the ranged weapon to increase the critical hit's momentum or shoot the foe as you attack in melee, dealing 2 additional damage per weapon damage die. Both of these options discharge the ranged weapon, which typically means you have to reload it before firing it again.","content_source_id":17},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3436,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3436,"name":"Fatal Aim d12","uuid":"4177238772426266","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-27T21:14:19.669094+00:00","description":"It’s possible to hold the stock of this weapon under one arm so you can fire it with a single hand as long as the other hand isn’t holding a weapon, shield, or anything else you would need to move and position, to ensure the weapon doesn’t slip out from under your arm. However, if you use both hands, the weapon can make fatal attacks. When you wield the weapon in two hands, it gains the [fatal d12](link_trait_1670) trait. Holding the weapon underarm stably enough to fire is significantly more complicated than just releasing one hand from the weapon, so to switch between the two grips, you must do so with an [Interact](link_action_19733) action rather than [Releasing](link_action_19755) or as part of reloading.","content_source_id":185},"after":{"id":3436,"name":"Fatal Aim d12","uuid":"4177238772426266","meta_data":{"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-05-27T21:14:19.669094+00:00","description":"It’s possible to hold the stock of this weapon under one arm so you can fire it with a single hand as long as the other hand isn’t holding a weapon, shield, or anything else you would need to move and position, to ensure the weapon doesn’t slip out from under your arm. However, if you use both hands, the weapon can make fatal attacks. When you wield the weapon in two hands, it gains the [fatal d12](link_trait_1670) trait. Holding the weapon underarm stably enough to fire is significantly more complicated than just releasing one hand from the weapon, so to switch between the two grips, you must do so with an [Interact](link_action_19733) action rather than [Releasing](link_action_19755) or as part of reloading.","content_source_id":185},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3460,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3460,"name":"Relic","uuid":"2735161210254535","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-06-04T00:08:05.490005+00:00","description":"Some extraordinary magic items grow in power along with a character, gaining abilities that add to an adventurer's legend. These are called relics, and owning one can define a character more than any other magic item.\n\nRelics begin as a simple item, called a relic seed, which is little more than a functional item with a minor magical effect associated with it. As the owner of the relic grows in power, so does the relic. It develops gifts, which are new magical abilities and activations. These abilities might be themed to the relic, the character, or the nature of the campaign. If a relic is passed to another character, this process begins anew, sometimes granting the same abilities again over time, but possibly unlocking entirely new powers. If someone else takes the relic from its owner, it usually works for a while, though it might lose its power incrementally over time if not returned to its owner. How the relic changes in such a circumstance is up to you and should fit the story.\n\nThe decision to add relics to the game is entirely up to you as the GM. If you decide to add them, you'll need to adjust treasure somewhat. It's also wise to consider how many players you expect to end up with relics. Will they each get one? Or will there be just one or two tied to the theme of the campaign?\n\nDiscovering a Relic\n-------------------\n\nSome relics might begin as ordinary items with a rich history. They might be part of a character's starting gear, only to have their true powers uncovered later during play. Other relics can be acquired during play as part of the ongoing story. Regardless of their origin, these powerful items might not appear to be much at first, but they contain the potential to become something truly great.\n\nFor example, an old, tarnished amulet found around the neck of a buried king might turn out to be an item of deep historical significance that awakens to great power. The seemingly ordinary family sword, passed down to each new generation, might unlock hidden potential through the deeds of its owner.\n\nThe PCs might immediately recognize a relic for its ability, or they might carry it for a time before its true nature becomes apparent. The story of a relic should be a tale of discovery. At first, a relic's wielder likely doesn't fully understand the item's power, or might be unable to use it, learning of its abilities only after a momentous event or fortuitous breakthrough. Ultimately, relics are powerful tools in service of the story, working as a valuable tie to the narrative, but their growth and development are in your hands. Because of the place relics hold in the story, they aren't available for purchase, nor can they be crafted.\n\nPay attention to the characters' backstories for potential relics, and look for spots in your narrative that might be suitable for campaign relics. If you're planning to use relics in your game, let the players know in advance, since their ideas and plans can guide you and give them greater investment in the relics.\n\n### Background Relics\n\nA background relic is tied to the history of a character, and its form and abilities should draw inspiration from the story of their character’s life or the past of the item. The relic could be a gift from a friend or mentor, an heirloom from the character’s family, a found object from their upbringing, or even the first item they ever crafted. The player should select the form of the relic (a battered longsword, a copper ring, or a threadbare red cloak, for example).\n\n### Campaign Relics\n\nA campaign relic is drawn from the ongoing story of the campaign. You decide the entirety of the item, from its form to its aspects (described below) as part of the story of the campaign. Use campaign relics to reinforce and foreshadow the themes of your game. Relics come to those who need them to do great deeds, after all, so finding a relic with the perfect aspects for your future challenges is entirely likely. Unlike background relics, campaign relics typically have magical abilities when first found.\n\n#### Relic Aspects\n\nEach relic is associated with aspects—typically two—that speak to its overall concept and purpose. The individual gifts each have an associated aspect. You should almost always select gifts that have an aspect matching one of those found on the relic. For example, a brass dagger recovered from the Medina Mudii'a might have the [fire](link_trait_3491) and [mind](link_trait_3497) aspects, which means that it could have the [flare bolt](link_feat_29523) gift (which has the [fire aspect](link_trait_3491)), but not the [rolling geode](link_feat_29506) gift (which has the [earth aspect](link_trait_3488)).\n\nUsually, you can determine at least one aspect of a relic easily by looking at the history of the item or personality of the character. For example, if a player decides that their background relic is a rusty mace wielded by the character's great grandmother in battle against rising undead hordes, the mace might have the [life aspect](link_trait_3494), as it was used to slay countless undead creatures. There's no harm in letting the player choose an aspect for a background relic; through play, the item will reveal another aspect associated with it. In the previous example, the mace might reveal itself to have powers against demons as well, in which case its aspects might be celestial and life.\n\n**Advancing a Relic**\n\nAs a relic's bearer performs mighty deeds and advances their story, the relic gets stronger. The most basic advancement for a relic is its level, which always matches that of its owner. Weapons and armor can gain fundamental runes normally. You decide what, if any, property runes can be added to a given relic; by default, they can't have property runes, like any other specific item.\n\nThe more complex advancement comes from gifts. The Relic Gifts table shows the typical number of gifts a relic should have at a given level, but relics don't follow this strictly. Rather, gifts arise according to the pace of the story, the needs of the campaign, and the relationship between the character and the relic. Generally speaking, this results in a relic gaining one gift for every 4 levels its bearer has, but this might fluctuate as the campaign progresses. For example, a relic might gain its first gift at 4th level after the bearer defeats a powerful foe. It might then gain its second at 7th, after they perform a special ritual. That same relic might not gain another gift until 13th level and then again at 16th as the player reaches other major milestones.\n\nThe gift types—[minor](link_trait_3479), [major](link_trait_3480), and [grand](link_trait_3481)—indicate their general power level. Again, the table indicates what's generally appropriate at certain levels, but you can alter them as you see fit. You should usually avoid giving a [minor gift](link_trait_3479) at 10th level or higher, because it just won't be that impressive, though some of them scale well enough to be interesting at higher levels. The Gold Piece Equivalent entry for each gift helps you determine how much you should reduce treasure when using relics (see Adjusting Treasure below).\n\n**Table 2–22: Relic Gifts**\n\n| Number of Gifts | Minimum Level | Gift Type | Gold Piece Equivalent |\n\n|---|---|---|---|\n\n| 1 | 1st | Minor | 20 gp |\n\n| 2 | 5th | Minor | 160 gp |\n\n| 3 | 9th | Major | 700 gp |\n\n| 4 | 13th | Major | 3,000 gp |\n\n| 5 | 17th | Grand | 15,000 gp |\n\nYou decide what gifts a relic gains, generally by either selecting a single gift or offering two paths for the relic to grow and allowing the player to choose, but this should be informed by the story and the nature of the character bearing the relic. A relic should complement the bearer, bolstering the bearer's strengths and helping to overcome their weaknesses. Within that framework, you should try to maintain a cohesive theme for the relic.\n\n**Adjusting Treasure**\n\nWhen you incorporate relics into your game, you can adjust the treasure gained by the party down to account for the relics increasing in power. Essentially, some of the treasure from the Party Treasure by Level table on page 59 should be replaced with relic seeds and gifts instead. You can use the relic's minimum level, replacing a permanent item of that level, or you can use the gp equivalent. Keep in mind that relic gifts are often a little more powerful than other items with the same Price even when they start out, and they often scale without any additional costs, so PCs with relics will usually be a bit more powerful.\n\nIf you prefer, you can grant relics in addition to other rewards. This means PCs will be much more powerful, but you're rewarding their investment in the story.\n\n**Making Relic Seeds**\n\nA relic seed can be quite simple: imagine a standard item with two aspects and an appearance that matches the theme. You can also use an existing magic item for a campaign relic; pick two aspects for it, and tweak its appearance or characteristics to make it clearly different from other items of its type. You can choose a tradition for the seed and apply that trait to the seed and all the gifts of the seed. This tradition might be derived from the background of the item, or it might appear or change through story moments involving the relic.\n\nIf you want a relic to have an additional special benefit, you can design it to grant a bonus to a skill, typically a +1 item bonus for a 3rd-level relic.\n\n**Relic Gifts**\n\nGifts are divided up into three tiers. [Minor gifts](link_trait_3479) grant useful, often scaling abilities and are available early in a character's career. [Major gifts](link_trait_3480) define a relic, determining its true purpose and granting powerful abilities. [Grand gifts](link_trait_3481) are the pinnacle of power, and most relics never have more than one.\n\nThe more gifts there are of one aspect, the more the relic reflects that aspect, and the more influence the aspect has on the character who wields it. An item with multiple [shadow](link_trait_3499) gifts might begin to lose its color. With four or five, the character that wields it might take on an ashen tone and the relic might become entirely made of shadow.\n\n**Gift Saves and Spell Attack Modifiers**\n\nMany gifts allow for a saving throw or have other abilities that change as the relic goes up in level. The DC for any saving throw called for by a gift is the higher of its owner’s class DC or spell DC. The spell attack modifier of a gift is 10 lower than that DC. A relic’s counteract modifier is equal to its owner’s counteract modifier.\n\n> ### Player-Driven Relics\n> \n> Though these rules assume you as the GM are providing relic gifts as a form of treasure with input from the players, you can instead have the players make all the decisions for their relics. Encourage the players to choose different styles of items and aspects to match their characters' themes, rather than simply choosing the most powerful combination of options. Have players describe how their relic gets more powerful in the story. What acts from previous sessions lent the relic power? What special meditations or practices did they perform to unlock new gifts? How does it feel to have the relic grow?\n> \n> As the item and the character level up, the player chooses which gifts the item gets from the list as a part of character advancement. You still adjust treasure as normal for incorporating relics into your game. In fact, if the player tries to optimize the combinations, they will likely be more powerful than under the standard method\n> \n> ### Runes as Gifts\n> \n> You can substitute runes for gifts. If you choose to allow property runes on the relic, you'll want them to take up rune slots. Otherwise, you can give as many or few as you prefer, just like any other gifts. Runes are sorted into [minor](link_trait_3479), [major](link_trait_3480), and [grand](link_trait_3481) categories, but you should use their normal level and Price when you adjust treasure, instead of the number and levels on the Relic Gifts table. If you're using the player-driven relics variant, it's recommended you do not include this option.\n> \n> #### [Air](link_trait_3482)\n> \n> Armor ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [energy-resistant](link_item_6927) or [greater energy resistant](link_item_6926) (cold or electricity), [invisibility](link_item_7052); Armor ([Grand](link_trait_3481)) [winged](link_item_7958)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [returning](link_item_7708); Weapon ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [animated](link_item_6703), [shock](link_item_7761), [thundering](link_item_7890); Weapon ([Grand](link_trait_3481)) [greater shock](link_item_7760), [greater thundering](link_item_7889)\n> \n> #### [Celestial](link_trait_3485)\n> \n> Weapon ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [holy](link_item_7040)\n> \n> #### [Death](link_trait_3486)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [ghost touch](link_item_6992), [wounding](link_item_7962)\n> \n> #### [Earth](link_trait_3488)\n> \n> Armor ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [energy-resistant](link_item_6927) or [greater energy resistant](link_item_6926) (acid); Armor ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [fortification](link_item_6974); Armor ([Grand](link_trait_3481)) [greater fortification](link_item_6973)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [shifting](link_item_7755)\n> \n> #### [Fiend](link_trait_3490)\n> \n> Armor ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [energy-resistant](link_item_6927) or [greater energy resistant](link_item_6926) (acid, cold, or fire)\n> \n> Weapon ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [unholy](link_item_7911)\n> \n> #### [Fire](link_trait_3491)\n> \n> Armor ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [energy-resistant](link_item_6927) or [greater energy resistant](link_item_6926) (fire)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [flaming](link_item_6961); Weapon ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [greater flaming](link_item_6960)\n> \n> #### [Life](link_trait_3494)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [vitalizing](link_item_7920); Weapon ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [greater vitalizing](link_item_7919)\n> \n> #### [Mind](link_trait_3497)\n> \n> Armor ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [raiment](link_item_7683); Armor ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [invisibility](link_item_7052)\n> \n> #### [Plant](link_trait_3498)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [shifting](link_item_7755)\n> \n> #### [Shadow](link_trait_3499)\n> \n> Armor ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [shadow](link_item_7751); Armor ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [greater shadow](link_item_7748);\n> \n> Armor ([Grand](link_trait_3481)) [major shadow](link_item_7749)\n> \n> #### [Water](link_trait_3502)\n> \n> Armor ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [energy-resistant](link_item_6927) or [greater energy resistant](link_item_6926) (cold or fire), [slick](link_item_7784); Armor ([Major](link_trait_3480)) [greater](link_item_7782) or [major slick](link_item_7783)\n> \n> Weapon ([Minor](link_trait_3479)) [shifting](link_item_7755)","content_source_id":7},"after":{"id":3460,"name":"Relic","uuid":"2735161210254535","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-06-04T00:08:05.490005+00:00","description":"Some extraordinary magic items grow in power along with a character, gaining abilities that add to an adventurer's legend. These are called relics, and owning one can define a character more than any other magic item.\n\nRelics begin as a simple item, called a relic seed, which is little more than a functional item with a minor magical effect associated with it. As the owner of the relic grows in power, so does the relic. It develops gifts, which are new magical abilities and activations. These abilities might be themed to the relic, the character, or the nature of the campaign. If a relic is passed to another character, this process begins anew, sometimes granting the same abilities again over time, but possibly unlocking entirely new powers. If someone else takes the relic from its owner, it usually works for a while, though it might lose its power incrementally over time if not returned to its owner. How the relic changes in such a circumstance is up to you and should fit the story.\n\nThe decision to add