2","page":"317"},"class_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-07-26T19:00:53.576364+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the oracle class.","content_source_id":256},"after":{"id":3631,"name":"Oracle","uuid":"5425687449005451","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=817","book":"Player Core 2","page":"317"},"class_trait":true},"created_at":"2024-07-26T19:00:53.576364+00:00","description":"This indicates content from the oracle class.","content_source_id":256},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3635,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3635,"name":"Capacity 2","uuid":"3983697842860298","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=845","book":"NPC Core","page":"50"}},"created_at":"2024-07-27T21:05:18.237272+00:00","description":"Weapons that have the capacity trait typically have multiple barrels or chambers capable of containing a bolt or round of ammunition. Capacity is always accompanied by a number indicating the number of barrels or chambers. After a capacity weapon is fired, you can select the next loaded barrel or chamber as an [Interact](link_action_19733) action that doesn't require a free hand. You can use abilities that let or require you to [Interact](link_action_19733) to reload to switch barrels or chambers of a capacity weapon instead. Each barrel or chamber can be individually reloaded after it's fired as a separate [Interact](link_action_19733) action.","content_source_id":16},"after":{"id":3635,"name":"Capacity 2","uuid":"3983697842860298","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=845","book":"NPC Core","page":"50"}},"created_at":"2024-07-27T21:05:18.237272+00:00","description":"Weapons that have the capacity trait typically have multiple barrels or chambers capable of containing a bolt or round of ammunition. Capacity is always accompanied by a number indicating the number of barrels or chambers. After a capacity weapon is fired, you can select the next loaded barrel or chamber as an [Interact](link_action_19733) action that doesn't require a free hand. You can use abilities that let or require you to [Interact](link_action_19733) to reload to switch barrels or chambers of a capacity weapon instead. Each barrel or chamber can be individually reloaded after it's fired as a separate [Interact](link_action_19733) action.","content_source_id":16},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3653,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3653,"name":"Attached","uuid":"6602176486008476","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=539","book":"Player Core","page":"282"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-07-29T19:21:40.637948+00:00","description":"An attached weapon must be combined with another piece of gear to be used. The trait lists what type of item the weapon must be attached to. You must be wielding or wearing the item the weapon is attached to in order to attack with it. For example, [shield spikes](link_item_7754) are attached to a shield, allowing you to attack with the spikes instead of a shield bash. An attached weapon is usually bolted onto or built into the item it’s attached to, and typically an item can have only one weapon attached to it. An attached weapon can be affixed to an item with 10 minutes of work and a successful DC 10 Crafting check; this includes the time needed to remove the weapon from a previous item, if necessary. Typically the weapon can’t be used if the item it’s attached to is broken. If an item is destroyed, its attached weapon can usually be salvaged.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":3653,"name":"Attached","uuid":"6602176486008476","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=539","book":"Player Core","page":"282"},"important":true,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-07-29T19:21:40.637948+00:00","description":"An attached weapon must be combined with another piece of gear to be used. The trait lists what type of item the weapon must be attached to. You must be wielding or wearing the item the weapon is attached to in order to attack with it. For example, [shield spikes](link_item_7754) are attached to a shield, allowing you to attack with the spikes instead of a shield bash. An attached weapon is usually bolted onto or built into the item it’s attached to, and typically an item can have only one weapon attached to it. An attached weapon can be affixed to an item with 10 minutes of work and a successful DC 10 Crafting check; this includes the time needed to remove the weapon from a previous item, if necessary. Typically the weapon can’t be used if the item it’s attached to is broken. If an item is destroyed, its attached weapon can usually be salvaged.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3842,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3842,"name":"Animal Companion","uuid":"8472414784209824","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":true,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-08-20T17:09:52.260863+00:00","description":"An animal companion is a loyal comrade who follows your orders. Your animal companion has the [animal](link_trait_2409) and [minion](link_trait_2527) traits, and it gains 2 actions during your turn if you use the [Command an Animal](link_action_19614) action to command it; this replaces the usual effects of Command an Animal, and you don’t need to attempt a Nature check. If your companion dies, you can spend a week of [downtime](link_trait_1466) to replace it at no cost. You can have only one animal companion at a time.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":3842,"name":"Animal Companion","uuid":"8472414784209824","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":true,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-08-20T17:09:52.260863+00:00","description":"An animal companion is a loyal comrade who follows your orders. Your animal companion has the [animal](link_trait_2409) and [minion](link_trait_2527) traits, and it gains 2 actions during your turn if you use the [Command an Animal](link_action_19614) action to command it; this replaces the usual effects of Command an Animal, and you don’t need to attempt a Nature check. If your companion dies, you can spend a week of [downtime](link_trait_1466) to replace it at no cost. You can have only one animal companion at a time.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":3843,"type":"trait","before":{"id":3843,"name":"Familiar","uuid":"3605522605907992","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":true,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-08-20T17:10:05.075972+00:00","description":"Familiars are mystically bonded creatures tied to your magic. Most familiars were originally [animals](link_trait_2409), though the ritual of becoming a familiar makes them something more. Common choices for familiars include bats, cats, foxes, ravens, and snakes. Some familiars are different, usually described in the ability that granted you a familiar; for example, a druid’s leshy familiar has the [plant](link_trait_2938) or [fungus](link_trait_2445) trait instead of animal. You can replace a familiar or gain a new one as described in the [Pet](link_feat_20407) feat.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":3843,"name":"Familiar","uuid":"3605522605907992","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":true,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-08-20T17:10:05.075972+00:00","description":"Familiars are mystically bonded creatures tied to your magic. Most familiars were originally [animals](link_trait_2409), though the ritual of becoming a familiar makes them something more. Common choices for familiars include bats, cats, foxes, ravens, and snakes. Some familiars are different, usually described in the ability that granted you a familiar; for example, a druid’s leshy familiar has the [plant](link_trait_2938) or [fungus](link_trait_2445) trait instead of animal. You can replace a familiar or gain a new one as described in the [Pet](link_feat_20407) feat.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":4173,"type":"trait","before":{"id":4173,"name":"Reach 10 ft.","uuid":"3411057040924673","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-29T00:31:19.571199+00:00","description":"This weapon can be used to attack creatures up to 15 feet away.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4173,"name":"Reach 10 ft.","uuid":"3411057040924673","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":false,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-29T00:31:19.571199+00:00","description":"This weapon can be used to attack creatures up to 15 feet away.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":4185,"type":"trait","before":{"id":4185,"name":"Time","uuid":"4673057540790920","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=313","book":"Bestiary 2","page":"310"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:08:27.451893+00:00","description":"","content_source_id":240},"after":{"id":4185,"name":"Time","uuid":"4673057540790920","meta_data":{"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Traits.aspx?ID=313","book":"Bestiary 2","page":"310"},"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:08:27.451893+00:00","description":"","content_source_id":240},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":4213,"type":"trait","before":{"id":4213,"name":"Holy (creature)","uuid":"519991618549708","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T18:49:37.224031+00:00","description":"Creatures with this trait are strongly devoted to holy causes and often have weakness to [unholy](link_trait_1846). If a creature with weakness to holy uses a holy item or effect, it takes damage from its weakness.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4213,"name":"Holy (creature)","uuid":"519991618549708","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T18:49:37.224031+00:00","description":"Creatures with this trait are strongly devoted to holy causes and often have weakness to [unholy](link_trait_1846). If a creature with weakness to holy uses a holy item or effect, it takes damage from its weakness.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]},{"table":"trait","id":4214,"type":"trait","before":{"id":4214,"name":"Unholy (creature)","uuid":"2953289258892922","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T18:50:27.540873+00:00","description":"Creatures with this trait are strongly devoted to unholy causes, and often have weakness to [holy](link_trait_1630). If a creature with weakness to unholy uses an unholy item or effect, it takes damage from its weakness.","content_source_id":3},"after":{"id":4214,"name":"Unholy (creature)","uuid":"2953289258892922","meta_data":{"important":false,"class_trait":false,"unselectable":false,"ancestry_trait":false,"creature_trait":true,"archetype_trait":false,"companion_type_trait":false,"versatile_heritage_trait":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T18:50:27.540873+00:00","description":"Creatures with this trait are strongly devoted to unholy causes, and often have weakness to [holy](link_trait_1630). If a creature with weakness to unholy uses an unholy item or effect, it takes damage from its weakness.","content_source_id":3},"display_fields":[]}],"prerequisites":[{"table":"creature","type":"creature","uuid":"722858796387375","name":"Oozeform Chair","row":{"name":"Oozeform Chair","level":-100,"rarity":"COMMON","meta_data":{"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"106","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Companions.aspx?ID=55"}},"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"722858796387375","inventory":null,"notes":null,"details":{"description":"Your companion is an alchemical [ooze](link_trait_2448) that extends pseudopods to move around."},"roll_history":null,"operations":[{"id":"d116656e-d3f6-4e67-a0e5-00b