\n\n*   If your companion is Medium or smaller, it grows by one size.\n    \n*   Increase its Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, and Wisdom modifiers by 1.\n    \n*   Increase its proficiency rank for Perception and all saving throws to expert. Increase its proficiency ranks in Intimidation, Stealth, and Survival to trained, and if it was already trained in one of those skills from its type, increase its proficiency rank in that skill to expert.\n    \n*   Increase its unarmed attack damage from one die to two dice (for instance 1d8 to 2d8)","operations":[{"id":"84e005c3-8a05-41f1-acad-a5688ee74c4f","type":"giveAbilityBlock","data":{"type":"feat","abilityBlockId":40304}}]}]}}],"name":"Next Advancement","actions":null,"level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","prerequisites":[],"frequency":"","cost":"","trigger":"","requirements":"","access":"","description":"You advance an animal companion, usually due to one of your class feat choices.","special":"","type":"action","meta_data":{},"traits":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0"},{"id":4302541392659529,"created_at":"","operations":[{"id":"9921ac76-0334-48bd-b661-0209da83b4dd","type":"adjValue","data":{"variable":"SENSES_IMPRECISE","value":"motion sense, 30"}}],"name":"Motion Sense","actions":null,"level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","prerequisites":[],"frequency":"","cost":"","trigger":"","requirements":"","access":"","description":"Your oozeform chair can sense nearby creatures through vibration in the air. This is an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet.","special":"","type":"sense","meta_data":{"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"106","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Companions.aspx?ID=55"}},"traits":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0"},{"id":3725444017242910,"created_at":"","operations":[],"name":"Mount","actions":null,"level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","prerequisites":[],"frequency":"","cost":"","trigger":"","requirements":"","access":"","description":"This companion is especially suited for riding and ignores the restrictions against using non-land Speeds and moving and Supporting you on the same turn while it is carrying a rider.","special":"","type":"action","meta_data":{"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"106","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Companions.aspx?ID=55"}},"traits":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0"},{"id":7902105097017992,"created_at":"","operations":[],"name":"Support","actions":"ONE-ACTION","level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","prerequisites":[],"frequency":"","cost":"","trigger":"","requirements":"The creature is an animal companion.","access":"","description":"A pseudopod extends out from your chair, retrieving an unattended object within 15 feet. If you don't have a hand free to receive the object, the chair drops it in your space.","special":"If the animal uses the Support action, the only other actions it can use on this turn are basic [move](link_trait_1505) actions to get into position to take advantage of the Support benefits; if it has already used any other action this turn, it can’t Support you.","type":"action","meta_data":{"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"106","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Companions.aspx?ID=55"}},"traits":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0"},{"id":4322909037039800,"created_at":"","operations":[],"name":"Extend Pseudopod","actions":"ONE-ACTION","level":1,"rarity":"COMMON","prerequisites":[],"frequency":"","cost":"","trigger":"","requirements":"Your companion has learned its advanced maneuver through nimble or savage advancement.","access":"","description":"Your chair lengthens itself, granting its pseudopod [Strike](link_action_19856) the [reach 10 feet](link_trait_4173) trait until the beginning of your next turn.","special":"","type":"action","meta_data":{"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"107","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Companions.aspx?ID=55"}},"traits":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0"}],"spells":null,"deprecated":false,"abilities_added":[],"experience":0,"hp_current":0,"hp_temp":0,"stamina_current":0,"resolve_current":0,"operation_data":null,"type":"creature"},"aliases":[],"binding":{"operation_id":"d85a1f8e-a36b-4c34-ba83-01b58455e3e8","item_uuid":"3341821474558316"},"display_fields":[{"path":["details","description"],"before":"Your companion is an alchemical [ooze](link_trait_2448) that extends pseudopods to move around.","after_template":"Your companion is an [alchemical](link_trait_1529) [ooze](link_trait_2448) that extends pseudopods to move around.","bindings":[]},{"path":["abilities_base","1","description"],"before":"Your oozeform chair can sense nearby creatures through vibration in the air. This is an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet.","after_template":"Your [oozeform chair](link_creature_{{allocated_id:722858796387375}}) can sense nearby creatures through vibration in the air. This is an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet.","bindings":[{"uuid":"722858796387375","table":"creature","name":"Oozeform Chair","content_source_id":16}]},{"path":["abilities_base","2","description"],"before":"This companion is especially suited for riding and ignores the restrictions against using non-land Speeds and moving and Supporting you on the same turn while it is carrying a rider.","after_template":"This companion is especially suited for riding and ignores the restrictions against using non-land Speeds and moving and [Supporting](link_feat_34004) you on the same turn while it is carrying a rider.","bindings":[]},{"path":["abilities_base","3","special"],"before":"If the animal uses the Support action, the only other actions it can use on this turn are basic [move](link_trait_1505) actions to get into position to take advantage of the Support benefits; if it has already used any other action this turn, it can’t Support you.","after_template":"If the animal uses the [Support](link_feat_34004) action, the only other actions it can use on this turn are basic [move](link_trait_1505) actions to get into position to take advantage of the [Support](link_feat_34004) benefits; if it has already used any other action this turn, it can’t [Support](link_feat_34004) you.","bindings":[]}]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"2231238570519876","name":"Phistophilus Fiddle","row":{"name":"Phistophilus Fiddle","bulk":"1","level":3,"rarity":"UNIQUE","description":"**Aspects** artistry and fiend\n\n* * *\n\nMade of pure gold with platinum strings, the phistophilus fiddle shouldn't be able to play a note, but play it does, so beautifully that it can move almost any audience. The fiddle was stolen from the [contract devil](link_creature_10242) who created it, and the cunning fiend still wants to reclaim the instrument. Fiendish misfortunes often befall its owners, allowing it to switch hands. The fiddle is a handheld [virtuoso instrument](link_item_7604).\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [little helper](link_feat_29519), [muse](link_feat_28851) (Performance)\n\n**Major Gifts** [charming](link_feat_28852), [fiendish bargain](link_feat_29520)\n\n**Grand Gift** [artistic perfection](link_feat_28854) (Performance)","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"size":"MEDIUM","craft_requirements":null,"usage":"held in 2 hands","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"charges":{},"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"unselectable":false,"starfinder":{},"quantity":1,"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"205","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2408"}},"operations":[{"id":"6dc958e0-89f2-426c-974c-bc779962143a","type":"addBonusToValue","data":{"variable":"SKILL_PERFORMANCE","value":1,"type":"item","text":"while playing the phistophilus fiddle"}}],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"2231238570519876","price":null,"traits":[1504,3460],"availability":null},"aliases":[{"family":"Phistophilus Fiddle","names":["phistophilus fiddle"],"citation_ids":[2408,4937]}],"binding":null,"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Aspects** artistry and fiend\n\n* * *\n\nMade of pure gold with platinum strings, the phistophilus fiddle shouldn't be able to play a note, but play it does, so beautifully that it can move almost any audience. The fiddle was stolen from the [contract devil](link_creature_10242) who created it, and the cunning fiend still wants to reclaim the instrument. Fiendish misfortunes often befall its owners, allowing it to switch hands. The fiddle is a handheld [virtuoso instrument](link_item_7604).\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [little helper](link_feat_29519), [muse](link_feat_28851) (Performance)\n\n**Major Gifts** [charming](link_feat_28852), [fiendish bargain](link_feat_29520)\n\n**Grand Gift** [artistic perfection](link_feat_28854) (Performance)","after_template":"**Aspects** [artistry](link_trait_3483) and fiend\n\n* * *\n\nMade of pure gold with platinum strings, the [phistophilus fiddle](link_item_{{allocated_id:2231238570519876}}) shouldn't be able to play a note, but play it does, so beautifully that it can move almost any audience. The fiddle was stolen from the [contract devil](link_creature_10242) who created it, and the cunning fiend still wants to reclaim the instrument. Fiendish misfortunes often befall its owners, allowing it to switch hands. The fiddle is a handheld [virtuoso instrument](link_item_7604).\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [little helper](link_feat_29519), [muse](link_feat_28851) (Performance)\n\n**Major Gifts** [charming](link_feat_28852), [fiendish bargain](link_feat_29520)\n\n**Grand Gift** [artistic perfection](link_feat_28854) (Performance)","bindings":[{"uuid":"2231238570519876","table":"item","name":"Phistophilus Fiddle","content_source_id":16}]}]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"3341821474558316","name":"Animal Pseudopod","row":{"name":"Animal Pseudopod","bulk":null,"level":0,"rarity":"COMMON","description":"An [agile](link_trait_1569) pseudopod attack.","group":"WEAPON","hands":null,"size":"MEDIUM","craft_requirements":"","usage":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"brawling","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"d6","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":"B"},"charges":{},"category":"unarmed_attack","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"unselectable":true,"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"106","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Companions.aspx?ID=55"}},"operations":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"3341821474558316","price":{},"traits":[2398,1569],"availability":null},"aliases":[],"binding":null,"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"8338913217540863","name":"Sleuth's Pipe","row":{"name":"Sleuth's Pipe","bulk":"0.1","level":3,"rarity":"UNIQUE","description":"**Aspects** luck and mind\n\n* * *\n\nA famed detective once owned the long, curved sleuth's pipe, taking it with them on investigations, keeping it in hand or mouth while cogitating. The pipe might have passed down through generations. Or, when an owner dies without heirs, it could go up for auction, be given to family friends, or remain at the scene of a crime to be found later. The sleuth's pipe has sapience that eventually awakens, allowing the [relic](link_trait_3460) to act as a helpful assistant in investigations.\n\nEven while this sapience sleeps within the pipe, it grants you a +1 item bonus to Perception checks to [Sense Motive](link_action_19847), and if you're an [investigator](link_class_110), any checks you make to [Pursue a Lead](link_feat_30995).\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [repository of knowledge](link_feat_29711)\n\n**Major Gifts** [intelligent relic](link_feat_29688), [steal luck](link_feat_29699)\n\n**Grand Gift** [mental bastion](link_feat_29714)","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"size":"MEDIUM","craft_requirements":null,"usage":"held in 1 hand","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"charges":{},"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"unselectable":false,"starfinder":{},"quantity":1,"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"205","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2409"}},"operations":[{"id":"a04a4b05-53c8-47b5-81fc-b89bcf38aff8","type":"addBonusToValue","data":{"variable":"PERCEPTION","value":1,"type":"item","text":"to Sense Motive"}}],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"8338913217540863","price":null,"traits":[1504,3460],"availability":null},"aliases":[{"family":"Sleuth's Pipe","names":["sleuth s pipe"],"citation_ids":[2409,4938]}],"binding":null,"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Aspects** luck and mind\n\n* * *\n\nA famed detective once owned the long, curved sleuth's pipe, taking it with them on investigations, keeping it in hand or mouth while cogitating. The pipe might have passed down through generations. Or, when an owner dies without heirs, it could go up for auction, be given to family friends, or remain at the scene of a crime to be found later. The sleuth's pipe has sapience that eventually awakens, allowing the [relic](link_trait_3460) to act as a helpful assistant in investigations.\n\nEven while this sapience sleeps within the pipe, it grants you a +1 item bonus to Perception checks to [Sense Motive](link_action_19847), and if you're an [investigator](link_class_110), any checks you make to [Pursue a Lead](link_feat_30995).\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [repository of knowledge](link_feat_29711)\n\n**Major Gifts** [intelligent relic](link_feat_29688), [steal luck](link_feat_29699)\n\n**Grand Gift** [mental bastion](link_feat_29714)","after_template":"**Aspects** [luck](link_trait_3495) and mind\n\n* * *\n\nA famed detective once owned the long, curved [sleuth's pipe](link_item_{{allocated_id:8338913217540863}}), taking it with them on investigations, keeping it in hand or mouth while cogitating. The pipe might have passed down through generations. Or, when an owner dies without heirs, it could go up for auction, be given to family friends, or remain at the scene of a crime to be found later. The [sleuth's pipe](link_item_{{allocated_id:8338913217540863}}) has sapience that eventually awakens, allowing the [relic](link_trait_3460) to act as a helpful assistant in investigations.\n\nEven while this sapience sleeps within the pipe, it grants you a +1 item bonus to Perception checks to [Sense Motive](link_action_19847), and if you're an [investigator](link_class_110), any checks you make to [Pursue a Lead](link_feat_30995).\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [repository of knowledge](link_feat_29711)\n\n**Major Gifts** [intelligent relic](link_feat_29688), [steal luck](link_feat_29699)\n\n**Grand Gift** [mental bastion](link_feat_29714)","bindings":[{"uuid":"8338913217540863","table":"item","name":"Sleuth's Pipe","content_source_id":16}]}]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"8452974248299523","name":"Inventor's Chair","row":{"name":"Inventor's Chair","bulk":"3","level":4,"rarity":"UNIQUE","description":"**Aspects** artistry and emotion (dedication)\n\n* * *\n\nInitially crafted by a gifted inventor who no longer had the use of their legs, the inventor's chair is a [traveler's chair](link_item_7904). It's a marvel of engineering, utilizing clockwork mechanisms to maneuver about. The chair comes equipped with [wheel blades](link_item_15502), and portions of its frame contain [sterling artisan's tools](link_item_6724). The inventor's chair might be a family heirloom or a gift from someone who inherited it. It could instead sit unused in its inventor's abandoned estate, awaiting another user.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [emotion surge](link_feat_29512), [muse](link_feat_28851) (Crafting)\n\n**Major Gifts** [emotion conduit](link_feat_29514), [enthralling](link_feat_28853)\n\n**Grand Gift** [artistic perfection](link_feat_28854) (Crafting)","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"size":"MEDIUM","craft_requirements":null,"usage":"","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"charges":{},"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"unselectable":false,"starfinder":{},"quantity":1,"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"205","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2407"}},"operations":[{"id":"5378776c-43b7-4c2c-b4cf-77fe30319050","type":"addBonusToValue","data":{"variable":"SKILL_CRAFTING","value":1,"type":"item","text":"to Craft items using the integrated artisan's toolkit"}}],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"8452974248299523","price":null,"traits":[1504,3460],"availability":null},"aliases":[{"family":"Inventor's Chair","names":["inventor s chair"],"citation_ids":[2407,4936]}],"binding":null,"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Aspects** artistry and emotion (dedication)\n\n* * *\n\nInitially crafted by a gifted inventor who no longer had the use of their legs, the inventor's chair is a [traveler's chair](link_item_7904). It's a marvel of engineering, utilizing clockwork mechanisms to maneuver about. The chair comes equipped with [wheel blades](link_item_15502), and portions of its frame contain [sterling artisan's tools](link_item_6724). The inventor's chair might be a family heirloom or a gift from someone who inherited it. It could instead sit unused in its inventor's abandoned estate, awaiting another user.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [emotion surge](link_feat_29512), [muse](link_feat_28851) (Crafting)\n\n**Major Gifts** [emotion conduit](link_feat_29514), [enthralling](link_feat_28853)\n\n**Grand Gift** [artistic perfection](link_feat_28854) (Crafting)","after_template":"**Aspects** [artistry](link_trait_3483) and [emotion](link_trait_3489) (dedication)\n\n* * *\n\nInitially crafted by a gifted inventor who no longer had the use of their legs, the [inventor's chair](link_item_{{allocated_id:8452974248299523}}) is a [traveler's chair](link_item_7904). It's a marvel of engineering, utilizing clockwork mechanisms to maneuver about. The chair comes equipped with [wheel blades](link_item_15502), and portions of its frame contain [sterling artisan's tools](link_item_6724). The [inventor's chair](link_item_{{allocated_id:8452974248299523}}) might be a family heirloom or a gift from someone who inherited it. It could instead sit unused in its inventor's abandoned estate, awaiting another user.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [emotion surge](link_feat_29512), [muse](link_feat_28851) (Crafting)\n\n**Major Gifts** [emotion conduit](link_feat_29514), [enthralling](link_feat_28853)\n\n**Grand Gift** [artistic perfection](link_feat_28854) (Crafting)","bindings":[{"uuid":"8452974248299523","table":"item","name":"Inventor's Chair","content_source_id":16}]}]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"8797079847352829","name":"Watch of Lost Ages","row":{"name":"Watch of Lost Ages","bulk":"0.1","level":3,"rarity":"UNIQUE","description":"**Aspects** emotion (misery) and time\n\n* * *\n\nThe origins of the watch of lost ages, a silver pocket watch, are enigmatic. Its construction matches no known culture, and its appearance shifts back and forth from battered and tarnished to shiny and new without cause or apparent reason. The watch exudes a sense of melancholy and loss, and anyone holding it is acutely aware of the impermanence of all things and the march of time, moving ever forward.\n\nThis [relic](link_trait_3460) might show up in a mysterious ruin or spontaneously appear in a spellcaster's hand after they cast a [time](link_trait_4185) spell. The [relic](link_trait_3460) grants you a +1 item bonus to [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753) about historical subjects.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [fervor](link_feat_29513), [sands of the hourglass](link_feat_29806)\n\n**Major Gifts** [fervent spell](link_feat_29515), [temporal pulse](link_feat_29808)\n\n**Grand Gift** [time reversal](link_feat_29810)","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"size":"MEDIUM","craft_requirements":null,"usage":"held in 1 hand","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"charges":{},"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"unselectable":false,"starfinder":{},"quantity":1,"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"205","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2410"}},"operations":[],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"8797079847352829","price":null,"traits":[1504,3460],"availability":null},"aliases":[{"family":"Watch of Lost Ages","names":["watch of lost ages"],"citation_ids":[2410,4939]}],"binding":null,"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Aspects** emotion (misery) and time\n\n* * *\n\nThe origins of the watch of lost ages, a silver pocket watch, are enigmatic. Its construction matches no known culture, and its appearance shifts back and forth from battered and tarnished to shiny and new without cause or apparent reason. The watch exudes a sense of melancholy and loss, and anyone holding it is acutely aware of the impermanence of all things and the march of time, moving ever forward.\n\nThis [relic](link_trait_3460) might show up in a mysterious ruin or spontaneously appear in a spellcaster's hand after they cast a [time](link_trait_4185) spell. The [relic](link_trait_3460) grants you a +1 item bonus to [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753) about historical subjects.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [fervor](link_feat_29513), [sands of the hourglass](link_feat_29806)\n\n**Major Gifts** [fervent spell](link_feat_29515), [temporal pulse](link_feat_29808)\n\n**Grand Gift** [time reversal](link_feat_29810)","after_template":"**Aspects** [emotion](link_trait_3489) (misery) and [time](link_trait_3501)\n\n* * *\n\nThe origins of the [watch of lost ages](link_item_{{allocated_id:8797079847352829}}), a silver pocket watch, are enigmatic. Its construction matches no known culture, and its appearance shifts back and forth from battered and tarnished to shiny and new without cause or apparent reason. The watch exudes a sense of melancholy and loss, and anyone holding it is acutely aware of the impermanence of all things and the march of time, moving ever forward.\n\nThis [relic](link_trait_3460) might show up in a mysterious ruin or spontaneously appear in a spellcaster's hand after they cast a [time](link_trait_4185) spell. The [relic](link_trait_3460) grants you a +1 item bonus to [Recall Knowledge](link_action_19753) about historical subjects.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [fervor](link_feat_29513), [sands of the hourglass](link_feat_29806)\n\n**Major Gifts** [fervent spell](link_feat_29515), [temporal pulse](link_feat_29808)\n\n**Grand Gift** [time reversal](link_feat_29810)","bindings":[{"uuid":"8797079847352829","table":"item","name":"Watch of Lost Ages","content_source_id":16}]}]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"944653220160268","name":"Fortune's Favor","row":{"name":"Fortune's Favor","bulk":"0","level":3,"rarity":"UNIQUE","description":"**Aspects** luck and mind\n\n* * *\n\nBlessed by Nivi Rhombodazzle, this striking silver necklace is adorned with sparkling sapphires that draw the eye of any who see it. Over the years, this necklace has appeared in many paintings and illustrations, usually around the neck of a carefree and daring adventurer or a stylish rake gambling vast sums of coin. Finding this [relic](link_trait_3460) is always seen as a sign of great fortune to come, but when that luck runs out, the necklace is lost just as quickly.\n\nWearing the [relic](link_trait_3460), you quickly realize how distracting it can be, granting you a +1 item bonus on Deception checks made to [Feint](link_action_19633) and on Games Lore checks made to gamble or determine the outcome of a game of chance.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [whammy](link_feat_29697)\n\n**Major Gifts** [clean luck](link_feat_29698), [perception filter](link_feat_29712)\n\n**Grand Gift** [against all odds](link_feat_29700)","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"size":"MEDIUM","craft_requirements":null,"usage":"worn","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"charges":{},"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"unselectable":false,"starfinder":{},"quantity":1,"source":{"book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"204","url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2406"}},"operations":[{"id":"c013f74b-c390-486c-8af2-898799d53f4d","type":"addBonusToValue","data":{"variable":"SKILL_DECEPTION","value":1,"type":"item","text":"to Feint"}}],"content_source_id":16,"version":"1.0","uuid":"944653220160268","price":null,"traits":[1460,1527,1504,3460],"availability":null},"aliases":[{"family":"Fortune's Favor","names":["fortune s favor"],"citation_ids":[2406,4935]}],"binding":null,"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Aspects** luck and mind\n\n* * *\n\nBlessed by Nivi Rhombodazzle, this striking silver necklace is adorned with sparkling sapphires that draw the eye of any who see it. Over the years, this necklace has appeared in many paintings and illustrations, usually around the neck of a carefree and daring adventurer or a stylish rake gambling vast sums of coin. Finding this [relic](link_trait_3460) is always seen as a sign of great fortune to come, but when that luck runs out, the necklace is lost just as quickly.\n\nWearing the [relic](link_trait_3460), you quickly realize how distracting it can be, granting you a +1 item bonus on Deception checks made to [Feint](link_action_19633) and on Games Lore checks made to gamble or determine the outcome of a game of chance.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [whammy](link_feat_29697)\n\n**Major Gifts** [clean luck](link_feat_29698), [perception filter](link_feat_29712)\n\n**Grand Gift** [against all odds](link_feat_29700)","after_template":"**Aspects** [luck](link_trait_3495) and mind\n\n* * *\n\nBlessed by Nivi Rhombodazzle, this striking silver necklace is adorned with sparkling sapphires that draw the eye of any who see it. Over the years, this necklace has appeared in many paintings and illustrations, usually around the neck of a carefree and daring adventurer or a stylish rake gambling vast sums of coin. Finding this [relic](link_trait_3460) is always seen as a sign of great fortune to come, but when that luck runs out, the necklace is lost just as quickly.\n\nWearing the [relic](link_trait_3460), you quickly realize how distracting it can be, granting you a +1 item bonus on Deception checks made to [Feint](link_action_19633) and on Games Lore checks made to gamble or determine the outcome of a game of chance.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [whammy](link_feat_29697)\n\n**Major Gifts** [clean luck](link_feat_29698), [perception filter](link_feat_29712)\n\n**Grand Gift** [against all odds](link_feat_29700)","bindings":[]}]}],"inserts":[{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"5798588885875556","name":"Blue Dragonfly Poison","row":{"bulk":"0.1","name":"Blue Dragonfly Poison","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5798588885875556","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":3,"price":{"gp":7},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1566,1476],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1992","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"67"},"charges":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false},"operations":[],"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n[Boggards](link_trait_2426) brew a potent toxin made from blue dragonflies. Swampseers consume this mixture to awaken their [divine](link_trait_1475) powers, but the [poison](link_trait_1476) causes debilitating hallucinations in most other creatures.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 17 Fortitude; **Onset** 10 minutes; **Maximum Duration** 30 minutes; **Stage 1** dazzled (10 minutes); **Stage 2** dazzled and frightened 1 (10 minutes); **Stage 3** frightened 1 and confused 1 (1 minute)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"primary":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1992","captured_at":"2026-10-01T19:38:40.183Z","sha256":"d46a90ab91c88f95a53233baf22771be45a42023ddb62aee2a6d153a66af2993"},"copy_of":null,"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"6116429865927994","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","row":{"bulk":"0.1","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6116429865927994","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"cp":"","gp":3,"pp":"","sp":""},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1553,1442],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1956","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"58"}},"operations":[],"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an affliction suppressant is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an affliction suppressant, you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"primary":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1956","captured_at":"2026-10-01T19:38:27.464Z","sha256":"b598e7b448e312542ad25f16de4790bdda9a340921a9b77c830153a2a814f069"},"copy_of":{"table":"item","id":15205,"source_id":11},"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an affliction suppressant is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an affliction suppressant, you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","after_template":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an [affliction suppressant](link_item_{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}) is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an [affliction suppressant](link_item_{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}), you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","bindings":[{"uuid":"6116429865927994","table":"item","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","content_source_id":16}]}]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"6159371436995626","name":"Stone","row":{"bulk":"0","name":"Stone","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6159371436995626","group":"MATERIAL","hands":null,"level":0,"price":{},"usage":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2359","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"169"},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":true},"operations":[],"description":"Stone was one of the earliest materials used to create tools, and crafters can still fashion it into a variety of implements, weapons, and even armor. Simple stone objects are made from common materials such as flint or basalt, while exquisite stone objects might be made from crystal, obsidian, or semi-precious gems. Particularly notable stone armors or weapons might even be crafted entirely from a giant emerald, ruby, or sapphire, though they can still use the base statistics presented below. Stone can replace the striking surface of any melee weapon as long as it has no complex moving parts, and ammunition can be crafted with it. Stone can replace metal components in chain and composite armor; only plate armor that specifically describes itself as being made from stone can be crafted from this material.\n\n| Stone Objects | Hardness | HP | BT |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Thin Items | 4 | 16 | 8 |\n| Items | 7 | 24 | 12 |\n| Structures | 14 | 48 | 24 |\n\n#### Stone Object (Low-Grade)\n\n**Price** 1 sp (per Bulk)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"primary":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2359","captured_at":"2026-10-01T19:40:47.455Z","sha256":"7b827b8c905190fb1947b87ad7da44aaa57679f7f0e90394baffbb8b3c54a99c"},"copy_of":null,"display_fields":[]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"7729946021244911","name":"Bone Specimen","row":{"bulk":"1","name":"Bone Specimen","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"7729946021244911","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":0,"price":{"sp":1},"usage":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2358","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"169"},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false},"operations":[],"description":"A durable material when properly treated, [bone](link_item_15403) can replace wood and metal when creating armor, shields, and weapons. The statistics for [bone](link_item_15403) are applicable to a variety of other sturdy [animal](link_trait_2409)-based products, such as chitin, horn, ivory, coral, and shell, which can also be classified as [bone](link_item_15403) for the purposes of determining item statistics. [Bone](link_item_15403) elements from certain [beasts](link_trait_2422), like the horn of a [unicorn](link_creature_10352) or the spikes of a manticore, may even yield [magical](link_trait_1504) properties when worked by a skilled crafter.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"primary":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2358","captured_at":"2026-10-01T19:40:47.198Z","sha256":"722b77629134c83c2927b5f503f913c2b7c25d95596bea8858f03e2eda7cb05a"},"copy_of":null,"display_fields":[]}],"sources":[{"id":1,"name":"Player Core","row":{"id":1,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq02eoj?Pathfinder-Player-Core","keys":null,"name":"Player Core","group":"pathfinder-core","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":986,"item":266,"mode":4,"class":8,"sense":38,"spell":491,"trait":238,"action":96,"ancestry":8,"creature":20,"heritage":50,"language":25,"archetype":8,"background":40,"class-feature":237,"content_update":1950,"physical-feature":5,"versatile_heritage":5}},"created_at":"2023-10-13T17:01:05.041818+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder Player Core","operations":[],"artwork_url":null,"description":"The Pathfinder Player Core presents a new entry point to Pathfinder Second Edition, with everything a player needs to learn how to play the game! Choose from eight ancestries, eight complete character classes, and hundreds of feats and spells to make unique characters ready for deadly adventures in a world beset by magic and evil! This 464-page hardcover tome is the definitive rules resource for all Pathfinder Second Edition players!","require_key":false,"contact_info":"","is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[]}},{"id":3,"name":"Common Core","row":{"id":3,"url":null,"keys":null,"name":"Common Core","group":"common-core","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":131,"heritage":3,"content_update":100}},"created_at":"2025-08-19T02:45:48.489733+00:00","deprecated":false,"foundry_id":null,"operations":[],"artwork_url":null,"description":"Content that's shared between Pathfinder Second Edition and Starfinder Second Edition.","require_key":false,"contact_info":null,"is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[]}},{"id":7,"name":"GM Core","row":{"id":7,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq02ej3?Pathfinder-GM-Core","keys":null,"name":"GM Core","group":"pathfinder-core","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":90,"item":675,"spell":1,"trait":59,"action":1,"language":9,"content_update":729}},"created_at":"2023-12-03T18:43:29.957134+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder GM Core","operations":[],"artwork_url":null,"description":"Unleash your imagination, creating worlds and stories beyond measure with the new Pathfinder GM Core for Pathfinder Second Edition! This comprehensive 336-page hardcover rulebook gives Game Masters everything they need to craft thrilling tales of adventure, from a single-night’s dungeon delve to complex epics spanning years. Within these pages you’ll find clear guidelines for creating new hazards and monsters, tools to design challenging, balanced encounters, and rules for rewarding characters for the dastardly challenges you array before them! Pathfinder GM Core also contains a dragon’s hoard of magic items and treasure to entice and reward your players, from simple healing potions to magic weapons and armor and legendary artifacts, including dozens of brand-new items!","require_key":false,"contact_info":null,"is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[1]}},{"id":8,"name":"Monster Core","row":{"id":8,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq02ej4?Pathfinder-Monster-Core","keys":null,"name":"Monster Core","group":"pathfinder-core","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"item":2,"sense":1,"spell":3,"trait":65,"creature":492,"language":4,"physical-feature":2}},"created_at":"2024-03-24T16:17:47.581819+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder Monster Core","operations":[],"artwork_url":null,"description":"Heroes are defined by their foes—from shambling skeletons to terrifying dragons, each enemy leaves a mark on their growing legend. Make your legends memorable with foes from the new Pathfinder Monster Core rulebook for Pathfinder Second Edition! This 376-page hardcover book is packed with a wide range of monsters useful to all Pathfinder campaigns, giving the Game Master plenty of threats to throw at their adventurers, at any level of experience. The lavishly illustrated tome also includes guidelines for reading monster entries and adjusting existing monsters to tailor fit your story! This is the definitive resource for Pathfinder Second Edition monsters!","require_key":false,"contact_info":null,"is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[1]}},{"id":11,"name":"Core Rulebook","row":{"id":11,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq01zp3?Pathfinder-Core-Rulebook","keys":null,"name":"Core Rulebook","group":"legacy","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":282}},"created_at":"2024-04-18T07:53:09.197853+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","operations":[],"artwork_url":"","description":"This comprehensive 640-page guide to the Pathfinder roleplaying game provides everything you need to set out into a world of limitless fantasy adventure! Choose from ancestries like elf, human, and goblin and classes like alchemist, fighter, and sorcerer to create a hero of your own design, destined to become a legend! The new Pathfinder rules are easier to learn and faster to play, and they offer deeper customization than ever before!","require_key":false,"contact_info":null,"is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[]}},{"id":12,"name":"Dark Archive","row":{"id":12,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq02d8j?Pathfinder-Dark-Archive","keys":null,"name":"Dark Archive","group":"pathfinder-core","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":298,"item":51,"mode":2,"spell":83,"trait":24,"action":1,"archetype":11}},"created_at":"2024-04-18T07:54:37.693741+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder Dark Archive","operations":[{"id":"449a1eca-5519-40ef-8e48-fb9455b7090d","data":{"value":"{\"opId\":\"fc37a4c6-a52e-4c6d-981f-20080ab7c944\",\"option\":{\"id\":\"260203f1-b8d7-44b8-81fb-303b3f3bd1a8\",\"type\":\"CUSTOM\",\"title\":\"Time\",\"description\":\"Whether by accident, fate, or purposeful meddling, you exist slightly outside of time. While initially unmoored by moments, the countless march of milliseconds builds up to drift you further and further out of sync with your natural timeline, often in contradictory directions. You might view this as a blessing, perhaps as a sign you're somehow beyond mortality or you can't be contained within reality's limitations, or you might view it as a cruel curse that causes your own life to slip by adrift even as you gain power over time. Many oracles of time are without faith and either come to rely upon their own instincts to survive or else turn to strange rituals and forbidden magic in an attempt to break free of time's grasp. Those oracles who worship deities most often worship Pharasma, goddess of fate who sees all possible futures for all who ever lived, or Alseta, goddess of transitions and the passage through time.\\n\\n**Mystery Benefit** Time passes more swiftly for you than it does for those around you, enabling you to cover more distance in what others perceive as the same amount of time. You gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speed. At 6th level, this increases to a +15-foot status bonus; at 10th level, this increases to a +20-foot status bonus; at 14th level, this increases to a +25-foot status bonus; and at 18th level, it increases to a +30-foot status bonus. Your disjointed movement makes it harder for creatures to hit you as you move. You gain a +1 status bonus to AC against attacks made against you from reactions or free actions while you're moving.\\n\\n**Trained Skill** Occultism\\n\\n**Granted Cantrip** [time sense](link_spell_5526)\\n\\n**Revelation Spells** initial: [temporal distortion](link_spell_5499); advanced: [time skip](link_spell_5512); greater: [manifold lives](link_spell_5524)\\n\\n**Related Domains** fate, time\\n\\n#### Curse of Turbulent Moments\\n\\nTime passes differently for you than everyone else. You experience fluxes that might manifest as minor day-to-day changes in your apparent age, such as a gray lock of hair or a disappearing wrinkle, or as occasional ghostly temporal afterimages that slightly trail your movement.\\n\\n**Minor Curse** As you draw upon your mystery, time's passage becomes more disjointed, aging, regressing, or warping you out of sync. You become enfeebled 1. In addition, you take a –2 penalty to saving throws against effects that would make you fatigued or slowed.\\n\\n**Moderate Curse** Time distorts further, increasing your muscular atrophy, age regression, or warping while making effects pass you by at an increased rate. The value of your enfeebled condition increases to 2 and the penalty from your minor curse increases to –3. Your status bonus to AC against attacks made against you from reactions or free actions while you're moving increases to +2. In addition, spells affecting you last less time; their duration is reduced by half, to a minimum of 1 round. This doesn't reduce the spell's duration for other targets affected by the same spell. Finally, all non-permanent conditions affecting you that have a duration measured in rounds, minutes, or hours have their duration reduced by half, to a minimum of 1 round. Any afflictions (such as [poisons](link_trait_1476), [diseases](link_trait_1857), and [curses](link_trait_1855)) affecting you have their maximum duration, onset time, and time for each stage reduced by half. Spells, conditions, and afflictions that last “until your next daily preparations” last for 12 hours or until your next daily preparations, whichever comes first. This doesn't change the duration you're temporarily immune, the rate at which you can use abilities that have a frequency, or any other features based on the passage of time.\\n\\n**Major Curse** You become so out of sync with time that it's hard for you to act, but when you do act, you do so with incredible speed. You become slowed 1, the value of your enfeebled condition increases to 3, and the penalty from your minor curse increases to –4. Time passes so much faster for you that your steps appear as a blur of motion to others. You gain a +4 status bonus to initiative rolls. Whenever you move, you're concealed while you're moving and until the start of your next turn. As normal for concealment where your location is still obvious, you can't use this concealment to [Hide](link_action_19726) or [Sneak](link_action_19850). Your status bonus to AC against attacks made against you from reactions or free actions while you're moving increases to +4.\",\"operations\":[{\"id\":\"d3d29cb9-01e9-4fba-b22f-0924e22e452c\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"d2b0e98f-340d-4b6a-b672-2a7e9953c63b\",\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"type\":\"num\",\"value\":0},\"type\":\"num\",\"operator\":\"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS\",\"value\":6}],\"trueOperations\":[{\"id\":\"625c5288-880b-47ca-b0a5-cbf9f70380c1\",\"type\":\"addBonusToValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SPEED\",\"value\":15,\"type\":\"status\",\"text\":\"\"}}],\"falseOperations\":[]}},{\"id\":\"a9c2e88b-a3ff-441a-afbe-b3c1e79b50a6\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"0baa984e-932c-431e-9065-b7c206ace7dd\",\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"type\":\"num\",\"value\":0},\"type\":\"num\",\"operator\":\"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS\",\"value\":10}],\"trueOperations\":[{\"id\":\"52fcd328-00e9-4937-a405-e9d1fd00bffc\",\"type\":\"addBonusToValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SPEED\",\"value\":20,\"type\":\"status\",\"text\":\"\"}}],\"falseOperations\":[]}},{\"id\":\"3faefb73-ad5e-4d0c-a51a-61dffa5ea479\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"7c92ad36-ca06-4eca-90dc-3092a2e9f8d6\",\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"type\":\"num\",\"value\":0},\"type\":\"num\",\"operator\":\"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS\",\"value\":14}],\"trueOperations\":[{\"id\":\"6513d965-ad30-4c22-90d5-824fcffccabf\",\"type\":\"addBonusToValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SPEED\",\"value\":25,\"type\":\"status\",\"text\":\"\"}}],\"falseOperations\":[]}},{\"id\":\"1d4459bb-96c4-4937-be2b-da4fecefd49d\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"ead4bde0-c4ba-4636-9272-5de21600c006\",\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"type\":\"num\",\"value\":0},\"type\":\"num\",\"operator\":\"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUALS\",\"value\":18}],\"trueOperations\":[{\"id\":\"99a84dc1-b240-405c-92e4-b27bd73b28bd\",\"type\":\"addBonusToValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SPEED\",\"value\":30,\"type\":\"status\",\"text\":\"\"}}],\"falseOperations\":[]}},{\"id\":\"f171ddc5-4edf-4bd5-b455-500d529f0dc0\",\"type\":\"addBonusToValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"AC_BONUS\",\"value\":1,\"type\":\"status\",\"text\":\"Applies to attacks made against you from reactions or free actions while you're moving.\"}},{\"id\":\"985a4189-6c1f-47cd-851f-50fab94ee5df\",\"type\":\"adjValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SKILL_OCCULTISM\",\"value\":{\"value\":\"T\"}}},{\"id\":\"f759ecdc-e8d6-4db3-b15b-ab92c7391e0e\",\"type\":\"giveSpell\",\"data\":{\"spellId\":5526,\"type\":\"NORMAL\",\"castingSource\":\"ORACLE\",\"rank\":1}},{\"id\":\"cbec2c87-3e69-46ad-98dd-31cc14a6ddc4\",\"type\":\"giveSpell\",\"data\":{\"spellId\":5499,\"type\":\"FOCUS\",\"castingSource\":\"ORACLE\",\"rank\":1}},{\"id\":\"251b1f14-28e2-40b9-a63f-dde163235eea\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"4afa7e2c-449b-4570-bc29-e3c97b245f0e\",\"name\":\"FEAT_NAMES\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"FEAT_NAMES\",\"type\":\"list-str\",\"value\":[]},\"type\":\"list-str\",\"operator\":\"INCLUDES\",\"value\":\"advanced revelation\"}],\"trueOperations\":[{\"id\":\"ee8041b7-9519-4dab-bfb1-8a9a40238230\",\"type\":\"giveSpell\",\"data\":{\"spellId\":5512,\"type\":\"FOCUS\",\"castingSource\":\"ORACLE\",\"rank\":3}}],\"falseOperations\":[]}},{\"id\":\"5a7839c3-b665-472f-85f9-9c94fa87859b\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"76c8cadf-9907-4471-87dc-ae232cf76aa8\",\"name\":\"FEAT_NAMES\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"FEAT_NAMES\",\"type\":\"list-str\",\"value\":[]},\"type\":\"list-str\",\"operator\":\"INCLUDES\",\"value\":\"greater revelation\"}],\"trueOperations\":[{\"id\":\"8920ce7c-b5c3-4e0d-b00f-5fde5ce9cd6d\",\"type\":\"giveSpell\",\"data\":{\"spellId\":5524,\"type\":\"FOCUS\",\"castingSource\":\"ORACLE\",\"rank\":6}}],\"falseOperations\":[]}},{\"id\":\"3058558d-4650-49ad-8e88-73c2692cbf70\",\"type\":\"addBonusToValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SPEED\",\"value\":10,\"type\":\"status\",\"text\":\"\"}}]}}","variable":"INJECT_SELECT_OPTIONS"},"type":"injectSelectOption"}],"artwork_url":"","description":"From the fringes, the unknown beckons. Pathfinder Dark Archive contains secrets that any player or GM can use to reveal the paranormal lurking in their Pathfinder games! This spine-tinglingly secretive 224-page hardcover rulebook presents two new character classes perfect for delving into the unexplained: Unleash the untold power of your mind as the psychic or leverage supernatural secrets and mystic implements as the thaumaturge!","require_key":false,"contact_info":null,"is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[1]}},{"id":13,"name":"Secrets of Magic (in progress)","row":{"id":13,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq027uy?Pathfinder-Secrets-of-Magic","keys":null,"name":"Secrets of Magic (in progress)","group":"legacy","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":85,"item":192,"spell":185,"trait":15,"archetype":6,"background":21,"content_update":991,"class_archetype":7}},"created_at":"2024-04-18T07:55:57.36985+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder Secrets of Magic","operations":null,"artwork_url":null,"description":"Discover the untold potential of magic! Secrets of Magic, the newest hardcover rulebook for the Pathfinder Roleplaying Game! Secrets of Magic brings the popular magus and summoner classes into Pathfinder Second Edition, unlocking heroes who combine magical might with martial prowess and offering command of a powerful magical companion creature. The lavishly illustrated, 256-page rulebook contains hundreds of new spells with potent offerings for all spellcasting character classes, magic items for any player character, and lore detailing the fundamental structure and theories of magic. A special section within the volume—the Book of Unlimited Magic—presents new methods of spellcasting, with elementalism, geomancy, shadow magic, rune magic, and even pervasive magic to give every place and creature in your game a magical spin!","require_key":false,"contact_info":null,"is_published":true,"required_content_sources":[11]}},{"id":14,"name":"Advanced Player's Guide (in progress)","row":{"id":14,"url":"https://paizo.com/products/btq023ih?Pathfinder-Advanced-Players-Guide","keys":null,"name":"Advanced Player's Guide (in progress)","group":"legacy","user_id":null,"meta_data":{"counts":{"feat":704,"content_update":2554}},"created_at":"2024-04-18T07:57:29.089653+00:00","deprecated":null,"foundry_id":"Pathfinder Advanced Player's Guide","operations":[{"id":"1082e990-bbb1-4c01-aac8-956f3d0938e8","data":{"value":"{\"opId\":\"d2036ef7-5e7a-4a7e-9483-366733464bf0\",\"option\":{\"id\":\"37197dbf-d4d1-401b-989a-0ee9ccdeddab\",\"type\":\"CUSTOM\",\"title\":\"Superstition Instinct\",\"description\":\"A deep distrust of magic drives you to forgo and counter the metaphysical nonsense of spellcasters. Whether you're a member of a superstitious family or culture that distrusts magic, a warrior in constant battle against wizards and witches, a survivor of a magical accident that instilled an intense aversion in your mind and body, or a scion of a bloodline known for its magic resistance, your rage is inimical to magic. This makes you an excellent mage hunter but slow to trust practitioners of magical arts. Your extremely restrictive anathema grants you powers beyond those of other instincts.\\n\\n#### **Anathema**\\n\\nWillingly accepting the effects of magic spells (including from scrolls, wands, and the like), even from your allies, is anathema to your instinct. You can still drink potions and invest and activate most magic items you find, though items that cast spells are subject to the same restrictions as all other spells. If an ally insists on using magic on you despite your unwillingness, and you have no reason to believe they will stop, continuing to travel with that ally of your own free will counts as willingly accepting their spells (as do similar circumstances) and thus is also anathema to your instinct.\\n\\n#### **Superstitious Resilience (Instinct Ability)**\\n\\nWhile raging, you gain a +2 status bonus to all saves against magic. Increase your damage from [Rage](link_feat_24801) from 2 to 4 against creatures that can cast spells. Once every 10 minutes, when you Rage, you regain Hit Points equal to the temporary Hit Points you gain from that Rage action.\\n\\n#### **Specialization Ability (7th)**\\n\\nIncrease the damage from [Rage](link_feat_24801) from 4 to 8 against creatures that can cast spells. If you have greater raging specialization, instead increase the damage from Rage to 12 against creatures with spells and 8 against other creatures.\\n\\n#### **Raging Resistance (9th)**\\n\\nChoose two associated magical traditions: arcane and occult, arcane and primal, divine and occult, or divine and primal. The resistance from your raging resistance class feature applies against all damage you take from spells cast with these two traditions of magic, regardless of the type of damage dealt by the spell.\",\"operations\":[{\"id\":\"a0fc6172-3731-479d-8180-0c2ec52a0c40\",\"type\":\"giveAbilityBlock\",\"data\":{\"type\":\"feat\",\"abilityBlockId\":25056}}]}}","variable":"INJECT_SELECT_OPTIONS"},"type":"injectSelectOption"},{"id":"6c74d13c-b0be-471d-bcaa-a2500c17c2b6","data":{"value":"{\"opId\":\"8285e7d2-ea5a-4e96-a512-c358f892e91b\",\"option\":{\"id\":\"d31e2e11-c44b-4a21-a212-710ce60ca982\",\"type\":\"CUSTOM\",\"title\":\"Psychopomp\",\"description\":\"For good or ill, your ancestors' deeds drew the attention of [psychopomps](link_trait_2457), or you might somehow count one in your family tree. The presence of these shepherds of souls and enemies of undeath has left an indelible mark on you.\\n\\n**Spell List** [divine](link_trait_1475)  \\n**Bloodline Skills** Intimidation, Religion  \\n**Granted Spells** cantrip: [_vitality lash_](link_spell_4936), 1st: [_heal_](link_spell_4656), 2nd: [_calm_](link_spell_4426), 3rd: [_holy light_](link_spell_4660), 4th: [_planar tether_](link_spell_4773), 5th: [_death ward_](link_spell_5698), 6th: [_spirit blast_](link_spell_4853), 7th: [_execute_](link_spell_4609), 8th: [_spirit song_](link_spell_6079), 9th: [_massacre_](link_spell_4718)  \\n**Bloodline Spells** initial: [_sepulchral mask_](link_spell_5263), advanced: [_spirit veil_](link_spell_5273), greater: [_shepherd of souls_](link_spell_5267)  \\n**Blood Magic** The border between life and death becomes blurred to you. Either you gain a +2 status bonus to Fortitude saving throws for 1 round, or a target takes 1 damage per spell level. The damage is negative if the target is living or positive if the target is undead. If the spell already deals that type of damage, combine it with the spell's initial damage before determining weaknesses and resistances.\",\"operations\":[{\"id\":\"43ca65b3-b246-40c3-b7e9-9b6124cb1f21\",\"type\":\"defineCastingSource\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"CASTING_SOURCES\",\"value\":\"SORCERER:::SPONTANEOUS-REPERTOIRE:::DIVINE:::ATTRIBUTE_CHA\"}},{\"id\":\"0c4cd3ed-c558-4c97-b4a5-0ece8fab024b\",\"type\":\"adjValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SKILL_INTIMIDATION\",\"value\":{\"value\":\"T\"}}},{\"id\":\"e0816892-99d4-4d4a-93c3-f43333c614c5\",\"type\":\"adjValue\",\"data\":{\"variable\":\"SKILL_RELIGION\",\"value\":{\"value\":\"T\"}}},{\"id\":\"83b89d3d-6608-4008-aac7-b2d45e7c4dbf\",\"type\":\"giveSpell\",\"data\":{\"spellId\":4936,\"type\":\"NORMAL\",\"castingSource\":\"SORCERER\",\"rank\":null}},{\"id\":\"f8f47c71-531a-4aad-8a81-cae4d07abbad\",\"type\":\"giveSpell\",\"data\":{\"spellId\":4656,\"type\":\"NORMAL\",\"castingSource\":\"SORCERER\",\"rank\":1}},{\"id\":\"8d7069c7-c77f-4c23-8325-b28531cbe726\",\"type\":\"conditional\",\"data\":{\"conditions\":[{\"id\":\"782b5195-3aa8-4d24-9f0d-5af88ee5ec6c\",\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"data\":{\"name\":\"LEVEL\",\"type\":\"num\",\"value\":0},\"type\":\"num\",\"operat